@keys[�"Breaking News!"lI'm live here at <imp>Tri Island</imp>, a mysterious island discovered recently off the coast of Makya."�Trainers from all over the world are making their way over as there have been sightings of extremely rare Pokemon and resources."�With no region claiming major jurisdiction over the island, there have been reports of multiple factions creating base camps in the area."}The only thing that's certain here is the battling as Trainers duke it out over territory and access to these new wild areas."NBut for now, we'll be providing live coverage of the event. Over and out."1Uh -- yes? Did you want to ask me something?"LWell then don't -- can you not -- I'm not a big fan of being stared at."�I just like... I’m a wanderer. Or, rather, not a wanderer -- but I don't have a home -- or, well -- excuse me. I spend most of my time in caves."�I don't know? I mean -- no, I know, but rather I'm not sure why -- I mean, what kind of question is that? I'm a Pokémon trainer."AOr I was. And I’m... rather good at it. And not much else."bA friend's. Just a friend's. I'm good at -- they entrust me with the training. I get results."aI mean, that sounds -- that's not what I really meant. I'm -- I'm -- I was -- let's move on."(Heyo, \PN. Hear you’ve been busy."YYou’re just racking up badges like they’re nothing, huh? Mavis must be so proud."5It’s not a compliment. Just stating the facts."~And the fact is that you’re not getting anywhere now unless you come meet me, for reasons that make me too angry to explain."*I’ve got a <imp>gift</imp> for you."�I’m literally friends with two - I mean ONE - of those gym leaders, and I was the commanding officer for half the people keeping track of Rafael."Word gets around."kI also know that you’re gonna have some issues getting <imp>across that river</imp> without my help."Yikes."Yeah, Mavis is… Mavis."CYou know, you… ah, nevermind. Eye on the prize and all that."JSpeaking of which, you need to get <imp>across the river</imp>, yeah?"0We might be able to reach an arrangement...")But. But... you know how this works."TQuid pro quo, yeah? I know you’ve scratched a few avatars off of my hit list."TGonna be clear as crystal here: you’re doing better than most of the rangers."gSuch as the ones that recently just got mauled by a particularly ornery <imp>Titanix avatar</imp>."SYou know me so well. Put the thing in the ground – well, more in the ground."cIt’s ripping through the mine yard in <imp>Grouz</imp> at the moment, which is… a problem."YIf it goes down particular routes we could be facing a VERY uncomfortable situation."IThe rangers? Dealing with rampaging Tauros and crossroads hauntings."gAvatars are out of their paygrade. Not that we don’t send them in anyways and hope for the best."hSpeaking of which: <imp>Grouz</imp>. Squad went out and didn’t leave a scratch on the damn thing."/You can split it right open, though, yeah?"YYou don’t know what busy looks like, kid. You think I’m not trying to work here?"fI know you cut a deal with Helena. Same here: you accelerate my timetable, I do the same for you."USo make your way down to <imp>Grouz</imp> and turn that Titanix to slag. Please?"rI’ll check back in on you when I hear that behemoth’s gone. Promise I’ll make it worth your while, too."Capisce? Good. Bye."…She hung up."ABefore you can put your phone away, it starts ringing again."%It seems like an important call."*\PN, I need your help. It’s urgent."4You know the <imp>catacombs</imp> under Prizca?"JThere’s an entrance in the <imp>sewers</imp>. I need you here, now."ZI’ll explain when you get here – this isn’t the most secure way to communicate."DIt’s bad, though. Real bad. I need a trainer of your caliber."[Thanks. I know this is sudden, but I can’t overstate how much I need your help ASAP."JListen, kid, if I could call in a couple Chasm strike teams, I would."uBut things change, and now all I have is you. You are NOT going to like the consequences if you don’t help me."Please."=Bring the best team you’ve got. It’s gonna get ugly."?Hey, just checking in. What’s going on? Making progress?"SOh, wow. Really trying your li’l heart out, aren’t you? More than one gym!",Ah, don’t get all broken up about it."[You could be in the big city with six badges under your belt and it wouldn’t matter."Why, I never."6Haven’t you heard blood’s thicker than water?""Practically a type advantage.")Well, whatever -- keep your secrets."8As for me, I’m taking a break before facing Noel."nYou don’t know him -- and, let’s be honest, you probably never will -- but he’s kind of a big deal."bSo while you’re scuttling to and fro like a Falinks without an officer, I’ll be relaxing."Wish you were here!"He hung up…"(Wow, that was… a complete breeze."A joke, honestly."&That’s my sixth badge now. You?"Wow. I remember that."1Wait, how did you even schedule a challenge?"4I made an appointment before I got on the ship."2You... you're serious about this, aren't you?"That can’t be right."You’re better than that."UNot by much, but if you’re lying, then… you’re taking this seriously. Huh."Hah! That never gets old."LYou remind me of… I guess a Zangoose, right? So angry, but so normal.",But you are really angry, aren’t you?"\Well, you’ve certainly made good time, but this is where things start getting harder."1You’ve still got a lot of ground to cover."!See you at the championship!"4I’ll make sure to look in the stands for you."He hung up… again."/Hey, \PN. Things going well on your front?"0Good. You’ve got eight badges now, right?"xThat’s... it’s something. You’ll excuse me if I’m not too preoccupied with the whole gym challenge shebang."That makes one of us."KBetween the avatars and... recent developments... I’ve been swamped."XYeah, frickin’ tell me about it. I know exactly what you’re talking about, too."ZListen: I know the stress is probably getting to you, but we’re in the endgame now."_Be a hero, become Champion, go home to Mavis. Everyone’s happy, right? Smiles all round."(So, yeah, just a li’l bit longer."}Take down those avatars if you can spare the time, come back to Prizca for the Championship, and... we’ll see about Yezera."&Thanks, \PN. I know it’s a lot."Thanks."MWhoever the hell it is helping Yezera, they’ve been making the rounds."iGood news is that you seem to be their priority. Haven’t been, y’know, rampaging. Which is good."�I’ve had zero luck trying to track them down. I’d hire Alessa again if she’d return my calls – but, hey, that’s why I have you, right?"Yes and no. You’re gonna have to cut through some of the best trainers in the region, but it ain’t just busywork this time."jNot that it ever is – thanks, by the way – but this one should be especially interesting for you."jThat’s what I like to hear. This ain’t gonna be an easy operation, but I trust in your abilities."gMostly in committing violence. Lots of violence. Though, actually, maybe try talking this one out?"4You’re gonna want to hear this one. Trust me."wI mean, you’ve got a minute before the Championship anyways. This op is... it’s pretty dire, importance- wise."gI’ve got a confirmed sighting on Yezera. She’s back in her hometown – <imp>Whitebloom</imp>."eYezera’s got a few titans on her and some kind of master plan, so she’s your first priority."a\PN... thanks in advance. Try and be understanding with Yezera. She’s... dealt with a lot." But do what you have to do."\Do what you have to do, come back to Prizca for the tournament, and go home a Champion."$Happy endings all-round, right?"Right. Bye."2Apologies for the interruption, young master."%Or should I say, young champion.""My heartfelt congratulations."...""Regardless, I bear good news."VYou have received a formal invitation from MonumentSoft, a subsidiary of LuxTech."AThey desire your presence at the <imp>Battle Monument</imp>."hApparently it hosts quite the grueling challenge, an “AI Trainer Gauntlet” as they describe it."EThere is to be some manner of reward for successful completions."eThe Monument is best reached by sea. Should you wish to visit, I will see you there immediately."AThat is all. I will distract you no further, young champion."+She must really want to talk with you."Hello to you, young one."It is I, Dr. Hekata."TDo not worry about how I learned of your cellphone number. I simply divined it."2I have a topic to discuss of some importance."PI beseech you—<imp>visit my abode in Grouz</imp>. There we shall discuss.",They must really want to talk with you."DApologies for the interruption to your adventure, young master."wHowever, given that you've sent a number of Pokemon to Storage, I thought it best that I inform you of my project."GTo make it short: Your family owns an unused Estate here in Makya."pSince you're taking on the Makyan Gym Challenge, I took the initiative to renovate the grounds for our use."dI've set up a system that sends the Pokemon you store in your PC to this <imp>PokÉstate</imp>."GI'll take care of them there while you are busy with your journey."pI love Pokemon variety, so I've prepared lots of <imp>EXP Candy</imp> to give you as your collection grows."COnce you've earned some, I'll send them to you through the PC."nI'll continue to wait for you on the boat. If you want to visit the PokÉstate, send me a ping at any PC."%I'll take you there immediately."?That is all. I will distract you no further, young master."H\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]The Tarot Amulet spasms like something dying."uYou feel your pupils dilate and somewhere bleak and broken almost comes into view at the corners of your vision."SA woman’s voice whispers from that place – almost familiar, but not quite."8You shouldn’t have reversed that amulet, dearest."<The woman who gave it to you was trying to protect you."QNow, though, charms for safe beginnings turn to invitations of dire endings."gMaybe there’s something to learn from interlacing your journey with the path of ordeals, though."zEnjoy this brief, bitter taste of the end, darling, and I’ll try and pull some strings should you prove victorious.":\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]Once again the amulet twitches."UOnce again, you can almost make something out, just past your peripheral vision."Once again, she speaks."(Oh? You’re back, dearest. Lovely."UThese people are tied inextricably to this region’s secrets; its conspiracies."oLet me implant a bit of my demesne into theirs, and I might be able to tease them open like a faulty lock."@You want to know more, don’t you? Want them to trust you?")Then prepare to enjoy another trial."3\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]It’s the amulet again."^It isn’t the thing itself that’s in pain. No, something else is – something larger."'Something is wrong in this region.",Another challenge, another opportunity."yI never put much stock into mysticism until my hand was forced. I’m so glad to see my investment paying dividends."MThese people don’t even know I’m threading their fate through yours!"cI paint an impressed expression on their malleable faces – so long as you can walk the walk."/Go on, dearest. You know the rules by now."Y\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]The reversed amulet spasms and the other place impends on you."-That voice… it’s painfully familiar."*Oh, you already know who I am, child."nI’m the one that’s waiting for you at the end of the line. The end of your line… and of every line."&Makya is a place rich in history."VThat’s why you endure these tastes of my demesne, isn’t it? To learn history?"=Well, even history ends. You’ll understand eventually."6Go on. Show me what a conqueror you are, darling."a\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]At this point, you can almost hear fate whimpering through the amulet."3Her voice shushes it, but does not comfort it."�Where did Imogene get this thing? I doubt she realized the significance of the sliver of stone she implanted within this amulet."QIt was uplifted from a forbidden place where history is tortuous and frayed."�Its latent power, the witch’s arcana, and, of course, my… expertise… all aligned to make my little bits of influence possible."-I hope you feel lucky, darling: you are."Always." \i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]....."MThere’s something calming about the hellscape you can almost perceive."*It’s a calm hell; quiet and somber." Her voice is much the same."�If only I could twist these gym leaders’ roles without having to suffuse their arenas with my demesne and all its… antipathy."*History ends quietly, but not kindly."OHere, our day-to-day lives are much like what you endure in these battles."Oh, don’t pity me. My only point is that I would gladly spare you the intensity of fate’s dying gasps if I could, trust me."Trust me, darling."}\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]As the amulet twists and writhes, you can feel the tension of invisible threads being pulled taut."8They are wrapped around the amulet, and around you."sSomewhere behind you they frayed into thousands of strands, and ahead of you they extend to somewhere distant."There they all end.":You understand by now, don’t you? Makya is history.">You, darling, are a history to me – a singular history."3And I am a singular history projected forward."�You have the benefit of what we’ll call a privileged reference frame, and I thank you dearly for letting me glimpse through your eyes at it."0Not to mention making a few… alterations."+Don’t think too hard on it, dearest."5\i[TAROTAMULET_ACTIVE]The amulet has gone still."^Something is changing – the threads are being woven back together, or severed, or both."4Someone is taking matters into their own hands."No, that isn’t me."0We both know who it is, though, don’t we?"dYou should probably stop her from doing that, or one of us could end up in the other’s place."IYou were not made for the terminus, and I was not made for a utopia."=And no human was made for the paradise she’s planning.",…\PN, you know who I am, don’t you?"]We won’t be speaking for a little while, but know that I’m watching over you, child."My child."…Agonizingly familiar."[But, still, she is a stranger to you, this woman who almost has your mother’s voice."	\PN."$I’m swallowing my pride here."EI need your help with something... more important than my pride."You like that, don't you?"5Helping people? Earning some coin along the way?"iI know things are dire everywhere right now, but… that’s why I need someone of your skill level."?Someone with experience cleaning up Team Chasm's mistakes."TMeet me in the <imp>Circuit Cave</imp>. It's under the <imp>Canal Desert</imp>."…He hung up."?The last of the genies whooshed past me a few moments ago.">I poked my head out to check where they're flying off to.".East, across the ocean. I've no idea why."WShit! The Drillers spotted them too. I can see them sending out some Flying-types."DMeet me in the Sandstone Estuary, on that sandbar full of junk."Quickly!"No."Why are you down here?"Who are you?"Whose Pokémon are those?"How do you know?"I doubt it."You want it gone?"What are they good for?"I'm busy."	Why?"On my way."A few badges."Not really."Why would I tell you?"Just beat Helena."	One."Shut up."Making headway."Couldn't be better."There's been trouble."More work?"	Yep!"Not this again.Iu;␀[[&"mPokemon Tectonic has features to help you make sense of its open world, and its many mechanical changes."rThe <imp>What Next?</imp> feature tells you what to do to progress the main story, if you forgot or got lost."7It can be found in the <imp>Game State</imp> menu."~The <imp>Battle Guide</imp> explains the battle mechanics, including mechanics that were reworked or are new in Tectonic."6It can be found in the <imp>Documents</imp> menu."CWhat sort of look would you prefer? You can change this later.".....\ts[10]"C...Of course, of course. I can arrange for a ship to take you."What was your name, again?"So you're \PN?"!So, what is your name, then?".Ah, right. Mavis's youngest child, right?"hWell, thank you for your family's past, uh... patronage. I'll set about arrangements on the double."kMom isn't happy. She's sick of us lee