 Avatar is us members of the Battle Club."^The regular folks sure are lucky so many skilled trainers decided to concentrate there...""Wowie, now that was a battle!"2The club's gonna love to hear about this one."2You should totally come give a talk sometime.Iu;␀�"[[P" The berry plant is growing."oSince the Eleig River is in the halfway point of Makya, it's become quite the gathering spot for Trainers."QThe trainers on the long stretch of river to the East are relatively casual.":That is, until you reach the desert research station."hThe trainers to the west are a bit more serious, especially as one approaches the Cave of Hatching."Hey, yo. Remember me?"3Eifion – guy with the Phione? How you doing?"*Awesome. You doing the gym challenge?"0Ah, what am I asking – of course you are."QNobody hauls around a killer team like that just for fun. Good luck on that."SSure, sure. Don’t mean to pry or anything. Happy to see you’re holding up."LYeah, I get that. I’ve been, uh, yeah, through the wringer, y’know?"*But you just gotta keep your head up."&Anyways, how about a quick match?"MPhione here hasn’t been slacking, and I want to show it a proper duel."You down?"cOh, yeah, take your time. I think I might need a few minutes to get Phione psyched up anyways."'Thanks. Don’t go easy on me, OK?"Whoa. We actually did it."GNot without some scrapes here and there – wait, let me heal you.".Figure I might as well pay you back, huh?"^Uh, kinda? I’ve trained worse, but, uh, this little fella isn’t exactly a juggernaut.">I wouldn’t be quaking in my boots if I had to face one."7OK, I think Phione’s good to go. Ready to fight?"3Good fight, good fight! Phione, you did great."OI mean, \PN, you obviously did way better, but, hey, that’s how it goes."wI used to do a lot better than this. Was pretty good, if I do say so myself, but, eh, it wasn’t really worth it."pYou ever run into someone yelling at his Pokémon after he loses and just think, like, who raised this guy?"DLike, yeah, you get results, but it’s not really sustainable."UThey have to feel like living, feeling beings first, and tools of battle second."Or, like, fifth."&You get what I’m saying, right?"fFigured as much. Look at me talking at you as if you aren’t obviously a better trainer than me."rI’m OK, but I make a lot of sloppy mistakes. Still trying to learn that whole positive reinforcement thing."LYou just gotta make them feel loved, and then they’ll try their best."RPushing them hard wrings potential out of them faster, but it burns them out."CEventually they’ll snap back, or just give up. Or leave you."iWell, sure, but they’re more than tools. They’re alive, and they have their own wants and needs."XAnd if you kinda lean into that, it works so much better than ordering them around."\Or… maybe not. Obviously you know what you’re doing. I’m not gonna preach to you."RI’ve talked enough. Probably should be listening more, but, uh, I gotta go."LMakya’s a big place, and Phione and I are gonna tour the whole thing."FAnd the rest of us, of course. So, uh, see you. And thanks again."xLi'l bit of havoc going down around here, just like the good ol' days! I'll show ya why we used to be the top dogs!"OBeaten by another freakishly-talented kid? Deja vu, that's what that is..."TAh, you ain't nothing. I could beat you any day of the week. Just not... today."!I totally lost my surfboard!"At least I can swim."Prizca Bridge"%Prizca Sewers Auxiliary Entrance"hA line which might have read "Authorized Personnel Only" has been crisscrossed with crude graffiti."YI was thinking of bringing my toddlers to see the bridge. Guess that plan is ruined."Field trip's cancelled!";I'll look on my phone for anything interesting nearby."(Maybe I schedule a trip to the Gym?"North: Prizca West"South: County Park"West: Frostflow Farms"East: Eleig Stretch"YWhy'd they send a waitress to keep watch when an avatar's on the prowl? This is why!"}So, uh, when I said "this is why!" I was supposed to then beat you, and that, uh, didn't happen. So... I'm just gonna go now."dWell, uh... I guess you're gonna have to cover my shift, 'cause I gotta go hit the Pokécenter."aNow that the bridge is gone, I can swim in peace. Or I could if it wasn't for kids like you!"7Wow, you're just as annoying as the cars. I'm out."ECool surfing kid, but don't put me in the splash zone next time."DNo one else comes here, so I guess we're just a little strange."Great."
