self, that might set him straight."QI can still hear his incessant screaming. Please, just stop the kid already."GI'm sure crushing him in a battle will be enough to make him stop."sThank you. Now that his childish dream is done, we can finally get him to sit down and learn something useful."hHere, take this as payment. I'd offer money to anyone else, but Trainers like these sort of things."\One day, that kid will enroll in a college and get a degree that makes some good money."I'll be proud of him then."Traits: Pokemon and You!"Latest Log Entry"Log Off[*"QEn la televisión se está transmitiendo un programa de revisión del hogar."�Es evidente que la presentadora está entusiasmada, pero el sonido está silenciado, por lo que es difícil saber qué es lo que específicamente la entusiasma."/Una luz tenue brilla desde la computadora."S¡Hola a todos! ¡Tenemos un reporte extra especial de lo último en Pokémon!"(¡Hoy haremos un reporte en Rasgos!"@¿Qué significan? ¿Qué hacen? ¿Cuáles son los mejores?"Bueno…"Los Rasgos son pequeñas partes de la personalidad de un Pokémon que puedes descubrir después de pasar tiempo con ellos."�¡Los Pokémon no siempre se mostrarán completamente a la primera de cambio, tienes que formar un vínculo para aprender más sobre ellos!"Z¡No hacen nada en combate! ¡Cualquier Pokémon puede aprender a combatir por igual!"IA la hora de combatir, ¡Ninguna personalidad es mejor que el resto!"E¡Todo lo que importa es encontrar el Pokémon correcto para ti!"!¡Eso es todo por hoy, ciao!";Bueno, esta es probablemente mi última entrada aquí."La mina ha sido cerrada."8Permanentemente, esta vez. No puedo decir por qué."mEl Equipo Chasm ha enviado gente dentro y fuera de la mina cada pocas horas por los últimos tres días."RApesta tener que hacer esto, pero han ofrecido trabajos a todos en el equipo."DNo tendría permitido rechazar esa oferta, incluso si quisiera."iSupongo que tendré que trasladarme. Parece que me pondrán en algún lugar en el suroeste de Makya.":Voy a extrañar al pequeño Braden. Es un buen chico."Oh, buenas."rSin duda puedes escuchar a mi hijo arriba, gritando y corriendo vestido con ese estúpido disfraz de Pikachu."oNunca se calla sobre convertirse en una maestra Pokémon. Esos dibujitos deben haberle podrido el cerebro."iNecesita un golpe de realidad. Tiene que buscarse una carrera de verdad, como ser doctora o abogada."6Sabes qué. Te ves como un entrenador competente."\Si masacras cualquier “equipo” estúpido que haya formado, te daré una recompensa."<Haz que quede en ridículo, eso la pondrá en su lugar."dTodavía puedo escuchar sus gritos incesantes viniendo. Por favor, para a esa niña de una vez."SEstoy segura que aplastarla en un combate será suficiente para hacerlo parar."lGracias. Ahora que su sueño infantil se terminó, al fin podremos sentarla y enseñarle cosas útiles."{Ten, toma esto como pago. Le ofrecería dinero a cualquier otro, pero a los Entrenadores les gusta este tipo de cosas."eAlgún día, esa niña entrará a la facultad y conseguirá un título que le dará buen dinero.")Estaré orgullosa de ellla entonces."Rasgos: ¡Pokémon y Tú!"!Última Entrada del Registro"Apagar;[*"5A home review show is playing on the television."xThe host is obviously enthused, but the sound is muted, so it's hard to tell what specifically she's excited about."*A dim light shines from the computer."JHey y'all! We've got a super special report on the latest in Pokemon!"*Today we're doing a report on Traits!"AWhat do they mean? What do they do? Which ones are the best?"Well..."sTraits are little parts of a Pokemon's personality that you might discover after spending some time with them."yPokemon don't always show their hand as soon as you catch them, you need to bond with them to learn more about them!"UThey don't do anything in battle! Any Pokemon can learn to battle just the same!"HWhen it comes to battling, no personality is better than the other!";All that matters is finding the right Pokemon for you!" That's all for today, ciao!"4Well, this will probably be my last entry here."Mine's been closed."+Permanently, this time. Can't say why."gTeam Chasm has been sending people in and out of the mine every few hours for the last three days."XIt sucks that they're doing this, but they've offered jobs to everyone in the crew."HI wouldn't be allowed to turn down that offer, even if I wanted to."aGuess I'll have to relocate. Sounds like they'll be putting me somewhere in Southwest Makya."/Gonna miss little Braden. He's a good kid."Oh, hello there."tNo doubt you can hear my child upstairs, shouting and running around dressed up in that stupid Pikachu costume."bHe never shuts up about becoming a Pokemon master. Those cartoons must have rotted his brain."[He needs a reality check. He should find better career paths, like a doctor or lawyer."'You look like a competent trainer."ZIf you utterly destroy whatever stupid 'team' he's assembled, I'll give you a reward."BHave him make a fool of himself, that might set him straight."QI can still hear his incessant screaming. Please, just stop the kid already."GI'm sure crushing him in a battle will be enough to make him stop."sThank you. Now that his childish dream is done, we can finally get him to sit down and learn something useful."hHere, take this as payment. I'd offer money to anyone else, but Trainers like these sort of things."\One day, that kid will enroll in a college and get a degree that makes some good money."I'll be proud of him then."Traits: Pokemon and You!"Latest Log Entry"Log OffIu;␀�[["|I've always dreamed of being a Pokemon Trainer! Yesterday I went out and caught some. Now my mom HAS to let me be a trainer!"`You understand right? If I do well in my first battle, my mom will see what I'm capable of!"Battle?"You just don't get it."LET'S GOOOOOOOOOOOOO!!!!"6I'm down but not out. You can't ever put me down."..."Get lost kid."
