 Nidoking here."Isn't that right, buddy?":You see, my partner here has the Sheer Force ability."tIt means Nidoking can use moves that have random added effects, like Trample, without losing HP in the process."OI've just got one left. I'll sell it to you for $6,000. Fair market value."YSounds good. I'll be on patrol for awhile now, so hit me up if you change your mind.")Here ya go, pleasure doing business."&\PN hands over $6000 in exchange."&Guess I'll go back on patrol now."+Looks like you're a bit short on cash."PI get that, wasn't in the best financial spot myself before I joined Chasm."6Despite their pain, my team still loves battling."]To be honest, I don't deserve their forgiveness. I hurt them, but they still forgave me."<I get a bit emotional everytime I think about it, haha."West: Kilna Turf"North: East Tunnel"East: Grouz Mine"South-East: Amber Hills"Grouz Mine"|My my, I hope you aren't here to battle. I won't be able to tell my Pokemon anything if you keep taking my breath away."\Oh, you are? Ah, I suppose a rose as pretty as you would have some very sharp thorns..."]I laid out each of these starter tokens to maybe attract someone suitable... for battle."7Perhaps you'll be able to satisfy both criteria...":The top of the sign is labeled "Grouz Mine Bulletin.""DRemnants of old, yellowed papers are still stapled to the rest."What a disgrace."1We're supposed to be keeping this area safe."A call for you, Trainer."'The ranger hands you a cell phone."XHeard a certain metal worm is no longer with us. You won’t see me at the funeral."PAnyways, I’m a woman of my word – I’ll be your friend in high places."PI’m holed up in <imp>Helena’s place</imp>, west of the LuxTech eyesore."-North-west of the lake, can’t miss it."6Oh, and bring your team. I invited another guest."RAh, where were you in the good ol’ days? You would’ve made a great grunt!"8...That’s a compliment, by the way. See ya there."CYou gotta keep sharp! Don’t tell me you’re sick of fights."HOur guest’s pretty good, too. She might teach you a thing or two."Well, see ya."}You think I’M bad? Try working with Helena for a few years. Especially back when she had strike teams at her disposal."kYou’re strong. You’ve proven that. This’ll be a piece of cake. Trust me. So I’ll see ya there."…She hung up."Thanks for the help."Dr. Hekata's House"The door is boarded up."-Hello, \PN. It’s been quite some time!"�Though I’ve heard tales of someone that looked like you talking to someone that looked like me by a certain river that I know a certain Ditto appreciates."YWell, I say that, but I suppose I’ve never verified that she is, in fact, a Ditto."8I have never seen her un-transformed, specifically."\I have tried tossing a Poké Ball at her, with no effect other than a withering glower."hShe could be anything, I suppose, but what else can take human form for so long with such accuracy?"dA particularly persistent and vocal Zoroark? Perhaps some other Pokémon that learns Transform?"|Or perhaps she really is simply a doppelganger of eldritch origin, or a spirit haunting me for some forgotten transgression."?The one that gave you that amulet – not that it matters."kDon’t worry, I don’t take any offense! My doppelganger and I are more alike than we are different."QHow, precisely, would a Ditto learn to imitate my manners with such care...?"JI suppose it bears little tangible relevance to my situation, though."=Oh, I’m sorry I’m such a glum philosopher archetype."�If I must play a stock role in your story, I would prefer to be an oracle distributing wisdom, or a magical creature bestowing some blessing or artifact."CI hope you’re not expecting any wisdom or artifacts from me."[I fear I’m far too invested in my own quest for self- discovery to aid you in yours."�...Oh, that isn’t true. I can’t maintain a charade of indifference half as well as my companion. I am rather invested in you and yours."Thank you."�I could easily take the simple explanation afforded to all diviners: that I am interested in you because I have foretold some matter of interest in your future."aUnfortunately, I am insufferably honest, so I must confess that I simply enjoy your company."qIndeed. You are plainly at the center of a whorl of causality here – it takes no arcana to determine that."pI cannot ascertain the future with any degree of certainty, but I can plainly see which way the river cuts."AI would like to liberate its path of hindrances if possible."xOh! Excuse me, I refer merely to my interest in seeing your rather unique path through fate’s weave come to pass."]Well, that and a respectable appreciation for the quality of your character and company."�It was not my intent to imply an interest in an... assignation, if that was what you were asking. Such passions are not my lot in life."_Consider it a professional curiosity, if that might ease your concerns... or insecurities."FYou are of note not merely for your personality and character –"ithough I confess some partiality to both – but for the briar-knot of fate you are embedded within."TMany lives are wound around you. Around your fingers, or your throat, I wonder?"RPut plainly, you’re important, I’m curious, and I like our conversations."zEven the ones I am not privy to I imagine are enlightening for my other half, and her revelations may lead to my own."�Speaking of which, I am not merely here for pleasure. I had returned home for the express purpose of finding some clue as to my past."}I... cannot remember it. That this is my hometown, yes, and stray faint recollections from my youth, but beyond that nothing."`Not until a comparatively luminous memory of riding on a train with my imitator at my side."MWhatever had happened before that leg of our journey, I do not remember."KI only know that I am real, she is false, and I journey to prove such."+Not at all. But I must keep the faith."�After all, if I am merely some animal that has deluded itself into humanity... well, the ethical quandaries alone would drive me mad."nOh, plenty. Scraps of childhood, as I said. Being on the train is the first full memory of my modern era."�And from there, my memory is mostly whole – though the persistence and clarity of memory is something ethereal and unquantifiable."<Perhaps mine are fragmented and faded compared to most."GShe likes to elude me, and, though I am loathe to admit it, I her."_It is rare we get more than a fleeting moment alone. Things are now... different, however."fBeing here has driven my thoughts to doubt and darker places than that. I have found now answers."FThe other Imogene has already left, unable to bear it any longer."|She left a note stating simply that she knew what she must do, and that she goes now to a place of death and quiet oblivion."zI choose to interpret it as guidance to find a <imp>burial ground or mausoleum</imp>, and not as her last goodbyes..."2I’m unsure if there is a difference for us."0\PN… I don’t know that we should exist."aThere is something fundamentally wrong with us. Our state is not natural, nor is it tenable."$...Ignore my macabre ramblings."@I will follow her, and find the proof of my true existence."mIf you wish to bear witness to these revelations and watch as her lies crumble around her, come find us."DShe knows something dire that I do not. I must know what it is."GI'm trying to figure out why certain Avatars appear where they do."SThey're often species that'd make sense for the local ecology, but not always."-Sometimes they're just.... somewhat off."Beats me."xI heard the stories, but it's still hard to believe that Avatars just... fade from existence when they're defeated."oWhen I saw that you were winning, I was mentally prepared to grab a pickaxe and begin the cleanup efforts."It's holding a Life Orb!"*Ohoh, does another fly enter my trap?"6Watch yourself, you may find yourself mesmerized."3Tsk! It seems like you were too hot to handle."@Ah well, I suppose I could always ask Lainie to console me."'A spark. A flash. A line of roses."5We should take our tango once more from the top."But later, my dear."/I've found myself as a bit of a historian."eI'm learning about important dates in history. The founding of Prizca, the fall of the monarchy."VAll of them are fascinating, but I believe my favorite is the one we'll have, no?"Yes"No"No thanks."Sure, I'll pay."Sure thing."Really?"You're a pain."What do you mean?"What else?"...Which one are you?"The feeling's mutual."Oh?"In... what way?"Please don't be."How sure are you?"Any other memories?"Where is she now?[�"6¡Presentando, mi propio ataque de tipo Flexible!"Q¿De qué categoría es? ¿Físico, quizás especial? ¡Ambos, por supuesto!"A¡Tu Pokémon usa la que mejor le convenga según sus stats!"a¿Hay una trampa, te preguntas? …Sí… el movimiento falla el 20 por ciento de las veces."H¿Qué dices? Montones de Pokémon pueden aprender este movimiento."=¡Verdaderamente has encontrado lo mejor en movimientos!"QBien… sólo quería algo que hacer ahora que la mina que la mina cerró…"¡¿Qué haces?!"A¿Eres \PN, cierto? ¿El entrenador que la Profesora llamó?"?¡Así que ve a destruir ese Avatar antes de que nos mate!"~Solía usar un montón de Vidasferas. No me importaba si mis Pokémon se lastimaban siempre y cuando hicieran el trabajo."OPero ya no soy ese tipo de personas. Estoy intentando deshacerme de ellas."[El único Pokémon al que le doy una Vidasfera estos días es a mi confiable Nidoking."¿Es eso cierto, amigo?"=Ya ves, mi compañero tiene la habilidad Potencia Bruta."�Eso significa que Nidoking puede usar movimientos con efectos secundaraios aleatorios, como Pisotear, sin perder PS en el proceso."FSólo me queda una. Te la venderé por $6.000. Precio de mercado."aSuena bien. Estaré en patrulla por un rato ahora, así que háblame si cambias de opinión."+Aquí tienes, un gusto hacer negocios."\PN da los $6000."&Supongo que volveré a patrullar."'Parece que estás corto de dinero."[Lo entiendo, tampoco estaba en la mejor situación económica antes de unirme a Chasm.":A pesar de su dolor, mi equipo todavía ama combatir."VPara ser honestos, no merezco su perdón. Los lastimé, y aun así me perdonaron."FMe pongo un poco emocional cada vez que pienso al respecto, jaja."Oeste: Campo Kilna"Norte: Túnel Oriental"Este: Mina Grouz"Sureste: Colinas Ámbar"Mina Grouz"{Uy, espero que no estés aquí para combatir. No podré decirles nada a mis Pokémon si sigues quitándome el aliento."eOh, ¿Lo estás? Ah, supongo que una rosa tan bonita como tú tiene unas espinas muy afiladas..."RDejé una de cada ficha inicial para atraer a alguien digno... para combatir."6Quizás tú podrás satisfacer ambos criterios..."VLa parte superior del signo está marcada como “Boletín de las Minas Grouz.”">Remanentes de viejos papeles amarillos siguen engrapados."Vaya desgracia.">Se suponía que teníamos que mantener esta área segura.")Esta llamada es para ti, Entrenador." El ranger te da un celular."aEscuché que cierto gusano metálico ya no está entre nosotros. No me verás en el funeral."IComo sea, soy una mujer de palabra - Seré tu amiga en cargos altos."@Estoy en la <imp>casa de Helena</imp>, al oeste de LuxTech.".Al noroeste del lago, no puedes perderte."1Ah, y trae tu equipo. Tenemos otra invitada."XAh, ¿Dónde estabas en los buenos viejos tiempos? ¡Habrías sido un gran recluta!"4…Eso es un cumplido, por cierto. Te veo ahí."C¡Mantente fuerte! No me digas que estás cansado de combatir."YNuestra invitada es bastante buena también. Ella te puede enseñar un par de cosas."Bueno, nos vemos."�¿Piensas que YO soy mala? Intenta trabajar con Helena por algunos años. Especialmente cuando ella tenía equipos de asalto a su disposición."TEres fuerte. Has demostrado eso. Esto será pan comido. Creéme. Te veré ahí."…Colgó"Gracias por la ayuda."Casa de la Dr. Hekata"La puerta está cerrada."-Hola, \PN. ¡Hace cuánto que no te veo!"�Aunque he escuchado que alguien similar a ti estaba hablando con alguien similar a mi cerca de cierto río el cual sé que un cierto Ditto aprecia."oBueno, eso es lo que siempre digo, pero supongo que nunca he verificado que ella sea, en efecto, un Ditto."9Específicamente, nunca la he visto sin transformar."PHe intentando lanzarle una Poké Ball, pero no tuvo ningún efecto más que"{Podría ser cualquier cosa, supongo, ¿Pero qué más podría tomar una forma humana por tanto tiempo con tanta precisión?"k¿Un Zoroark particularmente persistente y vocal? ¿Quizás otro Pokémon que conozca Transformación?"�O quizás ella realmente es sólo un doppelganger de origen sobrenatural, o un espíritu acósandome por una transgresión olvidada."CAquella que te dió aquel amuleto – no es como si importara."d¡No te preocupes, no me ofendo! Mi doppelganger y yo tenemos más similitudes que diferencias."a¿Cómo, precisamente, podría un Ditto aprender a imitar mis modales con tanto cuidados...?"HAunque supongo que posee poca relevancia tangible en mi situación."KOh, disculpa que sea sólo el arquetipo de una filósofa melancólica."�Si debo jugar un rol en tu historia, preferiría ser la oráculo que distribuye sabiduría, o una criatura mágica portadora de una bendición o artefacto."BEspero que no estés esperando sabiduría o artefactos de mi."wTemo que estoy demasiado comprometida en mi propia búsqueda de auto-descubrimiento como para ayudarte en la tuya."�...Oh, eso no es verdad. No puedo mantener la farsa de indeferencia tan bien como mi compañera. Estoy bastante comprometida en lo tuyo."Gracias."�Podría simplemente tomar la simple explicación usadas por todos los adivinos: que estoy interesada en ti porque he presagiado algo interesante en tu futuro."xDesafortunadamente, soy insoportablemente honesta, por lo que debo confesar que simplemente disfruto tu compañía."�En efecto. Simplemente estás en el centro de un espiral de causalidad aquí – no necesitas ninguna arcana para determinar eso."`No puedo verificar el futuro con ningún grado de certeza, pero puedo ver a dónde va esto."?Me gustaría liberar su camino de molestias si es posible."s¡Oh! Discúlpame, me refiero meramente a mi intéres en ver el camino peculiar que el destino tejió para ti."ZBueno, eso y una respetable apreciación por la calidad de tu personaje y compañía."�No fue mi intención implicar un interés en una... reunión, si eso es lo que estás preguntando. Tales pasiones no son lo que busco."iConsíderalo una curiosidad profesional, si eso puede aliviar tus preocupaciones... o inseguridades."?Eres de notar no sólo por tu personalidad y personaje –"iAunque debo confesar algo de inclinación a ambos – excepto por el lazo que el destino te brindó."iVarias vidas están enrollados a tu alrededor. ¿Me pregunto si alrededor de tus dedos, o tu cuello?"cTe lo digo claramente, eres importante, tengo curiosidad, y me gustan nuestras conversaciones."�Incluso de aquellos que no estoy al tanto imagino que son iluminadores para mi otra mitad, y sus revelaciones podrían terminar en la mía."�Hablando de eso, no estoy aquí meramente por placer. Regresé a mi hogar para el mero propósito de encontrar alguna pista de mi pasado."~No... puedo recordarlo. Este es mi pueblo natal, sí, y me llegan vagos recuerdos de mi juventud, pero después de ahí, nada."gNo hasta a una, en comparación, luminosa memoria de subirme a un tren con mi imitadora a mi lado."SLo que sea que ocurró antes de esa parte de nuestra aventura, no lo recuerdo."QSólo sé que yo soy real, y ella es falsa, y mi travesía para demostrarlo.",En absoluto. Pero debo mantener la fé."�Después de todo, soy meramente un animal que se ha engañado para fingir humanidad... bueno, sólo los dilemas morales me enloquecerían."zOh, varios. Fragmentos de mi niñez, como lo dije. Estar en un tren es el primer recuerdo completo de mi era moderna."�Y de ahí en adelante, mi memoria está mayormente completa – pero la persistencia y la claridad de mi memoria es algo etéreo y incuantificable."VQuizás las mías están fragmentadas y borrosas comparadas a las de la mayoría."IA ella le gusta escapar de mi, y, aunque odie admitirle, yo de ella."fEs raro que tengamos más de un efímero momento a solas. Pero las cosas ahora son... diferentes."vEstar aquí ha llevado mis pensamientos a la duda y lugares más oscuros que eso. Ahora he encontrado respuestas."JLa otra Imogene ya se ha ido, al no poder soportarlo por más tiempo."�Dejó una nota simplemente diciendo que sabía lo que debía hacer, y que ahora irá a un lugar de muerte y la tranquilidad del olvida."zElijo interpretarlo como una pista para encontrar un <imp>cementario o mausoleo</imp>, y no como su último adiós..."9No estoy segura si hay una diferencia para nosotros."*\PN… no sé si deberíamos existir."cHay algo fundamentalmente malo con nosotros. Nuestro estado no es natural, tampoco sostenible.")...Ignora mis divagaciones macabras."DVoy a seguirla, y encontrar prueba de mis verdadera existencia."uSi deseas ser testigo de tales revelaciones y ver como sus mentiras se desmoronan a su alrededor, encuéntranos."<Ella sabe algo nefasto que yo no. Debo saber lo que es."SEstoy intentando pensar por qué ciertos Avatares aparecen en ciertos lugares."ZUsualmente son especies que harían sentido para la ecología local, pero no siempre."&A veces son sólo... incorrectos."Ni idea."Escuché las historias, pero todavía es díficil de creer que los Avatares sólo... se desvanecen una vez son derrotados."iCuando vi que estabas ganando, estaba mentalmente preparada para agarrar un pico y tomar los restos."$¡Tiene una Vidasfera equipada!")Jojo, ¿Otra mosca cae en mi trampa?"4Cuídate, ya que podrás encontrarte fascinado."A¡Tsk! Parece que fuiste demasiado caliente para sostenerte."JOh bueno, supongo que siempre le puedo pedir a Lainie que me console."2Un destello. Una chispa. Una línea de rosas."=Deberíamos llevar nuestro baile una vez más a la cima."Pero nos vemos, cariño."4Diría que soy algo así como una historiadora."|Estoy aprendiendo sobre algunas fechas importantes en la historia. La fundación de Prizca, la caída de la monarquía."_Todas ellas son fascinantes, pero diría que mi favorita es la de nuestro encuentro, ¿No?"Sí"No"No, gracias."Seguro, pagaré."Seguro."¿En serio?"Eres molesta."¿A qué te refieres?"¿Qué más?"¿...Cuál eres tú?"El sentimiento es mutuo."
¿Oh?"¿En... qué sentido?"Por favor no lo seas."¿Qué tan segura estás?"¿Algún otro recuerdo?"¿Dónde está ahora?;[�".Presenting, my very own Flex-type attack!"EIs it Physical, you ask? Special, perhaps? It's both, of course!"9Your Pokemon uses whichever is best for their stats!"MIs there a catch, hmmm? ...Yes...the move misses 20 percent of the time.":Whaddya say? Tons of Pokemon can be taught this move."1Truly you've struck the motherload of moves!"HFine... I just wanted something to do now that the mine's closed..."What're you doing?!"<You're \PN, right? The trainer the Professor called in?"7So go destroy that Avatar before we're all killed!"gI used to use a lot of Life Orbs. Didn't care if my Pokemon got hurt so long as they did the work."QBut I'm not that kind of person any more. I'm looking to rid myself of them."TThe only Pokémon who I give a Life Orb to nowadays is my trusty Nidoking here."Isn't that right, buddy?":You see, my partner here has the Sheer Force ability."tIt means Nidoking can use moves that have random added effects, like Trample, without losing HP in the process."OI've just got one left. I'll sell it to you for $6,000. Fair market value."YSounds good. I'll be on patrol for awhile now, so hit me up if you change your mind.")Here ya go, pleasure doing business."&\PN hands over $6000 in exchange."&Guess I'll go back on patrol now."+Looks like you're a bit short on cash."PI get that, wasn't in the best financial spot myself before I joined Chasm."6Despite their pain, my team still loves battling."]To be honest, I don't deserve their forgiveness. I hurt them, but they still forgave me."<I get a bit emotional everytime I think about it, haha."West: Kilna Turf"North: East Tunnel"East: Grouz Mine"South-East: Amber Hills"Grouz Mine"|My my, I hope you aren't here to battle. I won't be able to tell my Pokemon anything if you keep taking my breath away."\Oh, you are? Ah, I suppose a rose as pretty as you would have some very sharp thorns..."]I laid out each of these starter tokens to maybe attract someone suitable... for battle."7Perhaps you'll be able to satisfy both criteria...":The top of the sign is labeled "Grouz Mine Bulletin.""DRemnants of old, yellowed papers are still stapled to the rest."What a disgrace."1We're supposed to be keeping this area safe."A call for you, Trainer."'The ranger hands you a cell phone."XHeard a certain metal worm is no longer with us. You won’t see me at the funeral."PAnyways, I’m a woman of my word – I’ll be your friend in high places."PI’m holed up in <imp>Helena’s place</imp>, west of the LuxTech eyesore."-North-west of the lake, can’t miss it."6Oh, and bring your team. I invited another guest."RAh, where were you in the good ol’ days? You would’ve made a great grunt!"8...That’s a compliment, by the way. See ya there."CYou gotta keep sharp! Don’t tell me you’re sick of fights."HOur guest’s pretty good, too. She might teach you a thing or two."Well, see ya."}You think I’M bad? Try working with Helena for a few years. Especially back when she had strike teams at her disposal."kYou’re strong. You’ve proven that. This’ll be a piece of cake. Trust me. So I’ll see ya there."…She hung up."Thanks for the help."Dr. Hekata's House"The door is boarded up."-Hello, \PN. It’s been quite some time!"�Though I’ve heard tales of someone that looked like you talking to someone that looked like me by a certain river that I know a certain Ditto appreciates."YWell, I say that, but I suppose I’ve never verified that she is, in fact, a Ditto."8I have never seen her un-transformed, specifically."\I have tried tossing a Poké Ball at her, with no effect other than a withering glower."hShe could be anything, I suppose, but what else can take human form for so long with such accuracy?"dA particularly persistent and vocal Zoroark? Perhaps some other Pokémon that learns Transform?"|Or perhaps she really is simply a doppelganger of eldritch origin, or a spirit haunting me for some forgotten transgression."?The one that gave you that amulet – not that it matters."kDon’t worry, I don’t take any offense! My doppelganger and I are more alike than we are different."QHow, precisely, would a Ditto learn to imitate my manners with such care...?"JI suppose it bears little tangible relevance to my situation, though."=Oh, I’m sorry I’m such a glum philosopher archetype."�If I must play a stock role in your story, I would prefer to be an oracle distributing wisdom, or a magical creature bestowing some blessing or artifact."CI hope you’re not expecting any wisdom or artifacts from me."[I fear I’m far too invested in my own quest for self- discovery to aid you in yours."�...Oh, that isn’t true. I can’t maintain a charade of indifference half as well as my companion. I am rather invested in you and yours."Thank you."�I could easily take the simple explanation afforded to all diviners: that I am interested in you because I have foretold some matter of interest in your future."aUnfortunately, I am insufferably honest, so I must confess that I simply enjoy your company."qIndeed. You are plainly at the center of a whorl of causality here – it takes no arcana to determine that."pI cannot ascertain the future with any degree of certainty, but I can plainly see which way the river cuts."AI would like to liberate its path of hindrances if possible."xOh! Excuse me, I refer merely to my interest in seeing your rather unique path through fate’s weave come to pass."]Well, that and a respectable appreciation for the quality of your character and company."�It was not my intent to imply an interest in an... assignation, if that was what you were asking. Such passions are not my lot in life."_Consider it a professional curiosity, if that might ease your concerns... or insecurities."FYou are of note not merely for your personality and character –"ithough I confess some partiality to both – but for the briar-knot of fate you are embedded within."TMany lives are wound around you. Around your fingers, or your throat, I wonder?"RPut plainly, you’re important, I’m curious, and I like our conversations."zEven the ones I am not privy to I imagine are enlightening for my other half, and her revelations may lead to my own."�Speaking of which, I am not merely here for pleasure. I had returned home for the express purpose of finding some clue as to my past."}I... cannot remember it. That this is my hometown, yes, and stray faint recollections from my youth, but beyond that nothing."`Not until a comparatively luminous memory of riding on a train with my imitator at my side."MWhatever had happened before that leg of our journey, I do not remember."KI only know that I am real, she is false, and I journey to prove such."+Not at all. But I must keep the faith."�After all, if I am merely some animal that has deluded itself into humanity... well, the ethical quandaries alone would drive me mad."nOh, plenty. Scraps of childhood, as I said. Being on the train is the first full memory of my modern era."�And from there, my memory is mostly whole – though the persistence and clarity of memory is something ethereal and unquantifiable."<Perhaps mine are fragmented and faded compared to most."GShe likes to elude me, and, though I am loathe to admit it, I her."_It is rare we get more than a fleeting moment alone. Things are now... different, however."fBeing here has driven my thoughts to doubt and darker places than that. I have found now answers."FThe other Imogene has already left, unable to bear it any longer."|She left a note stating simply that she knew what she must do, and that she goes now to a place of death and quiet oblivion."zI choose to interpret it as guidance to find a <imp>burial ground or mausoleum</imp>, and not as her last goodbyes..."2I’m unsure if there is a difference for us."0\PN… I don’t know that we should exist."aThere is something fundamentally wrong with us. Our state is not natural, nor is it tenable."$...Ignore my macabre ramblings."@I will follow her, and find the proof of my true existence."mIf you wish to bear witness to these revelations and watch as her lies crumble around her, come find us."DShe knows something dire that I do not. I must know what it is."GI'm trying to figure out why certain Avatars appear where they do."SThey're often species that'd make sense for the local ecology, but not always."-Sometimes they're just.... somewhat off."Beats me."xI heard the stories, but it's still hard to believe that Avatars just... fade from existence when they're defeated."oWhen I saw that you were winning, I was mentally prepared to grab a pickaxe and begin the cleanup efforts."It's holding a Life Orb!"*Ohoh, does another fly enter my trap?"6Watch yourself, you may find yourself mesmerized."3Tsk! It seems like you were too hot to handle."@Ah well, I suppose I could always ask Lainie to console me."'A spark. A flash. A line of roses."5We should take our tango once more from the top."But later, my dear."/I've found myself as a bit of a historian."eI'm learning about important dates in history. The founding of Prizca, the fall of the monarchy."VAll of them are fascinating, but I believe my favorite is the one we'll have, no?"Yes"No"No thanks."Sure, I'll pay."Sure thing."Really?"You're a pain."What do you mean?"What else?"...Which one are you?"The feeling's mutual."Oh?"In... what way?"Please don't be."How sure are you?"Any other memories?"Where is she now?Iu;␀�[["What the..."&Nevermind. Kid, I need some help."BThat thing needs to go down, and I’m fresh out of Pokémon."&Please. We can’t let it escape."Don’t underestimate it."UYou'll need to send out <imp>two Pokemon at a time</imp> to even stand a chance."6I don’t have anything left. This is all on you."(I can’t thank you enough. Honest.">That thing was what we’re calling an <imp>Avatar</imp>."/They started showing up a few months back."MMost trainers aren't brave enough to take one on in a straight-up fight."lI heard 