 Aegis Insurance building."WThey'll probably have the good stuff up there, behind a group of minions no doubt."BMake sure you and your Pokemon are ready for a massive scrap."6This is it! This is exactly what I'm looking for."QYou've done a great service. We'll make sure everyone is brought to justice."DHere, as a reward. A wonderful Pokemon for a wonderful Trainer."/Farewell Trainer, the Rangers owe you one."Any luck?"Nothing? Nothing?!"7What did she do? How could there be nothing there?"2Damn. Months of investigation down the drain."CGuess I have to report this. The case will probably be closed."Thanks anyways."PHave you heard of the Black Market, located in the sewers beneath the city?";Once I find it, I'll be sure to dish out some justice."+Those ruffians give Prizca a bad name!"Poké Ball Depot"&Stone pillars tower over the gym."@They almost look like fingers, reaching through the ground."Prizca Traffic Control"\I'm following a list I found online: "Prizca West's Best Sights for Intrepid Tourists.""BThe agenda for today includes a visit to a... cement company."/Maybe it'll be less boring than it sounds."LClosed while Bence....participate in the Makya Championship Tournament."IHeavy graffiti covers a part that you think may have said "and Zoé""BPoor Bence and Zoé, the two can't seem to agree on anything."PIf they took working together more seriously, the Gym might be much harder!"5Zoé has a penchant for more supportive Pokemon."9Bence is the opposite. He mainly focuses on offense."_On the surface, the ideals seem conflicting, but they'd actually work together quite well."3So you've got the Solidarity Badge. Well done!"4You're well on your way to becoming a champion."FI bet the Trainers at the Battle Plaza are itching to battle you."Prizca's West Gym"Leaders: Bence, Zoé"Two birds for every stone."*Bence and Zoé.... Zence.... Boé...."lOh, forgive me, the thought of taking on two gym leaders at the same time is stressing me out a little."SI hope my current team will work well against them, but I can't know for sure."IHelp me out, pal, by being my test dummy? I'll wait for your answer."?The choice to battle me is an easy one. Got a round in ye?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."No regrets!"DHmm.... should I go make a different team? Agh, I'm not sure..."KIf only I had chosen different moves. Maybe I could have won that one."IRestoring my Pokemon to full health, though, ain't much of a choice."3Give me the chance, and we can face off again."jYour victory over the Prizca West Gym... it leaves me with no choice but to follow in your footsteps."Wish me luck!"TI'm on break. Nothing much to do until the rock shipment's done being unloaded.";What's that? You wanna know where the rocks come from?"KThere's a big quarry to the north, near one of the mountains up there."hIt's not part of Makya anymore, but there's a lot of historic ties, so business relations are good."You’re so inconsiderate."9You’re in town, and you didn’t even let me know?"Because I saw you." Oh, don’t make that face."9You talk a big game for someone in dueling distance."<Surprise! I’m here, in the city I said I would be in."Let’s cut to the chase."UI don’t know how you’ve gotten here so quickly, but I’m going to find out."Fight me."Wow, so rude."OI can’t believe you wouldn’t want to talk to your own flesh and blood."Right here, right now."*Oh, sure. Take all the time you need."]But you’re not getting any farther until you show me what dirty tricks you’re using."_Oh good. I’ve been looking forward to curbstomping your team since you picked a starter.""Ready to learn some humility?""Alright. OK. Sure, of course."bWhy wouldn’t you annihilate a team without a scratch on yours? How could I not expect this?"SWhy would I think my work would count for ANYTHING? Ugh. You’re infuriating."...I can’t believe it."jI spend MONTHS out here, grinding my ass off to get this far, and you traipse in like it’s nothing."3Why are you better? Why are you always better?"6Fine! I guess I’ll see you in the championship."'Watch your back out there, though."9I will get better, and then I’m going to find you."@Zain ever so graciously spared supplies from his Aid Kit..."That was… real close."Such a good try."JBut since I won, I guess that makes you a pretty good place to train."C’mon. One more bout."You’re joking."$You’re not even going to try?"0I can’t believe you’d even consider it."!You -- I can’t believe it."-You really are an asshole, aren’t you?"NYou just want an opportunity to be smugly superior, like you always have."TFigures. The only reason you’re doing this is to get more attention from mom."5Well, go on. See how far that attitude gets you."I’m leaving."Business Sector"0I finally got my hands on some Fire Stones!"'I got 'em at the Evolution Market."WIn case you're wondering -- it's a building in the very north of the Battle Plaza.":Right next to the entrance to the Tournament Grounds."The door is boarded up."OHello! Would you be interested in signing a petition to demolish the road?"oThis road currently has no financial benefit to the city ever since the bridge to the south was destroyed."?It's quite an eyesore, and it disrupts pedestrian traffic."Every signature counts.".Are you sure? Prizca only stands to gain!">Thank you so much! You've contributed to Prizca's future."Ah, you again.".Have you changed your mind about signing?"SEventually, we'll get enough signatures that the city's council has to listen."6The city will be much better off for pedestrians."Look at the shiny bird!"AI wanna go up there to talk to it, but my dads never let me."/When I grow up, I wanna be a shiny bird..."There you are. Ready now?"5You’re insufferable some times, you know that?"%That last one was… real close."A Shiny Corviknight!"3It's too busy watching the city to notice you."1It's weird seeing the streets here so empty."\It's a combination of the road closure, and the Battle Festival happening right nearby."The Grand Ho