d, yes, I TOLD THEM to reinforce it!"bThey didn’t, since they trust ex-Chasm about as far as they can throw them and – anyways!"ZFor very stupid, avoidable reasons, the river’s basically uncrossable without Surf."kIf you’re like me, you’re not gonna pack a Water-type everywhere you go, so just use this instead."]It’s just more practical. Stylish, too! Assuming you’re good at it. Which I’m not."&Go have fun and get those badges."lOh, and, uh, this is Helena’s place, so feel free to eat some of her food or something before you go."�Kick a vase over. Carve your name in the table. Er – maybe someone else’s name. Yezera’s name! She’d get a kick out of that. Heh."-You see your name carved onto the table."5You see the name "Yezera" carved onto the table."7You see the name "Tamarind" carved onto the table."=A vase filled with flowers sits delicately on the floor.":You could totally smash this thing, if you wanted to."*You decide against smashing the vase."fYou find a garbage bag, put the flowers in it, and swing it against the wall with all your might."RA garbage bag filled with rubble is all that remains of this once proud vase."Don't take the food."Take the food."Don't carve."Carve your name."Carve Yezera's name."Carve Tamarind's name."Good to see you."Damn it, Tamarind."We gonna fight again?"Give me a minute."OK."Use your real team."No, you're right."What do you mean?"We're very different."I hope I'm not."We've met."We're friends."We're rivals."Unfortunately."It's interesting."Get to the point."You had a gift?"Actually, I kinda did."Don't smash."Smash.Iu;␀z\[[�"2I've been stationed here to look for avatars.">I haven't been able to find any, though, so let's battle!"HI can probably take a break, with Trainers like you walking around."See ya."<Well, they don't pay me to bring my Max Revives home...")I'm tending to my Pokemon right now.""A portent felt, a divination."Chaos freed, eradication."Wishes are a solemn curse."&Left to rot, and they will burst."%A chain of flowers holding fast."#Will it crumble? Will it last?"+Old times renewed, ones you must face."+In lashing out, they find their grace."(YEEHAW, ALL ABOARD THE LOG EXPRESS!"=RECKON TO FACE US ON MORTAL, HEARTPOUNDING, LOG COMBAT?!",WOWIE! That was some fine log battling!":Any log rider is a friend o' mine, don'chu forget it!"jWe're just making sure that the logs sent downstream by the local Bibarel don't clog up the waterway."?It's honest work, and we get to have a little fun with it."RGood battle, Trainer. I'm sure everyone on the Stretch enjoyed watching that."	Hey."Gettin'... kinda nervous."/Tamarind’s gonna show. I’m sure of it."�Told her to meet me inside. I’ll go around the back, you go in the front, we’ll cut her off, no problems, clean and easy. Capisce?""Great. Like, yeah, of course."You’re my friend, right?"=Oh, yeah, I’m, like, yeah. I’m, like, totally ready."See? Normal Candy!"GDon’t be silly. We’re, like, totally gonna make things better."At least a little bit.";Um, like, good question, but isn’t it kinda obvious?"hLike, she’s gotta confess and tell us what she did, right? And then we’ll bring her to justice!"Y...OK, to be, like, totally honest with you: I’m worried you’re gonna betray me."SBecause she, like, did you a favor and you’re working with her and all that."vBut you won’t. I mean, like, she caused all of this! This entire place is mega-screwed because of what she did!",Eh! No! No talking! I can’t hear you!"}I am one hundred percent not interested in, like, anything you’re saying. I trust you. I trust you, and that’s that."lSo you go in and I’ll scoot ‘round the back, and we’ll do a pincer maneuver, alright? Let’s go!"West: Eleig River Crossing"East: Canal Desert"UI've been managing the wildlife here for years, I've become an honorary Bibarel!"aWhoa! That last move almost smashed the whole dam! I'll get right back to work fixing it up!"aAnother day, another trainer recklessly battled on this new dam. My Pokemon love the thrill!"?This is such a nice spot, I should bring a couch out here."kUsed to look a little more pretty before the Biberal cut down the trees, but I appreciate the company."Um... hey."9So, Tamarind and I, like, kissed and made up? Kinda?"GUm, not in that way. She’s like twenty-five years older than me."@I... \PN, I still really hate her. She is, like, the worst."�She’s this snooty arrogant brat that literally destroys things that get in her way for no reason. But, like, I can’t just punch her and make it better."...But I did punch her."ENot really! It was kind of a wimpy punch. Still, I had to do it."For baby Candy, at least."#I know, I know! It was stupid."VBut, like, I’ve thought about it so many times, and now I finally got to do it."LIt didn’t make me happy, but I can scratch it off the list, y’know?"DOh, not even. She deserves to be punched, like, at least twice."6What? That punching her doesn’t make it better?"hOr that I, like, decked her in the first place? Because the answer is yeah, I’m a learning Candy."HReally, I let her off easy. But, um, I didn’t really let her off."sI kinda... got hired? Like, I do not trust that hag for a second, so I’m gonna stick to her like a Remoraid."OShe’s gonna fix all the messed-up stuff that she and her cronies caused."OAnd she’s, like, totally overworked, so, um... yeah. I’m her aide now!"#And bodyguard. And conscience."WI get to get justice, and she gets to not have her labs be on fire. Everyone wins."@Heh… thanks. I’m, like, not sure of anything right now."VWho knows! Maybe I’ll think better of it tomorrow and firebomb her lab anyways!")Hey! What’s that supposed to mean?"UDo you think I’m just, like, this belligerent ditzy manic Spritzee dream girl?"]No, but, yeah, I get it. I don’t know that I’m, like, super cut out for this either."=Um. I think, like, you can get fired for that? So... no?""Maybe. I’ll think about it."uWell, now if I want to steal someone’s Pokémon back I can just have Tamarind order it, so, like, I guess not?"kI’m still gonna steal things. Let’s all be, like, honest for a second: I’m not changing my ways."MBut I am gonna be busier with other stuff now! So, yeah. There’s that."+Oh, by the way, Tamarind was all like:"�“If you want proof that I’m doing my damnedest to help this region” and then she blabbered about like a secret lab and horrible monsters."�Y’know. Like, containing an extradimensional evil and all that. Anyways, she gave me this key, but I don’t really, like, care?"�Like, sure, whatever, she did hard work. She wants to prove she’s good, she can put her money where her mouth is and prove it by working with me."SAnyways, um… you can have it? Maybe cool stuff? Maybe extradimensional evil?"$Um, anyways, yeah. I, um, yeah."Thanks."1Thanks, like, a lot. You’re a good friend.""But, um, I think that’s it."{I have to go with Tamarind now and make sure she doesn’t, like, kick a child or something on the way back to Prizca.">So, this is goodbye. And, well, you know what that means."E*sniff* Yeah... aww, \PN, we can’t be justice friends anymore."%We’ll just be regular friends."wI’m gonna see you again, I know, but… we had like an arc together! We had an arc, and now it’s over. *sniff*"{Aww, don’t tempt me. But, um, I kinda had my Pokémon tussle with Tamarind back there and they need to rest for now."2Maybe someday? Jeanne wants to kick your ass."MLike, not your Pokémon. You. Sorry! Watch your back out there, I guess."Oh!"GUm, listen, you’re really cute but I’m not really... into you?"PI’m, like, super into the sweep me off my feet romance story kinda thing?"�Like, theoretically if I needed to disguise myself while bad guys were searching and I had someone I could kiss to hide my face. Y’know. Cliche stuff."NBut, um, I’m not, like, into actual relationships? If that makes sense?"5No! We, like, didn’t learn anything from this."We un-learned things."4Listen, we are, like, the dumbest people alive."IThat’s why we’re obsessed with justice and, um, kinda impulsive!"9Mainly me, but you too. I know it. We’re twinsies."-...I’m gonna miss the hell out of you."mI know, I know! I’m not, like, going-going. But, like, it feels that way. And I miss you already. Hug?"KUm... \PN? I’m, not, like, the healthiest person? Like, in the head."^I’ve done some pretty iffy stuff myself because I was, like, well, this is for justice."Like that makes it OK."�So, um, maybe working with Tamarind is a way for me to get justice for myself, too? And, yeah, I could probably use some therapy too."�And I understand if you don’t wanna be my friend after hearing that, but, um, I hope I see you again anyways. I’m gonna make things better."TYou go stop Yezera. Make sure all my hard work doesn’t get, like, undone, OK?"hThank you, \PN. I… I gotta go. But I hope I see you again. Thanks for showing me what justice is."=...Ugh, that was cheesy. I, um, yeah. Love you. Toodles."7You’re cool. You’re, like, my favorite person."HI know you’ve still got, like, a lot of stuff to do, so go do it."`I’ve got stuff to do, too. If Tamarind wasn’t waiting I’d, like, hug you for an hour."jBut, um, gotta go, I guess. You’re... we’ll see each other again? Right? Yeah. Of course we will.")I, um, yeah. Love you. Bye. Toodles!"KOh, so it’s you again. You’ve arrived at a rather fortuitous time."pI’ve caught this pair of Makyan forms and would like some more data – but excuse me. Again, my manners."May I ask your name?"VAh, \PN. I’ve heard that name about. A pleasure to meet you properly this time."=How droll. I suppose I am a stranger, after all, though."`As I was saying: I would like some combat data. You seem to be quite adept at providing it."Shall we?"<Of course. I wouldn’t want the results to be tainted."JAdaptation via vendetta – I’m expecting viciousness. Let’s see."Shall we get down to it?"Highly educational."GIt would seem that both of them have been honed by their vendetta."dFrom what I’ve gleaned in local sources, the Sevipers became Steel-type to fend off Zangoose."nThey managed to drive the local Zangoose populations to extinction, yet even that didn’t stop the feud."cFighting until they died, and then even beyond. The tenacity of the Zangoose is admirable, no?"tThe Zangoose counter-adaptation – the Fighting-type – seems to be a product of their indestructible spirit."GCurious. Could these be the predators the Furrets adapted to beat?"5No, the Psychic type would hurt as much as help."nA mystery for another time. I would like to thank you for your help, but actions speak louder than words."!Take this, from my homeland."5Goodbye. I can’t say where I’ll end up next."rPerhaps the <imp>sewers beneath Prizca</imp>. If any biome might cause new forms to emerge, it would be that.".The Saurenaid is humming a pleasant tune."?It's strapped up with multiple cushioned seats for travel."%Kid, I, uh, heard the screaming."EFigured I ought to stay in case there was an attempted homicide."So I heard."*No problem. It’s my job... I think."...Fair. Not yet, though."!Sounds like it. Condolences."yUm, in case what she said is getting to you, I’m sorry. You made the right choice. She... she’s got some issues."fIf you want some proof that I really am trying my damnedest to make this place better, take this."BIt’s a lab where some stuff went down. None of it my fault."uOn top of everything else, I’ve been keeping extradimensional monsters at bay out of the kindness of my heart."Really."mI do want the best for this place. Hopefully once you see all the work I’ve done that’ll be obvious."KBut, um, I know I’m not really wanted right now, so I’ll be going.")You... you did the right thing, kid."Eleig Boating and Fishing""Eleig Valet, at your service."%Care to exchange business cards?"Sewage Maintenance"7LOG RIDE BATTLE! LOG RIDE BATTLE! LOG RIDE BATTLE!"eYou've mastered the ways of the log in such short time... are you some kinda log riding prodigy?"!See you later, log cowboy..."This is it!"(The great outdoors! Untamed nature!"%The great 