 simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."cOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it."Do you not agree?"/How disappointing, to dismiss it outright."IIf you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regirock, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."]G’afternoon. Took your sweet time showing your face ‘round these parts, didn’t ya?"eListen, I ain’t ‘bout to preach to ya. Just want to make some things clear ‘fore we fight.">‘Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."wWhat’s so damn infuriating ‘bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."NHow ‘bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?".Good. I ain’t ‘bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."iSorry, kid. You’re a mite too fast. Gotta slow you down. Regirock, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."|But, cheer up, kid. I’m ‘bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."BToo rough ‘nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"1Hey. Fancy meeting you in a place like this."aOh, don’t look so angry – Regirock and I are here to fight you, but we’ll get to that."RI know you’re more than a pretty face. You’re smart. Care to hear me out?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."CFor now, I’ve been ordered to slow you down. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."uFortunately, I’ve been sent to slow you down, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection."Hello, friend."FBusiness before pleasure: I have been sent to slow your progress.".To that end, I am accompanied by a titan."XBefore we attend to that, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."RNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regirock, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.".Prepare yourself. Regirock, if you would."Oh. Hey."IYeah, so, I knew you’d be here. Gym challenger, and, uh, all that."…Welp. This is awkward.";How do I say this… you interested in hearing us out?"bWe’ve kinda got the upper hand, but, y’know, don’t really wanna fight you. Whaddya say?"=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."dI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regirock. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"*Regirock, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."kOdds are Regirock isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"…Hey."xTsk tsk tsk. I’m not gonna lie to you: I’ve been trying to plan this conversation in my head for the past hour."RBut, um, you kinda interrupted me. So can I just say what I want to tell you?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."?Regirock – your watch is over. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YFarewell, and do not pursue me. Fate and fate alone will dictate when we next speak."eRegirock’s damn well spent. Flighty li'l things never like to be outside their tombs too long."*Ah, well. Got what I came for anyhow."�Let me tell you one last word of advice. You hurt Yez, I’ll find you. And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."jG’evening, kid. I’ll see ya around. Make sure I don’t hafta hurt you too bad when I do, ‘kay?";Au revoir, Regirock. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."PAnd as for you, that was an exciting fight. You’ve got my heart pounding."yIf you want to join us, come find Yezera. And if not, well, we’ll meet again. I’m looking forward to it already."So long."4I surmise Regirock will now return to its tomb."gThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts. It is of no matter."AWe have all but succeeded in our plans. This was a courtesy."7I will take my leave now. Thank you for your time."/There it goes. Back to where it came from."_Well, didn’t really expect to win anyways. Just wanted to slow you down, and, uh, I did.":So… bye. We’ll do this again sometime. I’m out."P*sigh* Buh-bye, Regirock. We don’t really, uh, need you anymore, I guess."?It was fun while it lasted… welp. Nothing lasts forever."ISpeaking of! Hopefully next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"KIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll give you a run for your money, ‘kay?"\Toodles. And don’t you dare follow – I’m playing hard to get, so respect it. Hah!"uMore than a million years ago, a meteor struck this area of Makya, plowing through a large mountain to the west."XThat large mountain became two smaller mountains, which we now know as Split Peaks."NThe impact site itself would fill with water and become Sweetrock Harbor."0The ocean to the east brings calming winds."KBut why? We might explain it with ocean currents, or weather patterns."FBut what makes the winds here calming? Of that, I am not so sure."<I really want to know who that was in the weird outfit.";Well, regardless, thanks for kicking them out of town."=I'm a firefighter, so I'm used to dealing with issues..."DBut "Cultist with a Regirock" is outside of my job description."Lightkeeper's House"Artisan Orbs" Sweetrock Elementary School"/"In loving memory of Mrs. and Mr. Diakos.""HI've been biking across the entire region over the past few months.":Crossing the Split Peaks was by far the hardest part."nThe view from these cliffs, and the feeling that I've finally accomplished my goal, made it all worth it."West: Split Peaks"South: Sandstone Estuary";"Sweetrock Harbor, satisfying the world's sweettooth!""!"A sister city of Canalave!"":I work at Sweetrock Candy factory, like many in town."IThat said, I rarely get to see Victoire, the manager and gym leader.":I gotta rely on rumors to know what her team is like.",Some of them are a bit hard to believe."DI heard some people saying that she uses a Sticky Web strategy."AWith Fairy and Steel-type Pokemon? How does she manage that?"$Huh, you really beat her, then?"4You gotta tell me what she's like as a trainer.""My curiosity's grown too big!"_Sweetrock Candy is sent all over the world, but more than 30% ends up in the Galar Region."#Those people love their candy."+Shh... don't give away my hiding spot!")Is it... is it safe to come out now?")How goes your journey, young master?"YI've purchased a Clefable teleportation license, and reserved this pier for our use.":We can travel to and from any of our usual locations."Where will we be heading?""Emma's Empoloreum!""0An Empoleon standee points you to the door."+Have you slid down the conveyor belts?"=Preeeetty sure we're not allowed to, but it's crazy fun."PMaybe not as fun as beating the 7th gym will be with my snazzy new Pokemon!";Which ones? You'll just have to battle me to find out!"XI cannot convey to you just how much I want to battle. Heh. So, you up to doing so?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."Rock 'Em, Torterra!"9Damn, even these 'mons couldn't leave a dent in you."EThink anyone in the lighthouse was watching our battle just now?"INo way around it, I'll need some healing before we square off again.",Got a good look at Victoire, I take it?"bShe as quirky as they say? I don't know why I bother asking. I'll be finding out soon myself."0The 7th badge... oh so sweet will it taste!"Sweetrock Harbor Gym"Leader: Victoire"The Candy Queen!"Sweetrock Candy Outlet"kWhat was once a printed notice has been covered entirely by a poster advertising the EXP-EZ Dispenser."Sweetrock Lighthouse"#Today's a good day for gaming."-A Piplup standee points you to the door."Berry Greenhouse"HI love to slide down the conveyor belt. But, my dad doesn't let me."UI have to stay by the school until he gets off work so I don't get into trouble."I'm gaming over here!"No."	Yes."I’ll listen."Don't need it."No, I don't."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
I do."Fine, talk."Not interested in talking."I know who you are."Don't threaten me."Clear."Wish that already."I'm with you."Alright, fine."Go away."That's insane."Degenerate?"Arceus's bosom?"That's fair."Sure, talk."Don't really care."It isn't worth it."Who cares?"Society will crumble."Good point."I'll listen."Don't care."You're wrong."I'm not guilty."
Sure."Not that simple."Pokémon would do better?"Fair enough."Maybe later."Sure, let's go.[&"EEs el final de la cinta transportadora. Es imposible de escalar."�Por la mayoría de la historia de Sweetrock, hemos dependido de la teletransportación de Clefable para llevar el cargamento de la fábrica al puerto."jInstalamos estas cintas transportadoras hace unos años, así que el acantilado ya no es un problema."[Eso sí, todavía dependemos de la teletransportación para entrar y salir del puerto."aParece que el Entrenador enfrente se está moviendo para bloquearte ir a ninguna otra parte."5¿Quieres acercarte? Parece un combate difícil.":Sabía que llegarías, mientras me quedara esperando."gDisculpa la pantomima – preferiría que mi identidad se mantenga envuelta en misterio por ahora."|Todo lo que requieres entender es de quién soy siervo – Yezera. Bajo su profunda guía, hemos logrado nuestros objetivos."uLos titanes han servido su propósito. Entonces vengo con una simple consulta: ¿No escucharás mi razonamiento?"OGracias. Nuestro objetivo es nada menos que un completo reorden del mundo."FMis camaradas tienen sus propios motivos, pero el mío es simple."�El mundo en el presente es voluble y falaz. La cultura y tecnología humano no sirve para nada excepto como un velo para disfrazar la verdad definitiva."vSólo el reino de los mitos antiguos, cuidado por los dioses, intacto por los humanos, puede dejarnos percibirlo."¿No estás de acuerdo?"1Que decepcionante, descartarlo rotundamente."XSi no tienes un ojo para la verdad, entonces no tenemos nada más de lo que hablar."mPerdóname este acto de pasión, pero espero que la furia de un titán pueda calmar mi corazón furioso.""Regirock, acata mis órdenes."SPor el contrario: tiene un soporte firme, si solo uno reflexiona en el asunto."|Lástima, tal fé vacilante es prácticamente inservible para mis propósitos. Requerimos una devoción inquebrantable."V*sigh* Estaría abandonando mi deber si no te detuviera como mínimo. Prepárate."eDebería animarte a ello. Juzga el peso del mundo que está en contra del mundo que podría ser."pLástima, sé que no meditaras tranquilamente ante él. Eres una amenaza. Eso es intolerable para nosotros."VEsta no será una victoria decisiva mía, pero no puedo dejarte pasar sin trabas.")…Me gustaría mucho poder creerte."pSi hablas la verdad, entonces te demando que repitas tus coinvicciones a Yezera la proxima vez que la veas."�Ella puede ver las maquinaciones de tu corazón más claramente que yo. Hasta entonces, sigues siendo un entrenador, al igual que yo."QA mis enemigos los aniquilo, a mis aliados los entreno. A ambos, en guardia."USi no vas a escuchar mis plegarias, entonces estás más allá de la salvación."ZLástima. Quizás la furia de un titán te iluminará en la claridad de los antiguos."NBuenas. Te tomaste tu tiempo para mostrar tu cara por estas partes, ¿eh?"cEscucha, no voy a intentar convencerte. Sólo quiero dejar las cosas claras antes de combatir."/Porque vamos a combatir. No queda de otra."LMuchas gracias. Realmente no me interesa demasiado toda esta pantomima."Estoy con Yezera, siempre."DEscucha, sólo voy a decir esto una vez: tienes que escucharla."ANo me importa si estás de acuerdo con ella. Solo escuchala."pY si la lastimas, voy a asegurarme de que desees que Mavis haya parado después de Zain. ¿Lo tienes claro?"*Sí que eres un mocoso engreído. Tsk"tLo más irritante sobre ti es que no puedo simplemente patear tu trasero para hacer que obedezcas. Eres fuerte."Q¿Pero qué tal si lo intento? El Titán debe ser bueno para algo, ¿cierto?"2Bien. No estaba por repetirme de todos modos."JAhora, vine aquí con un trabajo que hacer, y soy del tipo confiable."aLo siento, niño. Eres un poco muy rápido. Debo detenerte. Regirock, cariño, ve al frente."UJa. Tómalo de alguien que tiene idea, niño: aún no arañas ni la superficies."CPodría hacerte mucho más miserable si me concentrara a ello."~Pero, alégrate, niño. Voy a darte lo que siempre quieres: un buen combate. Enfrentar un Regi seguro debe alegrarte. Je.">Nah, no voy a creer eso. No sabes nada sobre Yezera y yo."CUna vieja pareja que se la pasa peleando, eso es lo que somos."C¿Quieres mostrarme que estás con nosotros? Dícelo a Yezera."wPor ahora, no me interesa dejarte ir tan fácil. Lo siento. Tumbar gente al suelo es mi trabajo, después de todo."YAh, bueno. Supongo que no importa cuanto lo intentas, los viejos hábitos no se van."CHablando de irse – ¿Échate un rato y déjate de mover, ok?"OJa. Nunca estuvieron tan contentos con mi forma de trabajar de encubierto.":Demasiado brusca y severa. No estoy hecha para esto.."|Así que, déjame decirte esto de forma clara: escuchas a Yezera. Todo lo que tenga que decir. Y no te atrevas a lastimarla."LEs todo lo que pido. Y, eh, no me enviaron aquí para charlar. ¿Listo?"4Hey. Curioso encontrarte en un lugar como este."oOh, no estés tan enojado – Regirock y yo estamos aquí para combatir contigo, pero ya llegaremos a eso."VSé que eres más que una cara bonita. Eres inteligente. ¿Te importa escucharme?"0Oww. Tenía un buen presentimiento contigo."]Cómo lo explico… bueno, odio usar la palabra, pero la sociedad moderna es degenerada."gEstamos distantes desde el momento perfecto de la creación. De algún modo hemos tomado el mundo."^Nada de respeto a nuestros mayores – los Pokémon primordiales que crearon el universo."uYezera va a reiniciar este mundo a sus origenes. Y luego la humanidad estará en el seno de Arceus una vez más."nNo me llames insano. Aunque estoy seguro que esta civilización arrogante y sin fé usaría ese término."_Soy meramente un devoto, y la devoción significa hacer sacrificios. Por ejemplo: el tuyo."MRealmente me gustas, pero… todos tenemos que sacrificarnos alguna vez."OLos Pokémon divinos ahora son tratados como no más que bestias de carga."MLos avatares son destruídos porque son una “amenaza a los humanos.”"dEl mundo ha perdido todo respeto, la esencia divina de la creación se ha diluido y destruído."FY ya que no pareces ser diferente, podré disfrutar este combate."~Arceus creó el mundo. Un mundo puro y perfecto, y reiniciarlo a su forma original nos dejará ser también puros y perfectos."OMe gustaría verme a mí mismo bendecido por la gracia de nuestro creador.".También me gustaría verte de esa forma."A su debido tiempo."=Por ahora, me han ordenado pararte los pies. ¿Bailamos?"(Bien. Sabía que había algo en ti."=Una chispa de fé. Soy un… muy buen juez de carácter."�Me encantaría sólo hablar contigo por un rato, pero fui instruído explícitamente a pararte. Así que combatiremos. No te lo tomes personal."Oh. ¿Demasiado atrevido?"GMis emociones suelen sacar lo peor de mi. Estoy casi desconsolado."(Bueno, supongo que soy un extraño."Afortunadamente, me han enviado para detenerte, así que tengo un desahogo conveniente para estos sentimientos de rechazo."Hola, amigo."TPrimero es la obligación que la devoción: me enviaron para parar tu progreso."*Para ese fin, me acompaña un titán."XSin embargo, antes de ir con eso, ¿Te puede interesar una breve discusión franca?"KPreferiría intentar convencer de la legitimidad de nuestra posición."Gracias por tu tiempo."KLa meta de Yezera es recrear las condiciones del mundo en sus albores."sLa ciencia moderna ha logrado un entendimiento y maestría casi completo sobre el mundo –  el mundo moderno."�Sin embargo, no puede entender el pasado. Al revertir su existencia, podremos estudiar el universo desde su concepción y obtener conocimiento universal."%Es la única manera de lograrlo."vSin esa reversión, la humanidad nunca logrará un entendimiento completo del universo. Lo vale cualquier precio."RAhora que nuestra conversación acabó, Regirock, por favor, haz los honores."XA todas las personas que intentan avanzar en la civilización debería importarles."REl conocimiento universal es un prerrequisito para una sociedad todopoderosa."bEse es mi objetivo. Ese es el objetivo de toda ciencia: el saber, y aplicar ese conocimiento."jTu ignorancia insinua que la discusión no nos llevará a ningún sitio. Dejemosla de lado, entonces."AEl conocimiento será mantenido en una nueva era primordial."FPodemos reconstruir por lo menos pequeños enclaves de humanidad."cDe ahí nuestro análisis y conquista empezará: una nueva sociedad con conocimiento absoluto.">Y, a raíz de este conocimiento absoluto, poder absoluto."UConsideralo. Por mientras, hay negocios que mencioné anteriormente. Perdóname."�Me alegra que tengas la sabiduría para estar de acuerdo.  Si deseas apoyarnos en nuestra campaña, estaré contento de recibirte."iLucharemos por una era de claridad. Pero por ahora, debo pararte. El trabajo es trabajo. Comencemos."SEncuentro esto altamente desafortundado. Serás dejado atrás por el progreso."APero si prefieres mantener tu ignorancia, no puedo ayudarte."$Preparate. Regirock, por favor."Oh. Hey."eSeh, así que, sabía que estarías aquí. Siendo un aspirante de los gimnasios y, eh, todo eso."…Bueno. Esto es raro."2Cómo digo esto… ¿Te interesa escucharnos?"fBásicamente tenemos la ventaja, pero, sabes, realmente no quiero combatir contigo. ¿Qué dices?">Oh. Eso es bueno. Genial. Honestamente no me lo esperaba."=Bueno, entiendo que mandoneamos bastante a los Pokémon.">Quizás es hora de igualar la posición un poco, ¿Sabes?"ITodos podemos reconciliarnos un poco por lo que sea que hicimos mal."wLos otros tienen sus razones, pero, eh, esta es la mía. Crear un mundo donde podamos ser perdonados. ¿Entiendes?",Bueno – como sea. ¿Sabes qué? Bien."YNo necesito tu permiso, y ciertamente no necesitamos tu ayuda. Regirock, cárgatelo."k¿...Tanta seguridad? Toma demasiado entrenamiento para tener un equipo tan fuerte en tan poco tiempo.";Pero, seh, no, lo entiendo. ¿Por qué nos ayudarías?"OMocoso malcriado. Quizás podamos forzar un poco de responsabilidad en ti."NUh. Realmente no sé cómo descomponerlo para ti. Tu… no tienes tiempo."HPrimero, ya hemos basicamente ganado. Segundo – ¡Piensa rápido!".Regirock, ¡Barre el suelo con su cuerpo!"(Oh. Realmente no, eh, esperaba eso."5Pensé que eras un mocoso estirado. Sin ofender."ABueno, ok. Quizás estaremos lado a lado algún día, ¿Sí?"BPero, eh, por ahora… se supone que debo combatir contra ti."XAsí que, eh, lo siento – ah, qué estoy diciendo, vivimos para esto. Prepárate."#Seh, supongo que eso funciona."Bien. Eso está… bien."4Vine aquí para molerte a palos de todos modos."|Chance es que Regirock no va a permanecer por mucho más, así que hagamos que cuente. Hazlo lo mejor que puedas, ¿Eh?"…Hey."uTsk tsk tsk. No voy a mentirte: Estuve intentando planear esta conversación en mi cabeza por esta última hora."_Pero, em, como que me interrumpiste. ¿Así que puedo sólo decirte lo que quiero decirte?"ABueh. Escucha, eh, Makya está en un lugar raro ahora mismo."hEl Team Chasm ha pisoteado sobre toda la región, y luego simplemente… ¿Se salieron con la suya?"�Así que, eh, seh, si alguna vez quisiste prueba de que los humanos ni pueden lograr la mayor justicia blanca-y-negra correctamente, ahí la tienes."UHabría sido simple arreglar esa pequeña metedura de pata. Pero no lo hicieron."bAsí que le estamos quitando el poder a los humanos, y ponerlos en las manos de los Pokémon."¿Lo es? ¡Lo es!"I¡¿Soy insano por querer un poco de maldito CASTIGO en este mundo?!"<Bueno, adivina qué. Si la gente no me lo da, lo HARÉ."(¡Y tengo la herramienta necesaria!" Es simple, Idi– ¡Idiota!"`¡Puedo rastrear a cualquier ex-Chasm y llevarlos a la corte yo misma si tengo que hacerlo!"g¡Pero simplemente no harían nada! Así que tengo que hacer las cosas personalmente, ¿Entiendes?"!Lo siento. Nada… personal."¡Sí!"GEllos son nobles y puros y – y – ¡Y nunca me decepcionarían!")¡No como tú! ¡Y todos los demás!"R¿Quieres ver? Vamos. ¡Mira el tipo de justicia que los Pokémon pueden dar!"Oh. Ajá."GQuizá me exalté un poco… bueno, sin daño no hay maldad, ¿Eh?"…Nah, eso es estúpido."^No voy a desperdiciar mi oportunidad. Tengo un Regi. Tu eres un prodigio. ¡Vamos a ELLO!"#¡Arrg, me haces enojar tanto!"!¡Nadie me malditas escucha!"
Bien."Sabes, bien, como sea."QConseguirás lo que todos los demás que enfrento consiguen. Lo que merecen."FRegirock – tu custodia finalizó. Si debes irte, entonces vete."ZAsí que regresa a su lugar de descanso… no importa. Hizo todo lo que desee y más.",Y en cuanto a ti, nos veremos otra vez."RAdiós, y no me persigas. El destino dictará la próxima vez que hablaremos."tUn Regirock bien usado. A los pequeños caprichosos nunca les gusta estar fuera de sus tumbas por mucho tiempo."7Ah, bien. De todos modos conseguí lo que buscaba."{Déjame darte un último consejo. Si lastimas a Yez, te encontraré. Y no será sólo para unas peleitas con animales."jBuenas tardes, chico. Te veré luego. Asegúrate de que no tenga que lastimarme cuando lo haga, ¿Ok?"8Au revoir, Regirock. Disfruta tu entierro, supongo."SY en cuanto a ti, ese combate fue emocionante. Mi corazón no dejaba de latir."{Si quieres unirte a nosotros, encuentra a Yezera. Y si no, bueno, nos encontraremos de nuevo. Ya estoy expectante por ello."Nos vemos.".Presumo que Regirock volverá a su tumba."mLos titanes son temperamentales e inadecuados para existir fuera de sus criptas. No es ningún problema."FTodos hemos triunfado en nuestros planes. Esto fue una cortesía.",Ahora me retiro. Gracias por tu tiempo."(Y ahí va. De regreso a donde vino."\Bueno, no esperaba ganar de todos modos. Sólo quería pararte un poco, y, eh, lo hice."DAsí que… adiós. Repetiremos esto en algún momento. Me voy."C*sigh* Adiosito, Regirock. Ya no te, eh, necesitamos, supongo."CFue divertido mientras duró… bueno. Nada dura para siempre."T¡Hablando de! ¡Espero que la próxima vez que hablemos sea en un mundo justo!":Si no lo es, entonces te daré un buen combate, ¿Ok?"WChao. Y no te atrevas a seguirme – Estoy jugando duro, así que respetalo. ¡Ja!"�Hace más de un millón de años, un meteoro estrelló esta área de Makya, barriendo a través de una gran montaña en el oeste."xEsa gran montaña se convirtió en otras dos montañas más pequeñas, que ahora conocemos como los Picos Partidos."REl sitio de impacto se llenó de agua y se convirtió en el Puerto Sweetrock.".El océano al este trae vientos serenos.."b¿Pero por qué? Podríamos explicarlo con las corrientes océanicas, o patrones climáticos."S¿Pero qué hace a los vientos aquí tan serenos? De eso, no estoy tan seguro."@Realmente quiero saber quién estaba en ese traje extraño.">Bueno, de todos modos, gracias por expulsarlo del pueblo."QSoy un bombero, así que estoy acostumbrado a lidiar con varios problemas..."NPero "Cultista con un Regirock" está fuera de mi descripción de empleo."Lightkeeper's House"Orbes Artesanos" Escuela Elemental Sweetrock"1“En memoria de el Sr. y la Sra. Diakos.”"GHe atravesado la región entera en bicicleta estos últimos meses."DCruzar los Picos Partidos fue por lejos la parte más difícil."La vista desde aquellos acantilados, y el sentimiendo de haber finalmente cumplido mi meta, hizo que todo valiera la pena."Oeste: Picos Partidos"Sur: Estuario Arenisca"D“¡Puerto Sweetrock, satisfaciendo la melosidad del mundo!”"(“¡La ciudad hermana de Canal!”"JTrabajo en la Fábrica de Dulces Sweetrock, como varios en el pueblo."UDicho esto, raramente llego a ver a Victoire, la directora y líder de gimnasio."<Debo depender de rumores para saber cómo es su equipo."2Algunas de ellas son algo difíciles de ceer."DI heard some people saying that she uses a Sticky Web strategy."B¿Con Pokémon de tipo Hada y Acero? ¿Cómo logra hacer eso?"*Eh, ¿Así que realmente la venciste?".Debes decirme cómo era como entrenadora.")¡Mi curiosidad es demasiado grande!"pLos caramelos de Sweetrock son enviados a todo el mundo, pero más del 30% terminan en la región de Galar."!Esa gente ama sus caramelos."&Shh... ¡No reveles mi escondite!"#¿Es... es seguro salir ahora?"-¿Cómo va su travesía, jóven maestro?"hCompré una licencia de teletransportación Clefable, y reservé este embarcadero para nuestro uso."SPodemos viajar hacia y desde cualquiera de nuestras localizaciones habituales."¿A dónde nos iremos?""Emma's Empoloreum!""0An Empoleon standee points you to the door."7¿Te has deslizado por las cintsa transportadoras?"ASeeeeeguramente no podemos hacer eso, pero es muy divertido."b¡Quizás no tan divertido como vencer al séptimo gimnasio con mis vistosos nuevos Pokémon!";¿Cuáles? ¡Tendrás que combatirme para descubrirlo!"TNo puedo expresarte lo mucho que quiero combatir. Entonces, ¿Estás para ello?"Entendido."-Estaré aquí hasta que desees combatir."¡A por ellos, Torterra!"?Rayos, ni siquiera estos 'mons pudieron darte un rasguño."F¿Crees que alguien en el faro estuvo observando nuestro combate?"LNo queda de otra, tengo que curarme un poco antes de combatir de nuevo."2¿Imagino que ya te encontraste con Victoire?"|¿Realmente es tan extravagante como dicen? No sé por qué me molesto en preguntar. Voy a descubrirlo pronto por mi cuenta.":¡La séptima medalla... ya puedo sentir su dulzura!.""Gimnasio del Puerto Sweetrock"Líder: Victoire"¡La Reina Caramelo!"%Canal de los Caramelos Sweetrock"{Lo que alguna vez fue un aviso impreso ha sido cubierto completamente por un cartel que anuncia el dispensador EXP-EZ."Faro Sweetrock"(Hoy es un buen día para el gaming."-A Piplup standee points you to the door."Invernadero de Bayas"QMe encanta deslizarme por la cinta transportadora. Pero mi papá no me deja."_Tengo que quedarme en la escuela hasta que salga del trabajo así no me meto en problemas."¡Gaming!"No."	Sí."Escucharé."No lo necesito."No, no lo haré."Eso es poco convincente."Pensaré al respecto."Lo haré."Bien, habla."No me interesa hablar."Sé quien eres."No me amenaces."Claro."Ya lo deseo."Estoy contigo."Muy bien."
Vete."Eso es insano."¿Degenerado?"¿El seno de Arceus?"Eso es justo."Seguro, habla."No me importa."No lo vale."¿A quién le importa?"La sociedad se colapsará."Buen punto."Escucharé."No me importa."Te equivocas."No soy culpable."Seguro."No es tan simple."%¿Los Pokémon lo harían mejor?"Es justo."Quizás luego."Seguro, vamos.;[&"HIt's the bottom of a conveyor belt. It'd be impossible to climb up."xFor most of Sweetrock's history, we've relied on Clefable teleportation to get cargo from the factory to the docks."eWe got these conveyor belts installed a few years back, so the cliffside isn't an issue anymore."TWe still have to rely on teleportation to get in and out of the harbor, though."PLooks like the Trainer ahead is moving to block you from going any further."?Do you want to approach them? It looks like a tough fight."1I knew you would arrive, should I only wait."\Excuse the charade – I would prefer my identity remain enshrouded in mystery for now."{All that you are required to understand is who I serve – Yezera. Under her profound guidance, we have achieved our goals."rThe titans have served their purpose. I come then with a simple inquiry: will you not listen to my reasoning?"PThank you. Our goal is naught less than a complete reordering of the world."<My comrades have their own motives, but mine is simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."cOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it."Do you not agree?"/How disappointing, to dismiss it outright."IIf you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regirock, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."]G’afternoon. Took your sweet time showing your face ‘round these parts, didn’t ya?"eListen, I ain’t ‘bout to preach to ya. Just want to make some things clear ‘fore we fight.">‘Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."wWhat’s so damn infuriating ‘bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."NHow ‘bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?".Good. I ain’t ‘bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."iSorry, kid. You’re a mite too fast. Gotta slow you down. Regirock, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."|But, cheer up, kid. I’m ‘bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."BToo rough ‘nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"1Hey. Fancy meeting you in a place like this."aOh, don’t look so angry – Regirock and I are here to fight you, but we’ll get to that."RI know you’re more than a pretty face. You’re smart. Care to hear me out?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."CFor now, I’ve been ordered to slow you down. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."uFortunately, I’ve been sent to slow you down, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection."Hello, friend."FBusiness before pleasure: I have been sent to slow your progress.".To that end, I am accompanied by a titan."XBefore we attend to that, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."RNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regirock, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.".Prepare yourself. Regirock, if you would."Oh. Hey."IYeah, so, I knew you’d be here. Gym challenger, and, uh, all that."…Welp. This is awkward.";How do I say this… you interested in hearing us out?"bWe’ve kinda got the upper hand, but, y’know, don’t really wanna fight you. Whaddya say?"=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."dI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regirock. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"*Regirock, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."kOdds are Regirock isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"…Hey."xTsk tsk tsk. I’m not gonna lie to you: I’ve been trying to plan this conversation in my head for the past hour."RBut, um, you kinda interrupted me. So can I just say what I want to tell you?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."?Regirock – your watch is over. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YFarewell, and do not pursue me. Fate and fate alone will dictate when we next speak."eRegirock’s damn well spent. Flighty li'l things never like to be outside their tombs too long."*Ah, well. Got what I came for anyhow."�Let me tell you one last word of advice. You hurt Yez, I’ll find you. And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."jG’evening, kid. I’ll see ya around. Make sure I don’t hafta hurt you too bad when I do, ‘kay?";Au revoir, Regirock. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."PAnd as for you, that was an exciting fight. You’ve got my heart pounding."yIf you want to join us, come find Yezera. And if not, well, we’ll meet again. I’m looking forward to it already."So long."4I surmise Regirock will now return to its tomb."gThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts. It is of no matter."AWe have all but succeeded in our plans. This was a courtesy."7I will take my leave now. Thank you for your time."/There it goes. Back to where it came from."_Well, didn’t really expect to win anyways. Just wanted to slow you down, and, uh, I did.":So… bye. We’ll do this again sometime. I’m out."P*sigh* Buh-bye, Regirock. We don’t really, uh, need you anymore, I guess."?It was fun while it lasted… welp. Nothing lasts forever."ISpeaking of! Hopefully next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"KIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll give you a run for your money, ‘kay?"\Toodles. And don’t you dare follow – I’m playing hard to get, so respect it. Hah!"uMore than a million years ago, a meteor struck this area of Makya, plowing through a large mountain to the west."XThat large mountain became two smaller mountains, which we now know as Split Peaks."NThe impact site itself would fill with water and become Sweetrock Harbor."0The ocean to the east brings calming winds."KBut why? We might explain it with ocean currents, or weather patterns."FBut what makes the winds here calming? Of that, I am not so sure."<I really want to know who that was in the weird outfit.";Well, regardless, thanks for kicking them out of town."=I'm a firefighter, so I'm used to dealing with issues..."DBut "Cultist with a Regirock" is outside of my job description."Lightkeeper's House"Artisan Orbs" Sweetrock Elementary School"/"In loving memory of Mrs. and Mr. Diakos.""HI've been biking across the entire region over the past few months.":Crossing the Split Peaks was by far the hardest part."nThe view from these cliffs, and the feeling that I've finally accomplished my goal, made it all worth it."West: Split Peaks"South: Sandstone Estuary";"Sweetrock Harbor, satisfying the world's sweettooth!""!"A sister city of Canalave!"":I work at Sweetrock Candy factory, like many in town."IThat said, I rarely get to see Victoire, the manager and gym leader.":I gotta rely on rumors to know what her team is like.",Some of them are a bit hard to believe."DI heard some people saying that she uses a Sticky Web strategy."AWith Fairy and Steel-type Pokemon? How does she manage that?"$Huh, you really beat her, then?"4You gotta tell me what she's like as a trainer.""My curiosity's grown too big!"_Sweetrock Candy is sent all over the world, but more than 30% ends up in the Galar Region."#Those people love their candy."+Shh... don't give away my hiding spot!")Is it... is it safe to come out now?")How goes your journey, young master?"YI've purchased a Clefable teleportation license, and reserved this pier for our use.":We can travel to and from any of our usual locations."Where will we be heading?""Emma's Empoloreum!""0An Empoleon standee points you to the door."+Have you slid down the conveyor belts?"=Preeeetty sure we're not allowed to, but it's crazy fun."PMaybe not as fun as beating the 7th gym will be with my snazzy new Pokemon!";Which ones? You'll just have to battle me to find out!"XI cannot convey to you just how much I want to battle. Heh. So, you up to doing so?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."Rock 'Em, Torterra!"9Damn, even these 'mons couldn't leave a dent in you."EThink anyone in the lighthouse was watching our battle just now?"INo way around it, I'll need some healing before we square off again.",Got a good look at Victoire, I take it?"bShe as quirky as they say? I don't know why I bother asking. I'll be finding out soon myself."0The 7th badge... oh so sweet will it taste!"Sweetrock Harbor Gym"Leader: Victoire"The Candy Queen!"Sweetrock Candy Outlet"kWhat was once a printed notice has been covered entirely by a poster advertising the EXP-EZ Dispenser."Sweetrock Lighthouse"#Today's a good day for gaming."-A Piplup standee points you to the door."Berry Greenhouse"HI love to slide down the conveyor belt. But, my dad doesn't let me."UI have to stay by the school until he gets off work so I don't get into trouble."I'm gaming over here!"No."	Yes."I’ll listen."Don't need it."No, I don't."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
I do."Fine, talk."Not interested in talking."I know who you are."Don't threaten me."Clear."Wish that already."I'm with you."Alright, fine."Go away."That's insane."Degenerate?"Arceus's bosom?"That's fair."Sure, talk."Don't really care."It isn't worth it."Who cares?"Society will crumble."Good point."I'll listen."Don't care."You're wrong."I'm not guilty."
Sure."Not that simple."Pokémon would do better?"Fair enough."Maybe later."Sure, let's go.Iu;␀&[[O"=A cap of rock is holding back a geyser of boiling water."PI was once considered a beauty, but the way of the water needed a disciple."I should dry off."_Legends say if I stay here for fourty day and nights, my inner qi will strengthen tenfold."4The way of the water is full of solice. Splash."W\PN! You made it. Took some effort to find this place but... man. It was worth it."7What? My all-grown-up companion here? Yeah. It is."\Sorry. Well, not sorry. You didn’t have to come. But you did. And I’m glad you did."dI think it’s soothing. I dunno, maybe I’m just a little more goth than I’d like to admit."|The waters here are special. Not just ice-cold and way too deep for me to be comfortable, but they’re saltwater, too."cOcean water, trapped down here. And for some reason... it makes Phione transform into Manaphy."CI don’t know why, or how. I’m not that smart. But it does."�I don’t even know if it’s really evolution. It’s – I don’t care. I don’t care how it works, or what it is scientifically."6It’s a Manaphy now. And I’m damn proud of it."(Yeah! I mean, I think so, at least."YI can’t believe it. A Pokémon of actual literal myth and legends, here beside me."Oh. Uh, yeah, thanks."�Um. I didn’t really have a lot to do with it. Phione came down here, danced around in the water here, and then it just kinda... transformed."KUnbelievable. A Manaphy. I raised a Pokémon like this, all by myself."oIt’s a Pokémon from myth. Supposedly they live at the ocean floor and can befriend anything and anyone."iThey’re not half-bad in a scrap, either. Truly just... amazing. An absolutely incredible Pokémon."vAnd it’s my best friend. It doesn’t hate me, or resent me, or fear me. It chose to be with me, of all people."mIt could’ve chosen anyone. It could’ve chosen you – you’re certainly a better trainer than I am."lAnd, yeah, thank you, sincerely, for everything. You’re great. And you’ve really helped me. Thanks.";Hmm. Yeah, not good enough. Gonna need one last favor."qI hope so! Not too many people have even seen one of these magical things. And fewer people have fought one."@Oh, we’re on the same wavelength. You know what it means."CThat’s right. One last showdown. You and me. My new Manaphy."QI’m gonna lose, I know. But I’m not going down easy, alright? You ready?"4Alright. Get ready. I want it to be a good one."<I’ve never been happier to throw down against anyone."oManaphy’s debut. I don’t care if it’s good or bad. I just want to see it in action. Let’s do this."(You good? I’m ready when you are."*Ah, wouldn’t have it any other way."IYou know, \PN, you’re a good friend. You don’t pull any punches."GI never could beat you, and I’m never going to, but that’s OK."WYou’ve made me better. Helped me out. I hope I’ve helped you too. I really do.")And, uh, yeah, I’m glad I met you."rGood. I’m – yeah, that’s all I’ve ever really wanted. Manaphy’s happy, you’re happy, I’m happy."FSorry, that’s just who I am. Big ol’ bleeding-heart, I guess."Oh!";Uh, well... I don’t know. I’ll think about it, OK?"NWe’ll see each other around. I, uh... I dunno if I see you in that way."?You know. If you’re saying what I think you’re saying."D...\PN, I really do care about you, though. You’re my friend."1And if you need me, I’ll be there, always."^Well, maybe not always. I’ve got my Pokémon to take care of. But you know what I mean."/I’ve done some stuff I’m not proud of."ZI’m gonna come clean: I’ve been working with Yezera on her plans for a while now."�Never felt like I was good enough. Didn’t feel like anyone was good enough for the love we got from our Pokémon. But maybe that was just me projecting."�Maybe I’m the asshole, y’know? And I’ve known that forever – I’m not that stupid – but it takes a wake-up call to realize it. And this was it."�So, yeah, if they want to ruin the world, they can do it without me. And you can stop them with a Phione at your side. Or a Manaphy now, I guess."II’ll be thinking about you. Wishing you the best, now and forever."IThanks for all of it. If you need me, ever, all you gotta do is ask.",Neither of us is finished, I know that."JI’m gonna try again at becoming Champion next year, I think. Maybe."GFuture’s uncertain. And you... you’ve got stuff to do, I know."DI wish you the best. I’m gonna be thinking about you, I know."cAnd if you need me, you damn well better ask me, OK? You’ve taken a weight off my shoulders."See you around, \PN."Is that...?"Tell me about it."Creepy, isn't it?"That's great."I'm proud of you."What's a Manaphy?"You're welcome."It was worth it."You know what this means."Not yet."Let's rock."Same here."Don't get sappy."Coffee sometime?[O"EUna capa de rocas está conteniendo un geiser de agua hirviendo."ZUna vez fui considerada una bella, pero el camino del agua necesitaba una discípula."Debería secarme."|Las leyendas dicen que si me quedo aquí por cuarenta días y cuarenta noches, mi qi interior se aumentará diez veces."7El camino del agua está lleno de soledad. Splash."a¡\PN! Llegaste. Tomó algo de esfuerzo encontrar este lugar pero... hombre. Valió la pena."9¿Qué? ¿Mi compañero ya todo-crecido? Seh. Lo es."kLo siento. Bueno, no lo siento. No tenías que venir. Pero lo hiciste. Y me alegra que lo hayas hecho."kCreo que es reconfortante. No sé, a lo mejor soy un poco más gótico de lo que me gustaría admitir."|Las aguas aquí son especiales. No es sólo helada y demasiado profunda para mi gusto, pero también son aguas saladas."kAgua océanica, atrapada aquí abajo. Y por alguna razón... hace que Phione se transforme en Manaphy."DNo sé por qué, o cómo. No soy tan inteligente. Pero lo hace."{Ni siquiera sé si es realmente evolución. Es – no me importa. No me importa cómo funciona, o qué es científicamente."OEs un Manaphy ahora. Y puedes asegurarte que estoy bien orgulloso de ello."%¡Sí! Osea, eso creo, al menos."KNo puedo creerlo. Un Pokémon de mitos y leyendas, aquí al lado mío."Oh. Eh, seh, gracias."�Em. No creo que haya tenido mucho que ver al respecto. Phione vino aquí, bailó alrededor del agua aquí, y luego sólo se... transformó."NNo puedo creerlo. Un Manaphy. Crié un Pokémon como este, por mi cuenta."kEs un Pokémon de mitos. Supuestamente viven en el fondo marino y pueden hacerse amigos de cualquiera."iTampoco se le da mal en una palea. Realmente es... increíble. Un Pokémon absolutamente increíble."tY es mi mejor amigo. No me odia, ni me resiente, ni me tiene miedo. Eligió estar conmigo, entre toda la gente."vPodría haber elegido a cualquiera. Podría haberte elegido a ti – ciertamente eres un mejor entrenador que yo."_Y, seh, gracias, sinceramente, por todo. Eres genial. Y realmente me has ayudado. Gracias."MHmm. Seh, no lo suficientemente bueno. Voy a necesitar un último favor."n¡Eso espero! No mucha gente ha visto una de estas cosas mágicas. Y muchas menos gente ha combatido una."=Oh, estamos en la misma onda. Ya sabes lo que significa."LEso es cierto. Un último enfrentamiento. Tú y yo. Y mi nuevo Manaphy."LVoy a perder, lo sé. Pero no voy a caer tan fácimente, ¿Ok? ¿Listo?"4Muy bien. Prepárate. Quiero que sea uno bueno.">Nunca he estado más feliz de haber desafíado a alguien."hEl debut de Manaphy. No me importa si es bueno o malo. Sólo quiero verlo en acción. Vamos a ello."7¿Estás bien? Estaré listo cuando tú lo estés."-Ah, no lo querría de ningún otro modo."?Sabes, \PN, eres un buen amigo. No te andas con chiquitas."DNunca podría vencerte, y nunca voy a hacerlo, pero está bien."WMe hiciste mejor. Me ayudaste. Espero también haberte ayudado. Realmente lo hago.".Y, eh, seh, me da gusto haberte conocido."lBien. Yo – seh, eso es todo lo que realmente quería. Manaphy es feliz, tú eres feliz, yo soy feliz."GLo siento, eso es sólo lo que estoy. Un gran sensiblero, supongo."
