ypes. Only unevolved Pokémon. It just got worse."dEveryone’s so predictable. They don’t understand Pokémon the way I do, fight the way I do."�I wandered all of Makya, catching only one Pokémon from each place I visited. Any time they failed me, I released them into the wild."fEven that grew old after a few months. The only person that’s broken up that boredom is… you."+So, \PN, I ask you: are you bored yet?"…Hmph."You will be. Eventually."…So you are like me."I’m sorry. I truly am."<You don’t have to tell me. It won’t change my mind.""Because we can change things."I can, at least. I will."@…This probably isn’t what you were expecting me to say."fDid you want me to quiver and quaver like a child? Stumble over my words and beg for forgiveness?"Sorry. This is me."gThis is the real me – the one I show to my Pokémon. The only ones I can truly talk to. And you."xAll of this is going to be clean white stone in a little while. I wanted to come back just to see it one last time."aCouldn’t stand the idea of talking to anyone. Not Mom, not anyone. It won’t matter soon."Remaking the world."vThe era of human dominance is at an end. With Regigigas’s power, I’ll reset everything back to the beginning."3When the world was new… full of potential…"4I want a world free from this constant boredom."GI want a world in which the ancient power of Pokémon is set free."$I want a brand new blank slate."Yes. I am."?Incapable of relating to humans, or even speaking to them."lMy heart races when they look at me. I am insane, or at least ill. But that doesn’t mean I’m wrong."GI’d expect nothing less. You’re just like me when I was young."/Wanting to be good. So they’d love me…"$…You understand, don’t you?"$Team Chasm uncovered the Regis."hTamarind understood them because she was a scientist. I understood them because they were Pokémon."8Regidrago, when humans cowered in fear of monsters."(Regice, when they huddled in caves."7Regirock, when they built fortifications of stone."(Registeel, 