, digging would be paused until the mineral could be extracted."+Mining saccharite takes time and care!"T<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: Have you ever been underground? What was it like?"Yo, champ in the making!"QSamorn might not look like it, but she was one of Team Chasm's top battlers.".Her specialties are Dragon and Bug-types."gThat makes Ice-type your silver bullet. She'll have some answers for it, but it's still a counter."qFlying and Rock are your next best bets. Steel is pretty good as well, since it resists both of her typings."7Best of luck in the final stretch of your Gym run."-Hoho! It's rare to see Samorn so lively."-Watching you two go at it was inspiring."The PC is turned off."\With how quiet the gym is, you think it'd stand out as rude if you tried to turn it on."4This statuette is made of a special white clay."RStatuettes like this, commonly known as "totems", are found throughout Makya."OThey are protected by regional law. Totems must stay where they are found!"nAnthropologists believe the spots where totems are found were of special importance to an ancient people."O<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: Why do you think these statuettes were made?"8Among the books on history, a scrapbook stands out."&The title is "Memories of Hoenn.""<A cute sticker of a Trapinch dominates the front cover."Sorry, am I in your way?")Wait, of course I am, I'm a trainer!";I've been reading about ancient Makyan hero- trainers."*You might be even stronger than them!"3I've got to stay here and continue my studies."An Eevee plushy."3A tag around its neck identifies it as "Lark"."+Beakers of chemicals line the shelves."*The majority appear to be weak acids."/The inscription is worn and hard to parse."KAh, \PN! I won’t waste your time by offering something hot to drink."4You’ve got a fight on your mind, don’t you?"8Good evening. Can I get you something? Tea? Coffee?"GYou’ve almost certainly wasted enough time here already, though."3Do you get nervous before facing a gym leader?"