Fine."About time."I hate you too."I love you.000Iu;␀�[["{The fridge contains dozens of tupper-ware containers, all marked with dates as well as specific Pokemon species names.["yEl frigorífico contiene docenas de tápers, todos marcados con tanto fechas como especies de Pokémon específicas.;["{The fridge contains dozens of tupper-ware containers, all marked with dates as well as specific Pokemon species names.Iu;␀@[[	"-A collection of Pokemon battling guides."<They seem like classics, likely more than 50 years old."A beat up old television."'It's been unplugged from the wall.[	"3Una colección de guías de combates Pokémon."?Parecen clásicos, presuntamente de hace más de 50 años."Un viejo televisor."Está desconectado.;[	"-A collection of Pokemon battling guides."<They seem like classics, likely more than 50 years old."A beat up old television."'It's been unplugged from the wall.0Iu;␀Oo[[�"PLooks like the Trainer ahead is moving to block you from going any further."?Do you want to approach them? It looks like a tough fight."yI knew you would seek Yezera. I am her humble servant, naturally, though I would rather keep my identity enshrouded."JPray excuse the charade – it will not be necessary for much longer."jUnder Yezera’s profound guidance, we have achieved our goals. The titans have served their purpose."LI come then with a simple inquiry: will you not listen to my reasoning?"PThank you. Our goal is naught less than a complete reordering of the world."<My comrades have their own motives, but mine is simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."uOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it. Do you not agree?"tHow disappointing, to dismiss it outright. If you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regice, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."TG’afternoon. Took your sweet time comin’ to find Yezera 'gain, didn’t ya?"CGot no interest in convincing you. Ain’t much of a preacher."�But I gotta set some ground rules 'fore we fight; establish some things. 'Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."uWhat’s so damn infuriating 'bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."LHow 'bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?",Good. I ain’t 'bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."[Sorry, kid. Yezera wants some peace 'n' quiet. Regice, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."zBut, cheer up, kid. I’m 'bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."@Too rough 'nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"Oh, hello."RSuch a picturesque place to meet. If only it were under better circumstances."]Regice and I have unfortunately been told to make sure Yezera has no unwelcome visitors."xBefore that, though… I know you’re more than a pretty face. You’ve got a spark to you. Will you listen to me?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."@For now, I’ve been ordered to remove you. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."�Fortunately, I’ve been sent to ensure you make it no farther, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection.".Hello, friend. Yezera wishes to be alone."NTo that end, I have been sent, and graciously afforded a titan to aid me."`Before we attend to your removal, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."PNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regice, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.",Prepare yourself. Regice, if you would."4Yo. Figure’d, uh, yeah, that you’d be here."bYezera’s here. You keep running into her. She, uh, doesn’t really want to talk right now."0I got a job to do, but, uh, not keen on it." So you want to hear us out?"]Swear we’ve got some good reasons. Even if I’m not that good at putting it in words."=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."bI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regice. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"(Regice, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."iOdds are Regice isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"-Well. Had to happen eventually, I guess."II’ve kinda sorta been planning what to say for the past few hours."cBut, um… I still don’t know. So can I just say what comes to mind and hope you understand?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."ARegice – your service has ended. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YWhen and where, fate shall decide, though I think I know where we shall settle this."8Do not pursue me. Your audience with Yezera awaits.""Seems Regice’s 'bout spent."ODidn’t exactly expect them to be so squirrelly, but them’s the breaks.".Figure it’s headin’ back to its home."eOne last thing, since you seem ‘bout ready to see Yez again: you hurt her and I’ll find you."=And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."sG’evening, kid. I’ll be seein’ you. Keep in mind how nice it feels to be havin’ all your bones intact."9Au revoir, Regice. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."XAnd as for you, I’m breathless. Speechless. You’re even better than I imagined."OIf you’d like to stop your pointless struggling against us, tell Yezera."4We’d love to have you. Until we meet again…"2I surmise Regice will now return to its tomb."SThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts."0It is of no matter. Our victory comes soon."JYezera may be displeased in my performance, but she is understanding."GIn the end, this will make no difference. Thank you for your time."See ya, Regice."Ah, who am I kidding."cIf either of us is gonna see it again, it’ll be you. Couldn’t really hold a candle to you."UHad to try anyways, just for Yezera. And I’m gonna have to do it again, right?"VGood practice, I guess. Well, think about it – everything, y’know? I’m out."U*sigh* So long, Regice. You never really were my type, anyways, so head on home."HAnd as for YOU, well, next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"MIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll have to buy us a li’l more time, 'kay?"FUntil then, I’ve got judgment to be a-judging. So long, "hero.""No."	Yes."I'll listen."Don't need it."No, I don’t."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
I do."Fine, talk."Not interested in talking."I know who you are."Don't threaten me."Clear."Wish that already."I'm with you."Alright, fine."Go away."That's insane."Degenerate?"Arceus's bosom?"That's fair."Sure, talk."Don't really care."It isn't worth it."Who cares?"Society will crumble."Good point."Don't care."You're wrong."I'm not guilty."
Sure."Not that simple."Pokémon would do better?"Fair enough.[�"aParece que el Entrenador enfrente se está moviendo para bloquearte ir a ninguna otra parte."5¿Quieres acercarte? Parece un combate difícil."�Sabía que buscarías a Yezera. Naturalmente, yo soy su humilder siervo, aunque preferiría mantener mi identidad como un misterio."NPor favor perdona esta pantomima – no será necesaria por mucho tiempo."sBajo la profunda guianza de Yezera, hemos alcanzado nuestros objetivos. Los titanes han servido su propósito."NEntonces vengo con una simple consulta: ¿No escucharás mi razonamiento?"OGracias. Nuestro objetivo es nada menos que un completo reorden del mundo."FMis camaradas tienen sus propios motivos, pero el mío es simple."�El mundo en el presente es voluble y falaz. La cultura y tecnología humano no sirve para nada excepto como un velo para disfrazar la verdad definitiva."�Sólo el reino de los mitos antiguos, cuidado por los dioses, intacto por los humanos, puede dejarnos percibirlo. ¿No estás de acuerdo?"�Que decepcionante, descartarlo rotundamente. Si no tienes un ojo para la verdad, entonces no tenemos nada más de lo que hablar."mPerdóname este acto de pasión, pero espero que la furia de un titán pueda calmar mi corazón furioso." Regice, acata mis órdenes."SPor el contrario: tiene un soporte firme, si solo uno reflexiona en el asunto."|Lástima, tal fé vacilante es prácticamente inservible para mis propósitos. Requerimos una devoción inquebrantable."V*sigh* Estaría abandonando mi deber si no te detuviera como minímo. Prepárate."eDebería animarte a ello. Juzga el peso del mundo que está en contra del mundo que podría ser."pLástima, sé que no meditaras tranquilamente ante él. Eres una amenaza. Eso es intolerable para nosotros."VEsta no será una victoria decisiva mía, pero no puedo dejarte pasar sin trabas.")…Me gustaría mucho poder creerte."pSi hablas la verdad, entonces te demando que repitas tus coinvicciones a Yezera la proxima vez que la veas."�Ella puede ver las maquinaciones de tu corazón más claramente que yo. Hasta entonces, sigues siendo un entrenador, al igual que yo."QA mis enemigos los aniquilo, a mis aliados los entreno. A ambos, en guardia."USi no vas a escuchar mis plegarias, entonces estás más allá de la salvación."ZLástima. Quizás la furia de un titán te iluminará en la claridad de los antiguos."IBuenas. Te tomaste tu tiempo para venir a por Yezera otra vez, ¿Eh?"?No me interesa convencerte. No es que sea una predicadora."Pero debo establecer un par de reglas antes de combatir; establecer un par de cosas. Porque vamos a combatir. No queda de otra."LMuchas gracias. Realmente no me interesa demasiado toda esta pantomima."Estoy con Yezera, siempre."DEscucha, sólo voy a decir esto una vez: tienes que escucharla."ANo me importa si estás de acuerdo con ella. Solo escuchala."pY si la lastimas, voy a asegurarme de que desees que Mavis haya parado después de Zain. ¿Lo tienes claro?"*Sí que eres un mocoso engreído. Tsk"tLo más irritante sobre ti es que no puedo simplemente patear tu trasero para hacer que obedezcas. Eres fuerte."Q¿Pero qué tal si lo intento? ¿El titán debe ser bueno para algo, cierto?"Bien. No voy a repetirme."JAhora, vine aquí con un trabajo que hacer, y soy del tipo confiable."aLo siento, niño. Yezera quiere un poco de paz y tranquilidad. Regice cariño, ve al frente."UJa. Tómalo de alguien que tiene idea, niño: aún no arañas ni la superficies."CPodría hacerte mucho más miserable si me concentrara a ello."|Pero, alégrate, niño. Voy a darte lo que siempre quieres: un buen combate. Enfrentar a un Regi debería darte ánimos. Je.">Nah, no voy a creer eso. No sabes nada sobre Yezera y yo."CUna vieja pareja que se la pasa peleando, eso es lo que somos."C¿Quieres mostrarme que estás con nosotros? Dícelo a Yezera."wPor ahora, no me interesa dejarte ir tan fácil. Lo siento. Tumbar gente al suelo es mi trabajo, después de todo."YAh, bueno. Supongo que no importa cuanto lo intentas, los viejos hábitos no se van."CHablando de irse – ¿Échate un rato y déjate de mover, ok?"OJa. Nunca estuvieron tan contentos con mi forma de trabajar de encubierto."9Demasiado brusca y severa. No estoy hecha para esto."|Así que, déjame decirte esto de forma clara: escuchas a Yezera. Todo lo que tenga que decir. Y no te atrevas a lastimarla."LEs todo lo que pido. Y, eh, no me enviaron aquí para charlar. ¿Listo?"Oh, hola."YTan pintoresco lugar para encontrarnos. Si tan solo fuera en mejores circunstancias."~Desafortunadamente, nos han dicho a Regice y a mi que nos aseguremos de que Yezera no tenga ningún visitante inoportuno."qPero, antes que eso… Sé que eres más que una cara bonita. Tienes una chispa en ti. ¿Piensas escucharme?"0Oww. Tenía un buen presentimiento contigo."]Cómo lo explico… bueno, odio usar la palabra, pero la sociedad moderna es degenerada."gEstamos distantes desde el momento perfecto de la creación. De algún modo hemos tomado el mundo."^Nada de respeto a nuestros mayores – los Pokémon primordiales que crearon el universo."vYezera va a reiniciar este mundo a sus orígenes. Y luego la humanidad estará en el seno de Arceus una vez más."nNo me llames insano. Aunque estoy seguro que esta civilización arrogante y sin fé usaría ese término."_Soy meramente un devoto, y la devoción significa hacer sacrificios. Por ejemplo: el tuyo."MRealmente me gustas, pero… todos tenemos que sacrificarnos alguna vez."OLos Pokémon divinos ahora son tratados como no más que bestias de carga."MLos avatares son destruídos porque son una “amenaza a los humanos.”"dEl mundo ha perdido todo respeto, la esencia divina de la creación se ha diluido y destruído."FY ya que no pareces ser diferente, podré disfrutar este combate."~Arceus creó el mundo. Un mundo puro y perfecto, y reiniciarlo a su forma original nos dejará ser también puros y perfectos."OMe gustaría verme a mí mismo bendecido por la gracia de nuestro creador.".También me gustaría verte de esa forma."A su debido tiempo."6Por ahora, me han ordenado detenerte. ¿Bailamos?"(Bien. Sabía que había algo en ti."=Una chispa de fé. Soy un… muy buen juez de carácter."�Me encantaría sólo hablar contigo por un rato, pero fui instruído explícitamente a pararte. Así que combatiremos. No te lo tomes personal."Oh. ¿Demasiado atrevido?"GMis emociones suelen sacar lo peor de mi. Estoy casi desconsolado."(Bueno, supongo que soy un extraño."�Afortunadamente, me han enviado para asegurarte que no avances, así que tengo un desahogo conveniente para estos sentimientos de rechazo."*Hola, amigo. Yezera desea estar sola."QPara ese fin, me han enviado aquí, con un titán a mi lado para escoltarme."cSin embargo, antes de proseguir a tu eliminación, ¿Te interesa una corta, franca discusión?"MPreferiría intentar convencerte de la legitimidad de nuestra posición."Gracias por tu tiempo."KLa meta de Yezera es recrear las condiciones del mundo en sus albores."sLa ciencia moderna ha logrado un entendimiento y maestría casi completo sobre el mundo –  el mundo moderno."�Sin embargo, no puede entender el pasado. Al revertir su existencia, podremos estudiar el universo desde su concepción y obtener conocimiento universal."%Es la única manera de lograrlo."vSin esa reversión, la humanidad nunca logrará un entendimiento completo del universo. Lo vale cualquier precio."PAhora que nuestra conversación acabó, Regice, por favor, haz los honores."XA todas las personas que intentan avanzar en la civilización debería importarles."REl conocimiento universal es un prerrequisito para una sociedad todopoderosa."bEse es mi objetivo. Ese es el objetivo de toda ciencia: el saber, y aplicar ese conocimiento."jTu ignorancia insinua que la discusión no nos llevará a ningún sitio. Dejemosla de lado, entonces."AEl conocimiento será mantenido en una nueva era primordial."FPodemos reconstruir por lo menos pequeños enclaves de humanidad."cDe ahí nuestro análisis y conquista empezará: una nueva sociedad con conocimiento absoluto.">Y, a raíz de este conocimiento absoluto, poder absoluto."UConsideralo. Por mientras, hay negocios que mencioné anteriormente. Perdóname."�Me alegra que tengas la sabiduría para estar de acuerdo.  Si deseas apoyarnos en nuestra campaña, estaré contento de recibirte."iLucharemos por una era de claridad. Pero por ahora, debo pararte. El trabajo es trabajo. Comencemos."SEncuentro esto altamente desafortundado. Serás dejado atrás por el progreso."APero si prefieres mantener tu ignorancia, no puedo ayudarte.""Preparate. Regice, por favor."3Hey. Supuse que, eh, seh, que estarías aquí."gYezera está aquí. Y no dejas de encontrartela. Ella, eh, realmente no quiere hablar ahora mismo."KTengo un trabajo que hacer, pero, eh, no estoy tan concentrado en él."¿Quiéres escucharnos?"TJuro que tengo buenas razones. Incluso si no soy bueno en ponerlas en palabras.";Oh. Eso es bueno. Genial. Honestamente no lo esperaba."=Bueno, entiendo que mandoneamos bastante a los Pokémon.">Quizás es hora de igualar la posición un poco, ¿Sabes?"ITodos podemos reconciliarnos un poco por lo que sea que hicimos mal."wLos otros tienen sus razones, pero, eh, esta es la mía. Crear un mundo donde podamos ser perdonados. ¿Entiendes?",Bueno – como sea. ¿Sabes qué? Bien."WNo necesito tu permiso, y ciertamente no necesitamos tu ayuda. Regice, cárgatelo."k¿...Tanta seguridad? Toma demasiado entrenamiento para tener un equipo tan fuerte en tan poco tiempo.";Pero, seh, no, lo entiendo. ¿Por qué nos ayudarías?"OMocoso malcriado. Quizás podamos forzar un poco de responsabilidad en ti."NUh. Realmente no sé cómo descomponerlo para ti. Tu… no tienes tiempo."HPrimero, ya hemos basicamente ganado. Segundo – ¡Piensa rápido!",Regice, ¡Barre el suelo con su cuerpo!"(Oh. Realmente no, eh, esperaba eso."5Pensé que eras un mocoso estirado. Sin ofender."ABueno, ok. Quizás estaremos lado a lado algún día, ¿Sí?"BPero, eh, por ahora… se supone que debo combatir contra ti."XAsí que, eh, lo siento – ah, qué estoy diciendo, vivimos para esto. Prepárate."#Seh, supongo que eso funciona."Bien. Eso está… bien."4Vine aquí para molerte a palos de todos modos."zChance es que Regice no va a permanecer por mucho más, así que hagamos que cuente. Hazlo lo mejor que puedas, ¿Eh?"4Bueno. Eventualmente tenía que pasar, supongo."FEstuve mas o menos planeando qué decir por estas últimas horas."tPero, em… todavía no lo sé. Así que, ¿Puedo simplemente decir lo que se me venga y esperar que entiendas?"ABueh. Escucha, eh, Makya está en un lugar raro ahora mismo."eEl Team Chasm pisoteado sobre toda la región, y luego simplemente… ¿Se salieron con la suya?"�Así que, eh, seh, si alguna vez quisiste prueba de que los humanos ni pueden lograr la mayor justicia blanca-y-negra correctamente, ahí la tienes."UHabría sido simple arreglar esa pequeña metedura de pata. Pero no lo hicieron."bAsí que le estamos quitando el poder a los humanos, y ponerlos en las manos de los Pokémon."¿Lo es? ¡Lo es!"I¡¿Soy insano por querer un poco de maldito CASTIGO en este mundo?!"<Bueno, adivina qué. Si la gente no me lo da, lo HARÉ."(¡Y tengo la herramienta necesaria!" Es simple, Idi– ¡Idiota!"`¡Puedo rastrear a cualquier ex-Chasm y llevarlos a la corte yo misma si tengo que hacerlo!"g¡Pero simplemente no harían nada! Así que tengo que hacer las cosas personalmente, ¿Entiendes?"!Lo siento. Nada… personal."¡Sí!"GEllos son nobles y puros y – y – ¡Y nunca me decepcionarían!")¡No como tú! ¡Y todos los demás!"R¿Quieres ver? Vamos. ¡Mira el tipo de justicia que los Pokémon pueden dar!"Oh. Ajá."GQuizá me exalté un poco… bueno, sin daño no hay maldad, ¿Eh?"…Nah, eso es estúpido."^No voy a desperdiciar mi oportunidad. Tengo un Regi. Tu eres un prodigio. ¡Vamos a ELLO!"#¡Arrg, me haces enojar tanto!"!¡Nadie me malditas escucha!"
Bien."Sabes, bien, como sea."QConseguirás lo que todos los demás que enfrento consiguen. Lo que merecen.">Regice – tu servicio ha terminado. Se debes irte, vete."ZAsí que regresa a su lugar de descanso… no importa. Hizo todo lo que desee y más.",Y en cuanto a ti, nos veremos otra vez."cCuándo y dónde, eso lo decidirá la fé, pero creo que sé dónde debemos terminar con esto."4No me persigas. tu audiencia con Yezera espera."!Parece que Regice se cansó."PNo esperaba que fueran exactamente escurridizos, pero supongo que así son.",Supongo que está regresando a su casa."lUna última cosa, ya que parece que estás listo para ver a Yez de nuevo: la lastimas y te encontraré."6Y no será sólo para unas peleitas con animales."mBuenas tardes chico. Ya te veré luego. Recuerda que tan bien se siente tener todos tus huesos intactos."6Au revoir, Regice. Disfruta tu entierro, supongo."^Y en cuanto a ti, estoy sin aliento. Sin palabras. Eres incluso mejor de lo que imaginé."CSi gustas parar tu inútil lucha ante nosotros, dile a Yezera.">Nos encantaría tenerte. Hasta que nos veamos de nuevo…",Presumo que Regice volverá a su tumba."ULos titanes son temperamentales e inadecuados para existir fuera de sus criptas.";No es ningún problema. Nuestra victoria viene pronto."QYezera podrá estar disconforme de mi rendimiento, pero ella es comprensiva."?Al final, esto no hará diferencia. Gracias por tu tiempo."Nos vemos, Regice.""Ah, a quién quiero engañar."dSi uno de nosotros va a verlo de nuevo, vas a ser tú. Realmente no tuve oportunidad contra ti."hTuve que intentarlo de todos modos, sólo por Yezera. Y voy a tener que hacerlo de nuevo, ¿Cierto?"YBuena práctica, supongo. Bueno, piensa al respecto – sobre todo, ¿Sabes? Me voy."U*sigh* Adiós, Regice. Nunca fuiste mi tipo, de todos modos, así que ve a casa."UY en cuanto a TI; bueno, ¡La próxima vez estaremos hablando en un mundo justo!"VSi no lo es, entonces, eh, tendré que conseguirnos un poco más de tiempo, ¿Va?"IHasta entonces, tengo un juicio al que juzgar. Adiós, “héroe.”"No."	Sí."Escucharé."No lo necesito."No, no es así."Eso es poco convincente."Pensaré al respecto."Lo haré."Bien, habla."No me interesa hablar."Sé quien eres."No me amenaces."Claro."Ya lo deseo."Estoy contigo."Muy bien."
Vete."Eso es insano."¿Degenerado?"¿El seno de Arceus?"Eso es justo."Seguro, habla."No me importa."No lo vale."¿A quién le importa?"La sociedad se colapsará."Buen punto."No me importa."Te equivocas."No soy culpable."Seguro."No es tan simple."%¿Los Pokémon lo harían mejor?"Es justo.;[�"PLooks like the Trainer ahead is moving to block you from going any further."?Do you want to approach them? It looks like a tough fight."yI knew you would seek Yezera. I am her humble servant, naturally, though I would rather keep my identity enshrouded."JPray excuse the charade – it will not be necessary for much longer."jUnder Yezera’s profound guidance, we have achieved our goals. The titans have served their purpose."LI come then with a simple inquiry: will you not listen to my reasoning?"PThank you. Our goal is naught less than a complete reordering of the world."<My comrades have their own motives, but mine is simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."uOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it. Do you not agree?"tHow disappointing, to dismiss it outright. If you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regice, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."TG’afternoon. Took your sweet time comin’ to find Yezera 'gain, didn’t ya?"CGot no interest in convincing you. Ain’t much of a preacher."�But I gotta set some ground rules 'fore we fight; establish some things. 'Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."uWhat’s so damn infuriating 'bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."LHow 'bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?",Good. I ain’t 'bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."[Sorry, kid. Yezera wants some peace 'n' quiet. Regice, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."zBut, cheer up, kid. I’m 'bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."@Too rough 'nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"Oh, hello."RSuch a picturesque place to meet. If only it were under better circumstances."]Regice and I have unfortunately been told to make sure Yezera has no unwelcome visitors."xBefore that, though… I know you’re more than a pretty face. You’ve got a spark to you. Will you listen to me?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."@For now, I’ve been ordered to remove you. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."�Fortunately, I’ve been sent to ensure you make it no farther, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection.".Hello, friend. Yezera wishes to be alone."NTo that end, I have been sent, and graciously afforded a titan to aid me."`Before we attend to your removal, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."PNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regice, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.",Prepare yourself. Regice, if you would."4Yo. Figure’d, uh, yeah, that you’d be here."bYezera’s here. You keep running into her. She, uh, doesn’t really want to talk right now."0I got a job to do, but, uh, not keen on it." So you want to hear us out?"]Swear we’ve got some good reasons. Even if I’m not that good at putting it in words."=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."bI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regice. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"(Regice, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."iOdds are Regice isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"-Well. Had to happen eventually, I guess."II’ve kinda sorta been planning what to say for the past few hours."cBut, um… I still don’t know. So can I just say what comes to mind and hope you understand?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."ARegice – your service has ended. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YWhen and where, fate shall decide, though I think I know where we shall settle this."8Do not pursue me. Your audience with Yezera awaits.""Seems Regice’s 'bout spent."ODidn’t exactly expect them to be so squirrelly, but them’s the breaks.".Figure it’s headin’ back to its home."eOne last thing, since you seem ‘bout ready to see Yez again: you hurt her and I’ll find you."=And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."sG’evening, kid. I’ll be seein’ you. Keep in mind how nice it feels to be havin’ all your bones intact."9Au revoir, Regice. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."XAnd as for you, I’m breathless. Speechless. You’re even better than I imagined."OIf you’d like to stop your pointless struggling against us, tell Yezera."4We’d love to have you. Until we meet again…"2I surmise Regice will now return to its tomb."SThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts."0It is of no matter. Our victory comes soon."JYezera may be displeased in my performance, but she is understanding."GIn the end, this will make no difference. Thank you for your time."See ya, Regice."Ah, who am I kidding."cIf either of us is gonna see it again, it’ll be you. Couldn’t really hold a candle to you."UHad to try anyways, just for Yezera. And I’m gonna have to do it again, right?"VGood practice, I guess. Well, think about it – everything, y’know? I’m out."U*sigh* So long, Regice. You never really were my type, anyways, so head on home."HAnd as for YOU, well, next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"MIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll have to buy us a li’l more time, 'kay?"FUntil then, I’ve got judgment to be a-judging. So long, "hero.""No."	Yes."I'll listen."Don't need it."No, I don’t."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
