 way to skin a Liepard."7I promise I’ll give you a fight worth the title.";Wouldn’t want you to. This isn’t a practice match."5This is the real thing. I’m going to enjoy it."Oh, no, we do."rIt’s fun. It’s fun and it’s a way to wrap this whole thing up. Closure’s stupid but it’s important."N…I know Mavis is going to be watching our duel. Makes me a little sick."TDon’t want it to be tainted by knowing I’m supposed to be "proving myself.""cNothing for it, though. One last battle? I’m not going to lose this one like all the others."_I’m going to lose it in my own way. Hah! Show me what you got, \PN. Show me who you are."0…It feels good to feel good after a loss."DCongratulations. You’re the Champion. Pretty big achievement."WI know your job isn’t exactly over – I don’t have my head stuck in the sand."[As your rival and as your opponent, good game. You beat me fair and square. Great job."PAs your brother, goodbye. I’m not gonna see you again for a little while."fI’m blocking Mavis on everything, picking a direction, and walking until I find something cool.""Thanks. Good luck to you too."SI’d stay, but I’ve got faith you’ve got this whole fiasco under control."7Gonna get a headstart on finding inner peace. Hah."Don’t flatter me.">It’s irresponsible... but, yeah, I need some time away."*I hope you can do the same, honestly."HGet away from Mavis, from the gyms, everything. It’d do you good."!Can’t change my mind, kid."YScrew Mavis. Screw the company. Screw the gyms, screw the Championship, screw Makya."Gonna go find out what I’m actually interested in, 'stead of just trying to one-up you for mommy. But thanks for the concern."Don’t. Seriously."yI know she’s our mom, but she’s the reason we’ve been at each other’s throats. Or, uh, I’ve been at yours."hI’m getting away from her. She wants to talk, she can start by not pitting us against each other."#…It is what it is, you know?"<You need me, you call, alright? I’ll pick up for you."HCongratulations, Champion. Love ya. Go be a hero and kick some ass."CI had assumed we'd meet later in the Tournament, to be honest."VOh well, no use worrying about the seeding now. Just need to focus on the battle." I'm going all in. Be ready."RHmm, a disappointing result. Seems like I won't be the first repeat champion."LBest of luck, it'll feel better to lose to the person who takes it all."&How d'ya do? Surprised to see me?">Well, I ain’t 'bout to let this opportunity pass me up."eDon’t much matter to me if the world’s endin'. C’mon. Let’s have us a grand ol’ fight."How d'ya do? \PN?"0Heard a lot 'bout you. The name’s Alessa."nI’m a… call me an old friend of Yezera’s. Real interested to see if you’re as good as she claims."Ya ready?"dAin’t too surprised ‘bout that one. I tried my best, honest, but I ain’t your rival. Heh."ROughta leave you to Yez. Ah, well, I figure I might get a second shot at you."1We’ll see, huh? I’ll be watchin’, kid."So y'are good, aren'tcha?"MYezera ain’t much of a liar, but I figured maybe she got a li'l rusty."bQuite a team, kid. And quite a trainer they got. I’ll be watchin', kid. I’ll be watchin'."Good day."3Did you not expect the Dreadnaught to be here?"sI’ve competed in every Championship since their inception. I wasn’t about to miss this one, avatars or no."'I want to face you. And now I can."tIt brings a smile to my face… though now that must be snuffed out, and my mind set… on the fight to come…"Z…Hmm. I lost. I don’t know why I expected to win so shortly after our last match."KAh well! It was fun while it lasted, and it was good to see you again."}In a way, I’m glad I lost so decisively. If I’d become Champion, the hassle of dealing with the gym would be a nightmare!"RGoodbye, \PN. Come talk to me again sometime, though. My door is always open."mOh, hey. I didn’t think I’d get this far. I didn’t think – well, didn’t think a lot of things."@Doesn’t matter now. Win or lose, I’m ready to face you."HAnd, uh, I’m looking forward to seeing you give 100%. Let’s go."/Yo. I’m Eifion. You’re, uh, \PN, yeah?"YThe kid who’s been running errands for Tamarind? Heard you’re, uh, pretty scary."QAbout half the trainers I talk to have lost to you at some point or another."2... I, uh, don’t plan on being one of them."
Damn!">I – I gave my best. My team did too. All I can ask for."hYou too, you know? You’re doing great. Really impressive. I’ll, uh, I’ll try again next year."@If there is one next year. Gonna be rooting for you anyhow."KHuh. Well, I see why you’ve got so many notches on your Poké Balls."wSomebody’s gonna humble you one day. Looking forward to seeing that – but I’m gonna root for you until then."[I like an underdog story, but I also like betting on the winning horse. G’luck, \PN."RFigured I’d be seein’ you again. It’s been a little while, hasn’t it?"VSeems like just yesterday you were showing up and showing down with me on Casaba."6I’m not about to go down so easy a second time."You ready? I am."=Heh. Guess I never should’ve figured I could beat you."$I’ll be rooting for you, kid."GShouldn’t call you kid, I guess. Barely recognize you, honestly."5Good luck. Even though I doubt you’ll need it."3Oh, well, look what the Shinx dragged in. \PN."LEight years ago, I lost to Yezera, and because of that Team Chasm fell."sI’ve been training since then. I’m planning on redeeming myself among the scattered remnants of your team."rNothing personal – I actually rather appreciate you. You’re just the most convenient point of comparison."MNow, let’s see if I can’t snuff out this child’s hopes and dreams."k*sigh* I’ll need to see my dentist. I think I lost an inch of enamel to grinding my teeth that hard."DWhat is it about you that makes you so infuriatingly adaptable?"FFine. Fine! I’ll resign myself to the only thing I’m good at."|I’ll turn this region into an economic powerhouse, become even richer than Mavis, and buy LuxTech out from under her."^Enjoy my petty revenge. And good luck with the Championship or whatever. I’m done here."$Hello! Hale and hearty, I hope?"{Oh, rest easy, I have no interest in the title. No, I am here because a champion is in the making, and they must be tested!"wTested with fire! Tested with toxin! Tested with the unyielding agony that only the truest c