Mine."?...There is nothing much to say to a dead woman, is there?"1Don’t be. It’s better to know the truth."...Imogene is dead."XI do not know if I ever did. Countless possibilities plagued me in sleepless hours."8Was this one too elegant to consider? Or too cruel?"RImogene has been dead for years. She died well before my memory on the train."KShe was a hermit and a recluse, a mystic and a witch, and now... gone."_I can feel... memories... bubbling up. They’re seeping in like blood through thin gauze."(I can’t let them in. I mustn’t!"MIf I remember who I am... I won’t be me anymore. I won’t be Imogene."...It is agonizing."{The silence, filled with the beat of my raging heart and the echoes of things I had thought left to blissful oblivion."No! You would kill me?"HIf I remember I will be – I will be undone! Unmade in an instant!"So I believed."pHah! How innocent I was, truly, never having witnessed something so horrible as to make one wish to forget."1I’m trying. I am trying with all my might!":I do not want this identity! I do not want this past!"XIf I witness this revelation it will shatter me! I know this with utmost certainty."And... so did she."�I do not know if she has already given in, but she bestowed upon me a gift before she left my presence for what I fear is the last time."Her Pokémon."?She would not entrust them to me if she planned to return."+...I am prepared. I can run no longer."eWilling or no, the truth descends upon me. I will greet it with all the fury I might yet muster.")Make your preparations, if you must."LAre you ready? I cannot do this alone. I require a mirror to gaze into."PI must dance, must ritualize this, must make into something comprehensible."bI need your support, and I know your adamant core resides within your abilities as a trainer."mMore than that, I know it is how you judge people. I would have you witness my soul, and know the truth."SDo what you must. I may wait a few moments longer... may keep the past at bay."FFor the last time, I take up this identity I have absconded with."I am Imogene."I am an oracle."I am a seeker of truth."@Bare your soul to me, wanderer! Let this be my last battle!"...So be it."I remember."oI remember the house, the old hardwood, the ticking of the grandfather clock, the smell of the river loam!"{The crushing of the drying autumn leaves, the warmth of a soft embrace, the bruising, the bleeding, the burning, the fight!"LThe love of the fight! The yearning to learn, to become something more!"_I remember her. I remember Imogene teaching us, teaching all of us... teaching us to be..."Go on ahead."9Find what has happened to my sister in this torment."RI... I will release our Pokémon, and then I will cease this long masquerade."!I will be trapped no longer."?The name on this gravestone is faded beyond recognition..."$Leave me. I must do this alone."There’s a note."�“I’ve released them. Our Pokémon go readily. I think they know. As for me... I remember. She loved Dittos. She kept dozens."SShe trained them not only in battle, but to imitate humans. To imitate... her."YI found it so curious, to see Pokémon pretending to be people. How lovely. How fun!"sShe took me in as if I was just another pink blob, and she taught me more than I can express, let alone repay."{I am not her, nor is my companion. We are but two mirrors set facing each other, endlessly reflecting a woman that is gone."hWe strayed further and further in our imitations every day. It could not last. Do not mourn for us."aThis is the truth, and it provides suffering and succor in equal measure, as it always does.">We are released from our bonds. We are Imogene no longer."<Now we are Imogene, sisters of a name, and that is all."Thank you."Goodbye."�P.S.: I have done things I should not have, in pursuit of this truth. I have endeavored to cause harm to you, to others, to the world entire."qI do not know if this was my own selfish need to know what in my heart of hearts I already saw yet denied --"Aor if, perhaps, Imogene was not the saint I remember her as."EIn either case, I will take responsibility for what I have done."�I cannot stand against you, and will gladly aid you in your coming trials. Not to aid the flow of fate, but because you are my friend."HBecause it is the right thing to do, and because it is what I want."bI cannot ask for more than a chance to make amends side by side with one such as yourself.”"@P.S.: I will gladly lend my aid to you, no matter who I am."TAsk for my assistance, and I will be there. I have plenty strength yet to give."jI do this not for you, who is of import to the flow of destiny, but for you, my friend and confidant."KBring me with you if you desire my company, or have need of my powers."?It is the least I can do... and the best I can imagine.”"...A Mew."@The infinitely-mutable Pokémon of myth, here in the flesh."3It chitters happily, swimming through the air."�Yet, somehow, there’s a macabre tinge to its movements, a slight touch of gallows humor to the way it darts around gravestones."HThere is a flash of sympathy in its eyes when it stares into yours."MIt knows what it is, and it knows what you are, and you know what it is."SIt stops and coils, floating for a moment to regard you with its vibrant eyes.")You see the conflict in its eyes –"�the desire to explore free and wide, the remembered thrill of the fight, the eagerness to repay its debt, the desire to accompany you."!It leaves the choice to you."%It winks at you as you catch it."lSometimes it will go missing, wandering on flights of fancy through landscapes and thoughtscapes alike."CSometimes in the witching hour objects will move on their own."cSometimes you find notes written in handwriting you can’t read, signed with a question mark."9You know it can leave any time it likes. It won’t."9It flips upside down, then rights itself in mid-air."\Perhaps mockery, perhaps a nod, perhaps just an idle motion of a recently-freed animal."Then, it’s gone."RA mirage that disappears with a strong breeze, dispelled like a waking dream."}If you come back, perhaps it will be here, waiting for you. They’ll say this place is haunted, but you know the truth."`It’s always liked graveyards, and it can afford to wait to make sure you won’t need it.""Now, it has nothing but time."0I BRING A WHOLE NEW MEANING TO DEATH METAL!"TNow that I think about it, what I'm doing down here is immensely disrespectful."&TAKE THE G OFF OF GRAVEYARD BABY!""BWAHHHHH BWAAAAHHHHH BWWOOOW!"Are you alright?"Which one are you?"What did you see?"Where's the other one?"..."I'm so sorry."	How?"Yeah, I'd guessed..."You have to remember."Better to know."Then don't remember."I'll prepare."Very well."Catch Imogene."Release Imogene forever.[}"...\PN."0Estoy aquí. Y tú también lo estás, veo."...No."+¿Acaso importa? ¿Alguna vez lo hizo?"&Algo que no debería haber visto."!Algo que nadie debería ver."cMás profundo. Luchando con la carga de la revelación que ella sabía que encontraría aquí."r¿Ya lo entiendes? ¿Puedes verlo a través de mis ojos – el reflejo de la carga de la que he sido testigo?"oPrimero viajé aquí sin saber por qué, o qué esperaba encontrar. Simplemente sabía que debía hacerlo."RY luego... luego me cayó como un adusto carroñero hacia un cádaver fresco."�¿No lo entiende? Caminé a través de estas lápidas, andando con un corazón que no dejaba de latir, buscando por el nombre que temía encontrar."El mío.":...No hay mucho que decirle a una mujer muerta, ¿No?".No lo estés. Es mejor conocer la verdad."...Imogene está muerta."`No sé si alguna vez lo hice. Incontables posibilidades me fastidiaron en horas sin sueño."D¿Era esta muy elegante para considerarla? ¿O demasiado cruel?"VImogene ha estado muerta por años. Murió mucho antes que mi memoria en el tren."ZElla era una ermitaña, una solitaria, una mística y una bruja, y ahora... no está."^Puedo sentir... memorias... reconstruyendose. Se filtran como la sangre en una fina gasa."/No puedo dejar que entren. ¡No tengo que!"@Si recuerdo quién soy... ya no seré yo. No seré Imogene."...Es agonizante."{El silencio, llenado con el ritmo de mi intenso corazón y los ecos de las cosas que pensé que dejé en un dichoso olvido." ¡No! ¿Acaso me matarías?"ISi recuerdo seré – ¡Seré destrozada! ¡Deshecha en un instante!"O eso creí."}¡Ja! Lo inocente que era, verdaderamente, jamás habiendo atestiguado algo tan horrible que hacen desear a uno olvidar."FLo estoy intentando. ¡Lo estoy intentando con todo lo que puedo!"9¡No quiero esta identidad! ¡No quiero este pasado!"Q¡Si atestiguo esta revelación me hará pedazos! Sé esto con toda certeza." Y... también lo hizo ella."No sé si ella ya se ha rendido, pero me otorgó un regalo antes de dejar mi presencia por lo que temo sea la última vez."Sus Pokémon."4Ella no me los confiaría si planeara regresar."-...Estoy preparada. Ya no puedo escapar."mLo quiera o no, la verdad aparece delante de mi. Me saludará con toda la furia que aún debo congregar.""Prepárate, si debes hacerlo."T¿Estás listo? No puedo hacer esto sola. Requiero un espejo al que contemplar."GDebo bailar, debo ritualizar esto, debo hacerlo algo comprensible."gNecesito tu apoyo, y sé que tu firme núcleo reside dentro de tus habilidades como un entrenador."lMás que eso, sé que es cómo juzgas a la gente. Te haría testigo de mi alma, y conocerás la verdad."[Haz lo que debas hacer. Puede que espere un poco más... manteniendo a raya el pasado."EPor última vez, tomo esta identidad en la que me he abscondido."Soy Imogene."Soy una oráculo."$Soy una buscadora de la verdad."K¡Muéstrame tu alma, nómada! ¡Deja que esta sea mi último combate!"...Que así sea."Lo recuerdo."f¡Recuerdo la casa, la vieja madera, el tictac del reloj del abuelo, el olor que emanaba el río!"{El aplastamiento de las hojas secas de otoño, el calor de un suave abrazo, los moretones, el sangrado, el ardor, la lucha!"R¡El amor por la lucha! ¡El anhelo de aprender, de convertirme en algo más!"fLa recuerdo. Recuerdo a Imogene enseñándonos, enseñándonos a todos... enseñándonos a ser..."Continúa."AEncuentra lo que le ha pasado a mi hermana en este tormento."NVoy... voy a liberar nuestros Pokémon, y luego cesaré esta larga farsa."Ya no estaré atrapada."?El nombre en esta lápida está borroso e irreconocible..."#Déjame. Debo hacer esto sola."Hay una nota."�“Los he liberado. Nuestros Pokémon marchan listos. Creo que ya lo saben. En cuanto a mi... lo recuerdo. Ella amaba a los dittos. Ella tenía docenas."`Los entrenó no sólo para los combates, pero para imitar humanos. Para imitarla... a ella."cLo encontré tan curioso, ver a Pokémon fingiendo ser personas. Que bonito. ¡Qué divertido!"zElla me mantuvo como si fuera otra masa rosa, y me enseñó más de lo que puedo expresar, mucho menos recompensarlo."�No soy ella, ni tampoco lo es mi compañera. No somos más que dos espejos mirándonos uno al otro, continuamente reflejando una mujer que ya no está."cNos apartamos más y más de nuestras imitaciones cada día. No podía durar. No nos lamentes."bEsta es la verdad, y provee sufrimiento y socorro en la misma cantidad, como siempre lo hace."=Fuimos liberadas de nuestros lazos. Ya no somos Imogene."<Ahora somos Imogene, hermanas de nombre, y eso es todo."Gracias."Adiós."xPD: He hecho cosas que no debería, en búsqueda de esta verdad. He intentado lastimarte, a otros, al mundo entero."zNo sé si fue mi propia necesidad egoísta de saber lo que en mi interior más profundo ya ví más tuve que negar --"9o si, quizás, Imogene no fue la santa que recuerdo."GEn cualquier caso, tomaré la responsabilidad por lo que he hecho."�No puedo enfrentarte, y con gusto te acompañaré en tus pruebas venideras. No para ayudar el flujo del destino, pero porque tú eres mi amigo."6Porque es lo correcto, y porque es lo que quiero."_No puedo pedirte más que una oportunidad de enmendar ambos lados con alguien como tú.”"<PD: Con gusto te daré mi ayuda, no importa quién sea."IPide por mi ayuda, y estaré allí. Aún tengo mucha fuerza que dar."jNo hago esto para ti, quien es el importe del flujo del destino, pero para ti, mi amigo y confidente."JLlévame contigo si deseas mi compañía, o si necesitas de mi poder."EEs lo menos que puedo hacer... y lo mejor que puedo imaginar.”"...Un Mew."HEl Pokémon infinitamente-mutable de mitos, aquí en carne y hueso."5Canta con felicidad, nadando a través del aire."�Aún así, de algún modo, hay un matiz macabro en sus movimiento, un pequeño toque de humor negro en la forma en que se mueve por las lápidas."KHay un destello de simpatía en sus ojos cuando contempla a los tuyos.";Sabe lo que es, y sabe lo que eres, y sabes lo que es."_Se detiene y se enrosca, flotando por un momento para contemplarte con sus ojos vibrantes."'Notas el conflicto en tus ojos –"�el deseo de explorar sin límites, el recordado entusiasmo para combatir, el afán por pagar su deuda, el deseo de acompañarte."Deja la decisión en ti."#Te guiña el ojo al atraparla."jA veces desaparecerá, deambulando en elegantes vuelos a través de tanto paisajes como pensamientos."LA veces en la hora de las brujas los objetos se moverán por su cuenta."rA veces te encuentras notas escritas en una letra que no puedes leer, firmada con un signo de interrogación."=Sabes que puede irse cuando sea que quiera. No lo hará."8Da un giro al revés, luego se endereza en el aire."kQuizás como burla, quizás asiente, quizás un quieto movimiento de un animal recientemente-liberado."Luego, se va."WUn milagro que desaparece con una fuerte brisa, disperso como un sueño caminante."xSi regresas, quizás estará aquí, esperando por ti. Dicen que este lugar está embrujado, pero conoces la verdad."mSiempre le han gustado los cementerios, y puede permitirse esperar hasta asegurarse que no la necesitas."*Ahora, no tiene nada más que tiempo."2¡TRAIGO UN NUEVO SIGNIFICADO AL DEATH METAL!"MAhora que lo pienso, lo que estoy haciendo es inmensamente irrespetuoso."2¡ME CEMENTO COMO LA SIGUIENTE ESTRELLA BABY!"$¡BWAHHHHH BWAAAAHHHHH BWWOOOW!"¿Estás bien?"¿Cuál eres tú?"¿Qué viste?"¿Dónde está la otra?"..."Lo siento tanto."¿Cómo?"!Seh, lo habría adivinado..."Tienes que recordarlo."Mejor saberlo."Entonces no lo recuerdes."Me prepararé."Muy bien."Atrapar Imogene."$Liberar a Imogene para siempre.;[}"...\PN.",I’m here. And you are as well, I see."...No."!Does it matter? Did it ever?"!Something I should not have."&Something that no one should see."ZDeeper in. Struggling with the burden of the revelation she knew she would find here."mDo you understand yet? Can you see it within my eyes – the reflection of what I have borne witness to?"^At first I journeyed here not knowing why, or what I hoped to find. I simply knew I must."SAnd then... then it fell upon me like some grim scavenger upon a fresh corpse."�Don’t you understand? I walked these graves, pacing with an ever-quickening heart, hunting for the one name I dreaded to find."
Mine."?...There is nothing much to say to a dead woman, is there?"1Don’t be. It’s better to know the truth."...Imogene is dead."XI do not know if I ever did. Countless possibilities plagued me in sleepless hours."8Was this one too elegant to consider? Or too cruel?"RImogene has been dead for years. She died well before my memory on the train."KShe was a hermit and a recluse, a mystic and a witch, and now... gone."_I can feel... memories... bubbling up. They’re seeping in like blood through thin gauze."(I can’t let them in. I mustn’t!"MIf I remember who I am... I won’t be me anymore. I won’t be Imogene."...It is agonizing."{The silence, filled with the beat of my raging heart and the echoes of things I had thought left to blissful oblivion."No! You would kill me?"HIf I remember I will be – I will be undone! Unmade in an instant!"So I believed."pHah! How innocent I was, truly, never having witnessed something so horrible as to make one wish to forget."1I’m trying. I am trying with all my might!":I do not want this identity! I do not want this past!"XIf I witness this revelation it will shatter me! I know this with utmost certainty."And... so did she."�I do not know if she has already given in, but she bestowed upon me a gift before she left my presence for what I fear is the last time."Her Pokémon."?She would not entrust them to me if she planned to return."+...I am prepared. I can run no longer."eWilling or no, the truth descends upon me. I will greet it with all the fury I might yet muster.")Make your preparations, if you must."LAre you ready? I cannot do this alone. I require a mirror to gaze into."PI must dance, must ritualize this, must make into something comprehensible."bI need your support, and I know your adamant core resides within your abilities as a trainer."mMore than that, I know it is how you judge people. I would have you witness my soul, and know the truth."SDo what you must. I may wait a few moments longer... may keep the past at bay."FFor the last time, I take up this identity I have absconded with."I am Imogene."I am an oracle."I am a seeker of truth."@Bare your soul to me, wanderer! Let this be my last battle!"...So be it."I remember."oI remember the house, the old hardwood, the ticking of the grandfather clock, the smell of the river loam!"{The crushing of the drying autumn leaves, the warmth of a soft embrace, the bruising, the bleeding, the burning, the fight!"LThe love of the fight! The yearning to learn, to become something more!"_I remember her. I remember Imogene teaching us, teaching all of us... teaching us to be..."Go on ahead."9Find what has happened to my sister in this torment."RI... I will release our Pokémon, and then I will cease this long masquerade."!I will be trapped no longer."?The name on this gravestone is faded beyond recognition..."$Leave me. I must do this alone."There’s a note."�“I’ve released them. Our Pokémon go readily. I think they know. As for me... I remember. She loved Dittos. She kept dozens."SShe trained them not only in battle, but to imitate humans. To imitate... her."YI found it so curious, to see Pokémon pretending to be people. How lovely. How fun!"sShe took me in as if I was just another pink blob, and she taught me more than I can express, let alone repay."{I am not her, nor is my companion. We are but two mirrors set facing each other, endlessly reflecting a woman that is gone."hWe strayed further and further in our imitations every day. It could not last. Do not mourn for us."aThis is the truth, and it provides suffering and succor in equal measure, as it always does.">We are released from our bonds. We are Imogene no longer."<Now we are Imogene, sisters of a name, and that is all."Thank you."Goodbye."�P.S.: I have done things I should not have, in pursuit of this truth. I have endeavored to cause harm to you, to others, to the world entire."qI do not know if this was my own selfish need to know what in my heart of hearts I already saw yet denied --"Aor if, perhaps, Imogene was not the saint I remember her as."EIn either case, I will take responsibility for what I have done."�I cannot stand against you, and will gladly aid you in your coming trials. Not to aid the flow of fate, but because you are my friend."HBecause it is the right thing to do, and because it is what I want."bI cannot ask for more than a chance to make amends side by side with one such as yourself.”"@P.S.: I will gladly lend my aid to you, no matter who I am."TAsk for my assistance, and I will be there. I have plenty strength yet to give."jI do this not for you, who is of import to the flow of destiny, but for you, my friend and confidant."KBring me with you if you desire my company, or have need of my powers."?It is the least I can do... and the best I can imagine.”"...A Mew."@The infinitely-mutable Pokémon of myth, here in the flesh."3It chitters happily, swimming through the air."�Yet, somehow, there’s a macabre tinge to its movements, a slight touch of gallows humor to the way it darts around gravestones."HThere is a flash of sympathy in its eyes when it stares into yours."MIt knows what it is, and it knows what you are, and you know what it is."SIt stops and coils, floating for a moment to regard you with its vibrant eyes.")You see the conflict in its eyes –"�the desire to explore free and wide, the remembered thrill of the fight, the eagerness to repay its debt, the desire to accompany you."!It leaves the choice to you."%It winks at you as you catch it."lSometimes it will go missing, wandering on flights of fancy through landscapes and thoughtscapes alike."CSometimes in the witching hour objects will move on their own."cSometimes you find notes written in handwriting you can’t read, signed with a question mark."9You know it can leave any time it likes. It won’t."9It flips upside down, then rights itself in mid-air."\Perhaps mockery, perhaps a nod, perhaps just an idle motion of a recently-freed animal."Then, it’s gone."RA mirage that disappears with a strong breeze, dispelled like a waking dream."}If you come back, perhaps it will be here, waiting for you. They’ll say this place is haunted, but you know the truth."`It’s always liked graveyards, and it can afford to wait to make sure you won’t need it.""Now, it has nothing but time."0I BRING A WHOLE NEW MEANING TO DEATH METAL!"TNow that I think about it, what I'm doing down here is immensely disrespectful."&TAKE THE G OFF OF GRAVEYARD BABY!""BWAHHHHH BWAAAAHHHHH BWWOOOW!"Are you alright?"Which one are you?"What did you see?"Where's the other one?"..."I'm so sorry."	How?"Yeah, I'd guessed..."You have to remember."Better to know."Then don't remember."I'll prepare."Very well."Catch Imogene."Release Imogene forever.Iu;␀�0[[^"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."1A Totem calls. I’ve seen more than enough."}They got away. They won. A few that were dressed up like ancient Makyan priests, and whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."4Remember what I said about the big open secret?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them."~They’ve got at least one Regi, probably more, so there’s a strong temptation to wreak havoc. Trust me – I’d know."JHate to say it, but you just need to keep being your usual self, kid."JOr, no, I shouldn’t call you kid. Take this – you’ve earned it."AUsed to give these to Chasm strike teams, for cave scouting."UIt’ll get you just about anywhere in the region – nobody hides from you now."3So go get those badges and save the day, hero."Who are you?"Why are you doing this?"Shut up, edgelord."Who are they?"What do they want?"Why Yezera?"Not my problem."You wanted power?"You wanted money?"You wanted knowledge?"Why should I care?"Then why is Yezera..."How many Regis are stolen?"They're opening that door."Your point?[^"FMe temo que Yezera y los otros se fueron. Solo somos tú… y yo."9Ganamos. No hay razón para que siga aquí. Ninguna."KAdemás del inmenso disfrute que extraeré al desmantelar a tu equipo."IUn amigo de Yezera. Aparte de eso, estoy enmascarado por una razón."aPreguntaría quién eres, pero siendo franco realmente no importa. Voy a descubrirlo pronto.":Sólo hay unos cuantos tipos de personas en el mundo."=Te lo acabo de decir: porque humillarte será divertido."VA no ser que te refieras a extraer a Regidrago, en cuyo caso, no, no te lo diré."kLos humanos tienen esta infuriante autodestructiva necesidad de contar secretos. Yo soy mejor que eso."3Bueno, veo que el diálogo no duró demasiado."Bien. Sufre."%Pero no vine aquí para charlar."rTe lo aseguro, no es nada personal – nadie ha tenido nada interesante que decir. Tú no eres la excepción."[Pero tu eres especialmente habilidoso, lo entiendo, y eso está correlacionado al ego.".Déjame mostrarte lo que realmente vales."p…Ah, que así sea. Dudo que pudiera infundir algo de humildad a tráves de tu dura cabeza de todos modos."CEres bueno jugando a los juegos superficiales – bien por ti."6Un Tótem llama. Ya he visto más que suficiente."oSe escaparon. Ganaron. Algunos que estaban enmascarados, incluyendo quién demonios fuera ESE. Y Yezera..."_Ojalá supiera. Ese tipo era un narcisista y un idiota, eso es todo lo que te puedo decir."&El resto de ellos… quién sabe." Podría ser cualquier cosa."wPero si estaban buscando específicamente a Regidrago, y Yezera estaba con ellos… quizá incluso liderandolos…",…No lo sé. No tiene ningún sentido."IElla debería ser la última persona que llevaría a cabo algo así."PLo es. Ahora es tu problema, y sé que no te va a gustar eso, pero así es.":Esto es más grande que sólo un Pokémon legendario."8¿Recuerdas lo que dije de un gran secreto abierto?"~Las cuevas alrededor de Makya son tumbas para los Regis. Las extrañas de las que estaba hablando antes. Unas como estas."]Bueno, unos cuantos equipos arqueológicos fueron a estudiarlos hace un par de décadas."~E incluso encontraron a los Regis, unas ricas vetas de minerales, y las ruinas, y entendieron que podían aprovechar todo eso."�Conseguimos un poco de soporte corporativo de parte de Andris y Mavis, y boom: Team Chasm. Yo era uno de esos arqueologos originales."�…Algunos de nosotros. Helena quería estar al mando de su propia región. Andris quería una parte de todo ese crimen organizado."OY yo, estudiar a los Regis. Y algunas personas querían dejarme bien sola."mTenía un equipo con Regidrago a mi lado, y ellos no, así que podía estudiar lo que malditas quisiera."VAlgunos de nosotros. Yo no. Tenía cinco Regis – ¿Para qué necesitaba dinero?"MSi quería equipamiento de laboratorio, le mandaría una lista a Helena."\Vivía en una estación de investigación y comía ramen. Los mejores días de mi vida."qSólo quería estudiar a los Regis, y con su poder, nadie podía decirme que no. Gracioso como eso funciona."%Lo haces sonar tan puro y noble."vTenía curiosidad. Quería respuestas. Las obtuve – ¿Quién podría decirme que no con un Regidrago a mi lado?"\Por no mencionar el poderío del Team Chasm, porque mi investigación era MUY rentable."VEstaba llegando a eso, pero también, hey, podrías ser útil algún día, ¿Sí?"AComo estaba diciendo: encontramos a los cinco Regis menores."XMe tomó años, pero decifré sus inscripciones y entendí su verdadera naturaleza."eEso nos llevó a Regigigas, y a ese punto estabamos abarcando más de lo que podíamos sostener."[Gigas era más poderoso que el resto de los Regis juntos, y también más inteligente."{Moldear la tierra, revertirla a un tipo de arcilla primigenia. Crear sellos y guardias a los que nada podría atravesarlos."2Y, claro, podía usar un potente Gigaimpacto."jTambién podía hacer… otras cosas. Encontramos una manera de crear Pokémon etéreos con su poder."=Eran hostiles, poderosos – tenían que ser encerrados."�Y para el momento en el que Yezera pateó nuestra puerta y nos dijo que paremos, estaba básicamente confirmando lo que ya sabíamos."sEstabamos jugando con fuego. Si seguíamos usando a Regigigas, corríamos el real riesgo de destruir el mundo."qO al menos permanentemente cambiarlo. Así que pusimos a cada Regi de vuelta a su tumba y fuimos legítimos."kLas tumbas fueron reforzadas, por supuesto – nada puede atravesar las cámaras de los Regis menores."RLa cámara de Gigas sólo puede ser abierta por los otros cinco Regis juntos."\No lo sé. Ella estaba de acuerdo: era muy peligroso. Éramos criminales, no lunaticos."KSé que las cosas… no han ido bien con ella, ¿Pero esto? Es insano."iQuién sabe. Sabíamos que lagunos grupos estaban intentando recuperarlos – siempre lo han estado."U¿Pero lograrlo? No había forma. Imposible. Pero… aparentemente Yezera puede."3…Probablemente. Puede que ya lo hayan hecho."dPero la cámara de Gigas está en lo profundo, y si no han roto el sello aún, sería por nada."[O si la han vuelto a sellar. Puedo intentar ir y comprobarlo, pero… no prometo nada."VMi PUNTO es que si no ayudas, mejor que te acostumbres a ver sólo piedra blanca.">Vas a ver mucho de eso si alguien deja libre a Regigigas."4Escucha, no lo sé. No sé un montón de cosas."�Así que déjame hablar con Andris, nuestros rangers, Helena, a quién sea que pueda encontrar. Ya veremos qué mal están las cosas."XY si esos ladrones muestran sus caras arriba del suelo, puedes enfrentarte a ellos."�Tienen por lo menos un Regi, probablemente más, así que hay una fuerte tentación para sembrar el caso. Creeme – lo sabría."HOdio decir esto, pero tienes que continuar siendo tú mismo, chico."DO, no, no debería llamarte chico. Toma esto – te lo ganaste."USolíamos darle estos a los equipos de asalto Chasm, para investigar las cuevas."UPodrás llegar a cualquier parte de la región – nadie se esconde de ti ahora."=Así que consigue esas medallas y salva el día, héroe."¿Quién eres?"¿Por qué haces esto?"Cállate, edgelord."¿Quién era?"¿Qué es lo que quieren?"¿Por qué Yezera?"No es mi problema."¿Querías poder?"¿Querías dinero?"¿Querías conocimiento?"$¿Por qué debería importarme?" Entonces por qué Yezera…"'¿Cuántos Regis han sido robados?" Están abriendo esa puerta."¿Tu punto?;[^"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."1A Totem calls. I’ve seen more than enough."}They got away. They won. A few that were dressed up like ancient Makyan priests, and whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."4Remember what I said about the big open secret?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them.