Wushu"Rogue Monkey"Wild Horse"Swift Horse"	King"	Test"Test 2"High King"MellowIu;␀J<[[_"gWhile it is young, it uses the nutrients that are stored in the seed on its back in order to grow."�To support its weight, Ivysaur's legs and trunk grow thick and strong. If it spends more time lying in the sunlight, it's a sign that the bud will bloom soon."_Its plant blooms when it is absorbing solar energy. It stays on the move to seek sunlight."tFrom the time it is born, a flame burns at the tip of its tail. Its life would end if the flame were to go out."_In the rocky mountains where Charmeleon live, their fiery tails shine at night like stars."fIf Charizard becomes furious, the flame at the tip of its tail flares up in a whitish-blue color."�Its shell is not just for protection. Its rounded shape and the grooves on its surface minimize resistance in water, enabling Squirtle to swim at high speeds."�Its large tail is covered with rich, thick fur that deepens in color with age. The scratches on its shell are evidence of this Pokémon's toughness in battle."dThe jets of water it spouts from the rocket cannons on its shell can punch through thick steel."�Its voracious appetite compels it to devour leaves bigger than itself without hesitation. It releases a terribly strong odor from its antennae."hA steel-hard shell protects its tender body. It quietly endures hardships while awaiting evolution."dWater-repellent powder on its wings enables it to collect honey, even in the heaviest of rains."}Evolutionary power has supercharged its wings and their toxic scales, which turn to pure energy at the slightest provocation."fPredators not warned off by its brightly-colored body are jabbed with the toxic barb on its head."�It remains virtually immobile while it clings to a tree. However, on the inside, it busily prepares for evolution. This is evident from how hot its shell becomes."rIt prefers hit-and-run attacks using its powerful poison stingers, trying to evade blows to its fragile body."�Its final evolution has sent its killer instinct into overdrive. It obeys its trainer unfailingly, but will grow impatient without a good fight."�It has an extremely sharp sense of direction. It can unerringly return home to its nest, however far it may be removed from its familiar surroundings."�This Pokémon flies around, patrolling its large territory. If its living space is violated, it shows no mercy in thoroughly punishing the foe with its sharp claws."dIt spreads its gorgeous wings wide to intimidate enemies. It races through the skies at Mach 2."YCautious in the extreme, its hardy vitality lets it live in any kind of environment."iWith its long fangs, this surprisingly violent Pokémon can gnaw away even thick concrete with ease."{It shows no interest in anything that isn't fresh. If you take it shopping with you, it will help you pick out ingredients."qIt makes its Rattata underlings gather food for it, dining solely on the most nutritious and delicious fare."vFarmers whose fields are troubled by bug Pokémon appreciate Spearow for its vigorous appetite and look after it."�Its long neck and elongated beak are ideal for catching prey in soil or water. It deftly moves this extended and skinny beak to pluck prey."�Ekans curls itself up in a spiral while it rests. Assuming this position allows it to quickly respond to a threat from any direction with a glare."jTransfixing prey with the face-like pattern on its belly, it binds and poisons the frightened victim."`It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled."fThis intelligent Pokémon roasts hard berries with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."�If it stores too much electricity, its behavior turns aggressive. To avoid this, it occasionally discharges excess energy and calms itself down."�Rarely, a Pikachu grows to incredible size instead of evolving into Raichu. It can power settlements so long as it's fed properly."dIt can loose 100,000-volt bursts of electricity, instantly downing foes several times its size."�It loves to bathe in the grit of dry, sandy areas. By sand bathing, this Pokémon rids itself of dirt and moisture clinging to its body."xIts claws and horns often break off. The broken claws and horns can be used to carve plows for tilling farm fields."nLife on mountains covered with deep snow has granted this Pokémon a body of ice that's as hard as steel."�It lives in snowy mountains on southern islands. When a blizzard rolls in, this Pokémon hunkers down in the snow to avoid getting blown away."�Its highly toxic barbs are thought to have developed as protection for this small-bodied Pokémon. When enraged, it releases a horrible toxin from its horn."�When Nidorina are with friends or family, they keep their barbs tucked away to prevent hurting each other. It becomes nervous if separated from the others."�It pacifies offspring by placing them in the gaps between the spines on its back. The spines will never secrete poison while young are present."wIts large ears are flapped like wings when it is listening to distant sounds. It extends toxic barbs when angered."�It's nervous and quick to act aggressively. The potency of its poison increases along with the level of adrenaline present in its body."�When it goes on a rampage, it's impossible to control. But in the presence of a Nidoqueen it's lived with for a long time, Nidoking calms down."bMany appear when the night skies are filled with shooting stars. They disappear with sunrise."�On every night of a full moon they come out to play. When dawn arrives, they return to their quiet mountain retreats and sleep nestled up against each other."�A Clefable uses its wings to skip lightly as if it were flying. Its bouncy step lets it even walk on water. On quiet, moonlit nights, it strolls on lakes."�From its mouth spew flames that seem to resemble the spirits of the deceased. Some people mistakenly think this fire is a ghost."^Legend has it that this mystical Pokémon was formed when nine saints coalesced into one."qIn hot weather, this Pokémon makes ice shards with its six tails and sprays them around to cool itself off."|It lives on mountains perpetually covered in snow and is revered as a deity incarnate. It appears draped in a blizzard."|It constantly demands treats and gifts from its Trainer. An expensive and fashionable hoard is necessary for evolution."�The gifts it received have become a tail of golden light. It weaponizes pure avaricious energy in battle, gaining in power as it is pampered."fIt has a very soft body. If it starts to roll, it will bounce all over and be impossible to stop."{By freely changing the wavelength of its voice, Jigglypuff sings a mysterious melody sure to make any listener sleepy."�The surfaces of its saucerlike eyes are always covered with a thin layer of tears. If any dust gets in this Pokémon's eyes, it is quickly washed away."�Their skin is so thin that they'll be burned if sunlight hits them. When it gets cold out, they gather together to warm one another's bodies."}Its thick fangs are hollow like straws, making them unexpectedly fragile. These fangs are specialized for sucking blood."�Both of its legs have turned into wings. Without a sound, Crobat flies swiftly toward its prey and sinks its fangs into the nape of its target's neck."eIf exposed to moonlight, it starts to move. It roams far and wide at night to scatter its seeds."�A horribly noxious honey drools from its mouth. One whiff of the honey can result in memory loss. Some fans are said to enjoy this overwhelming stink, however."cThe bud bursts into bloom with a bang. It then starts scattering allergenic, poisonous pollen."`When the heavy rainfall season ends, it is drawn out by warm sunlight to dance in the open."pNo matter how much it eats, the mushrooms growing on its back steal away most of the nutrients it consumes."_The large mushroom on its back controls it. It often fights over territory with Shiinotic."[Its big eyes are actually clusters of tiny eyes. At night, its kind is drawn by light."vThe powdery scales on its wings are hard to remove from skin. They also contain poison that leaks out on contact."~Around their crops, farmers plant trees that Diglett like to eat as a way of getting Diglett to plow the fields for them."nDugtrio's heads are sleek and smooth and incredibly hard. It can dig through any soil with its headbutts."�Its head sports an altered form of whiskers made of metal. When in communication with its comrades, its whiskers wobble to and fro."~Its shining gold hair provides it with protection. It's reputed that keeping any of its fallen hairs will bring bad luck."�It loves coins, so if you give it one, you can make friends with Meowth easily. But it's fickle, so you can't count on that friendship lasting."kBehind its lithe, elegant appearance lies a barbaric side. It will tear apart its prey on a mere whim."�Scientists are divided as to whether its incredible length inspired internet memes, or whether seeing memes caused a Meowth to undergo unprecedented evolution."yIt's impulsive, selfish, and fickle. It's very popular with some Trainers who like giving it the attention it needs."qIts round face is a symbol of wealth. Persian that have bigger, plumper faces are considered more beautiful."�These daring Pokémon have coins on their foreheads. Darker coins are harder, and harder coins garner more respect among Meowth."eAfter many battles, it evolved dangerous claws that come together to form daggers when extended."iIf its chronic headache peaks, it may exhibit odd powers. It seems unable to recall such an episode."gIt appears by waterways at dusk. It may use telekinetic powers if its forehead glows mysteriously."�It can spontaneously become enraged. Everyone near it clears out as it rampages and the resulting loneliness makes it angrier still."nIt has been known to become so angry that it dies as a result. Its face looks peaceful in death, however."~When its anger rose beyond a critical point, this Pokémon gained power that is unfettered by the limits of its physical body."`It has a brave and trustworthy nature. It fearlessly stands up to bigger and stronger foes."�Legends tell of it fighting alongside a general and conquering a whole country. Those hearing its bark feel compelled to grovel before it."hIts magnificent bark conveys a sense of majesty. Anyone hearing it can't help but grovel before it."|In rivers with fast-flowing water, this Pokémon will cling to a rock by using its thick lips, which act like a suction cup."uThis Pokémon's sweat is a slimy mucus. When captured, Poliwhirl can slither from its enemies' grasp and escape."�Its percentage of body fat is nearly zero. Its body is entirely muscle, which makes it heavy and forces its swimming prowess to develop."`If Poliwag and Poliwhirl hear its echoing cry, they respond by gathering from far and wide."It can read others' minds and will teleport away when danger approaches. You must clear your mind if you want to catch it."yIt stares at a silver spoon to amplify its psychic powers before it lets loose. Apparently, gold spoons are no good."�Alakazam's brain continually grows, making its head far too heavy to support with its neck. This Pokémon holds its head up using its psychokinetic power instead."�Machop exercises by hefting around a Graveler as if it were a barbell. There are some Machop that travel the world in a quest to master all kinds of martial arts."�Machoke works out every day even as it helps with tough labor. On its days off, this Pokémon heads to the fields and mountains to exercise and train."�It can lift heavy loads with the greatest of ease. It can even heft dump trucks. But its clumsy fingers prevent it from doing any precision work."�Bellsprout's thin and flexible body lets it bend and sway to avoid any attack. From its mouth, this Pokémon spits a corrosive fluid that melts even iron."mIf its prey is bigger than its mouth, it slices up the victim with sharp leaves, then eats every morsel."�It attracts prey with aromatic honey, then melts them in its mouth. Acid that has dissolved many prey becomes sweeter, making it even more alluring."zTentacool is not a particularly strong swimmer. It drifts across the surface of shallow seas as it searches for prey."�It communicates with others of its kind by lighting up the red orbs on its head. When the orbs are blinking, it's a warning sign."�The longer it lives, the more its edges are chipped and worn away. However, this Pokémon's heart will remain hard, craggy, and rough always."�This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom."When Golem grow old, they stop shedding their shells. Those that have lived a long, long time have shells green with moss."�Geodude compete against each other with headbutts. The iron sand on their heads will stick to whichever one has stronger magnetism."�They eat rocks and often get into a scrap over them. The shock of Graveler smashing together causes a flash of light and a booming noise."�It fires rocks charged with electricity. Even if the rock isn't fired that accurately, just grazing an opponent will cause numbness and fainting."eAbout an hour after birth, its fiery mane and tail grow out, giving it an impressive appearance."cVery competitive, this Pokémon will chase anything that moves fast in the hopes of racing it."{This Pokémon will look into your eyes and read the contents of your heart. If it finds evil there, it promptly hides away."�Brave and prideful, this Pokémon dashes airily through the forest, its steps aided by the psychic power stored in the fur on its fetlocks."�Slowpoke uses its tail to catch prey by dipping it in rivers. However, it often forgets what it's doing and spends entire days just loafing at water's edge."�A metamorphosed Shellder has latched onto Slowbro's tail. The tail can't be used for fishing anymore, forcing Slowbro to grudgingly swim and catch prey instead."bWhen its head was bitten, toxins entered Slowpoke's head and unlocked an extraordinary power."|Because Galarian Slowpoke eat the seeds of a plant that grows only in Galar, their tails have developed a spicy flavor."�If this Pokémon squeezes the tongue of the Shellder biting it, the Shellder will launch a toxic liquid from the tip of its shell."cSlowking can solve any problem present to it, but no one can understand a thing Slowking says."{It's frequently the cause of power outages, which is why some power plants send out electrical signals that it can't stand."`When rain clouds form, many Magneton gather in high places to wait for lightning to strike."ZIt evolved from exposure to a special magnetic field. Three units generate magnetism."�The stalk this Pokémon carries in its wings serves as a sword to cut down opponents. In a dire situation, the stalk can also serve as food."~The stalks of leeks are thicker and longer in the Galar region. Farfetch'd that adapted to these stalks took on a unique form."�After deflecting attacks with its hard leaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp leek stalk. The leek stalk is both weapon and food."kBy alternately raising and lowering its two heads, it balances itself to be more stable while running."uIt collects data and plans three times as wisely, but it may think too much and fall into a state of immobility."�Seel hunts in the frigid sea underneath sheets of ice. When it needs to breathe, it breaks through the ice with the sharply protruding section of its head."aIt sunbathes on the beach after meals. The rise in its body temperature helps its digestion."�Its main source of food is the slimy industrial waste of factories. This Pokémon's numbers have been decreasing in recent years."�Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction."mA Grimer, which had been brought in to solve a problem with garbage, developed over time into this form."xThe garbage it eats causes continuous chemical changes in its body, which produce its exceedingly vivid coloration."�This Pokémon's tongue is always hanging out. It uses its tongue with great dexterity to dig up sand from the seabed in its search for food."Cloyster swims by swallowing water, then jetting it out toward the rear. It shoots spikes from its shell using the same system."�When exposed to a strong wind, a Gastly's gaseous body quickly dwindles away. They cluster under the eaves of houses to escape the ravages of wind."jOn moonless nights, Haunter searches for someone to curse, so it's best not to go out walking around."Should you feel yourself attacked by a sudden chill, it is evidence of an approaching Gengar. There is no escaping it. Give up."~Onix has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling."jIt chews its way through boulders with its sturdy jaws. Its eyes can see in the darkness underground."�Its crystalline parts resist all attempts to identify them. Titanix's gravitational abilities make some scientists speculate the crystals are neutron matter."wA Pokémon that nourishes itself by eating dreams, it is thought to share common ancestry with Munna and Musharna."uWhile it is an extremely dangerous Pokémon, people who are in need of a good, sound sleep call it their savior."jIf it senses danger approaching, it cloaks itself with bubbles from its mouth so it will look bigger."�Kingler has an enormous, oversized claw, which it waves in the air to communicate with others. However, because the claw is so heavy, it quickly tires."Its claw has become so large that if it finds itself unable to clamp its opponent, it will just smack them with the blunt side."jIt rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode."�They appear in great numbers at electric power plants. Because they feed on electricity, they cause massive and chaotic blackouts in nearby cities."zWhen excited, it discharges the electric current it has stored in its belly, then lets out a great, uproarious laugh."^The tissue on the surface of its body is curiously similar in composition to an Apricorn."�These Pokémon get nervous when they're not in a group of six. The minute even one member of the group goes missing, Exeggcute become cowardly."}Each of its three heads has its own thoughts. When they want to go in different directions, Exeggutor becomes unable to move."�As it grew taller and taller, it outgrew its reliance on psychic powers, while within it awakened the power of the sleeping dragon."�This Pokémon wears the skull of its deceased mother. Sometimes Cubone's dreams make it cry, but each tear Cubone sheds makes it stronger."}This Pokémon overcame its sorrow to evolve a sturdy new body. Marowak faces its opponents bravely, using a bone as a weapon."wIts custom is to mourn its lost companions. Mounds of dirt by the side of the road mark the graves of the Marowak."kTo brush up on its fighting skills, it will challenge anyone. It has a very strong competitive spirit."WIts legs can stretch double. First-time foes are startled by its extensible reach."mIts punches slice the air. They are launched at such high speed, even a slight graze could cause a burn."tIf you are enchanted by its smooth, dance-like kicks, you may get a closer experience with one than you'd like."�It licks filth clean with its tongue. Whatever it licks always stinks afterward, so whether it's really clean is... questionable."Their saliva contains lots of components that can dissolve anything. The numbness caused by their lick does not dissipate."�Getting up close to a Koffing will give you a chance to observe, through its thin skin, the toxic gasses swirling inside. It blows up at the slightest stimulation."fTop-grade perfume is made using its internal poison gasses by diluting them to the highest level."Long ago, during a time when droves of factories fouled the air with pollution, Weezing changed into this form for some reason."�It is so dense, while on a run it forgets why it started running in the first place. It apparently remembers sometimes if it demolishes something."�Rhydon has a horn that serves as a drill. This Pokémon occasionally rams into streams of magma, but the armor-like hide prevents it from feeling the heat."lIt puts rocks in holes in its palms and uses its muscles to shoot them. Geodude are shot at rare times."rIt carefully carries a round, white rock that it thinks is an egg. It's bothered by how curly its hair looks."hIt walks carefully to prevent its egg from breaking. However, it is extremely fast at running away."]This kindhearted Pokémon nurses sick Pokémon to health. It senses feelings of sadness."�Its vines snap off easily and painlessly if they are grabbed, allowing it to make a quick getaway. The lost vines are replaced by new growth the very next day."WIts vines grow so profusely that, in the warm season, you can't even see its eyes."�Though it looks like a plant, its green color comes from its jade scales. Looking into its eyes is said to bring three years of bad luck."�While the snakes covering it are hard as granite, its skin is soft. Predators attacking its unprotected limbs have to contend with its powerful digging claws."�Although it's carrying its baby in a pouch on its belly, Kangaskhan is swift on its feet. It intimidates its opponents with quick jabs."|Mother and daughter fight alongside each other, delivering blows in quick succession. Their battle bond is unbreakable."�They swim with dance-like motions and cause whirlpools to form. Horsea compete to see which of them can generate the biggest whirlpool."�It's the males that raise the offspring. While Seadra are raising young, the spines on their backs secrete thicker and stronger poison."`It stores energy by sleeping at underwater depths at which no other life-forms can survive."�Although known for their splendid tail fins, Goldeen apparently compete among themselves to see whose horn is thickest and sharpest."Trainers who are crazy for Seaking are divided into horn enthusiasts and fin enthusiasts. The two groups do not get along well."kThey obsessively count the pebbles in their rivers, becoming irate if the result is an unlucky number."�Fearsome Pokémon lining a river in a grand procession is a sign of a Makyan Seaking. They offer endless blessings in exchange for servitude."�This Pokémon gets nibbled on by Lumineon and others. Thanks to its red core, it regenerates fast, so it's unconcerned by their snack attacks."�This Pokémon has an organ known as its core. The organ glows in seven colors when Starmie is unleashing its potent psychic powers."^It habitually mimics foes. Once mimicked, the foe cannot take its eyes off this Pokémon."hEmanations from its fingertips solidify the air into invisible walls that repel even harsh attacks."uIt can radiate chilliness from the bottoms of its feet. It'll spend the whole day tap-dancing on a frozen floor."mIts amusing movements make it very popular. It releases its psychic power from the pattern on its belly."�While young, they live together deep in the mountains, training themselves in how to fight with their scythes and move at high speeds."ZIt has a steel-hard body. It intimidates foes by upraising its eye-patterned pincers."�Only exceptionally aggressive or well-trained Pokémon will willingly engage one in combat. Its ripping pincers threaten to turn foes to shrapnel."iA violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone."�If its face gets even slightly dirty, Smoochum will bathe immediately. But if its body gets dirty, Smoochum doesn't really seem to care."cIts cries sound like human speech. However, it is impossible to tell what it is trying to say."�It's not good at storing electricity yet. This Pokémon sneaks into people's homes, looking for electrical outlets to eat electricity from."�While it's often blamed for power outages, the truth is the cause of outages is more often an error on the part of the electric company."�In terms of electrical-energy output, Electivire is one of the best among all Electric Pokémon. It discharges high-voltage currents from its tails."�This Pokémon makes its home near volcanoes. At the end of the day, Magby soaks in magma, resting and recovering from the day's fatigue."_When it breathes deeply, heat mirages form around its body, making it hard to see clearly."�When Magmortar inhales deeply, the fire burning in its belly intensifies, rising in temperature to over 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit."nAlthough it's tough, it can't handle cold well. When night falls, it buries itself in leafage and sleeps."�When the buzz of its wings becomes a roar, it's about to bolt at full speed. It isn't uncommon for its charges to send opponents through buildings."fWith its Herculean powers, it can easily throw around an object that is 100 times its own weight."They can be seen watching the sky, trying to find a place to stand for when they inevitably attempt to deadlift the world."}When Tauros begins whipping itself with its tails, it's a warning that the Pokémon is about to charge with astounding speed."�Miltank's milk has been sought after due to its taste and nutrition. The local treat of Castelia City, Casteliacones, is made from fresh Moomoo Milk."�Its swimming muscles are weak, so it is easily washed away by currents. In places where water pools, you can see many Magikarp deposited there by the flow."gBrutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times."oOnce endangered, they are now overabundant. Their mournful songs have died out as the population rebounds."�The musical staff around its body is made of ice particles. The symbols are indecipherable, but some say they've heard Saurenaid speak its own language."sWith its astonishing capacity for metamorphosis, it can get along with anything - except for its fellow Ditto."iEevee has an unstable genetic makeup that suddenly mutates due to the environment in which it lives."`When Vaporeon's fins begin to vibrate, it is a sign that rain will come within a few hours."zIts lungs contain an organ that creates electricity. The crackling sound of electricity can be heard when it exhales."_A dedicated omnivore, Flareon will eat anything - as long as it's been slow-roasted first."tIts fur is so sensitive, it can feel minute shifts in the air and predict the weather...and its foes' thoughts."qWhen exposed to the moon's aura, the rings on its body glow faintly and it's filled with a mysterious power."aJust like a plant, it uses photosynthesis. As a result, it is always enveloped in clear air."_It lowers its body heat to freeze its fur. The hairs then become like needles it can fire."�Sylveon's ribbon-like feelers emit an aura that erases any sense of hostility, enabling it to stop fights. Its feelers allow it to read their Trainer's feelings."|Its fluffiness, friendliness, and massive size make it beloved by nearly everyone. Attackers don't know where to begin."~This Pokémon was created using the cutting-edge science of 20 years ago, so many parts of it have since become obsolete."ZWith planetary development software installed, it became capable of working in space."zIts programming was modified to enable it to travel through alien dimensions. Seems there might have been an error..."�Rely on LuxTech's literal firewall! Featuring a unique* typing and cutting-edge network threat purgation protocols, this innovative new form has your back."�Because some Omanyte manage to escape after being restored or are released into the wild by people, this species is becoming a problem."|Its heavy shell is thought to be the reason this ancient Pokémon died out. It's apparently a distant ancestor of Octillery."uThis Pokémon likes to team up with the strongest Pokémon it can find. Some researchers fear its dormant power."�Some people claim this Pokémon ruled over an unnatural subterranean realm long ago. It resembles an enemy from a popular video game."rThis species is almost entirely extinct. Kabuto molt every three days, making their shells harder and harder."vKabutops slices its prey apart and sucks out the fluids. The discarded body parts become food for other Pokémon."�Its fossils were found in the depths of Makyan caves. However, it is alien to anything from the same time. It resembles a monster from a popular video game."�After evolution, this Pokémon began to resemble other extinct Pokémon of their time. They multiply by converting native biomass into more Kabuto."�It flew through the open skies over the ancient continent as if they were its own. When it touched ground, its walk was weak and slow."tIn ancient times, this Pokémon was an apex predator. It has the strength to fly with a Tyrantrum in its claws."vIt conceals food under the long fur on its body. It carts around this food stash and swallows it without chewing."Its stomach is said to be incomparably strong. Even Muk's poison is nothing more than a hint of spice on Snorlax's tongue."�Dratini continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels."�Dragonair stores an enormous amount of energy inside its body. It is said to alter weather conditions in its vicinity via crystals on its neck and tail."^It is said to make its home somewhere in the sea. It guides crews of shipwrecks to shore."eA legendary bird Pokémon that is said to appear to doomed people who are lost in icy mountains."zIts feather-like blades are composed of psychic energy and can shear through thick iron sheets as if they were paper."cThis legendary bird Pokémon is said to appear only when a thundercloud parts into two halves."�One kick from its powerful legs will pulverize a dump truck. Supposedly, this Pokémon runs through the mountains at over 180 mph."gOne of the legendary bird Pokémon. It is said that its appearance indicates the coming of spring."�This Pokémon's sinister, flame-like aura will consume the spirit of any creature it hits. Victims become burned-out shadows of themselves."tCreated from the DNA of Mew, this Pokémon is a dangerous combination of overwhelming power and a savage heart."�It's very intelligent and can use an incredible variety of moves. Many believe that all other Pokémon are descendants of this one."bIt uses the leaf on its head to determine the temperature and humidity. It loves to sunbathe."MThe buds that ring its neck give off a spicy aroma that perks people up."eMeganium's breath has the power to revive dead grass and plants. It can make them healthy again."[It has a timid nature. If it is startled, the flames on its back burn more vigorously."kBe careful if it turns its back during battle. It means that it will attack with the fire on its back."bIt has a secret, devastating move. It rubs its blazing fur together to cause huge explosions."�Said to purify lost, forsaken souls with its flames and guide them to the afterlife. Its form had been influenced by the energy of Mt. Coronet."jIts powerful, well-developed jaws are capable of crushing anything. Even its Trainer must be careful."eOnce it bites down, it won't let go until it loses its fangs. New fangs quickly grow into place."kWhen it bites with its massive and powerful jaws, it shakes its head and savagely tears its victim up."�This Pokémon is very cautious. It stands on its tail in order to see enemies from far away. If it does then it alert its pack by thumping its tail on the ground."rIt makes a nest to suit its long and skinny body. It uses tunnels in order to make a quick getaway from foes."tThe eye on its stomach enables its psychic powers and never blinks. Dirt and dust are telekinetically repelled."|It burrows at night, leaving only the eye on its stomach exposed. The eye will stare into space while the rest of it sleeps."\It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, the movement can rarely be seen."_When it needs to think, it rotates its head 180 degrees to sharpen its intellectual power."}Its down insulates it against any cold. In winter it will lay dormant beneath snow banks, only to pop out during spring."iWhen its shadow passes over someone, they feel a horrible chill. Some Trainers find it invigorating."jIt is timid and clusters together with others. The fluid secreted by its feet indicates its location."lThe spot patterns on its back grow larger or smaller depending on the number of stars in the night sky."kIt lies still in the same pose for days in its web, waiting for its unsuspecting prey to wander close."jIt attaches silk to its prey and sets it free. Later, it tracks the silk to the prey and its friends."kIt shoots positive and negative electricity between the tips of its two antennae and zaps its enemies."{It blinds prey with an intense burst of light. With the prey incapacitated, the Pokémon swallows it in a single gulp."}Togepi shares its joy with the people who take care of it. It can act maliciously, causing havoc and bad luck to its enemies."cThey say that it will appear before kindhearted, caring people and shower them with happiness."eIt shares many blessings with people who respect one another's rights and avoid needless strife."oIt usually forages for food on the ground but may, on rare occasions, hop onto branches to peck at shoots."kThey say that it stays still and quiet because it is seeing both the past and future at the same time."bIt stores lots of air in its soft fur, allowing it to stay cool in summer and warm in winter."oIf its coat becomes fully charged with electricity, its tail lights up. It fires hair that zaps on impact."gThe tail's tip shines brightly and can be seen from far away. It acts as a beacon for lost people."\It swings its large, nutrient-filled tail around to fight opponents bigger than itself."^The tip of its tail is filled with oil that is lighter than water, so it acts as a float."^The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it's in the water."kIt prefers an arid atmosphere. It leaks water that looks like tears when adjusting its moisture level."nIt disguises itself as a tree to avoid attack. It hates water, so it will disappear if it starts raining."jIt drifts on winds. It is said that when Hoppip gather in fields and mountains, spring is on the way."bIt spreads its petals to absorb sunlight. It also floats in the air to get closer to the sun."lEven in the fiercest wind, it can control its fluff to make its way to any place in the world it wants."dIts tail is so powerful that it can use it to grab a tree branch and hold itself up in the air."STo eat, it deftly shucks nuts with its two tails. It rarely uses its arms now."nIt lives by drinking only dewdrops from under the leaves of plants. It is said that it eats nothing else."]It gets energy from warm sunlight and is known for its habit of moving in pursuit of it."jIf it flaps its wings really fast, it can generate shock waves that will shatter windows in the area."{This six-legged Pokémon is easily capable of transporting an adult in flight. The wings on its tail help it stay balanced."dWhen the temperature cools in the evening, they emerge from water to seek food along the shore."eThis carefree Pokémon has an easygoing nature. While swimming, it always bumps into boat hulls."eFeared and loathed by many, it is believed to bring misfortune to all those who see it at night."QBecoming active at night, it is known to swarm with numerous Murkrow in tow."cIt likes playing mischievous tricks, such as screaming and wailing to startle people at night."`Its cries sound like incantations to torment the foe. It appears where you least expect it."\Shaped like ancient writing, it is a huge mystery whether language or Unown came first."XIt grows strong by pushing up against others en masse. It loves eating sweet fruit."hTo keep its pitch-black tail hidden, it lives quietly in the darkness. It is never first to attack."kIts tail has a small brain of its own. Beware! If you get close, it may react to your scent by biting."�Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig's."eIt looks just like a pinecone. Its shell protects it from bird Pokémon that peck it by mistake."mIt remains immovably rooted to its tree. It scatters pieces of its hard shell to drive its enemies away."�Scientists believe that it used to fly with its wings during ancient times. Nowadays it burrows under the ground, sharing tunnels with other Pokémon."�This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles."wThe gentle Dududunsparce will put Pokémon that wander into its nest onto its back and carry them to the entrance."fIt flies straight at its target's face, then clamps down on the startled victim to inject poison."uIts flight is soundless. It uses its lengthy tail to carry off its prey... Then its elongated fangs do the rest."]Small Pokémon flee from its scary face. It is, however, considered by women to be cute."eIt can make most any Pokémon run away simply by opening its mouth wide to reveal its big fangs."hThe small spikes covering its body developed from scales. They inject a toxin that causes fainting."nFishers detest this troublesome Pokémon because it sprays poison from its spines, getting it everywhere."{Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname "sea fiend." It slurps up poison to nourish itself."oIt stores berries inside its shell. To avoid attacks, it hides beneath rocks and remains completely still."eIts paws conceal sharp claws. If attacked, it suddenly extends the claws and startles its enemy."kThey live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination."�Its sturdy, curved claws are ideal for traversing precipitous cliffs. From the tips of these claws drips a nerve-destroying venom."�Because of Sneasler's virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on frozen highlands."cBefore food becomes scarce in wintertime, its habit is to hoard food in many hidden locations."mAlthough it has a large body, it is quite skilled at climbing trees. It eats and sleeps in the treetops."�It is believed that the swampy terrain of its ancient home region gave Ursaluna its burly physique and capacity to manipulate peat at will."YIts body is made of magma. If it doesn't keep moving, its body will cool and harden."gIts body is as hot as lava and is always billowing. Flames will occasionally burst from its shell."]If it smells something enticing, it dashes off headlong to find the source of the aroma."cBecause the long hair all over its body obscures its sight, it just keeps charging repeatedly."hIts impressive tusks are made of ice. The population thinned when it turned warm after the ice age."pThey prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water."�It will regrow any branches that break off its head. People keep particularly beautiful Curesola branches as charms to promote safe childbirth."|Sudden climate change wiped out this ancient kind of Corsola. This Pokémon absorbs others' life-force through its branches."lBe cautious of the ectoplasmic body surrounding its soul. You'll become stiff as stone if you touch it."iUsing its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a Mantine's underside to scavenge for leftovers."eIt traps foes with the suction cups on its tentacles, then smashes them with its rock-hard head."vWhen it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back."iWhile elegantly swimming in the sea, it ignores Remoraid that cling to its fins seeking food scraps."�Food rots and milk curdles in their presence. Because of this, they're commonly seen fleeing from angered Pokémon such as Miltank or Alcremie."�It pelts houses with hail that sounds like knocking, trying to get those inside to open a door or window. People used to import Skarmory to defend against them."^It carries food all day long. When someone is lost in the mountains, it shares that food."UDespite being clad entirely in iron-hard armor, it flies at speeds over 180 mph."`To corner prey, they check each other's location using barks that only they can understand."bThe flames it breathes when angry contain toxins. If they cause a burn, it will hurt forever."~They are the steeds of the Elite Four of the Apocalypse, and their howls will ring in the end of days... or so the stories go."�Phanpy uses its snout to shower itself with water. However, its snout is so strong that when it bumps into you, it may send you flying."cThe longer and bigger its tusks, the higher its rank in its herd. The tusks take long to grow."kThe curved antlers subtly change the flow of air to create a strange space where reality is distorted."�The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well."bOnce it becomes an adult, it has a tendency to let its comrades plant footprints on its back."uBorn deep underground, it comes aboveground and becomes a pupa once it has finished eating the surrounding soil."iIts shell is as hard as sheet rock, and it is also very strong. Its thrashing can topple a mountain."`If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward."�Raikou embodies the speed of lightning. This Pokémon's roars send shock waves shuddering through the air and ground as if lightning bolts were crashing down."�Entei embodies the passion of magma. This Pokémon is thought to have been born in the eruption of a volcano. It blasts fire that consumes all that it touches."�Suicune embodies the compassion of a pure spring of water. It runs across the land with gracefulness. This Pokémon has the power to purify dirty water."hIt is said to be the guardian of the seas. It is rumored to have been seen on the night of a storm."jA legend says that its body glows in seven colors. A rainbow is said to form behind it when it flies."�This Pokémon traveled through time to come from the future. It bolsters grass and trees with its own strength, and it can heal wounds, too."�Treecko has small hooks on the bottom of its feet that enable it to scale vertical walls. This Pokémon attacks by slamming foes with its thick tail."�The leaves growing out of Grovyle's body are convenient for camouflaging it from enemies in the forest. This Pokémon is a master at climbing trees in jungles."�The leaves growing on Sceptile's body are very sharp. This Pokémon is very agile - it leaps all over the branches of trees and jumps on its foe from above or behind."sThese Pokémon travel in small groups, searching for travelers to rob. As they march, their tails drum a beat."}Though they are skilled with swordplay, they never fight fair. They swish their tails in unison to intimidate groups of prey."�This Pokémon's tail is so heavy it must run on all fours to spear foes. The sound of wind in its feathers is the only warning before impact."�Torchic has a place inside its body where it keeps its flame. Give it a hug - it will be glowing with warmth. This Pokémon is covered all over by a fluffy coat of down."uCombusken battles with the intensely hot flames it spews from its beak and with outstandingly destructive kicks."�Blaziken has incredibly strong legs - it can easily clear a 30-story building in one leap. This Pokémon's blazing punches leave its foes scorched and blackened."sThis Pokémon is drawn to sounds of revelry. It is commonly sighted in the crowd at fairgrounds and festivals."{This Pokémon invents a new dance routine every day. After performances, it tosses treats and trinkets into the crowd."�This Pokémon ensures festivities will remain both safe and lively. It deftly leaps between tents and rooftops, subduing anyone who would ruin the fun."�In water, Mudkip breathes using the gills on its cheeks. If it is faced with a tight situation in battle, this Pokémon will unleash its amazing power."�The surface of Marshtomp's body is enveloped by a thin, sticky film that enables it to live on land. This Pokémon plays in mud on beaches."_It can swim while towing a large ship. It bashes down foes with a swing of its thick arms."�This Pokémon was only found recently, as upheavals unsealed ancient caves rife with old life, where it promptly hid from sight in narrow spaces."yThis Pokémon is much stronger than before, yet lazy. It is quick to make friends, but it might eat them in a pinch."�Living in underwater caves with no light has given this Pokémon great sensitivity to vibrations. It pinpoints prey with extreme precision."tIt has a very tenacious nature. Its acute sense of smell lets it chase a chosen prey without ever losing track."gIt chases down prey in a pack of around ten. They defeat foes with perfectly coordinated teamwork."bA Pokémon with abundant curiosity. It shows an interest in everything, so it always zigzags."fIt charges prey at speeds over 60 mph. However, because it can only run straight, it often fails."lThought to be the oldest form of Zigzagoon, it moves in zigzags and wreaks havoc upon its surroundings."\This very aggressive Pokémon will recklessly challenge opponents stronger than itself."�It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch."jIt lives among the tall grass and in forests. It repels attacks by raising up the spikes on its rear."eIt drinks dew that collects on its silk and waits for evolution. Its hard cocoon repels attacks."gIt has an aggressive nature. It stabs prey with its long, narrow mouth to drain the prey's fluids."cIt never forgets any attack it endured while in the cocoon. After evolution, it seeks payback."iIt violently flutters its wings to scatter toxic dust when attacked. It becomes active after sunset."�Its horns efficiently regulate its body temperature. It seeks out Fire- and Ice-type predators to charge itself with energy for evolution."�Its silk makes it blend in with snowy rocks. If attacked, its only recourse is to make itself unappetizing by chilling its own body."�It is less hostile than the Hoennian form, but vicious towards former predators. Its mouthparts inject a fluid similar to liquid nitrogen."}Its flame is kept burning by an organ similar to a Bunsen burner. Curious Pokémon often try to put it out, to no avail."�Its abdomen is actually a sophisticated torch drive. Their migrations can be tracked by following broken trees left by supersonic flybys."lIt searches about for clean water. If it does not drink water for too long, the leaf on its head wilts."fIt has a mischievous spirit. If it spots an angler, it will tug on the fishing line to interfere."]The rhythm of bright, festive music activates Ludicolo's cells, making it more powerful."gWhen it dangles from a tree branch, it looks just like an acorn. It enjoys scaring other Pokémon."mIt lives deep in forests. With the leaf on its head, it makes a flute whose song makes listeners uneasy."bBy flapping its leafy fan, it can whip up gusts of 100 feet per second that can level houses."�This Pokémon is very gutsy and will fight powerful opponents without backing down. On the other hand, when it is hungry it will weaken and cry loudly."bIt dives at a steep angle as soon as it spots its prey. It catches its prey with sharp claws."WIt makes its nest on steep sea cliffs. Riding updrafts, it soars to great heights."\It is a messenger of the skies, carrying small Pokémon and eggs to safety in its bill."bIt is highly attuned to the emotions of people and Pokémon. It hides if it senses hostility."cIt has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future."_It has the power to predict the future. Its power peaks when it is protecting its Trainer."\A master of courtesy and swordsmanship, it fights using extending swords on its elbows."�Its legs can generate oils, helping it glide through the water. The antenna on its head can secrete a thick, sugary syrup that is used to attract prey."_It flaps its four wings to hover and fly freely in any direction--to and fro and sideways."cIt spouts poison spores from the top of its head. These spores cause pain all over if inhaled."jIt scatters poisonous spores and throws powerful punches while its foe is hampered by inhaled spores."kIf it eats just three leaves in a day, it is satisfied. Other than that, it sleeps for 20 hours a day."dIts stress level rises if it cannot keep moving constantly. Too much stress makes it feel sick."~It is the world's most slothful Pokémon. However, it can exert horrifying power by releasing pent-up energy all at once."lIt can sometimes live underground for more than 10 years. It absorbs nutrients from the roots of trees."aBecause it moves so quickly, it sometimes becomes unseeable. It congregates around tree sap."ZA most peculiar Pokémon that somehow appears in a Poké Ball when a Nincada evolves."`If it senses danger, it scares the foe by crying out with the volume of a jet-plane engine."XThe shock waves from its cries can tip over trucks. It stamps its feet to power up."ZIts roar in battle shakes the ground like a tremor--or like an earthquake has struck."hIt grows stronger by enduring harsh training. It is a gutsy Pokémon that can withstand any attack."hIt loves to match power with big-bodied Pokémon. It can knock a truck flying with its arm thrusts."`Its magnetic nose consistently faces north. Travelers check Nosepass to get their bearings."QIt freely controls three small units called Mini-Noses using magnetic force."HIt shows its cute side by chasing its own tail until it gets dizzy."]It is highly popular among female Trainers for its sublime fur. It does not keep a nest."bIt dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself."�Attackers find their weaknesses and regrets reflected in the jewel Rubarior carries. If it feels unloved, it will make its Trainer cry."`Attached to its head is a huge set of jaws formed by horns. It can chew through iron beams."�Fans argue whether it's the cutest terrifying Pokémon or the creepiest cute Pokémon. It will act cute or scary depending on its trainer's whims."�When Aron evolves, its steel armor peels off. In ancient times, people would collect Aron's shed armor and make good use of it in their daily lives."�During territorial disputes, Lairon fight by slamming into each other. Close inspection of their steel armor reveals scratches and dents."�Long ago, there was a king who wore a helmet meant to resemble the head of an Aggron. He was trying to channel the Pokémon's strength."_It eats just one berry a day. By enduring hunger, its spirit is tempered and made sharper."WThrough yoga training, it gained the psychic power to predict its foe's next move."�This Pokémon can go up to four years without eating a single meal. Through intense training, it is able to fight in a manner indistinguishable from a dance."hIt stores static electricity in its fur for discharging. It gives off sparks if a storm approaches."iIt discharges electricity from its mane. It creates a thundercloud overhead to drop lightning bolts."XIf not calmed during storms, it will cause havoc by trying to race lightning bolts."dIt absorbs electricity from telephone poles. It shorts out its body to create crackling noises."]It cheers on friends. If its friends are losing, its body lets off more and more sparks."oIt lives around clean ponds. At night, its rear lights up. It converses with others by flashing its light."WWith its sweet aroma, it guides Volbeat to draw signs with light in the night sky."kOver the winter, it closes its bud and endures the cold. In spring, the bud opens and releases pollen."jRoselia that drink nutritionally rich springwater are said to reveal rare coloration when they bloom."eWith the movements of a dancer, it strikes with whips that are densely lined with poison thorns."mThere is nothing its stomach can't digest. While it is digesting, vile, overpowering gases are expelled."YIt gulps anything that fits in its mouth. Its special enzymes can dissolve anything."eIt lives in massive rivers that course through jungles. It swarms prey that enter its territory."gIt can swim at speeds of 75 mph by jetting seawater through its body. It is the bandit of the sea."�Its propulsion system is the basis for many ramjet engine designs. It eats four times its body weight in food before a battle and will still be hungry by the end."pIt eats one ton of food every day. It plays by shooting stored seawater out its blowholes with great force."bThe biggest of all Pokémon. It can dive to a depth of almost 10,000 feet on only one breath."pThe magma in its body reaches 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit. Its hump gets smaller when it uses Fire-type moves."nIf angered, the humps on its back erupt in a shower of molten lava. It lives in the craters of volcanoes."�Magma builds up in its body over time. If this Pokémon does not regularly erupt, it might accidentally destroy the area around it."\It burns coal inside its shell for energy. It blows out black soot if it is endangered."kIt bounces around on its tail to keep its heart pumping. It carries a pearl from Clamperl on its head."gIt uses black pearls to amplify its psychic power. It does an odd dance to gain control over foes."_The chances of two Spinda having identical spot patterns is less than one in four billion."gIt makes an inescapable conical pit and lies in wait at the bottom for prey to come tumbling down."}It generates ultrasonic waves by violently flapping its wings. After making its prey faint, it melts the prey with acid."hKnown as "The Desert Spirit," this Pokémon hides in the sandstorms it causes by beating its wings."kIt prefers harsh environments such as deserts. It can survive for 30 days on water stored in its body."^Packs of them follow travelers through the desert until the travelers can no longer move."iSwablu is very friendly towards humans, so a Swablu may land on your head and act like a fluffy hat."�Altarias often glide through the clouds while singing or humming. While normally kind, Altaria will attack foes without mercy if provoked."�This Pokémon's singing can bring even the most stoic Trainers to tears. Those who fall asleep on it are said to experience beautiful dreams."eIts fur would all stand on end if it smelled a Seviper nearby. Its sharp claws tear up its foes."kConstant polishing makes the edge of the blade on its tail extremely sharp. It's Zangoose's archrival."�Even being bisected by a Seviper's tail couldn't quell its rage. It attacks enemies on a physical and spiritual level simultaneously."~Its iron body is impenetrable to nearly all attacks. When coiled, it can fire metal projectiles using magnetic induction."iIt was discovered at the site of a meteor strike 40 years ago. Its stare can lull its foes to sleep."jIt absorbs solar energy during the day. Always expressionless, it can sense what its foe is thinking."cIts whiskers make a superb radar. They are used to locate prey, even in the murkiest of water."kIt makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything--if it is alive, Whiscash will eat it."dIts hardy vitality enables it to adapt to any environment. Its pincers will never release prey."xLoving to battle, this Pokémon pinches all Pokémon that enter its territory with its pincers and throws them out."bIt moves by spinning on its foot. It is a rare Pokémon that was discovered in ancient ruins."SIt is said that it originates from clay dolls made by an ancient civilization."This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. Lileep once lived in warm seas that existed approximately 100,000,000 years ago."�It has short legs and can't walk very fast, but its neck and tentacles can extend to over three times their usual length to nab distant prey."�Anorith can swim swiftly by pulling its eight wings through the water like oars on a boat. This Pokémon is an ancestor of modern bug Pokémon."~After evolution, this Pokémon emerged onto land. Its lower body has become stronger, and blows from its tail are devastating."`It is the shabbiest Pokémon of all. It forms in schools and lives at the bottom of rivers."^It is the world's most beautiful Pokémon. There are many works of art featuring Milotic."�Swimming through the air in places of unmourned tragedy, Feebas are easily located due to the sobbing noises they emit when alone."eMilotic are unburdened by sadness. They are said to help restless souls pass into the afterlife."mIt has the ability to change its form into the sun, the rain, or a snow cloud, depending on the weather."uIt changes its shading to match its surroundings so it can sneak up on prey. Only its belly patterns stay fixed."gIt loves vengeful emotions and hangs in rows under the eaves of houses where vengeful people live."qStrong feelings of hatred turned a puppet into a Pokémon. If it opens its mouth, its cursed energy escapes."�Its pink claws and feet appear to be made of flesh, but are actually raw negative energy. When it is finally fully unzipped, it moves on to its next life."kIf it finds bad children who won't listen to their parents, it will spirit them away--or so it's said."_Its body is hollow. It is said that those who look into its body are sucked into the void."`It comes to those whose lives have come to an end and escorts their souls to the afterlife."sThe bunch of fruit around its neck ripens twice a year and is delicious. It's a highly favored tropical snack."hThere is an orb inside its mouth. When it hops, the orb bounces all over and makes a ringing sound."MEmitting ultrasonic cries, it floats on winds to travel great distances."�Swift as the wind, Absol races through fields and mountains. Its curved, bow-like horn is acutely sensitive to the warning signs of natural disasters."�It's loved for its elegantly intimidating looks. It may herald a coming cataclysm, but nothing gets between a trainer and a fashionable Pokémon."TIn Sinnoh, certain folklore says a house will prosper if a Snorunt lives there."_It can instantly freeze moisture in the atmosphere. It uses this power to freeze its foes."�It only closes its mouth to bite its foes, forcing its trainers to learn to interpret its emotions via its changes in eye shape, ear direction, and body temperature."fLegends in snowy regions say that a woman who was lost on an icy mountain was reborn as Froslass."iIt's more efficient for Spheal to roll than to walk. When this Pokémon is happy, it claps its fins."tThis Pokémon has a habit of spinning round things on its nose, whether those things are Poké Balls or Spheal."�Walrein's tusks keep growing throughout its life. Tusks broken in battle will grow back to their usual impressive size in a year."YIt is protected by a sturdy shell. Once in a lifetime, it makes a magnificent pearl."cIt lives deep in the sea. With a tail shaped like a small fish, it attracts unsuspecting prey."qIts swimming form is exquisitely elegant. With its thin mouth, it feeds on seaweed that grows between rocks."�This Pokémon was discovered during deep-sea exploration. Its appearance hasn't changed in 100,000,000 years, so it's called a living fossil."fDuring the spawning season, countless Luvdisc congregate at coral reefs, turning the waters pink."dIt gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds."�Bagon is a solitary Pokémon that doesn't form groups with others of its kind. It also has a head hard enough to cleave a boulder in one strike."�Shelgon ignores its hunger entirely, never eating any food. Apparently, Shelgon will evolve once all its energy stores are used up."�While basking in the joy of flight generally keeps this Pokémon in high spirits, it turns into an uncontrollable menace if something angers it."}From its rear, Beldum emits a magnetic force that rapidly pulls opponents in. They get skewered on Beldum's sharp claws."�Using magnetic forces to stay aloft, this Pokémon flies at high speeds, weaving through harsh mountain terrain in pursuit of prey."�Metagross is the result of the fusion of two Metang. This Pokémon defeats its opponents through use of its supercomputer-level brain."sThe third of the titans, built to commemorate an era of stonecraft. It is as resilient as an ancient monolith."qThe second of the titans, built to commemorate an era of ice. It is as implacable as an encroaching glacier."~The fourth of the titans, built to commemorate an era of metalworking. It is as unfailing as a master swordsmith's blade."The fifth of the titans, built to commemorate an era of electricity. It is as inscrutable as a cutting-edge supercomputer."vThe first of the titans, built to commemorate an era when dragons ruled. It is as terrifying as an apex predator."pThe creator of the titans, who shaped the primal clay in the golden age. Its creative powers are boundless."�Latias is highly sensitive to the emotions of people. If it senses any hostility, this Pokémon ruffles the feathers all over its body and cries shrilly to intimidate them."�Latios has the ability to make others see an image of what it has seen or imagines in its head. This Pokémon is intelligent and understands human speech."�Kyogre is said to be the personification of the sea itself. Legends tell of its many clashes against Groudon, as each sought to gain the power of nature."�Groudon is said to be the personification of the land itself. Legends tell of its many clashes against Kyogre, as each sought to gain the power of nature."�Rayquaza is said to have lived for hundreds of millions of years. Legends remain of how it put to rest the clash between Kyogre and Groudon."]It is said to have the ability to grant any wish for just one week every thousand years."]DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen."�It relies heavily on water to keep its plant healthy, and thus it spends most of its time near lakes. When thirsty, the plant on its head wilts."VIt knows where pure water wells up. It carries fellow Pokémon there on its back."[Small Pokémon occasionally gather on its unmoving back to begin building their nests."aThe gas made in its belly burns from its rear end. The fire burns weakly when it feels sick."[It uses ceilings and walls to launch aerial attacks. Its fiery tail is but one weapon."gIt tosses its enemies around with agility. It uses all its limbs to fight in its own unique style."gBecause it is very proud, it hates accepting food from people. Its thick down guards it from cold."gIt lives a solitary life. Its wings deliver wicked blows that can snap even the thickest of trees."eThe three horns that extend from its beak attest to its power. The leader has the biggest horns."mThey flock around mountains and fields, chasing after bug Pokémon. Their singing is noisy and annoying."XIt lives in forests and fields. Squabbles over territory occur when flocks collide."eWhen Staravia evolve into Staraptor, they leave the flock to live alone. They have sturdy wings."eIt constantly gnaws on logs and rocks to whittle down its front teeth. It nests alongside water."bIt makes its nest by damming streams with bark and mud. It is known as an industrious worker."OWhen its antennae hit each other, it sounds like the music of a xylophone."_It signals its emotions with its melodies. Scientists are studying these melodic patterns."_All of its fur dazzles if danger is sensed. It flees while the foe is momentarily blinded."mStrong electricity courses through the tips of its sharp claws. A light scratch causes fainting in foes."ZLuxray's ability to see through objects comes in handy when it's scouting for danger."jA lifelong jungle dweller from 100 million years ago, it would snap obstructing trees with headbutts."bIts skull is as hard as iron. It is a brute that tears down jungle trees while catching prey."vIt was generated from a fossil dug out of a layer of clay that was older than anyone knows. It has a sturdy face."]Any frontal attack is repulsed. It is a docile Pokémon that feeds on grass and berries."ZIf its cloak is broken in battle, it quickly remakes the cloak with materials nearby."bWhen Burmy evolved, its cloak became a part of this Pokémon's body. The cloak is never shed."GIt flutters around at night and steals honey from the Combee hive."�It collects honey for its colony. At night, they cluster to form a beehive and sleep. If a colony loses their Vespiquen, a new Combee will take its place."\Its abdomen is a honeycomb for grubs. It raises its grubs on honey collected by Combee."fA pair may be seen rubbing their cheek pouches together in an effort to share stored electricity."oIt inflates the flotation sac around its neck and pokes its head out of the water to see what is going on."fIts flotation sac developed as a result of pursuing aquatic prey. It can double as a rubber raft."`It evolves by sucking the energy out of the small ball where it had been storing nutrients."kIf it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun's rays with its whole body."�The colors of this Pokémon change depending on its environment. When it senses danger, this Pokémon excretes a sticky purple liquid."eIt apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools."lThese Pokémon are called the "Signpost for Wandering Spirits." Children holding them sometimes vanish."dIt's drowsy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go."nWhen it senses danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into its fur."bThe ears appear to be delicate. If they are touched roughly, it kicks with its graceful legs."�It patterns its fur and attacks after human fighters it looks up to. Only the most over-the-top action movies can inspire it to reach its true potential."yAccording to legend, the Buneary of Makya came from the moon. They have incredible control of their prehensile ears."}The blue crystals that adorn Makyan Lopunny's fur resemble saccharite, but analysis shows that they're structurally distinct."�A wanderer, Makyan Haerobic has a deep sense of justice and will use the full force of its lunar powers to rescue weaker Pokémon."bWhen it's happy, Glameow demonstrates beautiful movements of its tail, like a dancing ribbon."bTo make itself appear intimidatingly beefy, it tightly cinches its waist with its twin tails."cIt protects itself by spraying a noxious fluid from its rear. The stench lingers for 24 hours."gIt sprays a stinky fluid from its tail. The fluid smells worse the longer it is allowed to fester."cImplements shaped like it were discovered in ancient tombs. It is unknown if they are related."_Ancient people believed that petitioning Bronzong for rain was the way to make crops grow."XIt can learn and speak human words. If they gather, they all learn the same saying."All Spiritomb's mischief and misdeeds compelled a traveler to use a mysterious spell to bind Spiritomb to an odd keystone."�Gible attacks anything that moves, and it drags whatever it catches into the crevice that is its lair. Despite the big mouth, Gible's stomach is small."�Jewels are buried in the caves these Pokémon nest in, but you'll be torn apart by claws and fangs the moment you enter one of these caves."�Garchomp makes its home in volcanic mountains. It flies through the sky as fast as a jet airplane, hunting down as much prey as it can."]The aura that emanates from its body intensifies to alert others if it is afraid or sad."gBy reading the auras of all things, it can tell how others are feeling from over half a mile away."�It fights in a state of complete clarity without mercy, fear, or stress. When it has achieved all its goals, it will simply cease to be."_It enshrouds itself with sand to protect itself from germs. It does not enjoy getting wet."eIt blasts internally stored sand from ports on its body to create a towering twister for attack."pIt burrows under the sand to lie in wait for prey. Its tail claws can inject its prey with a savage poison."fIt has the power in its clawed arms to make scrap of a car. The tips of its claws release poison."sInflating its poison sacs, it fills the area with an odd sound and hits flinching opponents with a poison jab."UIts knuckle claws secrete a toxin so vile that even a scratch could prove fatal."mIt binds itself to trees in marshes. It attracts prey with its sweet-smelling drool and gulps them down."�It hunts other nocturnal predators, trapping them with its sticky tendrils. Its maniacal laugh is a common sound on autumn nights."hAfter long exposure to sunlight, the patterns on its tail fins shine vividly when darkness arrives."cTo avoid detection by predators, it crawls along the seafloor using the two fins on its chest."XIn the spring, it grows berries with the texture of frozen treats around its belly."wIt lives a quiet life on mountains that are perpetually covered in snow. It hides itself by whipping up blizzards."{Blizzards follow it wherever it goes. It's often used as shelter by unsuspecting mountaineers, though it doesn't mind."bIts body is composed of plasma. It is known to infiltrate electronic devices and wreak havoc."mKnown as "The Being of Knowledge." It is said that it can wipe out the memory of those who see its eyes."]Known as "The Being of Emotion." It taught humans the nobility of sorrow, pain, and joy."gKnown as "The Being of Willpower." It sleeps at the bottom of a lake to keep the world in balance."\A Pokémon spoken of in legend. It is said that time began moving when Dialga was born."dIt is said to live in a gap in the spatial dimension parallel to ours. It appears in mythology."gIt dwells in volcanic caves. It digs in with its cross-shaped feet to crawl on ceilings and walls."{This Pokémon is said to live in a world on the reverse side of ours, where common knowledge is distorted and strange."yThose who sleep holding Cresselia's feather are assured of joyful dreams. It is said to represent the crescent moon."kIt drifts in warm seas. It always returns to where it was born, no matter how far it may have drifted."`It starts its life with a wondrous power that permits it to bond with any kind of Pokémon."aIt can lull people to sleep and make them dream. It is active during nights of the new moon."}The blooming of Gracidea flowers confers the power of flight upon it. Feelings of gratitude are the message it delivers."ZIt is told in mythology that this Pokémon was born before the universe even existed."pThey photosynthesize by bathing their tails in sunlight. When they are not feeling well, their tails droop."eWhen it gets dirty, its leaves can't be used in photosynthesis, so it always keeps itself clean."oIt can stop its opponents' movements with just a glare. It takes in solar energy and boosts it internally."bIt loves to eat roasted berries, but sometimes it gets too excited and burns them to a crisp."nWhen its internal fire flares up, its movements grow sharper and faster. When in trouble, it emits smoke."PIt has mastered fast and powerful fighting moves. It grows a beard of fire."rIt fights using the scalchop on its stomach. In response to an attack, it retaliates immediately by slashing."`As a result of strict training, each Dewott learns different forms for using the scalchops."}One swing of the sword incorporated in its armor can fell an opponent. A simple glare from one of them quiets everybody."hHard of heart and deft of blade, its turbulent blows crash into foes like ceaseless pounding waves."qExtremely cautious, one of them will always be on the lookout, but it won't notice a foe coming from behind."vWhen they see an enemy, their tails stand high, and they spit the seeds of berries stored in their cheek pouches."mThough it is a very brave Pokémon, it's also smart enough to check its foe's strength and avoid battle."bIt has black, cape-like fur that is very hard and decreases the amount of damage it receives."uBeing wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain."zThey steal from people for fun, but their victims can't help but forgive them. Their deceptively cute act is perfect."jStealthily, it sneaks up on its target, striking from behind before its victim has a chance to react."nIt's good at finding berries and gathers them from all over. It's kind enough to share them with friends."tIll tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter."vThis Pokémon lives in caves in volcanoes. The fire within the tuft on its head can reach 600 degrees Fahrenheit."pWhen it gets excited, embers rise from its head and tail and it gets hot. For some reason, it loves sweets."qThe water stored inside the tuft on its head is full of nutrients. Plants that receive its water grow large."wIt prefers places with clean water. When its tuft runs low, it replenishes it by siphoning up water with its tail."kIt eats the dreams of people and Pokémon. When it eats a pleasant dream, it expels pink-colored mist."vThe dream mist coming from its forehead changes into many different colors depending on the dream that was eaten."�When a Munna egg is placed in the care of a brooding dragon, it hatches into this form. It will repeatedly headbutt Togepi if placed near one."�Excess psychic energy is vented as smoke from the hole where its gem once was. Its heart functions as a second brain that lets it communicate telepathically."kThese Pokémon live in cities. They are accustomed to people. Flocks often gather in parks and plazas."sNo matter where in the world it goes, it knows where its nest is, so it never gets separated from its Trainer."vMales have plumage on their heads. They will never let themselves feel close to anyone other than their Trainers."wIts mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use the frequency and rhythm of these flashes to communicate."mThey have lightning-like movements. When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates."qWhen it overflows with power, the orange crystal on its body glows. It looks for underground water in caves."�The blasts of energy it makes from sunbeams have terrifying power. However, it's not able to fire its blasts at night or on rainy days."�In Makyan myth, they were born from meteors that fell when the moon was split by an angry god. Their unfathomably dense armor deflects most anything."mIt was first unearthed in forbidden lands. Its body doesn't abide by the physical laws of this universe."It is more comfortable in alien dimensions than on Earth. The rocky parts of its body can't be analyzed by modern science."�They can't be understood or predicted, making them dangerous opponents. At the end of their lifespan they return to their home universe, reporting to a higher will."oThe heart-shaped mark left on a body after a Woobat has been attached to it is said to bring good fortune."zAnyone who comes into contact with the ultrasonic waves emitted by a courting male experiences a positive mood shift."WBy spinning its body, it can dig straight through the ground at a speed of 30 mph."zMore than 300 feet below the surface, they build mazelike nests. Their activity can be destructive to subway tunnels."uAudino's sense of hearing is superb. Not even a pebble rolling along over a mile away will escape Audino's ears."�They are brought into hospitals when conventional medicine fails. They can hear the number of heartbeats a person has left, but will never tell."iAlways carrying squared logs, they help out with construction. As they grow, they carry bigger logs."tThis Pokémon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch."jRather than rely on force, they master moves that utilize the centrifugal force of spinning concrete."wBy vibrating its cheeks, it emits sound waves imperceptible to humans. It uses the rhythm of these sounds to talk."dIt lives in the water and on land. It uses its long, sticky tongue to immobilize its opponents."dThey shoot paralyzing liquid from their head bumps. They use vibration to hurt their opponents."mWhen it encounters a foe bigger than itself, it wants to throw it. It changes belts as it gets stronger."xTying their belts gets them pumped and makes their punches more destructive. Disturbing their training angers them."kSince this Pokémon makes its own clothes out of leaves, it is a popular mascot for fashion designers."oIt protects itself from the cold by wrapping up in leaves. It stays on the move, eating leaves in forests."vIt keeps its eggs warm with heat from fermenting leaves. It also uses leaves to make warm wrappings for Sewaddle."eIts bite injects a potent poison, enough to paralyze large bird Pokémon that try to prey on it."nIt is usually motionless, but when attacked, it rotates at high speed and then crashes into its opponent."lWith quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails."yPerhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud."lLike the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind."wSince they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants."{Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities."�Its well-developed legs were the result of a life spent on mountains covered in deep snow. The scent it exudes from its flower crown heartens those in proximity."�It seems to pride itself on living in inhospitable conditions. If others take up residence nearby, it will move to even colder climes."�It utters royal proclamations and tyrannical edicts on a whim, becoming petulant when its disobedient subjects can't understand it."xRed and blue Basculin usually do not get along, but sometimes members of one school mingle with the other's school."nClads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream."tThey live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping."{The special membrane covering its eyes can sense the heat of objects, so it can see its surroundings even in darkness."kThey never allow prey to escape. Their jaws are so powerful, they can crush the body of an automobile."rWhen it sleeps, it pulls its limbs into its body and its internal fire goes down to 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit."~Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees Fahrenheit, making enough power that it can destroy a dump truck with one punch."�The colder they get, the more energetic they are. They freeze their breath to make snowballs, using them as ammo for playful snowball fights."�Though it has a gentle disposition, it's also very strong. It will quickly freeze the snowball on its head before going for a headbutt."_Arid regions are their habitat. They move rhythmically, making a sound similar to maracas."sWhen it finds a stone of a suitable size, it secretes a liquid from its mouth to open up a hole to crawl into."rCompeting for territory, Crustle fight viciously. The one whose boulder is broken is the loser of the battle."hProud of its sturdy skull, it suddenly headbutts everything, but its weight makes it unstable, too."oIt can smash concrete blocks with its kicking attacks. The one with the biggest crest is the group leader."gThe guardians of an ancient city, they always fly the same route while keeping watch for invaders."oEach of them carries a mask that used to be its face when it was human. Sometimes they look at it and cry."jGrave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies."hIt's said that this Pokémon was formed when an ancient clay tablet was drawn to a vengeful spirit."qNever touch its shadowlike body, or you'll be shown the horrific memories behind the picture carved into it."uThis Pokémon inhabited ancient seas. Although it can only crawl, it still comes up onto land in search of prey."�Carracosta completely devours its prey - bones, shells, and all. Because of this, Carracosta's own shell grows thick and sturdy."�This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. As research suggested, Archen is unable to fly. But it's very good at jumping."�It needs a running start to take off. If Archeops wants to fly, it first needs to run nearly 25 mph, building speed over a course of about 2.5 miles."_Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places."WConsuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies."�It's unclear what the objects embedded in its body are or where they came from. More must be added over time, though, as anything it absorbs is quickly dissolved."qTo protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon."pBonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents."�A once-departed soul, returned to life. Derives power from resentment, which rises as energy atop its head and takes on the forms of foes."qIt likes to settle grudges and fulfill final wishes. It does so to ensure peaceful passage to the afterlife."mThese Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms."_Cinccino's body is coated in a special oil that helps it deflect attacks, such as punches."{They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see."rAccording to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights."qThey can predict the future from the placement and movement of the stars. They can see Trainers' life spans."gThey drive away attackers by unleashing psychic power. They can use telepathy to talk with others."]When their two divided brains think the same thoughts, their psychic power is maximized."fWhen Reuniclus shake hands, a network forms between their brains, increasing their psychic power."{They are better at swimming than flying, and they happily eat their favorite food, peat moss, as they dive underwater."]Swanna start to dance at dusk. The one dancing in the middle is the leader of the flock."gThis Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. It sleeps buried in snow."jSnowy mountains are this Pokémon's habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas."{Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards."vThe turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon's fur. People use it to mark the seasons."bThey migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring."tThe energy made in its cheeks' electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding."fFor some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet."qThese Pokémon evolve by wearing the shell covering of a Shelmet. The steel armor protects their whole body."gIt lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball, then releases poison spores."mIt lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion."rIf its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return."mThe fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent's habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished."~They are drawn to mysterious machinery and internet influencers. Because of this, they are common in online horror media."�They led explorers to an ancient sunken city in the abyss. Its people had uploaded their minds into machines that slowly failed over the ages."zThey attach themselves to large-bodied Pokémon and absorb static electricity, which they store in an electric pouch."�Galvantula attacks its foes with the electricity stored in the fur in its abdomen. To protect itself from threats, it uses electrically charged webs."mIt absorbs the iron it finds in the rock while clinging to the ceiling. It shoots spikes when in danger."bThey attach themselves to cave ceilings, firing steel spikes at targets passing beneath them."tThe two minigears that mesh together are predetermined. Each will rebound from other minigears without meshing."qA minigear and big gear comprise its body. If the minigear it launches at a foe doesn't return, it will die."kIts red core functions as an energy tank. It fires the charged energy through its spikes into an area."wOne alone can emit only a trickle of electricity, so a group of them gathers to unleash a powerful electric shock."tThese Pokémon have a big appetite. When they spot their prey, they attack it and paralyze it with electricity."yThey crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean."TRumors of its origin are linked to a UFO crash site in the desert 50 years ago."WIt uses psychic power to control an opponent's brain and tamper with its memories."vLitwick shines a light that absorbs the life energy of people and Pokémon, which becomes the fuel that it burns."IIt arrives near the moment of death and steals spirit from the body."]The spirits burned up in its ominous flame lose their way and wander this world forever."yThey mark their territory by leaving gashes in trees with their tusks. If a tusk breaks, a new one grows in quickly."tA broken tusk will not grow back, so it diligently sharpens its tusks on river rocks after the end of a battle."rTheir sturdy tusks will stay sharp even if used to cut steel beams. These Pokémon are covered in hard armor."xTheir snot is a barometer of health. When healthy, their snot is sticky and the power of their ice moves increases."oIt freezes its breath to create fangs and claws of ice to fight with. Cold northern areas are its habitat."tWhen the weather gets hot, these Pokémon turn into water vapor. Cryscross are almost never seen during summer."uWith its icy chains, Cryogonal freezes those it encounters. It then takes its victims away to somewhere unknown."jIt evolves when bathed in an electric-like energy along with Karrablast. The reason is still unknown."vWhen its body dries out, it weakens. So, to prevent dehydration, it wraps itself in many layers of thin membrane."yIt conceals itself in the mud of the seashore. Then it waits. When prey touch it, it delivers a jolt of electricity."�Its conspicuous lips lure prey in as it lies in wait in the mud. When prey gets close, Stunfisk clamps its jagged steel fins down on them."wIn fights, they dominate with onslaughts of flowing, continuous attacks. With their sharp claws, they cut enemies."sUsing the long fur on its arms like whips, it launches into combo attacks that, once started, no one can stop."tIt warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move."`Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It's been active for thousands of years."xIt flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control."jIgnoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey."jBisharp pursues prey in the company of a large group of Pawniard. Then Bisharp finishes off the prey."\Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit."VTheir fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt."xThey will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger."sThey fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying."fScreaming a bloodcurdling battle cry, this huge and ferocious bird Pokémon went out on the hunt."{Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz."vWatching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones."�It stomps on smaller opponents with its powerful legs, sometimes toppling in the process. If its house is broken, terrible wailing emits until it is repaired."�It steeps the remains of prey within the jar it protects, stirring the concoction with its claws. Folklore says its soul is kept within the diseased mass."yIt draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them."bThey attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor."kLacking sight, it's unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves."sAfter it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along."lIt responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!"|The base of volcanoes is where they make their homes. They shoot fire from their five horns to repel attacking enemies."tWhen volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona's fire provided a replacement for the sun."jIt has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon."xSpoken of in legend, this Pokémon used its phenomenal power to destroy a castle in its effort to protect Pokémon."MLegends say this Pokémon confounded opponents with its swift movements."rWhen it is resolute, its body fills with power and it becomes swifter. Its jumps are then too fast to follow."xTornadus expels massive energy from its tail, causing severe storms. Its power is great enough to blow houses away."~The spikes on its tail discharge immense bolts of lightning. It flies around the Unova region firing off lightning bolts."rLands visited by Landorus grant such bountiful crops that it has been hailed as "The Guardian of the Fields.""cAccording to legend, this Pokémon's love gave rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui."gWhen Reshiram's tail flares, the heat energy moves the atmosphere and changes the world's weather."uConcealing itself in lightning clouds, it flies throughout the Unova region. It creates electricity in its tail."sIt generates a powerful, freezing energy inside itself, but its body became frozen when the energy leaked out."qIts melodies are sung with a special vocalization method that can control the feelings of those who hear it."kThis Pokémon existed 300 million years ago. Team Plasma altered it and attached a cannon to its back."yThis Pokémon brings victory. It is said that Trainers with Victini always win, regardless of the type of encounter."nSuch a thick shell of wood covers its head and back that even a direct hit from a truck wouldn't faze it."oThey strengthen their lower bodies by running into one another. They are very kind and won't start fights."iWhen it takes a defensive posture with its fists guarding its face, it could withstand a bomb blast."xAs it walks, it munches on a twig in place of a snack. It intimidates opponents by puffing hot air out of its ears."|When the twig is plucked from its tail, friction sets the twig alight. The flame is used to send signals to its allies."Using psychic power, it generates a fiery vortex of 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit, incinerating foes swept into this whirl of flame."�It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings."dIts swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute's time."�It appears and vanishes with a ninja's grace. It toys with its enemies using swift movements, while slicing them with throwing stars of sharpest water."wIt has ears like shovels. Digging holes strengthens its ears so much that they can sever thick roots effortlessly."}As powerful as an excavator, its ears can reduce dense bedrock to rubble. When it's finished digging, it lounges lazily."cDespite the beauty of its lilting voice, it's merciless to intruders that enter its territory."pThe hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going."nWhen attacking prey, it can reach speeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its prey off with a colossal kick."hThe powder that covers its body regulates its temperature, so it can live in any region or climate."lThe beaks of bird Pokémon can't begin to scratch its stalwart body. To defend itself, it spews powder."|The patterns on this Pokémon's wings depend on the climate and topography of its habitat. It scatters colorful scales."�They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger. These hot-blooded Pokémon are quick to fight."�With fiery breath of more than 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, they viciously threaten any challenger. The females protect the pride's cubs."�When it finds a flower it likes, it dwells on that flower its whole life long. It floats in the wind's embrace with an untroubled heart."iWhen the flowers of a well-tended flower bed bloom, it appears and celebrates with an elegant dance."|In times long past, governors of castles would invite Florges to create flower gardens to embellish the castle domains."vIf it has sunshine and water, it doesn't need to eat, because it can generate energy from the leaves on its back."gThey inhabit mountainous regions. The leader of the herd is decided by a battle of clashing horns."oIt does its level best to glare and pull a scary face, but it can't help grinning if anyone pats its head."�It charges ahead and bashes its opponents like a berserker, uncaring about any hits it might take. Its arms are mighty enough to snap a telephone pole."aHistorically, in the Kalos region, these Pokémon were the designated guardians of the king."vIt has enough psychic energy to blast everything within 300 feet of itself, but it has no control over its power."�The eyeball patterns on the interior of its ears emit psychic energy. It keeps the patterns tightly covered because that power is too immense."�If anyone dares to grab its hilt, it wraps a blue cloth around that person's arm and drains that person's life energy completely."{The complex attack patterns of its two swords are unstoppable, even for an opponent greatly accomplished at swordplay."�Apparently, it can detect the innate qualities of leadership. According to legend, whoever it recognizes is destined to become king."tIn the past, rather than using perfume, royal ladies carried a Spritzee that would waft a fragrance they liked."�Its scent is so overpowering that, unless a Trainer happens to really enjoy the smell, they will have a hard time walking alongside it."{It uses both white and black magic. It harvests the flowers that grow on witches who regularly walk between life and death."TBecause it eats nothing but sweets, its fur is as sticky sweet as cotton candy."�Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human's, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area."�It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent's will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide."�It lures its prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids."�They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline."�Barbaracle's legs and hands have minds of their own, and they will move independently. But they usually follow the head's orders."aIt looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution."XTales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return."eBorn in pristine waters, they escape detection by blending in seamlessly with underwater plants."UThey gallop on the ocean floor, cleaning it by collecting algae on their hooves."~Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock."dBy expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots."iThe frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight."It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds."�This is an ancient Pokémon, revived in modern times. It has a violent disposition, and it'll tear apart anything it gets between its hefty jaws."oThis Pokémon is from about 100,000,000 years ago. It has the presence of a king, vicious but magnificent."�This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. In the past, it lived with others of its kind in cold lands where there were fewer predators."rAurorus was restored from a fossil. It's said that when this Pokémon howls, auroras appear in the night sky."�With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against."�It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers."�It's said that somewhere in the world, there's a mineral vein housing a large pack of slumbering Carbink. It's also said that this pack has a queen."bIt can instantly create many diamonds by compressing the carbon in the air between its hands."^It's covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly."}Its entire body is covered with gooey mucus that can dissolve anything. Be sure to put gloves on if you're going to touch it."uIt attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that's the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers."The iron in Sliggoo's drinking water turned its shell metallic. This Pokémon doesn't come out of its shell on sunny days."�Able to freely control the hardness of its metallic shell. It loathes solitude and is extremely clingy-it will fume and run riot if those dearest to it ever leave its side."wIt never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime."~According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest."|Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It's kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body."^It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on."jIt enwraps its prey in its hairlike arms. It sings joyfully as it observes the suffering of its prey."{Using air of -50 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains."wThe way several Bergmite and Dreepy like to huddle on its back makes it look like an aircraft carrier made of ice."nThis Pokémon barrels along steep mountain paths, cleaving through the deep snow with its hard icy armor."uEven a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves."|The ultrasonic waves it emits from its ears can reduce a large boulder to pebbles. It swoops out of the dark to attack."aWhen the horns on its head shine in seven colors, it is said to be sharing everlasting life."wWhen its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more."iSome say it can change to an even more powerful form when battling those who threaten the ecosystem."dIt gathers things it likes and passes them through its loop to teleport them to a secret place."iIt expels its internal steam from the arms on its back. It has enough power to blow away a mountain."}It sends its feathers, which are as sharp as blades, flying in attack. Its legs are strong, so its kicks are also formidable."rThis narcissistic Pokémon is a clean freak. If you don't groom it diligently, it will stop listening to you."�It nocks its arrow quills and shoots them at opponents. When it simply can't afford to miss, it tugs the vine on its head to improve its focus."tThe air stored inside the rachises of Decidueye's feathers insulated the Pokémon against Hisui's extreme cold."�If you try too hard to get close to it, it won't open up to you. Even if you do grow close, giving it too much affection is still a no-no."�It can act spoiled if it grows close to its Trainer. A powerful Pokémon, its sharp claws can leave its Trainer's whole body covered in scratches."�Although it's rough mannered and egotistical, it finds beating down unworthy opponents boring. It gets motivated for stronger opponents."^The balloons it inflates with its nose grow larger and larger as it practices day by day."It gets excited when it sees a dance it doesn't know. This hard worker practices diligently until it can learn that dance."fTo Primarina, every battle is a stage. It takes down its prey with beautiful singing and dancing."yIt pecks at trees with its hard beak. You can get some idea of its mood or condition from the rhythm of its pecking."WIt can bend the tip of its beak to produce over a hundred different cries at will."~They smack beaks with others of their kind to communicate. The strength and number of hits tell each other how they feel."}It wanders around in a never-ending search for food. At dusk, it collapses from exhaustion and falls asleep on the spot."lOnce it finds signs of prey, it will patiently stake out the location, waiting until the sun goes down."kIf you find its nest, you shouldn't stick your hand inside. You'll get bitten by an irritated Grubbin."�It buries itself in fallen leaves and barely moves, munching away on humus. If you accidentally step on one, you'll get a shock!"�It has an organ that generates electricity in its abdomen. It concentrates energy in its jaws and fires off jolts of electricity."yIts hard pincers are well suited to both offense and defense. Fights between two Crabrawler are like boxing matches."jIt stores coldness in its pincers and pummels its foes. It can even smash thick walls of ice to bits!"�It wins the hearts of its enemies with its passionate dancing and then uses the opening it creates to burn them up with blazing flames."�Cutiefly is able to detect the aura of living things, which it uses to find flowers. Cutiefly tend to gather around beings feeling strong emotions."�Ribombee hates rain as it turns its hair dirty and its pollen damp. When storms are on the horizon, Ribombee hides in tree hollows waiting for it to pass."�As they develop, their disposition grows more violent and aggressive. Many Trainers find them too much to handle and abandon them."xThe sharp rocks in its mane can cut like knives. Lycanroc wears its prey down by degrees before finishing them off."�Bathed in the setting sun of evening, Wolferoc has undergone a special kind of evolution. An intense fighting spirit underlies its calmness."�It goads enemies into attacking, withstands the hits, and in return, delivers a headbutt, crushing their bones with its rocky mane."{They're weak, so they move in schools. However, they can also often be seen all alone, having strayed from the school."|They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off."To attack, this Pokémon sends toxic spikes flying at its enemies. Ones that come close get mown down by the claws on its feet."�It loves playing in the mud. If it isn't showered with mud on a daily basis, it gets stressed out and stops listening to its Trainer."It remains calm and unmoving no matter the situation. It mixes dirt with the saliva in its mouth to make a special kind of mud."�When two Dewpider meet, they display their water bubbles to each other. Then the one with the smaller bubble gets out of the other's way."|It usually passes its time in the water. When its belly is full, it stores its subdued prey in the water bubble on its head."When the sun rises, Fomantis spreads its four leaves and bathes in the sunlight. The tip of its head has a pleasant aroma."dFor self-protection, it pretends to be a bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear keen-edged petals."�It scatters its shining spores around itself. Even though they're dangerous, nighttime tours of forests where Morelull live are popular."�It puts its prey to sleep and siphons off their vitality through the tip of its arms. If one of its kind is weakened, it helps by sending it vitality."`The males will do whatever the females tell them. They give the females most of their food."kSalazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it."�It boasts power enough to split large trees in half. The organ on its rear releases an odor that it uses to communicate with others of its kind."}It waves its hands wildly in intimidation and warning. Life is over for anyone who doesn't run away as fast as possible."wBecause of its sweet, delicious aroma, bird Pokémon are always after it, but it's not intelligent enough to care."�It's protected by its hard sepals, so it plays with bird Pokémon without worry. They peck it relentlessly, but it doesn't care."jA master of grand and beautiful kicks, it can knock out even kickboxing champions with a single blow."�It stretches sticky vines out from its head and picks flowers to adorn itself with. When it doesn't have any flowers, it feels uneasy."|It normally spends its time meditating in the treetops. It throws Poké Balls and gives other Pokémon orders as it pleases."�They use their saliva to stick leaves to their shoulders. You can tell what troop they belong to from the position of the leaves."wIt will pick up anything it finds on the ground. Sometimes it finds coins, so Murkrow and Meowth will go after it."gThe shell covering its body is as hard as diamond. This Pokémon will do anything it takes to win."tIt likes the shovel on its head, so Sandygast will get serious and fight any children who come to take it back."�Each of its grains of sand has its own will. Palossand eats small Pokémon and siphons away their vital essence while they're still alive."�The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore."~A Pokémon weapon developed for a specific mission, it went berserk during an experiment, so it was cryogenically frozen."rThis is its form once it has awakened and evolved. Freed from its heavy mask, its speed is greatly increased."|It lives in the ozone layer, where it becomes food for stronger Pokémon. When it tries to run away, it falls to the ground."lIt stays asleep from the moment it's born. When it falls into a deep sleep, it stops moving altogether."�It lives in volcanoes and eats sulfur and other minerals. Materials from the food it eats form the basis of its explosive shell."`When it's surprised or agitated, the 14 fur spikes on its back will stand up involuntarily."�Although it's a quiet, lonely Pokémon, if you try to look at what's under its rag, it will become agitated and resist violently."�It burrows beneath the sand, radiating psychic power from the protuberance on its head. It waits for prey as it surveys the area."rIf a child it has made friends with is bullied, Drampa will find the bully's house and burn it to the ground."wIt wraps its prey in green seaweed and sucks away their vitality. It only likes to go after big prey like Wailord."�It smacks the scales on its head against rocks or against the ground to frighten its opponents. It can also contact its friends with these noises."lIt makes noise by clanging its scales together. When the rhythm has reached its peak, Hakamo-o attacks."~When it howls after finishing off its prey, the metallic sounds of its celebrating comrades can be heard from all around."�Although it's called a guardian deity, if a person or Pokémon puts it in a bad mood, it will become a malevolent deity and attack."�It heals the wounds of people and Pokémon by sprinkling them with its sparkling scales. This guardian deity is worshiped on Akala."dAlthough it's called a guardian deity, it's violent enough to crush anyone it sees as an enemy."�This guardian deity of Poni Island manipulates water. Because it lives deep within a thick fog, it came to be both feared and revered."oEven though its helpless, gaseous body can be blown away by the slightest breeze, it doesn't seem to care."yThe king who ruled Alola in times of antiquity called it the "cocoon of the stars" and built an altar to worship it."�Sometimes the result of its opening an Ultra Wormhole is that energy and life-forms from other worlds are called here to this world."yRecords of it exist in writings from long, long ago, where it was known by the name "the beast that calls the moon.""~It looks somehow pained as it rages around in search of light, which serves as its energy. It's apparently from another world."fA life-form from another world, it was dubbed a UB and is thought to produce a strong neurotoxin."|Although it's alien to this world and a danger here, it's apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives."mA life-form that lives in another world, its body is thin and supple, but it also possesses great power."�One of the mysterious life-forms known as Ultra Beasts. Astonishing electric shocks emanate from its entire body, according to witnesses."fOne of the dangerous UBs, high energy readings can be detected coming from both of its huge arms."SThis Ultra Beast's body, which is as thin as paper, is like a sharpened sword."zA dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found."\This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world."oIt stores hundreds of liters of poisonous liquid inside its body. It is one of the organisms known as UBs."|It appeared from an Ultra Wormhole. Each one appears to be made up of many life-forms stacked one on top of each other."�It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the explosion of its own head. It's apparently one kind of Ultra Beast."�It synchronizes its consciousness with others to understand their feelings. This faculty makes it useful for taking care of people."�It slips into the shadows of others and mimics their powers and movements. As it improves, it becomes stronger than those it's imitating."�It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they'll be electrocuted by the flying sparks."{It melts particles of iron and other metals found in the subsoil, so it can absorb them into its body of molten steel."Revered long ago for its capacity to create iron from nothing, for some reason it has come back to life after 3,000 years."nIt attacks with rapid beats of its stick. As it strikes with amazing speed, it gets more and more pumped."�When it's drumming out rapid beats in battle, it gets so caught up in the rhythm that it won't even notice that it's already knocked out its opponent."zBy drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle."�It has special pads on the backs of its feet, and one on its nose. Once it's raring to fight, these pads radiate tremendous heat."sIt kicks berries right off the branches of trees and then juggles them with its feet, practicing its footwork."�It's skilled at both offense and defense, and it gets pumped up when cheered on. But if it starts showboating, it could put itself in a tough spot."mWhen it gets wet, its skin changes color, and this Pokémon becomes invisible as if it were camouflaged."mHighly intelligent but also very lazy, it keeps enemies out of its territory by laying traps everywhere."�Its nictitating membranes let it pick out foes' weak points so it can precisely blast them with water that shoots from its fingertips at Mach 3."�It eats berries nonstop, a habit that has made it more resilient than it looks. It'll show up on farms, searching for yet more berries."zCommon throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon has strong teeth and can chew through the toughest of berry shells."�Jumping nimbly about, this small-bodied Pokémon takes advantage of even the slightest opportunity to disorient larger opponents."eThe lessons of many harsh battles have taught it how to accurately judge an opponent's strength."With their great intellect and flying skills, these Pokémon very successfully act as the Galar region's airborne taxi service."iOften found in gardens, this Pokémon has hairs on its body that it uses to assess its surroundings."xAs it grows inside its shell, it uses its psychic abilities to monitor the outside world and prepare for evolution."{It emits psychic energy to observe and study what's around it, and what's around it can include things over six miles away."�Cunning and cautious, this Pokémon survives by stealing food from others. It erases its tracks with swipes of its tail as it makes off with its plunder."lWith a lithe body and sharp claws, it goes around stealing food and eggs. Boltund is its natural enemy."~It whirls around in the wind while singing a joyous song. This delightful display has charmed many into raising this Pokémon."rThe cotton on the head of this Pokémon can be spun into a glossy, gorgeous yarn, a Galar regional specialty."}If its fleece grows too long, Wooloo won't be able to move. Cloth made with the wool of this Pokémon is surprisingly strong."dIts majestic horns are meant only to impress the opposite gender. They never see use in battle."�It starts off battles by attacking with its rock-hard horn, but as soon as the opponent flinches, this Pokémon bites down and never lets go."xThis Pokémon rapidly extends its retractable neck to sink its sharp fangs into distant enemies and take them down."�It balances itself like a sumo wrestler, making it nearly impossible to topple. Its squishy flesh is even more resilent than its shell."This gluttonous Pokémon only assists people with their work because it wants treats. As it runs, it crackles with electricity."rIt sends electricity through its legs to boost their strength. Running at top speed, it easily breaks 50 mph."`It can race around like a unicycle, even on rough, rocky terrain. Burning coal sustains it."�By rapidly rolling its legs, it can travel at over 18 mph. The temperature of the flames it breathes exceeds 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit."}While it's engaged in battle, its mountain of coal will burn bright red, sending off sparks that scorch the surrounding area."gAs soon as it's born, it burrows into an apple. The apple serves as both a food source and a home."sIt flies on wings of apple skin and spits a powerful acid. It can also change its shape into that of an apple."}A nectarous scent wafts from its body, luring in the bug Pokémon it preys on. The skin on its back is especially yummy."�The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out."cSeven syrpents live inside an apple made of syrup. The syrpent in the center is the commander."eIt spews sand from its nostrils. While the enemy is blinded, it burrows into the ground to hide."^Its unique style of coiling allows it to blast sand out of its sand sac more efficiently."�Its rough belly scales can pulverize entire quarries for sand to use in battle. Its fights with Flygon in the center of desert storms are the stuff of legend."�This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda whole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake and tries to swallow a Pokémon other than its preferred prey."nAfter it's eaten its fill, its movements become extremely sluggish. That's when Cramorant swallows it up."�It spins its tail fins to propel itself, surging forward at speeds of over 100 knots before ramming prey and spearing into them."�It manipulates the chemical makeup of its poison to produce electricity. The voltage is weak, but it can cause a tingling paralysis."lThis short-tempered and aggressive Pokémon chugs stagnant water to absorb any toxins it might contain."�It subconsciously broadcasts the audio of its battles over radio waves. Tuning in at the right time will let you hear the performance of a lifetime."�It wraps prey up with its heated body, cooking them in its coils. Once they're well-done, it will voraciously nibble them down to the last morsel."~While its burning body is already dangerous on its own, this excessively hostile Pokémon also has large and very sharp fangs."�Even solid titanium will melt in its coils. It uses the massive mirage it creates to confuse Volcarona in their frequent contests."�Its tentacles tear off easily, but it isn't alarmed when that happens, it knows they'll grow back. It's about as smart as a three-year-old."{Searching for an opponent to test its skills against, it emerges onto land. Once the battle is over, it returns to the sea."{The teacup in which this Pokémon makes its home is a famous piece of antique tableware. Many forgeries are in circulation."�Leaving leftover black tea unattended is asking for this Pokémon to come along and pour itself into it, turning the tea into a new Polteageist."pIt spends days relaxing on the beach. Its rest is often interrupted by someone who confuses it for a drink."lDespite its refreshing scent, those who drink of its colorful liquid are swiftly put into a deep sleep."sIf this Pokémon senses a strong emotion, it will run away as fast as it can. It prefers areas without people."�Using the braids on its head, it pummels foes to get them to quiet down. One blow from those braids would knock out a professional boxer."�If you're too loud around it, you risk being torn apart by the claws on its tentacle. This Pokémon is also known as the Forest Witch."tIt sneaks into people's homes, stealing things and feasting on the negative energy of the frustrated occupants."tWith sly cunning, it tries to lure people into the woods. Some believe it to have the power to make crops grow."}Its hairs work like muscle fibers. When its hairs unfurl, they latch on to opponents, ensnaring them as tentacles would."\They say that any patisserie visited by Milcery is guaranteed success and good fortune."_When Alcremie is content, the cream it secretes from its hands becomes sweeter and richer."�So tall it seems to defy the heavens, it lords its elevated position over other Pokémon. It grants its Trainer knowledge of sweet and sour."�The six of them work together as one Pokémon. Teamwork is also their battle strategy, and they constantly change their formation as they fight."�It stores electricity in each spine. Even if one gets broken off, it still continues to emit electricity for at least three hours."|It eats snow that piles up on the ground. The more snow it eats, the bigger and more impressive the spikes on its back grow."�It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away."pOnce a year, on a specific date and at a specific time, they gather out of nowhere and form up in a circle."�This Pokémon keeps its heat-sensitive head cool with ice. It fishes for its food, dangling its single hair into the sea to lure in prey."{Through its horns, it can pick up on the emotions of creatures around it. Positive emotions are the source of its strength."�It carries electrically roasted seeds with it as if they're precious treasures. No matter how much it eats, it always gets hungry again in short order."�If a job requires serious strength, this Pokémon will excel at it. Its copper body tarnishes in the rain, turning a vibrant green color."~These Pokémon live in herds. Their trunks have incredible grip strength, strong enough to crush giant rocks into powder."�After evolution, it has taken on the appearance of a great monument. If revered, it will protect nearby villages from all manner of disaster."|The powerful muscles in its tail generate its electricity. Compared to its lower body, its upper half is entirely too small."�This Pokémon lived on prehistoric seashores and was able to preserve food with the ice on its body. It went extinct because it moved so slowly."Its mighty legs are capable of running at speeds exceeding 40 mph, but this Pokémon can't breathe unless it's underwater."sThe skin on its face is impervious to attack, but breathing difficulties made this Pokémon go extinct anyway."�The special metal that composes its body is very light, so this Pokémon has considerable agility. It lives in caves because it dislikes the rain."�Nostalgic for the cavern home it has outgrown, it will weep molten glass. Those without trainers may find company serving as rookeries for bird Pokémon."|It gathers static electricity from its surroundings. The beams it launches when down on all fours are tremendously powerful."�If this weak Pokémon is by itself, a mere child could defeat it. But if Dreepy has friends to help it train, it can evolve and become much stronger."�Without a Dreepy to place on its head and care for, it gets so uneasy it'll try to substitute any Pokémon it finds for the missing Dreepy."nApparently the Dreepy inside Dragapult's horns eagerly look forward to being launched out at Mach speeds."{This Pokémon has slumbered for many years. Some say it's Zamazenta's elder sister, others say the two Pokémon are rivals."{This Pokémon slept for aeons while in the form of a statue. It was asleep for so long, people forgot that it ever existed."�It was inside a meteorite that fell 20,000 years ago. There seems to be a connection between this Pokémon and the Dynamax phenomenon."~If Kubfu pulls the long white hair on its head, its fighting spirit heightens and power wells up from the depths of its belly."�Inhabiting the mountains of a distant region, this Pokémon races across sheer cliffs, training its legs and refining its moves."{Once the vines on Zarude's body tear off, they become nutrients in the soil. This helps the plants of the forest grow."xGlastrier has tremendous physical strength, and the mask of ice covering its face is 100 times harder than diamond."|As it dashes through the night, Spectrier absorbs the life-force of sleeping creatures. It craves silence and solitude."�Calyrex is a merciful Pokémon, capable of providing healing and blessings. It has the power to cause hearts to mend and plants to spring forth."@This Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system."GThis Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system. Again!"{This is the form Castform takes on the brightest of days. Its skin is unexpectedly hot to the touch, so approach with care."|This is the form Castform takes when soaked with rain. When its body is compressed, water will seep out as if from a sponge."�This is the form Castform takes when covered in snow. Its body becomes an ice-like material, with a temperature near -5 degrees Celsius."uThis is the form Castform takes when sand sweeps up. Its body is made of particles that are constantly spinning."yThis is the form Castform takes when the moon rises. The particles in its body take on mystical fae-like properties."|This is the form Castform takes when an eclipse covers the sky. It moves around using its hands made of pure psychic energy."|This Rotom has possessed a convection microwave oven that uses a special motor. It also has a flair for manipulating flames."yThis form of Rotom enjoys coming up with water-based pranks. Be careful with it if you don't want your room flooded."zRotom assumes this form when it takes over a refrigerator powered by a special motor. It battles by spewing cold air."�In this form, Rotom applies its new power over wind to its love of pranks. It will happily blow away any important documents it can find."�This is Rotom after it's seized control of a lawn mower that has a special motor. As it mows down grass, it scatters the clippings everywhere."�Radiant light caused Dialga to take on a form with the appearance of the creator. Dialga now wields such colossal strength that this must be its true form."�It soars across the sky in a form that greatly resembles the creator of all things. Perhaps this is Palkia's strategy for gaining Arceus's powers."�Giratina loses its legs upon changing into this form. This Pokémon must hail from a world where the heavens and the earth are as one."Even Basculin, which devours everything it can with its huge jaws, is nothing more than food to organisms stronger than itself."rIt has foreseen that a world of truth will arrive for people and Pokémon. It strives to protect that future."It's said that this Pokémon battles in order to protect the ideal world that will exist in the future for people and Pokémon."xThe power that lay hidden in its body now covers its horn, turning it into a sword that can slice through anything."mSpirits that wander this world are placed into Pumpkaboo's body. They're then moved on to the afterlife."mWhen taking spirits to the afterlife, large Pumpkaboo prefer the spirits of adults to those of children."gMassive Pumpkaboo are said to be the product of areas where a great number of lost souls lingered."�Eerie cries emanate from its body in the dead of night. The sounds are said to be the wails of spirits who are suffering in the afterlife."lLarge Gourgeist put on the guise of adults, taking the hands of children to lead them to the afterlife."^Supersized Gourgeist aren't picky. They will forcefully drag anyone off to the afterlife."�This is Zygarde when about 10% of its pieces have been assembled. It leaps at its opponent's chest and sinks its sharp fangs into them."|This is Zygarde's perfected form. From the orifice on its chest, it radiates high-powered energy that eliminates everything."�It creates an electric charge by rubbing its feathers together. It dances over to its enemies and delivers shocking electrical punches."tThis Oricorio relaxes by swaying gently. This increases its psychic energy, which it then fires at its enemies."tIt summons the dead with its dreamy dancing. From their malice, it draws power with which to curse its enemies."�Weak Wishiwashi school together to concentrate their power. Their united force makes them the demon of the sea, feared near and far."�If its core stays exposed, it will soon die off. It's possible that it may survive if it's put into a Poké Ball quickly enough."{Sad that its true identity may be exposed, Mimikyu will mercilessly seek revenge on any opponent that breaks its neck."|This is Necrozma's form while it's absorbing the power of Solgaleo, making it extremely ferocious and impossible to control."yLunala no longer has a will of its own. Now under the control of Necrozma, it continuously expels all of its energy."sThe light pouring out from all over its body affects living things and nature, impacting them in various ways."pThe slightest shock is sometimes enough to get this Pokémon to spit out the Arrokuda lodged in its throat."{The half-swallowed Pikachu is so startled that it isn't struggling yet, but it's still looking for a chance to strike back."�The hair on its head connects to the surface of its brain. When this Pokémon has something on its mind, its hair chills the air around it."�They diligently serve people and Pokémon so they can gather feelings of gratitude. The females are particularly good at babysitting."rHunger hormones affect its temperament. Until its hunger is appeased, it gets up to all manner of evil deeds."�Able to cut down anything with a single strike, it became known as the Fairy King's Sword, and it inspired awe in friend and foe alike."zNow that it's equipped with its shield, it can shrug off impressive blows, including the attacks of Dynamax Pokémon."�This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in defeating foes by raining many blows down on them. Its strikes are nonstop, flowing like a river."~It's said that this Pokémon once moved a large forest—and all the Pokémon living there—to a new location overnight."�Legend says that by using its power to see all events from past to future, this Pokémon saved the creatures of a forest from a meteorite strike."jWhen wounded, it stops moving. It goes as still as stone to meditate, sharpening its mind and spirit."�Darmanitan takes this form when enraged. It won't stop spewing flames until its rage has settled, even if its body starts to melt."�This form has gotten enough energy to go further beyond a normal Ampharos' power. It has been calculated that each orb has over 9000 volts of energy each in it."�Garchomp taking this form are rare due to its specific conditions required. This is good as it can turn a house into splinters if left unchecked."�The already aggressive Gyarados is only amplified by this form. All it can feel in this form is pure rage. Cruise ships have been bisected for getting in its path."�The pain of seeing those it cares for fall has brought out this form. Its pure heart powers its abilities to be much more powerful."|The pain of seeing those it wishes to protect fall has causes this form to emerge. Its red blades are powered by pure heart."|Psychic power has augmented its muscles. Its arms are able to stretch up to ten feet, and it can crush titanium in its grip."�The DNA from the original Mew has grown exponentially in this form. It has gained enough psychic power to control the minds of even the strongest willed people."zIt differs from other Basculin in several respects, including demeanor. It is much gentler than other color variants."vThis special Ursaluna can see in the dark with its left eye and protects itself with mud that is as hard as iron.">This form also exists to test the PBS Extensions feature.[_"�Se le puede ver durmiendo la siesta a la luz del sol. Hay una semilla en su espalda. Al absorber los rayos del sol, la semilla crece progresivamente."�Para sostener su bulbo, sus patas crecen fuertes. Si pasa más tiempo tumbado a la luz del sol, el capullo pronto se convertirá en una gran flor."�Se dice que la flor de Venusaur adquiere colores vivos si recibe mucha nutrición y luz solar. El aroma de la flor alivia las emociones de las personas."�La llama que arde en la punta de su cola es una indicación de sus emociones. La llama oscila cuando Charmander está feliz y arde cuando está enfadado."�Sus afiladas garras destruyen a los enemigos. Si se encuentra con un enemigo fuerte, se agita y la llama de su cola adquiere un color blanco azulado."�Vuela en busca de oponentes fuertes. Exhala llamas intensas que pueden derretir cualquier material. Nunca quemará a un enemigo más débil."�Su caparazón no es solo para protección. Su forma redondeada y las ranuras minimizan la resistencia en el agua, lo que le permite nadar a altas velocidades."Su gran cola está cubierta con un pelaje rico y espeso. Los rasguños en su caparazón son evidencia de su dureza  en combate."�Las trombas de agua que sobresalen de su caparazón son muy precisas. Sus balas de agua pueden clavar con precisión latas a más de 48 metros de distancia."�Su apetito voraz lo obliga a devorar hojas más grandes que él sin dudarlo. Desprende un olor terriblemente fuerte de sus antenas."�Su caparazón es tan duro como una losa de hierro. No se mueve mucho porque está preparando sus suaves entrañas para evolucionar dentro del caparazón."�Tiene una habilidad superior para buscar miel de las flores. Puede buscar, extraer y transportar miel a más de 10 kilómetros de distancia."�El poder evolutivo sobrecargó sus alas y escamas venenosas, las cuales se convertirán pura energía a la mínima provocación."�Tiene un sentido del olfato extremadamente agudo. Distingue sus tipos de hojas favoritas de las que no le gustan olfateándolas con su gran nariz."�Permanece inmóvil mientras se aferra a un árbol. Sin embargo, se prepara para la evolución. Esto es evidente por lo caliente que es su caparazón."�Un Beedrill es extremadamente territorial. Por razones de seguridad, nadie debe acercarse nunca a su nido. Si se enfada, atacará en un enjambre."�Su evolución final aumentó su instintos asesinos más allá del límite. Obedece a su entrenador sin rechistar, pero se impacientará sin una buena batalla."�Tiene un sentido de la orientación muy agudo. Puede regresar a casa a su nido infaliblemente, sin importar lo lejos que esté de su entorno familiar."�Vuela patrullando su gran territorio. Si se viola su espacio vital, no muestra piedad al castigar a fondo al enemigo con sus afiladas garras."�Este Pokémon tiene unas plumas preciosas. Muchos Entrenadores quedan tan cautivados por las plumas de su cabeza que lo eligen como su Pokémon."�Es extremadamente cauteloso. Incluso cuando está dormido, mueve constantemente las orejas y escucha el peligro. Hará su nido en cualquier lugar."�Sus robustos colmillos crecen constantemente. Para mantenerlos firmes, roe rocas y troncos. Incluso puede masticar las paredes de las casas."mNo le interesa nada que no esté fresco. Si lo llevas de compras, te ayudará a elegir los ingredientes."lHace que sus Rattata súbditos le traigan comida, y se alimenta de sólo la más nutritiva y deliciosa."�Su grito se puede escuchar a más de 8 Km. Si su agudo grito se escucha resonando por todas partes, es una señal de que están advirtiendo de un peligro."�Su cuello largo y pico alargado son ideales para atrapar presas en el suelo o el agua. Mueve hábilmente este pico alargado y delgado para atrapar presas."�Se enrosca en espiral mientras descansa. Esta posición le permite responder rápidamente a un enemigo desde cualquier dirección con la cabeza levantada."�Tiene un poder de constricción muy fuerte. Incluso puede aplastar bidones de acero. Una vez se enrosca alrededor de su enemigo, escapar es imposible."�Es incapaz de retener la electricidad. Cuando se sobresalta, descarga energía accidentalmente. Retiene mejor la energía a medida que envejece."�Almacena electricidad en las bolsas de sus mejillas. Cuando libera energía reprimida en un estallido, la energía eléctrica es igual a la de un rayo."�Si almacena demasiada electricidad, su comportamiento se vuelve agresivo. Para evitarlo, de vez en cuando descarga el exceso de energía y se calma."�Raremente, un Pikachu crece a un tamaño increíble en vez de evolucionar a Raichu. Puede alimentar centrales siempre y cuando sea alimentado apropiadamente."pPuede descargar 100,000 voltios de electricidad, acabando instántaneamente con rivales mucho más grandes."�Cuando se enrosca en una bola, hace que cualquier ataque rebote sin causar daño. Su piel se ha vuelto dura y sólida al vivir en el desierto."�Se enrosca en una bola para protegerse de los ataques enemigos. También para evitar un golpe de calor durante el día cuando las temperaturas suben mucho."mLa vida en las montañas lo cubrió de tanta nieve que obtuvo un cuerpo de hielo tan duro como el acero."xVive en montañas nevadas. Cuando una ventisca se levanta, se resguarda en la nieva para no ser levantado por esta."�Se cree que sus púas altamente tóxicas se desarrollaron como protección de su pequeño cuerpo. Cuando se enfurece, libera una toxina de su cuerno."�Cuando está con sus amigos o familiares, sus púas se guardan para evitar lesiones. Parece ponerse nervioso si se separa de los demás."�Es experto en enviar a los enemigos por los aires con duros placajes usando su cuerpo duro y escamoso. Es más fuerte cuando defiende a sus crías."�Ha desarrollado músculos que mueven libremente sus orejas en cualquier dirección. Incluso el más mínimo sonido no escapa a la atención de este Pokémon."�Su cuerno es más duro que un diamante. Si detecta una presencia hostil, todas las púas de su espalda se erizan a la vez y desafía a su rival."�Su cola gruesa contiene un poder destructivo capaz de derribar una torre de transmisión de metal. Una vez que se vuelve loco, no hay forma de detenerlo."�En las noches con muchas estrellas fugaces, se les puede ver bailando en un círculo hasta el amanecer, cuando sacian su sed con el rocío de la mañana."�Todas las noches de luna llena, salen a jugar. Cuando llega el amanecer, se van a dormir acurrucados unos contra otros en las montañas profundas."�Usa sus alas para dar saltitos como si estuviera volando. Su paso le permite incluso caminar sobre el agua. En las noches tranquilas se pasea por los lagos."�Al momento de su nacimiento, tiene una cola blanca. Se separa en seis si este Pokémon recibe mucho amor. Las seis colas se rizan magníficamente."�Durante mucho tiempo se ha dicho que cada una de las nueve colas encarna un poder encantado. Un Ninetales longevo tendrá un pelaje que brilla como el oro."}En climas cálidos, este Pokémon crea trozos de hielo con sus seis colas y los coloca alrededor de sí mismo para enfriarse."zVivo en montañas siempre cubiertas de nieve y es venerado como una divinidad. Parece estar cubierto en una ventisca."nConstantemente pide regalos a su Entrenador. Necesita acumular muchas cosas caras para poder evolucionar."�Los regalos que recibió se convirtieron en una cola de luz dorada. Ataca usando energía avariciosa pura, ganando poder mientras sea consentido."�Su cuerpo suave y flexible es muy dinámico. Cuando canta continuamente con todas sus fuerzas, su cuerpo se vuelve cada vez más de un color rosa intenso."�Todos se quedan dormidos al oir su canción. Las ondas de su voz cantando coinciden con las ondas cerebrales de alguien en un sueño profundo."�Su pelaje es lo último en lujo. Dormir junto a un Wigglytuff es simplemente divino. Su cuerpo se expande aparentemente sin fin cuando inhala."�Mientras vivían en oscuras cavernas, sus ojos se cerraron gradualmente y los privaron de la visión. Usan ondas ultrasónicas para detectar obstáculos."�Sus colmillos perforan incluso la piel gruesa. Le encanta darse un festín con la sangre de su víctima. Revolotea en la oscuridad y ataca por la espalda."�En el transcurso de la evolución, sus patas traseras se convirtieron en alas. Puede volar todo el día sin tener que detenerse."�Crece absorbiendo la luz de la luna. Durante el día, se entierra, dejando solo sus hojas expuestas para evitar que sus enemigos lo detecten."�Una miel muy nociva sale de su boca. Un poco puede provocar pérdida de memoria. Se dice que algunos fanáticos disfrutan de este hedor abrumador."�En las estaciones en las que produce más polen, el aire a su alrededor se vuelve amarillo con el polvo al caminar. Es muy tóxico y causa parálisis."�El color de sus pétalos adquieren un color más vivo con la luz del sol. Cuando el clima está nublado, intenta invocar al sol con una danza."�Un Paras tiene hongos tochukaso parásitos que crecen en su espalda. Crecen extrayendo nutrientes del huésped. Se valoran como medicina."�Infestan las raíces de los árboles grandes en masa y drenan los nutrientes. Cuando un árbol infestado muere, se trasladan a otro árbol todos a la vez."�Su capa de pelo fino y rígido que cubre todo su cuerpo ha evolucionado para protegerse. Sus grandes ojos detectan hasta las presas minúsculas."�Son nocturnos, solo están activos durante la noche. Su presa favorita son los insectos alrededor de las farolas, atraídos por la luz."�Se crían en la mayoría de las granjas. La razón es simple: dondequiera que caven, la tierra queda perfectamente labrada para cultivar deliciosas cosechas."�Debido a que los trillizos originalmente se separaron de un solo cuerpo, piensan exactamente igual. Trabajan en cooperación para excavar en el suelo."~Su cabeza lleva una forma alterada de pelos metálicos. Cuando se comunica con sus compañeros, sus pelos no dejan de moverse."uSu cabellera dorada le brinda protección. Se dice que quedarte con uno de sus cabellos te traerá mala fortuna."�Retrae sus afiladas garras en sus patas para escapar en silencio. Por alguna razón, le encantan las monedas brillantes que brillan con la luz."�Sus seis audaces bigotes detectan los movimientos del aire para determinar qué hay a su alrededor. Se vuelve dócil si lo agarran por los bigotes."�Los científicos no se deciden si su tamaño inspiró los memes, o ver los memes causaron que Meowth evolucione de forma inesperada."xEs impulsivo, egoísta y vanidoso. Es muy popular entre entrenadores que le gustan darle la atención que necesita."�Su cabeza redonda es un símbolo de riqueza. Los Persian que tienen cabezas más grandes y esponjosas son considerados más hermosos."�Este Pokémon temerario tiene monedas en su frente. Las monedas más oscuras son más duras, y estas son un símbolo de respeto para los Meowth."tDespués de muchas batallas, desarrolló peligrosas garras que se juntan para formar dagas cuando se extienden."�Cuando su dolor de cabeza se intensifica, comienza a usar poderes extraños, pero no recuerda sus poderes, por lo que parece aturdido y desconcertado."�Es un nadador experto. A veces se une a los nadadores competitivos en el entrenamiento. Utiliza poderes psíquicos cuando su frente brilla con luz."�Cuando comienza a temblar y su respiración se vuelve áspera, es una señal de ira. Como esto sucede instantáneamente, no hay tiempo para huir."nSe sabe que se enoja tanto que muere como resultado. Sin embargo, su rostro se ve pacífico en la muerte."�Cuando su ira llegó a un punto más allá del límite, este Pokémon ganó un poder liberado de los límites de su cuerpo físico."�Su excelente sentido del olfato asegura que no olvidará ningún olor. Utiliza su sentido del olfato para detectar las emociones de los demás."�Este Pokémon de pies ligeros recorre más de 10.000 Km en un solo día y noche. El fuego que arde salvajemente dentro de su cuerpo es su fuente de poder."iSus ladridos transmiten un sentimiento majestuoso. Cualquiera que lo escuche se rebajará ante este."�Es posible ver sus entrañas en espiral a través de su piel delgada. La piel también es muy flexible. Incluso los colmillos afilados rebotan en ella."�Su cuerpo siempre está mojado y resbaladiza con un fluido aceitoso. Debido a esto, puede resbalar y escaparse de las garras de cualquier rival."�Sus músculos desarrollados nunca se fatigan, por mucho que se ejercite. Puede nadar de un lado a otro a través de un océano entero sin esfuerzo."�El cabello rizado en su cabeza demuestra su condición de rey. Se dice que cuanto más largo y rizado es el cabello, más respeto se gana de sus pares."�Un Pokémon que duerme 18 horas al día. La observación reveló que usa Teletransporte para cambiar su ubicación una vez cada hora."�Se rumorea que un chico con habilidades psíquicas se transformó en Kadabra mientras ayudaba en la investigación de poderes extrasensoriales."�Si bien tiene fuertes habilidades psíquicas y una gran inteligencia, sus músculos son muy débiles. Usa poder psíquico para mover su cuerpo."�Se somete a un entrenamiento extenuante para dominar todas las artes marciales. Su fuerza le permite cargar a un luchador de sumo sobre sus hombros."�Un Machoke usa un cinturón para mantener su abrumador poder bajo control. Debido a que es tan peligroso, nadie nunca ha quitado el cinturón."�Es imposible defenderse de los puñetazos y tajos repartidos por sus cuatro brazos. Su espíritu de lucha estalla cuando se enfrenta a un oponente duro."�Su cuerpo delgado y flexible le permite doblarse y balancearse para evitar cualquier ataque. Su boca pierde un fluido que derrite incluso el hierro."�Por la noche, cuelga de la rama de un árbol con su parte trasera en forma de gancho y duerme. Si se mueve, puede despertarse en el suelo."�La larga enredadera que se extiende desde su cabeza se agita para atraer presas. Cuando una víctima se acerca, se la traga entera."�Está compuesto casi por completo de agua. Atrapa a su enemigo con sus dos largos tentáculos y los apuñala con aguijones venenosos de sus puntas."�Vive en formaciones rocosas complejas en el fondo del océano y atrapa a sus presas con sus 80 tentáculos. Sus esferas rojas brillan cuando se agita."�Escala senderos de montaña usando solo sus brazos. Debido a que se ven como rocas, los excursionistas pueden pisarlos sin darse cuenta."�Descienden de las montañas dando tumbos por pendientes empinadas. Son tan brutales que destrozan árboles y enormes rocas con atronadoras embestidas."~Se dice que vive en cráteres volcánicos en los picos de las montañas. Una vez al año muda su piel, que vuelve a la tierra."�Los Geodude compiten entre ellos a cabezazos. La arena metálica en sus cabezas se pegará en el que tenga un magnetismo más fuerte."Comen rocas y suelen pelear por ellas. Cuando dos Graveler se embisten entre ellos crean un destello de luz y un fuerte sonido."�Dispara rocas cargadas eléctricamente. Incluso si no es disparada con precisión, con sólo rozar un oponente será aturdido y debilitado."�Es muy débil al nacer. Apenas puede ponerse de pie. Sus piernas se vuelven más fuertes cuando tropieza y cae al tratar de seguir el ritmo de su padre."�Galopa en los campos y las llanuras. Pero una vez que se pone serio, sus melenas de fuego se encienden y resplandecen mientras alcanza los 240 Km/h."xEste Pokémon te mirará a los ojos para leer tu corazón. Si encuentra maldad en este, se esconderá de inmediato."}Audaz y orgulloso, este Pokémon corre a través del bosque, sus pasos seguidos por el poder psíquico guardado en su pelaje."�Atrapa presas sumergiendo la cola en el agua. Pero a menudo se olvida de lo que está haciendo y pasa los días holgazaneando a la orilla del agua."�Su cola tiene un Shellder sujeto con un mordisco. La cola ya no se puede usar para pescar. Esto lo obliga a nadar y atrapar presas."�Emprende investigaciones todos los días para resolver los misterios del mundo. Al parecer, se olvida de todo si se le cae el Shellder de la cabeza."wDebido a su alimentación a base de semillas sólo encontradas en Galar, sus colas desarrollaron un sabor picante."kSi aprieta la lengua del Shellder en su brazo, este disparará veneno desde la punta de su caparazón."jSlowking puede resolver cualquier problema que se le presente, pero nadie puede entender lo que dice."�Las unidades a sus lados son imanes extremadamente poderosos. Generan suficiente magnetismo para atraer objetos de hierro desde más de 90 metros."�En realidad son tres Magnemite unidos por magnetismo. Genera poderosas ondas de radio que elevan las temperaturas en 2,22º C en un radio de 1 Km."mEvolucionó a partir de la exposición a un campo magnético especial. Tres unidades generan magnetismo."�Siempre se le ve con un puerro. Aparentemente, hay puerros buenos y puerros malos. Este Pokémon ocasionalmente pelea para elegir puerros."wLos puerros en Galar son más grandes y gruesos. Los Farfetch'd que se adaptaron a estos tomaron una forma única."�Después de desviar los ataques con su escudo, contraataca con su tallo de puerro afilado. El tallo de puerro es a la vez arma y alimento."�Incluso mientras come o duerme, una de las cabezas permanece siempre atenta a cualquier señal de peligro. Cuando se ve amenazada, huye a más de 96 Km/h."�Una Pokémon con tres cabezas. Corre vigorosamente a través de llanuras cubiertas de hierba incluso en estaciones áridas con poca lluvia."�Seel busca presas en mares gélidos y cubiertos de hielo. Cuando necesita respirar, abre un agujero en el hielo con la parte que sobresale de su cabeza."�Le encanta dormitar sobre el hielo. Hace mucho tiempo, un marinero pensó erróneamente que este Pokémon durmiendo en un glaciar era una sirena."�Nacidos de lodo contaminado en el mar, su comida favorita es cualquier cosa sucia. Se alimentan de las aguas residuales bombeadas de las fábricas."�Prefiere hábitats cálidos y húmedos. En verano, las sustancias tóxicas en su cuerpo se intensifican, haciendo que apeste como basura putrefacta."fUn Grimer que fue traído para resolver un problema con la basura tomó esta forma con el tiempo."|La basura con la que se alimenta causó cambios químicos en su cuerpo, haciendo que su cuerpo sea mucho más colorido."�Por la noche, hace un agujero en el lecho marino con su lengua ancha para dormir. Cierra su caparazón, pero deja la lengua colgando."�Nada en el mar tragando agua y luego lanzándola hacia atrás. El Cloyster dispara púas desde su caparazón utilizando el mismo sistema."�Cuando se expone a un fuerte viento, su cuerpo gaseoso se reduce rápidamente. Se agrupan bajo los aleros de las casas para escapar del viento."�Si un Haunter te llama mientras está flotando en la oscuridad, no te acerques. Este Pokémon intentará lamerte con su lengua y robarte la vida."�En la noche más oscura, tu sombra puede alcanzarte de repente. En realidad, es un Gengar que corre a tu lado, fingiendo ser tu sombra."�Nunca pierde la dirección mientras hace un túnel, gracias a un imán en su cerebro. A medida que envejece, su cuerpo se vuelve más redondo y suave."�Vive incluso más bajo tierra que Onix. Este Pokémon cava hacia el núcleo de la tierra, alcanzando una profundidad de más de 9 Km bajo tierra."�Sus partes cristalinas resisten todo intento de identificarlo. Sus habilidades gravitacionales hacen que sea especulado que los cristales son materia de neutrón."�Si te pica la nariz mientras duermes, es una señal de que un Drowzee está sobre tu almohada tratando de comerse tu sueño a través de tus fosas nasales."�El movimiento de arco y el brillo del péndulo adormecen al enemigo en una profunda hipnosis. Mientras busca presas, pule su péndulo."�Agita su enorme garra de gran tamaño en el aire para comunicarse con los demás. Pero como la garra es tan pesada, este Pokémon se cansa rápidamente."�Tiene un parecido extraño e inexplicable con una Poké Ball. Al explotar al menor impacto, incluso los Entrenadores veteranos la tratan con precaución."ySus garras son tan grandes que si no puede aplastar a su oponente, simplemente los golpeara con el costado de estas."�Tiene un parecido extraño e inexplicable con una Poké Ball. Al explotar al menor impacto, incluso los Entrenadores veteranos la tratan con precaución."�Aparecen en gran número en las centrales eléctricas. Al alimentarse de electricidad, provocan apagones masivos y caóticos en las ciudades cercanas."kCuando se emociona, descarga la electricidad guardada en su barriga, luego se ríe despreocupadamente."fEl tejido en la superficie de su cuerpo es curiosamente similar a la composición de una Bonguri."�Se compone de seis huevos que se cuidan entre sí. Se atraen y dan vueltas. Evoluciona cuando comienzan a aparecer varias grietas."�Originalmente de los trópicos, sus cabezas crecen debido a la exposición a la luz solar. Cuando las cabezas caen, se agrupan para formar un Exeggcute."}Al crecer de forma exagerada, perdió su dependencia a sus poderes psíquicos, y despertó la fuerza de un dragón durmiente."�Suspira por la madre que nunca volverá a ver. Al ver su imagen en la luna llena, llora. Las manchas en el cráneo que lleva son de sus lágrimas."�Un Marowak es un Cubone que se ha endurecido al superar el dolor de perder a su madre. Su espíritu endurecido no se rompe fácilmente."wIts custom is to mourn its lost companions. Mounds of dirt by the side of the road mark the graves of the Marowak."�Tyrogue se estresa si no entrena todos los días. Al criar a este Pokémon, el Entrenador debe establecer un horario regular de entrenamiento."�Sus piernas se estiran y contraen libremente. Lanza patadas devastadoras sobre los enemigos. Después de la batalla, frota sus piernas cansadas."�Se dice que posee el espíritu de un boxeador que aspira a convertirse en campeón mundial. Tener un espíritu indomable significa que nunca se rendirá."�Su técnica de patear mientras gira es una mezcla notable de ataque y defensa. Hitmontop viaja más rápido girando que caminando."�Cada vez que ve algo desconocido, siempre lame el objeto porque memoriza las cosas por la textura y el sabor. Se desanima un poco por las cosas ácidas."oEnvuelve las cosas con su lengua extensible. Si te acercas demasiado a él, te quedarás empapado de baba."�Al acercarte a un Koffing podrás observar, a través de su fina piel, los gases tóxicos que hay en su interior. Explota a la menor estimulación."�Al diluir sus gases tóxicos, se puede extraer el más alto grado de perfume. Para Weezing, los gases de la basura son el festín perfecto."wHace tiempo, cuando el humo de las fábricas contaminaban el aire, Weezing cambió a esta forma por algún motivo."�Una vez que comienza a correr, no se detiene. Su diminuto cerebro lo vuelve tan estúpido que no puede recordar por qué comenzó a correr."�Su cuerno, que gira como un taladro, destruye edificios altos de un solo golpe. Se para sobre sus patas traseras y su cerebro está bien desarrollado."~Pone rocas en agujeros en sus palmas y usa sus músculos para dispararles. Los Geodude son disparados en raras ocasiones."mLe encantan las cosas blancas y redondas. Lleva una piedra en forma de huevo como imitación de Chansey."�Pone huevos excelentes todos los días. Los huevos son tan deliciosos que incluso aquellos que han perdido el apetito los devoran ansiosamente."�Blissey correrá hacia la persona que note triste para compartir un huevo de felicidad que traiga una sonrisa a cualquier rostro."�Sus enredaderas se rompen fácilmente si agarran, lo que le permite escapar. Las enredaderas perdidas son reemplazadas por un nuevas al día siguiente."~Atrapa a sus presas extendiendo los brazos hechos de enredaderas. Perder los brazos ante los depredadores no le preocupa."�Aunque parece una planta, su color verdoso viene de sus escamas color jade. Se dice que verlo a los ojos brinda tres años de mala suerte."�Aunque las serpientes cubriendo su cuerpo son tan duras como el granito, su piel es suave. Los depredadores que ataquen sus brazos tendrán que enfrentarse a sus garras."�Si te encuentras con un joven Kangaskhan jugando solo, nunca intentes atraparlo. Su madre seguramente estará en el área y se enfurecerá violentamente."ZMadre e hija luchan lado a lado, golpeando rápidamente. Su vínculo es impenetrable."�Al mover las aletas de su espalda de lado a lado, se mueve en cualquier dirección mientras mira hacia adelante. Escupe tinta para escapar si siente peligro."�Las púas venenosas sobre su cuerpo son muy apreciadas como ingredientes para la medicina herbal. No muestra piedad con nada que se acerque a su nido."�Duerme tranquilamente, en lo profundo del lecho marino. Cuando sale a la superficie, crea un enorme remolino que puede tragarse incluso a los barcos."�En la primavera, se pueden ver cardúmenes de Goldeen nadando en cascadas y ríos. Inflige un daño asombroso con su único cuerno."�Hace agujeros en las rocas de los lechos de los arroyos. Esta es una innovación que evita que sus huevos sean atacados o arrastrados por la corriente."mCuenta las piedras en los ríos obsesivamente, enojándose si el resultado es un número de mala suerte."�Si ves Pokémon aterradores en fila dentro de un río, hay un Seaking de Makya. Ofrecen bendiciones eternas a cambio de su servicio."�Se reúne con otros en la noche y brilla su núcleo rojo de forma intermitente. Puede regenerar extremidades si se las separan de su cuerpo."�La gente en la antigüedad imaginaba que se transformaba a partir de los reflejos de las estrellas que brillaban en las suaves olas de la noche."pHabitualmente imita a los enemigos. Una vez imitado, el enemigo no puede apartar los ojos de este Pokémon."�Es un maestro de la pantomima. Puede convencer a los demás de que existe algo invisible. Una vez creído, el objeto imaginario se vuelve real."aPuede irradiar frío desde sus pies. Pasará todo el día bailando tap en un piso congelado."jSus divertidos movimientos lo hacen muy popular. Libera su poder psíquico del patrón en su vientre."�Su velocidad cegadoramente rápida se suma a la agudeza de sus guadañas gemelas en el antebrazo. Estas pueden cortar troncos gruesos de un golpe."�Tiene un cuerpo tan duro como el acero. No se inmuta fácilmente por los ataques ordinarios. Agita sus alas para regular la temperatura de su cuerpo."�Sólo Pokémon demasiado agresivos o bien entrenados lo desafiarán a un combate. Sus pinzas pueden convertir a sus rivales en pedazitos."cUna violenta criatura que corta árboles con sus hachas y se escuda con su armadura de piedra."�Corre activamente, pero también se cae con frecuencia. Verifica su reflejo en la superficie de un lago para asegurarse de que su cara no esté sucia."�Se pavonea rítmicamente como si estuviera bailando. Sus movimientos son tan seductores que la gente que lo ve sacude las caderas sin darse cuenta."�Si toca metal y descarga la electricidad que tiene almacenada en su cuerpo, comenzará a balancear sus brazos en círculos para recargarse."�La electricidad impregna su cuerpo. Balancea sus brazos dando vueltas y vueltas para cargar electricidad antes de lanzar un puñetazo."kEmpuja las puntas de sus dos colas contra el enemigo, luego suelta más de 20,000 voltios de energía."�Si un Magby arroja llamas amarillas por la boca, goza de buena salud. Cuando está fatigado, el humo negro se mezclará con las llamas."�Explota llamas intensas por todo su cuerpo para intimidar a su enemigo. Crean ondas de calor que encienden la hierba y los árboles en el área."oLanza bolas de fuego de más de 1.980º C desde los extremos de sus brazos. Vive en cráteres volcánicos."�Sus pinzas son lo bastante fuertes como para romper troncos gruesos. Debido a que no le gusta el frío, excava y duerme bajo tierra en las noches frías."�Cuando su aleteo se vuelve muy intenso, está a punto de embestir con toda velocidad. No es raro que atraviese sus oponentes por edificios."�Se reúnen en los bosques en busca de la savia de los árboles. Está revestido con un caparazón duro como el acero. Usa su cuerno para arrojar a los enemigos."�Se los puede ver observando al cielo, intentando encontrar un lugar en el que pararse cuando inevitablemente intenten cargar el mundo."�No está satisfecho a menos que esté arrasando algo. Si no hay un oponente para que luche, cargará contra los árboles y los derribará para calmarse."nDa más de cinco galones de leche al día. Las personas que no pueden beber leche la convierten en yogur."�Sus músculos de natación son débiles, por lo que se lava fácilmente. En los lugares donde el agua se acumula, hay muchos Magikarp."�Es un Pokémon extremadamente vicioso y violento. Cuando los humanos comiencen a pelear, aparecere y quema todo hasta los cimientos."�La gente ha llevado a Lapras casi a la extinción. Por las noches, se dice que canta quejumbrosamente mientras busca los pocos que quedan de su especie."�El pentagrama alrededor de su cuerpo está hecho de partículas de hielo. Los símbolos son indescifrables, pero algunos dicen haberlo escuchado hablando su propio idioma."�Un Ditto reorganiza su estructura celular para transformarse. Sin embargo, si intenta cambiar en función de su memoria, se equivocará en los detalles."�Tiene una composición genética inestable que repentinamente muta debido a su entorno. La radiación de varias piedras hace que este Pokémon evolucione."�Experimentó una mutación espontánea y le crecieron aletas y branquias que les permiten vivir bajo el agua. Tiene la capacidad de controlar el agua."�Sus células generan energía débil que es amplificada por la electricidad estática de su pelaje para lanzar rayos. El pelaje está hecho de agujas eléctricas."�Su pelaje esponjoso libera calor en el aire para que su cuerpo no se caliente demasiado. Su temperatura corporal puede subir a un máximo de 900º C."�Un Espeon es leal a cualquier Entrenador que considere digno. Se dice que ha desarrollado poderes para proteger a su Entrenador del daño."�Evolucionó a partir de la exposición a la energía de la luna. Acecha a sus enemigos en la oscuridad. Los anillos de su cuerpo brillan cuando ataca."nAl igual que una planta, utiliza la fotosíntesis. Como resultado, siempre está envuelto en aire limpio."sComo técnica de protección, puede congelar completamente su pelaje para que sus pelos se ericen como agujas."�Sylveon's ribbon-like feelers emit an aura that erases any sense of hostility, enabling it to stop fights. Its feelers allow it to read their Trainer's feelings."zSu suavidad, amabilidad, y tamaño masivos lo hacen ser amado por casi todos. Los atacantes no saben dónde comenzar."�Es capaz de revertirse a los datos del programa para ingresar al ciberespacio. Está protegido contra copias, por lo que no se puede duplicar."�Fue creado usando el poder de la ciencia. Se le ha dado inteligencia artificial que le permite aprender nuevos gestos y emociones por sí mismo."{Se instaló un software adicional para convertirlo en un mejor Pokémon. Sin embargo, comenzó a actuar de manera extraña."�¡Confía en la literal firewall de LuxTech! Presentando un tipo único* y protocolos de purgación de punta, esta nueva forma es todo lo que necesitas."�Un Pokémon antiguo y extinto hace mucho tiempo que se ha regenerado a partir de fósiles. Si es atacado, se retrae en su caparazón duro."�Usa sus tentáculos para capturar a su presa. Se extinguió porque su caparazón creció demasiado, lo que hizo que sus movimientos fueran lentos y pesados."{A este Pokémon le gusta juntarse con los Pokémon más fuertes que puede encontrar. Investigadores temen su poder latente."�Algunas personas aseguran que este Pokémon gobernó un reino subterráneo antinatural hace mucho tiempo. Se asemeja a un enemigo de un popular videojuego."�Un Pokémon que se ha regenerado a partir de un fósil. Sin embargo, se han descubierto ejemplos vivos. Kabuto no ha cambiado en 300 millones de años."�Una vez nadaron bajo el agua para cazar presas. Evolucionaron para vivir en la tierra, como lo demuestran los cambios en sus branquias y patas."�Sus fósiles fueron encontrados en lo profundo de las cuevas de Makya. Pero no se parece en nada a criaturas de su era. Se asemeja a un monstruo de un popular videojuego."�Al evolucionar, este Pokémon empezó a asemejarse a otros Pokémon extintos de su tiempo. Se multiplican al convertir biomasa nativa en más Kabuto."�Aerodactyl es un Pokémon de la era de los dinosaurios. Se regeneró a partir de ADN extraído del ámbar. Se imagina que fue el rey de los cielos."xEn tiempos antiguos, este Pokémon era un gran depredador. Tiene la fuerza para cargar un Tyrantrum mientras vuela."\Engulle su peso en comida una vez al día, tragando la comida entera casi sin masticar."�El día típico de Snorlax consiste en comer y dormir. Es un Pokémon tan dócil que hay niños que usan su gran barriga como lugar para jugar."�Muda continuamente su piel vieja. Lo hace porque la energía vital dentro de su cuerpo crece constantemente hasta alcanzar niveles incontrolables."�Almacena una enorme cantidad de energía dentro de su cuerpo. Altera el clima a su alrededor al perder energía de los cristales en su cuello y cola."�Puede dar la vuelta al mundo en solo 16 horas. Es un Pokémon de buen corazón que conduce barcos perdidos y hundidos en una tormenta a tierra."�Es un Pokémon pájaro legendario que controla el hielo. El aleteo de sus alas enfría el aire. Se dice que cuando este Pokémon vuela, cae nieve."~Sus hojas similares a plumas están formadas de energía psíquica que puede cortar un hierro grueso como si fuera papel."�Es un pájaro legendario con la capacidad de controlar la electricidad. Vive en las nubes de tormenta. Obtiene poder si es alcanzado por rayos."�Una patada de sus fuertes piernas pueden pulverizar un cambión. Supuestamente, corre a través montañas a velocidades superiores a 180 m/h."�Es un Pokémon pájaro legendario que puede controlar el fuego. Si está herido, se sumerge en el magma fundido de un volcán para quemarse y curarse."�Su aura siniestra similar al fuego consumirá el espíritu de cualquier criatura que golpee. Las victimas se convierten en sombras de sí mismas."�Fue creado por manipulación genética. Sin embargo, a pesar de que el poder científico de los humanos hizo su cuerpo, no lograron darle un corazón cálido."�Se dice posee los genes de todos los Pokémon. Es capaz de hacerse invisible a voluntad, lo que evita que lo noten incluso si se acerca a las personas."�Agita su hoja para mantener a raya a los enemigos. Una dulce fragancia emana de la hoja, creando una atmósfera amistosa que calma a los luchadores."�Su cuello está rodeado de hojas enrolladas. Dentro de cada hoja hay un pequeño brote de árbol cuya fragancia hace que la gente esté llena de vida."�La fragancia de su flor alivia y calma las emociones. En la batalla, emite más de su aroma tranquilizador para debilitar el espíritu de lucha del enemigo."�Lanza llamas desde su espalda para protegerse. El fuego arde si está enfadado. Cuando está cansado, chisporrotea con una combustión incompleta."�Intimida a los enemigos con ráfagas de llamas y aire sobrecalentado. Su rápida agilidad le permite esquivar ataques mientras abrasa al enemigo."�Puede esconderse detrás de una neblina de calor que crea usando sus llamas. Typhlosion crea explosiones explosivas ardientes que reducen todo a cenizas."�Se dice que purifica las almas perdidas con sus llamas y los guía al más allá. Su forma fue influenciada por la energía del Monte Corona."�A pesar de su pequeño cuerpo, sus mandíbulas son muy poderosas. Si bien puede pensar que solo está mordiendo en broma, puede causar lesiones graves."�Una vez que sus mandíbulas aprisionan a su enemigo, no lo sueltan. Con sus colmillos bifurcados hacia atrás impide que su enemigo escape."�Abre su enorme boca para intimidar a los enemigos. En batalla, corre usando sus poderosas patas traseras para cargar al rival con una gran velocidad."�Se turnan para hacer guardia en la noche. El centinela despierta a los demás si siente peligro. Si uno se separa, se vuelve insomne por el miedo."�Tiene una estructura muy delgada. Cuando es atacado, puede pasar por espacios estrechos y escapar. A pesar de sus extremidades cortas, es muy ágil."}El ojo en su estómago activa sus poderes psíquicos y nunca parpadea. La tierra y el polvo son repelidos telekinéticamente."�Se esconde por la noche, dejándo sólo el ojo en su estómago expuesto. El ojo mirará hacia el espacio mientras el resto duerme."�Tiene un órgano interno que detecta la rotación de la tierra. Usando este órgano especial, Comienza a ulular exactamente a la misma hora todos los días."�Indefectiblemente atrapa presas en la oscuridad. Los Noctowl deben su éxito a la visión superior que les permite ver de noche, y a sus silenciosas alas."}Su plumaje lo insula de todo frío. En invierno dormirá entre montones de nieve, para sólo salir durante la primavera."uCuando su sombra pasa sobre alguien, sentirá un frío horrible. Algunos Entrenadores lo encuentran estimulante."�Se comunican usando un fluido que secretan desde donde las piernas se unen al cuerpo. Pueden transmitir sentimientos a los demás alterando su olor."�Se dice que en tierras con aire limpio, con el cielo estrellado, los Ledian prosperan. Por una buena razón, usan la luz de las estrellas como energía."�La red que teje puede considerarse su segundo sistema nervioso. Puede determinar su presa por las diminutas vibraciones que siente a través de la red."�Sus pies tienen diminutas garras que le permiten escabullirse en techos y paredes verticales. Constriñe a su enemigo con finas y fuertes telarañas de seda."�Cuando siente peligro, descarga electricidad positiva y negativa de sus dos antenas. Vive en profundidades más allá del alcance de la luz solar."�Los orbes que emiten luz en su espalda son muy brillantes. Se forman a partir de su aleta dorsal. Ilumina la oscuridad como la tinta de los mares profundos."�Como energía, utiliza los sentimientos positivos que emanan las personas y los Pokémon. Almacena sentimientos felices en su caparazón para compartirlos."�Se dice que es un Pokémon que trae buena suerte. Cuando ve a alguien que es puro de corazón, aparece un Togetic y comparte su felicidad con ellos."aNunca aparecerá donde haya conflictos. Sus avistamientos se han vuelto raros recientemente."�Sube corriendo a los árboles bajos que crecen en la sabana para picotear los nuevos brotes. Los ojos de un Natu parecen estar siempre observando algo."�Tiene el enigmático poder de prever el futuro. Algunas personas en diferentes tierras han creído durante mucho tiempo que son emisarios de otro mundo."�Su lana esponjosa se frota entre sí y crea una carga estática. Cuanta más energía se carga, más intensamente brilla la bombilla en la punta de su cola."�Su calidad de vellón cambia para generar electricidad estática con una pequeña cantidad de lana. Su piel está protegida contra la electricidad."�Emite tanta luz que se puede ver desde el espacio. En los viejos tiempos, la gente usaba su luz para enviar señales de un lado a otro con otros."�Está cubierto con un pelaje que repele el agua. Debido a ello puede nadar a través del agua a gran velocidad sin que la resistencia del agua lo frene."�Vive en el agua prácticamente todo el día. El color y el patrón de su cuerpo actúan como un camuflaje que dificulta que los enemigos lo detecten"�Su cola es muy saltarina como una pelota de goma. En días soleados, se reúnen en la orilla del agua y chapotean para divertirse."�Parece como si siempre estuviera llorando. En realidad, está ajustando los niveles de fluidos de su cuerpo eliminando el exceso."�Imita a un árbol para evitar enemigos. Pero como sus patas delanteras permanecen verdes durante todo el año, se identifica fácilmente en el invierno."�Va a la deriva con el viento. Si detecta que se aproximan fuertes vientos, un Hoppip se une a otros para prepararse para no ser arrastrado."�Florece cuando la temperatura supera los 64 grados F. Debido a que la floración de su flor cambia con la temperatura, se usa como termómetro."�Salta los vientos cálidos del sur para cruzar el mar y volar al extranjero. Aterriza cuando se encuentra con aire frío mientras está flotando."�Su cola termina con un diestro apéndice parecido a una mano. Sin embargo, debido a que usa tanto la cola, sus manos se han vuelto bastante torpes."ZPara comer, pela hábilmente nueces con sus dos colas. Ahora rara vez usa sus brazos."�Trata de conservar los nutrientes que han almacenado en sus cuerpos para la evolución. No comerán, subsistiendo solo con rocío de la mañana."�Convierte la energía solar en nutrición. Son muy activos durante el día cálido, pero de repente dejan de moverse tan pronto como se pone el sol."�Puede ver 360 grados sin mover los ojos. Es un gran volador capaz de hacer paradas repentinas y girar en el aire para perseguir a su presa."dAl batir sus alas, crea ondas de choque que infligen heridas internas críticas a los enemigos."�Suelen vivir en el agua, pero ocasionalmente salen a tierra en busca de comida. En tierra, cubren sus cuerpos con una película pegajosa y tóxica."�Un Quagsire caza dejando la boca bien abierta en el agua y esperando a que su presa entre por la borda. Como no se mueve, no tiene mucha hambre."�Murkrow era temido como portador de mala fortuna. Muestra un gran interés por cualquier cosa que brille. Incluso intentará robar anillos de mujeres."YAl volverse activo por la noche, se sabe que pulula con numerosos Murkrow a cuestas."�Asusta a la gente con un grito espeluznante y sollozante. Aparentemente usa sus esferas rojas para alimentarse el miedo de sus enemigos."}Sus gritos suenan como encantamientos. Aquellos que los escuchan son atormentados por dolores de cabeza y alucinaciones."�Tiene la forma de caracteres de texto antiguos. Aunque la investigación está en curso, es un misterio qué fue primero, los escritos o los Unown."�Le encanta comer frutas dulces. Las recoge con sus brazos en forma de orejas. Se reúnen en jardines de frutas, atraídos por la fragancia."�Usualmente dócil, un Wobbuffet contraataca ferozmente si su cola negra es atacada. Hace su guarida en cuevas donde espera el anochecer."�Come hierba y brotes de árboles. Mientras come, su cola hace movimientos de masticación y deglución como si también estuviera comiendo."�Ahora que las ondas cerebrales de su cabeza y cola están sincronizadas, el poder psíquico de este Pokémon es 10 veces mayor al de un Girafarig."�Un Pineco se cuelga de una rama y espera la presa. Mientras come, si alguien lo molesta sacudiendo su árbol, cae al suelo y explota."�Se mantiene dentro de su caparazón de acero que se abre cuando está atrapando presas, pero es tan rápido que no se puede ver el interior del caparazón."�Su cola con punta de taladro se usa para excavar en el suelo. Se sabe que este Pokémon hace su nido en las profundidades del suelo."�Este Pokémon usa su dura cola para hacer su nido en lo más profundo del subsuelo. Su nido puede llegar a medir más de 10 kilómetros."oEl amable Dududunsparce pondrá a Pokémon que caigan a su nido en su espalda y los llevará a la entrada."�Se desliza sin hacer un solo sonido. Agarra la cara de su enemigo con sus garras delanteras y traseras, y luego apuñala con su púa venenosa."vObserva a la presa mientras cuelga invertido de las ramas. Cuando se presenta la oportunidad, se lanza en picado."�Al mostrar sus colmillos y hacer una mueca aterradora, los Pokémon más pequeños corren aterrorizados. Parece triste por hacer huir a sus enemigos."�Tiene una mandíbula inferior muy bien desarrollada. Sus enormes colmillos son pesados, le hacen ladear la cabeza. A menos que se asuste, no intentará morder."�Un Qwilfish usa la presión del agua que traga para disparar púas tóxicas por todo su cuerpo. Nadar le resulta algo desafiante."ePescadores odian a este Pokémon porque dispara veneno de sus espinas, que llega a todas partes."�Sus espinas con forma de lanza y temperamento salvaje le ganaron el apodo de "Demonio del Mar". Se alimenta de veneno para curarse."�Un Shuckle se esconde en su caparazón mientras come bayas almacenadas. Las bayas se mezclan con sus fluidos corporales para convertirse en jugo."�Escala árboles clavando sus garras en forma de gancho en la corteza. Busca nidos desprotegidos y roba huevos para comer mientras los padres no están."vViven en regiones frías, formando grupos de cuatro o cinco que cazan presas con una coordinación impresionante."xSus garras curvas son ideales para atravesar acantilados. En la punta de estas garras se encuentra un veneno letal."�Debido al veneno virulento de Sneasler y su tremenda destreza en batalla, ninguna otra especie puede ganarle en los campos congelados."�Se lame las palmas de las manos que se endulzan al estar empapadas en miel. Hace su propia miel mezclando frutas y polen recolectado por Beedrill."�Se dice que hay muchos arroyos y árboles imponentes donde un Ursaring recolecta comida. Camina por su bosque recolectando comida todos los días."�Se cree que el terreno pantanoso de su antigua región de origen le dió a Ursaluna esta forma y la capacidad de manipular la turba."Vive en zonas volcánicas. Si su cuerpo se enfría, su piel se endurece y lo inmoviliza. Para evitarlo, duerme cerca del magma."�Su caparazón está hecho de magma endurecido. Decenas de miles de años viviendo en cráteres volcánicos ha convertido su cuerpo en magma."�Busca comida frotando su hocico contra el suelo. Le gustan los hongos que crecen bajo la hierba seca. De vez en cuando busca fuentes termales."�Está cubierto por una gruesa capa de pelo largo para soportar el frío. Usa sus colmillos para desenterrar comida que está bajo el hielo."Se extrajo un Mamoswine congelado del hielo que data de hace 10.000 años. Este Pokémon existe desde hace mucho, mucho tiempo."�Corsola vive en los cálidos mares del sur. Si el mar se contamina, los hermosos tallos de coral se decoloran y se deshacen en jirones."{Las ramas que le brotan de la cabeza se regeneran si se rompen. Las más bellas se emplean como amuleto en los partos."|Un cambio climático repentino acabó con esta especie de Corsola. Absorbe la fuerza vital de otros mediante sus ramas."sTen cuidado con el cuerpo ectoplasmático que rodea su alma. Si lo tocas, te pondrás rígido como una piedra."�Usa sus músculos abdominales para expulsar el agua tragada, luego derriba presas voladoras. Cuando se acerca la evolución, viaja río abajo."�Atrapa a su enemigo con sus tentáculos con ventosas antes de asestar el golpe final. Si el enemigo es demasiado fuerte, escupe tinta para escapar."_Un Pokémon amistoso que captura los sutiles flujos de agua de mar usando sus dos antenas."�En los días soleados, se pueden ver cardúmenes de Mantine saltando elegantemente sobre las olas. No le molesta el Remoraid en su ala."�La comida se pudre y la leche se corta en su presencia. Dado a esto, comúnmente escapan de Pokémon enojados como Miltank o Alcremie."�Bombardea a casas con un poderoso granizo, intentando que aquellos dentro abran una puerta o ventana. Las personas solían importar Skarmory para defenderse de ellos."�Lleva comida envuelta en su cola. Un famoso explorador logró escalar la montaña más alta del mundo gracias a que un Delibird compartió su comida."�Un Pokémon que tiene cuerpo y alas de acero. La gente en el pasado usaba plumas caídas de Skarmory para hacer espadas y cuchillos."�Se comunican entre sí usando una variedad de gritos para acorralar a sus presas. El trabajo en equipo de este Pokémon es simplemente incomparable."�En una manada de Houndoom, el que tiene los cuernos afilados hacia atrás cumple un rol de liderazgo. Eligen a su líder peleando entre ellos."�Son los corceles del Alto Mando del Apocalipsis, y sus aullidos se escucharán en el final de los tiempos... o así dicen las historias."�Sus grandes orejas sirven como amplios abanicos. Cuando hace calor, agita las orejas para refrescarse. Incluso los jóvenes son muy fuertes."wEs tan fuerte que puede transportar fácilmente un camión volquete. Su piel se ha endurecido tanto como una roca."�Sus magníficos cuernos alguna vez se vendieron a precios elevados como obras de arte. Como resultado, fue cazado al borde de la extinción."�Los orbes negros brillan con una luz insólita cuando el Pokémon coloca una barrera invisible. El pelaje de su barba conserva bien el calor."�Marca su territorio usando un fluido que se escapa de la punta de su cola. Se han encontrado unas 5.000 marcas diferentes de este Pokémon."�Nace en las profundidades de la tierra. Debe abrirse camino a través del suelo y llegar a la superficie para que pueda ver las caras de sus padres."�Un Pupitar crea un gas dentro de su cuerpo que expulsa bajo compresión para impulsarse. Su cuerpo puede resistir una colisión con acero sólido."|Puede derribar una montaña entera para hacer su nido. Vaga por las montañas en busca de nuevos oponentes para luchar."�Encarna la velocidad del relámpago. Sus rugidos envían ondas de choque que sacuden el aire y el suelo como si los relámpagos estuvieran cayendo."Entei encarna la pasión del magma. Se cree que nació en la erupción de un volcán. Lanza fuego que consume todo lo que toca."�Encarna la compasión de un manantial de agua pura. Corre por la tierra con una elegancia deslizante. Tiene el poder de purificar el agua sucia."�Un ligero aleteo de sus alas puede volar casas por los aires. Como resultado, elige vivir fuera de la vista en las profundidades del mar."~Se cree que sus plumas, que brillan en siete colores dependiendo del ángulo en el que la luz las golpee, traen alegría."�Este Pokémon vino del futuro cruzando el tiempo. Se cree que mientras aparezca Celebi, nos espera un futuro brillante y resplandeciente."�Hace su nido en los árboles del bosque. Protege ferozmente todo su territorio. Se dice que es el protector de los árboles del bosque."�Las hojas crecen del cuerpo de este Pokémon. Ayudan a ocultarlo de los ojos de sus enemigos mientras está en un bosque tupido cubierto de maleza."�En la jungla, su poder no tiene igual. Este Pokémon cultiva árboles y plantas cuidadosamente. Regula la temperatura de su cuerpo tomando el sol."sThese Pokémon travel in small groups, searching for travelers to rob. As they march, their tails drum a beat."}Though they are skilled with swordplay, they never fight fair. They swish their tails in unison to intimidate groups of prey."�This Pokémon's tail is so heavy it must run on all fours to spear foes. The sound of wind in its feathers is the only warning before impact."�Si es atacado, contraataca escupiendo bolas de fuego que forma en su estómago. A Torchic no le gusta la oscuridad porque no puede ver su entorno."�Arremete con 10 patadas por segundo. Su fuerte instinto de lucha lo obliga a mantener su ofensiva hasta que el oponente se rinde."�Aprende artes marciales que usan puñetazos y patadas. Sus plumas viejas se queman y en su lugar vuelven a crecer plumas nuevas y flexibles."sThis Pokémon is drawn to sounds of revelry. It is commonly sighted in the crowd at fairgrounds and festivals."{This Pokémon invents a new dance routine every day. After performances, it tosses treats and trinkets into the crowd."�This Pokémon ensures festivities will remain both safe and lively. It deftly leaps between tents and rooftops, subduing anyone who would ruin the fun."�En tierra, puede levantar grandes rocas con fuerza al plantar sus cuatro patas y empujar. Duerme enterrándose en la tierra a la orilla del agua."�Sus patas traseras endurecidas le permiten mantenerse erguido. Debido a que se debilita si su piel se seca, repone líquidos jugando en el barro."�Si detecta la proximidad de una tormenta y un maremoto, protege su nido junto al mar amontonando rocas. Nada tan rápido como una moto de agua."�Este Pokémon fue descubierto recientemente, luego de que se abrieran cuevas antiguas llenas de vida antigua, donde se escondía en espacios angostos."~Este Pokémon es mucho más fuerte que antes, pero perezoso. Hace amigos fácilmente, pero podrías comerlos en un apuro."�Al vivir en cuevas submarinas sin iluminación, este Pokémon ha desarrollado gran sensibilidad a las vibraciones. Ubica presas con extrema precisión."�Amenaza a los enemigos con los colmillos al descubierto. Persigue a los objetivos que huyen. Gira la cola y corre si el enemigo contraataca."~En la naturaleza, Mightyena vive en manada. Nunca desafían las órdenes de su líder. Derrotan a los enemigos en equipo."�Frotando su nariz contra el suelo, siempre deambula de un lado a otro en busca de algo. Se distingue por las huellas en zigzag que deja."�Es extremadamente rápido si solo tiene que correr en línea recta. Cuando ve una presa bajo el agua, salta y la atrapa con sus afiladas garras."jSe piensa que es la forma original de Zigzagoon, se mueve en zigzag y arrasa con todo a su alrededor."bEste Pokémon agresivo embestirá agresivamente a oponentes hasta más fuertes que sí mismo."�Después de desviar los ataques con su escudo, contraataca con su tallo de puerro afilado. El tallo de puerro es a la vez arma y alimento."{Se adhiere a las ramas de los árboles y come hojas. El hilo que escupe de su boca ralentiza el movimiento de sus enemigos."{Se prepara para la evolución usando la energía que almacenó mientras era un Wurmple. Vigila el entorno con sus dos ojos."�Sus alas con dibujos coloridos son su característica más llamativa. Vuela a través de campos cubiertos de flores recogiendo polen."�Para evitar ser detectado por sus enemigos, se esconde debajo de las hojas grandes y en los huecos de las ramas. También se adhiere hojas muertas."�Es un Pokémon nocturno que vuela de campos y montañas a la atracción de las farolas por la noche. Suelta polvo altamente tóxico de sus alas."�Sus cuernos regulan eficientemente su temperatura corporal. Busca depredadores de tipo Fuego o Hielo para cargarse con energía para evolucionar."�Su seda lo hace camuflarse entre rocas nevadas. Si es atacado, su único recurso es hacerse poco apetitoso congelando su propio cuerpo."�Es menos hostil que su forma de Hoenn, pero despiadado con antiguos depredadores. Su pieza bucal injecta un fluido similar al nitrogeno líquido."}Su llama no deja de arder gracias a un órgano similar a un mechero. Pokémon curiosos intentan apagarlo, sin resultado."�Su abdomen es similar a un propulsor de cohete. Sus migraciones pueden rastrearse observando árboles rotos por un vuelo supersónico."�Este Pokémon vive en estanques con agua limpia. Se sabe que transporta pequeños Pokémon llevándolos en la ancha hoja de su cabeza."�Por la noche, se deleita en salir de los ríos y asustar a la gente. Se alimenta del musgo acuático que crece en las rocas del lecho del río."~Cuando escucha música festiva, todas sus células se estimulan y comienza a moverse al ritmo. No se acobarda ante nadie."�Se cuelga de las ramas y absorbe los nutrientes. Cuando termina de comer, su cuerpo se vuelve tan pesado que cae al suelo con un golpe."�Habita en el bosque y es hábil para trepar a los árboles. Su nariz larga y puntiaguda es su punto débil. Pierde poder si se agarra la nariz."�Se dice que llega con vientos fríos e invernales. Temido desde hace mucho tiempo como guardián de los bosques, vive en bosques profundos sin gente."�Aunque es pequeño, es muy valiente. Se enfrentará a un Skarmory más grande en pie de igualdad. Sin embargo, su voluntad se debilita si tiene hambre."�Un Swellow se lanza sobre su presa desde muy arriba. Nunca pierde sus objetivos. Se eleva a los cielos en busca de tierras con un clima cálido."�Hace su nido en un acantilado al borde del mar. Tiene problemas para mantener batir sus alas al volar. Se eleva en las corrientes ascendentes."~Roza la superficie de las olas mientras vuela. Cuando detecta una presa, usa su gran pico para recoger a la víctima con agua."�Tiene el poder de sentir las emociones de las personas y Pokémon con los cuernos en la cabeza. Se pone a cubierto si siente alguna hostilidad."�Tiene el poder psíquico para crear una rasgadura en las dimensiones y ver el futuro. Se dice que baila con placer en las mañanas soleadas."�Aparentemente no siente el tirón de la gravedad porque se sustenta con poder psíquico. Dará su vida para proteger a su Entrenador."gUn maestro de la cortesía y el manejo de la espada, lucha usando espadas extendidas en sus codos."�Se juntan en los charcos después de la lluvia de la tarde, deslizándose por la superficie del agua. Secreta miel con un dulce aroma de su cabeza."�Intimida a los enemigos con los patrones en forma de ojos en sus antenas. Se protege de la lluvia bajo grandes árboles y aleros."�Le encanta comer suelo húmedo y compostado en los bosques. Después de una lluvia prolongada, los puedes ver bailando en suelo compostado."�Esparce esporas por agujeros en el sombrero de su cabeza. Le encantan los climas cálidos y húmedos. Se alimenta de árboles y plantas."�Duerme prácticamente todo el día y toda la noche. No cambia de nido en toda su vida, pero a veces viaja grandes distancias nadando en los ríos."�No puede quedarse quieto porque está lleno de energía. Corre por campos y montañas todo el día para calmarse o no puede dormirá por la noche."�Hordas de Slaking se reúnen alrededor de los árboles cuando las frutas maduran. Esperan pacientemente a que caigan de los árboles."�Hace su nido en las raíces de un árbol poderoso. Usando sus antenas como bigotes, sondea su entorno en la oscuridad total del suelo."�Debido a que se lanza vigorosamente a gran velocidad, es muy difícil de ver. Escuchar sus distintivos gritos puede provocar dolor de cabeza."Flota en el aire aunque sus alas permanecen completamente inmóviles. El interior de su cuerpo es hueco y completamente oscuro."�Sus gritos equivalen al volumen de un avión a reacción. Inhala a través de sus canales auditivos. Puede llorar sin tener que recuperar el aliento."�Coloca los parlantes redondos sobre su cabeza para atacar a los enemigos con ondas ultrasónicas. Acumula energía al pisotear el suelo."�Tiene órganos generadores de sonido por todo el cuerpo. Se comunica con los demás ajustando el tono y el volumen de los gritos que emite."�Le encanta fortalecer su cuerpo por encima de todo. Si escuchas temblores en una cueva, es Makuhita haciendo un entrenamiento extenuante."�Tiene la costumbre de desafiar a otros sin dudarlo para probar su fuerza. Se sabe que detiene los trenes usando empujones con el antebrazo."�Su cuerpo emite un poderoso magnetismo. Se alimenta de presas que son atraídas por la fuerza. Su magnetismo es más fuerte en invierno."iExuda un fuerte magnetismo por todas partes. Controla tres pequeñas unidades llamadas Mini-Narices."�Su comportamiento adorablemente lindo lo hace muy popular. En batalla, hace que su cola se hinche. Amenaza a los enemigos con un gruñido agudo."�En lugar de mantener una guarida permanente, habitualmente busca lugares cómodos y duerme allí. Es nocturno y se vuelve activo al anochecer."�Excava hoyos ramificados en cuevas usando sus afiladas garras en busca de comida, gemas en bruto. Acecha en la oscuridad y rara vez se lo ve."|Atacantes verán sus debilidades y lamentos reflejados en la gema de Rubarior. Si no se amado, hará a su Entrenador llorar."�Sus mandíbulas gigantes son en realidad cuernos de acero que se transforman. Engaña a los enemigos con gestos adorables para morderlos con fuerza."�Fans discuten si es el Pokémon aterrador más adorable o el Pokémon adorable más aterrador. Actuará adorable o aterrador dependiendo de lo quiera su entrenador."�Está revestido con una armadura de acero mudándola al evolucionar. La vieja armadura se recupera como metal para fabricar productos de hierro."�Cuando dos Lairon se encuentran en la naturaleza, luchan por el territorio golpeándose entre sí. El sonido de su colisión se transmite por kilómetros."�Sus cuernos de hierro crecen poco a poco y determinan su edad. Las gubias en su armadura se usan con orgullo como recuerdos de las batallas."�Medita continuamente durante horas. Como resultado de un entrenamiento de yoga riguroso y dedicado, ha aprendido a volar con su poder espiritual."�A través de un entrenamiento de yoga muy duro, aprendió a predecir las acciones de su rival. Lucha con movimientos elegantes, similar a una danza."�Este Pokémon puede pasar cuatro años sin comer nada. A través de intenso entrenamiento, puede combatir de una manera indistinguible a una danza."�Genera electricidad usando la fricción de la atmósfera. En la época de aire especialmente árido, arde con violentas lluvias de chispas."Debido a que los rayos caen en sus cercanías, se cree que Manectric nació de un rayo. En la batalla, crean nubes de tormenta."[Si no es calmado durante una tormenta, causará estragos al tratar de perseguir rayos."�Tiene la característica de animar a sus compañeros Pokémon. Al cortar la electricidad que libera de sus patas, crea pompones para animar."�En una reunión de académicos, se anunció que la exposición simultánea a la electricidad de un Minun mejorará la circulación y aumentará la vitalidad."�Con sus luces traseras encendidas dibuja diseños geométricos en el cielo nocturno. Mueven sus nidos si el agua de su estanque se ensucia."�Un Pokémon nocturno que se activa al caer la noche. Dirige a los enjambres de Volbeat para dibujar más de 200 patrones distintos en el cielo."sDurante el invierno, cierra su capullo y aguanta el frío. En primavera, el capullo se abre y suelta el polen."�Al beber agua de manantial rica en nutrientes florece con hermosas flores. La fragancia de sus flores hace que sus enemigos se descuiden."kAtrae a la presa con un dulce aroma, luego la derriba con látigos espinosos escondidos en sus brazos."�Su líquido estomacal puede incluso digerir chatarra de hierro. De un solo trago, puede tragar algo que es tan grande como él mismo."�Su poderoso ácido estomacal es capaz de digerir casi cualquier cosa. Lo único en el mundo que un Swalot no puede digerir es su propio estómago."�Ataca a los barcos en enjambres, hundiéndolos. Aunque se dice que es un Pokémon muy vicioso, huye tímidamente tan pronto como se encuentra solo."�El gángster vicioso y astuto del mar. Su piel tiene le permite minimizar el arrastre en el agua. Su velocidad es de más de 120 Km/h."�Su sistema de propulsión es la base para varios diseños de ramjets. Come el cuádruple de su tamaño antes de un combate y estará hambriento al terminar."�Si bien este Pokémon suele vivir en el mar, puede sobrevivir en tierra, aunque no demasiado tiempo. Pierde vitalidad si su cuerpo se seca."�Respira a través de las fosas nasales que eleva sobre el mar. Al inhalar a su máxima capacidad, puede sumergirse cerca de 10,000 pies."�Almacena magma hirviendo en la joroba de su espalda. Puede transportar una carga de 100 Kg. Trabaja con los humanos desde hace mucho tiempo."�Vive en el cráter de un volcán. Cada 10 años, los volcanes de su espalda entran en erupción violentamente. Se está investigando el motivo."�El magma en su interior crece sin parar. Si este Pokémon no estalla regularmente, podría accidentalmente destruir el área a su alrededor."�Lucha usando la energía que obtiene al quemar carbón. Al soltar humo por sus fosas nasales, emite un sonido similar al claxon de una locomotora."�Manipula el poder psíquico a voluntad. No deja de rebotar incluso cuando está dormido. Le encanta comer hongos que crecen bajo tierra."�Usa las perlas negras en su cuerpo para amplificar su poder psíquico teniendo un control total sobre su rival. Jadea cuando lo hace."�Se distingue por un patrón de manchas que siempre es diferente. Su andar tambaleante tiene el efecto de entorpecer la puntería de su enemigo."�Sus grandes mandíbulas crujen las rocas. Debido a que su gran cabeza tiene dificultades para volver a ponerse en pie si cae de espaldas."�Pierde ondas ultrasónicas al frotar sus alas. Dado que sus alas aún están en proceso de crecimiento, solo puede volar distancias cortas."�El aleteo de sus alas suena como un canto. Para evitar que los enemigos lo detecten, se esconde agitando una nube de arena del desierto."�Después de pasar miles de años en los duros desiertos, su sangre se transformó en arena. Es nocturno, por lo que caza de noche."�Después de pasar miles de años en los duros desiertos, su sangre se transformó en arena. Es nocturno, por lo que caza de noche."�Un Pokémon que tiene alas como nubes. Después de soportar el invierno las bandadas de Swablu se acercan a las ciudades en primavera."�Canturrea con una hermosa voz de soprano. Vuela entre nubes blancas en el cielo azul. Lanza bolas de fuego muy calientes desde su boca."�El canto de este Pokémon puede hacer llorar a cualquier Entrenador. Aquellos que se duermen ante él dicen experienciar sueños maravillosos."�Cuando pelea, se para sobre sus patas traseras y ataca con las delanteras con afiladas garras. Su pelaje se eriza si se encuentra con Seviper."�Seviper y Zangoose son eternos rivales. Contrarresta la increíble agilidad de Zangoose con su venenosa cola con forma de espada."zIncluso ser bisecado por la cola de Seviper no pudo calmarlo. Ataca enemigos tanto físicamente como espiritualmente."�Su cuerpo metálico es impenetrable por casi todo ataque. Cuando se enrosca, puede disparar proyectiles de metal usando inducción magnética."�Se vuelve muy activo en la noche de luna llena. Este Pokémon fue descubierto por primera vez hace 40 años en el lugar donde cayó un meteorito."�La energía solar es la fuente del poder de este Pokémon. En los días soleados, grupos de Solrock se alinean frente al sol y absorben su luz."�Su cuerpo está cubierto con una película viscosa que actúa como una barrera para evitar que los gérmenes del agua fangosa entren en su cuerpo."�Puede predecir terremotos. Durante el día, duerme en el barro de un estanque. Al despertarse, se alimenta continuamente durante toda la noche."�Una vez que agarra a la presa con sus grandes pinzas, nunca la suelta. Es un Pokémon resistente que puede prosperar en cualquier entorno."�Un Pokémon brutal al que le encanta luchar. Los veteranos de cientos de batallas tiene unas pinzas gigantes marcadas con muchas cicatrices."�Se mueve girando sobre su único pie. Ha sido representado en murales que adornan las paredes de una ciudad que alguna vez fue bulliciosa."�Duerme mientras flota en el aire. Sus brazos están separados de su cuerpo. Se mantienen flotando gracias a la manipulación de su poder psíquico."~Se disfraza de alga marina balanceando sus tentáculos. La presa desprevenida que se acerca demasiado se la traga entera."mArrastra su pesado cuerpo por el fondo del mar. Anida en las aguas poco profundas de los mares cálidos."�Fue resucitado de un fósil. Anorith nada ondulando las ocho alas que tiene a los lados. Eran unos pies que se adaptaron a la vida en el mar."}Armaldo suele vivir en tierra. Sin embargo, cuando caza presas, se sumerge bajo el océano. Nada usando sus dos grandes alas."�Vive en estanques que están infestados de malas hierbas. Debido a su aspecto desesperadamente destartalado, pocos Entrenadores lo crían."�Se dice que vive en el fondo de grandes lagos. Considerado como el más bello de todos los Pokémon, ha sido representado en pinturas y estatuas."�Nada en el aire sobre lugares de tragedias no lloradas, son fácilmente localizables debido a los llantos que emiten en solitario."fMilotic ya no carga su tristeza. Se dice que ayudan a las almas inquietas a llegar al más allá."�Altera su forma dependiendo del clima. Los cambios en el clima como la temperatura y la humedad parecen afectar su estructura celular."�Tiene la capacidad de alterar los colores de su cuerpo para que coincida con su entorno. Vuelve a sus colores originales si se sobresalta."�Deambula en lo profundo de la noche en busca de emociones negativas como el rencor y la envidia. Vuelve a su nido cuando amanece."�Un muñeco de peluche abandonado se convirtió en este Pokémon. Se dice que vive en basureros y deambula en busca de los niños que los tiraron."�Sus garras y pies parecen estar hechos de carne, pero son energía negativa pura. Cuando se desabrocha por completo, va a su siguiente vida."�El resplandor de su único ojo escarlata hace que incluso los adultos se aterroricen. Es nocturno y deambula bajo el manto de la oscuridad."�Se cree que su cuerpo es hueco con solo una espectral bola de fuego ardiendo en su interior. Sin embargo, nadie ha podido confirmar esta teoría."tLa antena en su cabeza capta ondas de radio del mundo de los espíritus que le ordenan llevar a la gente allí."�Vuela agitando sus anchas hojas. El racimo de fruta que crece alrededor de su cuello es muy dulce. En primavera, esparce polen por su cuello."lEmite gritos al agitar un orbe en la parte posterior de su garganta. Se mueve con saltos revoloteantes."�Vuelan muy activamente cuando llega la temporada de calor. Se comunican entre ellos mediante siete gritos diferentes y distintivos."�Detecta agudamente cambios sutiles en el cielo y la tierra para predecir desastres naturales. Es un Pokémon longevo con una vida de 100 años."�Es amado por su estilo elegante e intimidante. Podrá ser el precursor de un cataclismo, pero nada se pone encima de un entrenador y su Pokémon con estilo."�Se mueven en grupos de alrededor de 5. En las regiones nevadas, se dice que cuando se los ve por la noche, la nieve llegará por la mañana."�Tiene el poder de congelar la humedad en la atmósfera. Una nube de cristales de hielo como diamantes se forma alrededor de su cuerpo."�Sólo cierra su boca para morder a sus oponentes, forzando a su entrenador a aprender sus emociones mediante cambios en sus ojos, orejas y temperatura."tCongela a los enemigos con un aliento helado de casi -50º C. Lo que parece ser su cuerpo es en realidad hueco."�Está completamente cubierto con un pelaje afelpado. Nunca siente el frío, aunque esté rodando sobre témpanos de hielo o buceando en el mar."�Vive en manadas sobre témpanos de hielo. Usando sus fuertes aletas, rompe el hielo. Se sumerge en el mar para cazar presas cinco veces al día."�Para proteger a su manada, el líder lucha contra cualquier enemigo, incluso a costa de su vida. Sus colmillos pueden romperse en la batalla."�Cierra de golpe su caparazón sobre la presa para evitar que escape. La perla que crea al evolucionar contiene una energía misteriosa."�Para resistir la presión del agua en las profundidades del mar, su columna vertebral es muy resistente. Su cola tiene ojos que se iluminan."�Un Gorebyss succiona los fluidos corporales de sus presas a través de su boca. Su color rosa claro se vuelve vívido al alimentarse."�Alguna vez se creyó extinto. La especie no ha cambiado en 100 millones de años. Camina sobre el fondo del mar usando sus aletas pectorales."�Luvdisc hace sus nidos con las ramas de Corsola. Existe una costumbre de dar un Luvdisc como regalo para expresar los sentimientos de amor."yFlotar en mar abierto es su forma de vida. Cuando encuentran un Pokémon herido, lo abrazan y lo llevan a la orilla."�Aunque es pequeño, este Pokémon es muy poderoso porque su cuerpo es un manojo de músculos. Lanza cabezazos con su cráneo férreo."�Apenas come mientras espera la evolución. Se vuelve más resistente al soportar el hambre. Su caparazón se desprende al evolucionar."�Después de muchos años, su estructura celular sufrió una mutación repentina para que le crecieran alas. Cuando se enfada se descontrola."�Cuando los Beldum forman un enjambre, se mueven al unísono como si fueran un solo Pokémon. Se comunican entre sí mediante ondas cerebrales."�Las garras que inclinan sus brazos acumulan el poder destructivo para rasgar gruesas láminas de hierro. Vuela a más de 96 Km/h."�Metagross tiene cuatro cerebros que están unidos por una red neuronal compleja. Como resultado, es más inteligente que una supercomputadora."zEl tercero de los titanes, construído para conmemorar una era de piedra. Es tan resiliente como un monolito antiguo."pEl segundo de los titanes, construído para conmemorar una era de hielo. Es tan implacable como un glaciar."�El cuarto de los titanes, construído para conmemorar una era donde se trabajaba con metales. Es tan confiable como la espada de un herrero maestro."El quinto de los titanes, construído para conmemorar una era de electricidad. Es tan inescrutable como una súper computadora."�El primero de los titanes, construído para conmemorar una era donde los dragones reinaban. Es tan terrorífico como un antiguo depredador."~El creador de los titanes, que le dió forma a la arcilla primitiva en la era dorada. Su poder creativo no tiene límite."�Hacen una pequeña manada de solo varios miembros. Rara vez hacen contacto con personas u otros Pokémon. Desaparecen si detectan enemigos."�Incluso escondido, detecta la ubicación de otros y sentir sus emociones. Su inteligencia le permite comprender los lenguajes humanos."�Kyogre ha aparecido en la mitología como el creador del mar. Después de largos años de pelea con Groudon, se llevó a dormir al fondo del mar."�Apareció en la mitología como el creador de la tierra. Duerme en el magma subterráneo y cree que los volcanes entran en erupción al despertar."yUn Pokémon que vuela sin cesar en la capa de ozono. Se dice que descendería al suelo si Kyogre y Groudon pelearan."�Se dice que hace que los deseos se cumplan. Mientras duerme, un caparazón cristalino envuelve su cuerpo para protegerlo de los enemigos."|Un Pokémon que mutó de un virus extraterrestre expuesto a un rayo láser. El órgano cristalino en su torso es su cerebro."mHecho de tierra, el caparazón de su espalda se endurece cuando bebe agua. Vive a lo largo de los lagos."vVive junto al agua en los bosques. Durante el día, sale del bosque para tomar el sol con su caparazón arbolado."nPequeños Pokémon de vez en cuando se juntan en su espalda inmóvil para comenzar a construir sus nidos."Escala con agilidad acantilados escarpados para vivir en lo alto de montañas escarpadas. Su fuego se apaga cuando duerme."YPara intimidar a los atacantes, estira el fuego en su cola para parecer más grande."pUtiliza un tipo especial de artes marciales que involucran todas sus extremidades. Su fuego nunca se apaga."ePorque es muy orgulloso, odia aceptar comida de la gente. Su espesa pelusa lo protege del frío."bVive solo, lejos de los demás. Al parecer, cada uno de ellos cree que es el más importante."sLos tres cuernos que se extienden desde su pico atestiguan su poder. El líder tiene los cuernos más grandes."]Se congregan en grandes cantidades. Aunque son pequeños, baten sus alas con gran poder."cVuela por bosques y campos en busca de Pokémon Bicho. Se mantiene dentro de una gran bandada."bTiene una naturaleza salvaje. Desafiará valientemente a enemigos que son mucho más grandes."[Con nervios de acero, nada puede perturbarlo. Es más ágil y activo de lo que parece."eHace su nido represando arroyos con corteza y lodo. Se le conoce como un trabajador industrioso."uMueve la cabeza de atrás hacia adelante, haciendo que sus antenas choquen entre sí y suenen como un xilófono."eCruza sus brazos como cuchillos frente a su pecho cuando llora. Puede componer melodías ad lib."kTodo su pelaje deslumbra si se siente peligro. Huye mientras el enemigo queda momentáneamente cegado."mSus garras sueltan electricidad con suficiente amperaje para causar desmayos. Viven en pequeños grupos."sTiene ojos que pueden ver a través de cualquier cosa. Detecta y captura presas escondidas detrás de objetos."aVivió en las selvas hace unos 100 millones de años. Su cráneo es tan duro como el hierro."jSu poderoso cabezazo tiene suficiente poder para romper incluso las cosas más duraderas al impactar."qUn Pokémon que vivió en las selvas hace unos 100 millones de años. Su piel facial es extremadamente dura."cCualquier ataque frontal es repelido. Es un Pokémon dócil que se alimenta de hierba y bayas."hPara protegerse de los vientos fríos e invernales, se cubre con un manto hecho de ramitas y hojas."qCuando Burmy evolucionó, su capa se convirtió en parte del cuerpo de este Pokémon. La capa nunca se muda."GLe encanta la miel de las flores y roba la miel que recoge Combee."ZUn Pokémon formado por otros tres. Lleva afanosamente dulce miel floral a Vespiquen."ZSu abdomen es un panal de larvas. Cría sus larvas en la miel recolectada por Combee."xHace bolas de pelo que crepitan con electricidad estática. Las almacena con bayas en los agujeros de los árboles."mTiene un saco de flotación que es como un collar inflable. Flota en el agua con la cabeza hacia afuera."tFlota usando su saco de flotación bien desarrollado. Ayuda en los rescates de personas que se están ahogando."sLa pequeña bola contiene los nutrientes necesarios para la evolución. Aparentemente, es muy dulce y sabrosa."aFlorece en épocas de fuerte luz solar. Intenta compensar todo lo que soportó como capullo."jSus colores y formas difieren de una región a otra. En la región de Sinnoh, se confirman dos tipos."cTiene un cuerpo flexible sin huesos. Si se arranca alguna parte de su cuerpo, vuelve a crecer."pUn Pokémon formado por los espíritus de las personas y los Pokémon. Le encantan las estaciones húmedas."kEstá somnoliento durante el día, pero vuela por la noche en grandes grupos. Nadie sabe a dónde van."�Golpea a los enemigos desenroscando bruscamente sus orejas enrolladas. Pica lo suficiente como para hacer que un adulto llore de dolor."sUn Pokémon extremadamente cauteloso. Cubre su cuerpo con el suave pelaje de sus orejas cuando siente peligro."�Ataca y se ve como luchadores humanos que admira. Sólo las películas de acción más exageradas pueden inspirarle a llegar a su verdadero potencial."qSegún las leyendas, los Buneary de Makya vienen de la luna. Tienen un gran control de sus orejas prensiles."�Los cristales azules que adornan su pelaje se asemejan a la sacarita, pero análisis muestran que son estructuralmente distintos."�Errando por el mundo, Haerobic de Makya tiene un gran sentido de justicia y usa toda la fuerza de sus poderes lunaras para rescatar a Pokémon más débiles."lAraña si está disgustado y ronronea cuando es cariñoso. Su volubilidad es muy popular entre algunos."\Es un bruto descarado que irrumpe en el nido de otro Pokémon y lo reclama como propio."qSe protege a sí mismo rociando un fluido nocivo desde su parte trasera. El hedor persiste durante 24 horas."rRocía un fluido de olor repugnante desde la punta de su cola para atacar. Su alcance es de más de 160 pies."kImplementos con esa forma fueron descubiertos en tumbas antiguas. Se desconoce si están relacionados."Uno causó sensación en las noticias cuando fue desenterrado en un sitio de construcción después de un sueño de 2000 años."�Parece como si siempre estuviera llorando. En realidad, está ajustando los niveles de fluidos de su cuerpo eliminando el exceso."nUn Pokémon que fue formado por 108 espíritus. Está ligado a una fisura en una extraña piedra angular."Anida en pequeños agujeros horizontales en las paredes de las cuevas. Salta para atrapar presas que se acercan demasiado."sExiste la creencia arraigada de que la medicina hecha con sus escamas curará incluso enfermedades incurables."pCuando pliega su cuerpo y extiende sus alas, parece un avión a reacción. Vuela a la velocidad del sonido."kEl aura que emana de su cuerpo se intensifica para alertar a los demás si tiene miedo o está triste."YTiene la capacidad de sentir las auras de todas las cosas. Entiende el habla humana."�Combate en un estado de claridad completa sin piedad, miedo, o estrés. Una vez haya logrado sus objetivos, simplemente dejará de ser."[Vive en lugares áridos. En lugar de transpirar, expulsa arena granulosa de su cuerpo."yExplota arena almacenada internamente desde los puertos de su cuerpo para crear un imponente tornado para el ataque."tAgarra a la presa con las garras de su cola e inyecta veneno. Se aferra con tenacidad hasta que el veneno toma."uTiene el poder en sus brazos con garras para hacer chatarra de un auto. Las puntas de sus garras liberan veneno."~Sus mejillas contienen sacos de veneno. Intenta atrapar a los enemigos con la guardia baja para pincharlos con dedos tóxicos."kSus garras en los nudillos secretan una toxina tan vil que incluso un rasguño podría resultar fatal."qAtrae a la presa con su saliva de olor dulce, luego la muerde. Necesita un día entero para comer una presa."�Caza a otros depredadores nocturnos, atrapándolo en sus zarcillos pegajosos. Su risa maníaca es un sonido común en noches de otoño."�Después de una larga exposición a la luz del sol, los patrones en las aletas de su cola brillan vívidamente cuando llega la oscuridad."pVive en el fondo del mar profundo. Atrae a sus presas mostrando los patrones en sus cuatro aletas caudales."aVive en montañas nevadas. Habiendo tenido poco contacto con humanos, es audazmente curioso."oAzota ventiscas en montañas que siempre están enterradas en la nieve. Es el abominable muñeco de nieve."~La ventisca lo sigue a donde sea que vaya. Es usado frecuentemente como un refugio por montañeros, y realmente no le importa."qSu cuerpo está compuesto de plasma. Se sabe que se infiltra en dispositivos electrónicos y causa estragos."tConocido como "El Ser del Conocimiento". Se dice que puede borrar la memoria de aquellos que observen sus ojos."mConocido como "El Ser de la Emoción". Le enseño a los humanos la nobleza de la pena, dolor y alegría."mConocido como "El Ser de la Voluntad". Duerme al fondo de una lado para mantener al mundo en equilibrio."qTiene el poder de controlar el tiempo. Aparece como una deidad antigua en los mitos de la región de Sinnoh."yTiene la capacidad de distorsionar el espacio. Se describe como una deidad en la mitología de la región de Sinnoh."tHabita en cuevas volcánicas. Se entierra con sus patas en forma de cruz para arrastrarse por techos y paredes."jUn Pokémon que se dice que vive en un mundo al revés del nuestro. Aparece en un antiguo cementerio."jPartículas brillantes se liberan de sus alas como un velo. Se dice que representa la luna creciente."zUn Pokémon que vive en mares cálidos. Infla el saco de flotación de su cabeza para ir a la deriva y buscar comida."hNacido en un fondo marino frío, nadará grandes distancias para regresar a su lugar de nacimiento."ePuede adormecer a las personas y hacerlas soñar. Está activo durante las noches de luna nueva."jVive en parches de flores y evita ser detectado enroscándose para parecerse a una planta con flores."bSe describe en la mitología como el Pokémon que dio forma al universo con sus 1.000 brazos."pHacen la fotosíntesis bañando sus colas con la luz del sol. Cuando no se sienten bien, sus colas se caen."~Evitan los ataques hundiéndose en las sombras del espeso follaje. Toman represalias con magistrales técnicas de azotes."xLevantan la cabeza para intimidar a los oponentes, pero solo lo dan todo cuando luchan contra un oponente poderoso."kExpulsa fuego por la nariz. Cuando se resfría, el fuego se convierte en humo negro como boca de lobo."�Todo lo que come se convierte en combustible para la llama de su estómago. Cuando se enfada, la intensidad de la llama aumenta."XHa dominado movimientos de lucha rápidos y poderosos. Le crece una barba de fuego."yLa vieira en su estómago está hecha del mismo elemento que las garras. Separa la vieira para usarla como cuchilla."kLas técnicas de vieiras difieren de un Dewott a otro. Nunca descuida el mantenimiento de sus vieiras."�Parte de la armadura en sus patas anteriores se convierte en una espada gigante. Su grito basta para intimidar a la mayoría de sus rivales."^Con corazón duro y filo diestro, ataca turbulentamente como si fuera una ola sin piedad."{Extremadamente cautelosos, se turnan para mantener una vigilancia constante de su nido. Se sienten inseguros sin un vigía."Hacen que los patrones de sus cuerpos brillen para amenazar a los depredadores. La vista aguda les permite ver en la oscuridad."|El cabello largo alrededor de su rostro proporciona un radar increíble que le permite sentir cambios sutiles en su entorno."qEste Pokémon extremadamente sabio sobresale en el rescate de personas varadas en el mar o en las montañas."�Su lindo acto es una artimaña. Cuando las víctimas bajan la guardia, descubren que les quitan sus objetos. Ataca con garras afiladas."�Sigilosamente, se acerca sigilosamente a su objetivo, golpeando por detrás antes de que su víctima tenga la oportunidad de reaccionar."oComparte la hoja de su cabeza con Pokémon de aspecto cansado. Se sabe que estas hojas alivian el estrés."qAtaca a los enemigos con golpes de su cola cubierta de espinas. Este Pokémon tiene un temperamento salvaje."sEste Pokémon vive en cuevas en volcanes. El fuego dentro del mechón de su cabeza puede alcanzar los 315º C."kUna llama arde dentro de su cuerpo. Esparce brasas de su cabeza y cola para chamuscar a sus oponentes."}No prospera en ambientes secos. Se mantiene húmedo disparando agua almacenada en el mechón de su cabeza desde su cola."jEl agua a alta presión expulsada de su cola es tan poderosa que puede destruir un muro de hormigón."xSe come los sueños de las personas y Pokémon. Cuando come un sueño placentero, expulsa una niebla de color rosa."ZCon la niebla de su frente, puede crear formas de cosas de los sueños que ha comido."ZCon la niebla de su frente, puede crear formas de cosas de los sueños que ha comido."�Cuando un huevo de Munna es colocado al cuidado de un dragón, incuba en esta forma. No parará de darle cabezazos a un Togepi si es colocado junto a uno."�Ventila energía psíquica como humo desde el hueco donde su gema solía estar. Su corazón funciona como un segundo cerebro que le permite usar telepatía."yEstos Pokémon viven en ciudades. Están acostumbrados a la gente. Las bandadas suelen reunirse en parques y plazas."vMucha gente cree que, en lo profundo del bosque donde vive Tranquill, hay un lugar pacífico donde no hay guerra."wLos machos tienen plumaje en la cabeza. Nunca se permitirán sentirse cerca de nadie más que de sus Entrenadores."Cuando las nubes de tormenta cubran el cielo, aparecerá. Puede atrapar un rayo con su melena y almacenar la electricidad."gCuando este Pokémon malhumorado se vuelve loco, lanza rayos desde su melena en todas direcciones."vFueron descubiertos hace cien años en una fisura de un terremoto. Dentro de cada uno hay un núcleo de energía."zDebido a que su energía era demasiado grande para ser contenida, la energía se filtró y formó cristales naranjas."�En la mitología de Makya, nacieron desde los meteoros que cayeron cuando la luna fue destruída por un dios furioso. Su armadura densa desvía todo ataque."_Fue descubierto en tierras prohibidas. Su cuerpo no sigue las leyes físicas del universo."�Se siente más cómodo en dimensiones alienígenas que en la Tierra. Las partes rocosas de su cuerpo no pueden ser analizadas por la ciencia moderna."�No pueden ser entendidos ni predecidos, haciéndolos peligrosos. Al final de su vida regresarán a su universo de origen, reportándose a una entidad superior."�La succión de sus fosas nasales le permite adherirse a las paredes de la cueva durante el sueño. Deja una marca en forma de corazón detrás."�Cualquiera que entre en contacto con las ondas ultrasónicas emitidas por un macho que corteja experimenta un cambio de humor positivo."dSe abre paso rápidamente a través del suelo juntando ambas garras y girando a gran velocidad."�A más de 300 pies bajo la superficie, construyen nidos laberínticos. Su actividad puede ser destructiva para los túneles del metro."�Su sentido auditivo es asombroso. Tiene una capacidad similar a la de un radar para comprender su entorno a través de sonidos leves."�Son traídos a hospitales cuando la medicina convencional falla. Pueden escuchar los latidos restantes de una persona, pero nunca lo dirán."{Estos Pokémon aparecen en las obras de construcción y ayudan con la construcción. Siempre llevan troncos cuadrados."aFortalecen sus cuerpos cargando vigas de acero. Muestran sus grandes músculos a sus amigos."}Usan pilares de hormigón como bastones. Conocen movimientos que les permiten balancear los pilares libremente en la batalla."�Al hacer vibrar sus mejillas, emite ondas de sonido imperceptibles para los humanos. Utiliza el ritmo de estos sonidos para hablar."]Vive en el agua y en la tierra. Utiliza su lengua larga y pegajosa para capturar presas."�Aumenta el poder de sus golpes haciendo vibrar los golpes en sus puños. Puede convertir una roca en escombros con un solo golpe."vCuando se encuentran con enemigos más grandes que ellos, intentan arrojarlos. Siempre viajan en grupos de cinco."vAtar sus cinturones los anima y hace que sus golpes sean más destructivos. Perturbar su entrenamiento los enoja."nEste Pokémon se hace ropa por sí mismo. Mastica hojas y las cose con hilo pegajoso que sale de su boca."lSe protege del frío envolviéndose en hojas. Se mantiene en movimiento, comiendo hojas en los bosques."�Mantiene sus huevos calientes con el calor de las hojas fermentadas. También usa hojas para hacer envolturas calientes para Sewaddle."lDescubre lo que sucede a su alrededor usando los sensores de su cabeza y cola. Es brutalmente agresivo."tPor lo general, está inmóvil, pero cuando es atacado, gira a gran velocidad y luego choca contra su oponente."eAltamente agresivo, usa las garras cerca de su cuello para clavarse y envenenar a sus oponentes."�Van a donde les lleve el viento. En los días de lluvia, su cuerpo es más pesado, por lo que se refugian debajo de grandes árboles."}Aparecen montados en torbellinos. Estos Pokémon se cuelan por los huecos de las casas y causan todo tipo de travesuras."�Dado que prefieren un suelo húmedo y rico en nutrientes, se sabe que las áreas donde vive Petilil son buenas para el cultivo de plantas."xLa fragancia de la guirnalda en su cabeza tiene un efecto relajante. Se marchita si un Entrenador no la cuida bien."�Sus piernas bien desarrolladas son el resultado de una vida en las montañas cubiertas de nieve. El aroma de su flor anima a aquellos a su alrededor."�Parece estar orgulloso de vivir en condiciones inhóspitas. Si otros empiezan a vivir a su alrededor, se mudará a climas aún más fríos."rSe pronuncia de forma real y tiránica repentinamente. Es irritado cuando sus súbditos no pueden entenderlo."�Los Basculin rojos y azules no suelen llevarse bien, pero a veces los miembros de un cardumen se mezclan con el cardumen del otro."cSe envuelve en las almas de sus compañeros que no sobrevivieron su camino en contracorriente."�Se mueve por debajo de la superficie de la arena, excepto por la nariz y los ojos. Una membrana oscura protege sus ojos del sol."�La membrana especial que cubre sus ojos puede sentir el calor de los objetos, por lo que puede ver su entorno incluso en la oscuridad."{Puede expandir el foco de sus ojos, lo que le permite ver objetos en la lejanía como si estuviera usando binoculares."yLos excrementos de Darumaka son calientes, por lo que la gente solía ponerlos en su ropa para mantenerse calientes."~Cuando se debilita en la batalla, se transforma en una estatua de piedra. Luego agudiza su mente y sigue luchando mentalmente."�Cuanto más frío esté, más energía tiene. Congela su aliento para hacer bolas de nieve, las que usa para jugar con otros de su especie."~Aunque normalmente es gentil, tiene mucha fuerza. Rápidamente congela la bola de nieve en su cabeza antes de dar un cabezazo."mLas regiones áridas son su hábitat. Se mueven rítmicamente, haciendo un sonido similar a las maracas."Hace un agujero en una roca adecuada. Si esa roca se rompe, el Pokémon permanece agitado hasta que localiza un reemplazo."�Posee unas patas de enorme fuerza, lo que le permite transportar pesadas losas durante muchos días, incluso cuando atraviesa terrenos áridos."vInmediatamente le da un cabezazo a cualquiera que haga contacto visual con él. Su cráneo es enormemente grueso."|Puede romper bloques de concreto con sus ataques de patadas. El que tiene la cresta más grande es el líder del grupo."|Los guardianes de una antigua ciudad, utilizan su poder psíquico para atacar a los enemigos que invaden su territorio."�Estos Pokémon surgieron de los espíritus de personas enterradas en tumbas en épocas pasadas. Cada uno conserva recuerdos de su vida anterior."}Pretenden ser ataúdes elaborados para dar lecciones a los ladrones de tumbas. Sus cuerpos están cubiertos de oro puro."tSe dice que este Pokémon fue formado cuando una antigua tabla antigua fue poseída por un espíritu vengativo."}Nunca toques su cuerpo parecido a una sombra, o se te mostrarán los horribles recuerdos detrás de la imagen tallada en él."�Hace unos 100 millones de años, estos Pokémon nadaban en los océanos. Se cree que también bajaron a la tierra para atacar a sus presas."nLa increíble fuerza de sus mandíbulas les permite masticar vigas de acero y rocas junto con sus presas."cRevivido de un fósil, se cree que este Pokémon es el ancestro de todos los Pokémon pájaro."eCorre mejor que vuela. Atrapa presas corriendo a velocidades comparables a las de un automóvil."zLa combinación de bolsas de basura y desechos industriales provocó la reacción química que creó a este Pokémon."~Absorben la basura y la hacen parte de sus cuerpos. Disparan un líquido venenoso de la punta de sus dedos de la mano derecha."�Es desconocido qué son los objetos en su cuerpo o de dónde vienen. Pero más deben ser agregados con el tiempo, ya que disuelve rápidamente todo lo que absorbe."mPara protegerse del peligro, ocultan sus verdaderas identidades transformándose en personas y Pokémon."�Cada uno tiene la capacidad de engañar a un gran grupo de personas simultáneamente. Protegen su guarida con un escenario ilusorio."�Un alma en pena, devuelta a la vida. Usa el poder del resentimiento, que aumenta la energía en su cabeza y copia la forma de sus rivales."}Le gusta terminar con los rencores y satisfacer deseos finales. Lo hace para asegurarse un paso tranquilo al más allá."{Estos Pokémon prefieren un hábitat ordenado. Siempre están barriendo y quitando el polvo, usando sus colas como escobas."}Su pelaje blanco se siente increíble al tacto. Su pelaje repele el polvo y evita que se acumule electricidad estática."�Observan atentamente tanto a los Entrenadores como a los Pokémon. Aparentemente, están mirando algo que sólo Gothita puede ver."�La luz de las estrellas es la fuente de su poder. Por la noche, marcan las posiciones de las estrellas usando el poder psíquico en piedras."�Pueden predecir el futuro a partir de la ubicación y el movimiento de las estrellas. Pueden ver la duración de la vida de los Entrenadores."pDebido a que sus cuerpos están envueltos en un líquido especial, pueden sobrevivir en cualquier ambiente."~Cuando sus cerebros, ahora divididos en dos, están pensando los mismos pensamientos, estos Pokémon exhiben su máximo poder."~Estos Pokémon extraordinariamente inteligentes luchan controlando brazos que pueden agarrar con un poder triturador de rocas."ZCuando es atacado, usa sus plumas para salpicar agua, escapando al amparo del rocío."rAdministra picotazos agudos y poderosos con su pico. Agita su largo cuello para dar fuertes golpes repetidos."}Este Pokémon se formó a partir de carámbanos bañados por la energía del sol de la mañana. Duerme enterrado en la nieve."oSe oculta de los ojos enemigos creando muchas pequeñas partículas de hielo y escondiéndose entre ellas."nSi ambas cabezas se enfadan a la vez, este Pokémon expulsa una ventisca, sepultándolo todo en la nieve."El cambio de estaciones cambia el color y el olor del pelaje de este Pokémon. La gente lo usa para marcar las estaciones."}Las plantas que crecen en sus cuernos cambian según la estación. Los líderes de la manada poseen magníficos cuernos."�Viven en las copas de los árboles y se deslizan usando el interior de una membrana similar a una capa mientras descargan electricidad."�Cuando se sienten amenazados, escupen un líquido ácido para ahuyentar a los atacantes. Este Pokémon tiene como objetivo a Shelmet."pEstos Pokémon evolucionan usando el caparazón de un Shelmet. La armadura de acero protege todo su cuerpo."�Por alguna razón, este Pokémon se asemeja a una Poké Ball. Liberan esporas venenosas para repeler a quienes intentan atraparlas."tMuestran sus gorras de Poké Ball para atraer a sus presas, pero muy pocos Pokémon se dejan engañar por esto."uParalizan a sus presas con veneno y luego las arrastran hasta sus guaridas, ocho kilómetros bajo la superficie."oSe impulsan expulsando el agua de mar absorbida de sus cuerpos. Su alimento favorito es la energía vital."pSon atraídos a maquinaria misteriosa e influencers. Debido a esto, son comunes en juegos online de terror."�Llevaron exploradores a una antigua ciudad hundida en el abismo. Su gente había subido sus mentes a las máquinas que fallaron a través del tiempo."}Se adhieren a los Pokémon de cuerpo grande y absorben la electricidad estática, que almacenan en una bolsa eléctrica."{Usa una telaraña cargada eléctricamente para atrapar a sus presas. Mientras está inmovilizada la consume tranquilamente."ePonen sus púas en las paredes de las cuevas y absorben los minerales que encuentran en la roca."tSe adhieren a los techos de las cuevas y disparan púas de acero a los objetivos que pasan por debajo de ellos."PEntrelazar dos cuerpos y girar genera la energía que necesitan para vivir."}Los miniengranajes giratorios giran a alta velocidad y se disparan repetidamente. Es peligroso si los engranajes no regresan."_El engranaje con el núcleo rojo gira a alta velocidad para una rápida carga de energía."�Estos Pokémon se mueven en cardúmenes. Tienen un órgano generador de electricidad, por lo que descargan electricidad si están en peligro."mEstos Pokémon tienen un gran apetito. Cuando ven a su presa, la atacan y la paralizan con electricidad."}Con sus bocas de succión, succionan a la presa. Luego usan sus colmillos para electrocutar a la presa con electricidad."cEste Pokémon nunca se había visto hasta que apareció de lejos en el desierto hace 50 años."`Utiliza poder psíquico para controlar el cerebro de un oponente y manipular sus recuerdos."hMientras enciende una luz y finge ser una guía, absorbe la fuerza vital de cualquiera que lo siga."ILlega cerca del momento de la muerte y roba el espíritu del cuerpo."ZSer consumido en la llama de Chandelure quema el espíritu, dejando atrás el cuerpo."}Marcan su territorio dejando cortes en los árboles con sus colmillos. Si se rompe un colmillo, crece uno nuevo rápidamente."sSus colmillos pueden romper rocas. Las batallas territoriales entre Fraxure pueden ser intensamente violentas."�Sus resistentes colmillos permanecerán afilados incluso si se usan para cortar vigas de acero. Están cubiertos con una dura armadura."~Su nariz siempre está goteando. Olfatea los mocos porque la mucosidad proporciona la materia prima para sus movimientos."~Congela su aliento para crear colmillos y garras de hielo con los que luchar. Las zonas frías del norte son su hábitat."uCuando el clima se vuelve cálido, estos Pokémon se convierten en vapor. Casi nunca ves Cryscross en el verano."]Nacen en nubes de nieve. Usan cadenas hechas de cristales de hielo para capturar presas."zEvoluciona cuando se baña en una energía similar a la eléctrica junto con Karrablast. La razón aún se desconoce."iHabiendo quitado su caparazón pesado, se vuelve muy ligero y puede luchar con movimientos de ninja."xSe esconde en el lodo de la orilla del mar. Luego espera. Cuando la presa lo toca, libera una descarga de energía."�Atrae a sus presas con sus labios mientras espera en el lodo. Cuando una presa se acerca, lo atrapa con sus colmillos metálicos."Han dominado combos elegantes. A medida que se concentran, sus movimientos de batalla se vuelven más rápidos y precisos."UUsan el largo pelaje de sus brazos como un látigo para golpear a sus oponentes."�Corre a través de cuevas estrechas, usando sus afiladas garras para atrapar presas. La piel de su cara es más dura que una roca."hSe cree que estos Pokémon fueron creados por la ciencia de una civilización antigua y misteriosa."�Se dice que Golurk recibió la orden de proteger a las personas y a los Pokémon por parte de los pueblos antiguos que los crearon."lLuchan a las órdenes de Bisharp. Se aferran a su presa e infligen daño hundiendo sus espadas en ella."pBisharp persigue a la presa en compañía de un nutrido grupo de Pawniard. Luego Bisharp remata a la presa."jSólo un Bisharp que se destaque antes los otros en su vasto ejército puede evolucionar a Kingambit."}Cargan salvajemente y dan cabezazos a todo. Sus cabezazos tienen suficiente fuerza destructiva para descarrilar un tren."Retarán cualquier cosa, incluso a oponentes fuertes, sin miedo. Sus peleas frecuentes los ayudan a volverse más fuertes."qCuantas más cicatrices tienen, más respeto obtienen estos valientes soldados del cielo de sus compañeros."DChillando sin piedad, este feroz Pokémon pájaro sale a cazar."mTienden a proteger sus posaderas con huesos adecuados que han encontrado. Persiguen a Pokémon débiles."sObservando desde el cielo, se abalanzan para atacar a Pokémon debilitados en el suelo. Se decoran con huesos."�Pisotea en oponentes más pequeños con sus poderosas piernas, a veces cayéndose en el proceso, si su casa es rota, emitirá terrbiles quejidos hasta que sea reparada."�Remoja los restos de su presa dentro del jarrón que protege, revolviendo el brebaje con sus garras. El folklore dice que su alma se queda dentro de la masa."|Usando sus lenguas muy calientes y cubiertas de llamas, queman los cuerpos de acero de Durant y consumen sus entrañas."mDurant cava nidos en las montañas. Construyen sus túneles complicados e interconectados en laberintos."xNo pueden ver, por lo que atacan y muerden para aprender sobre su entorno. Sus cuerpos están cubiertos de heridas."hComo sus dos cabezas no se llevan bien y compiten entre sí por la comida, siempre comen demasiado."fLas cabezas en sus brazos no tienen cerebro. Usan las tres cabezas para consumir y destruir todo."�La base de los volcanes es donde construyen sus hogares. Disparan fuego desde sus cinco cuernos para repeler a los enemigos que los atacan."yUn mar de fuego envuelve el entorno de sus batallas, ya que usan sus seis alas para dispersar sus escamas de brasas."{Tiene un cuerpo y un corazón de acero. Su resplandor es suficiente para hacer que incluso un Pokémon rebelde lo obedezca."�Su carga es lo bastante fuerte como para romper la pared de un castillo gigante de un solo golpe. Se habla de este Pokémon en las leyendas."�De su cabeza brotan cuernos tan afilados como cuchillas. Usando movimientos de torbellino, confunde y corta rápidamente a los oponentes."rAtraviesa el mundo, recorriendo la superficie de los océanos y los ríos. Aparece en las pintorescas costas."�Tornadus expulsa una energía masiva de su cola, provocando tormentas severas. Su poder es lo suficientemente grande como para volar casas."zLas púas de su cola descargan inmensos relámpagos. Vuela alrededor de la Región de Teselia disparando relámpagos."}La energía que brota de su cola aumenta la nutrición en el suelo, haciendo que los cultivos crezcan a un gran tamaño."`De acuerdo a la leyenda, el amor de este Pokémon dió vida fresca a través de todo Hisui."rCuando la cola de Reshiram se enciende, la energía térmica mueve la atmósfera y cambia el clima del mundo."hEste Pokémon aparece en las leyendas. En su cola tiene un generador gigante que crea electricidad."wGenera una poderosa energía helada dentro de sí mismo, pero su cuerpo se congeló cuando la energía se filtró."sLas melodías que canta Meloetta tienen el poder de poner contentos o tristes a los Pokémon que las escuchen."jEste antiguo Pokémon Bicho fue alterado por el Equipo Plasma. Actualizaron el cañón en su espalda."eCrea un suministro ilimitado de energía dentro de su cuerpo, que comparte con quienes lo tocan."�Las púas de su cabeza suelen ser blandas. Cuando las flexiona, las puntas se vuelven tan duras y afiladas que pueden perforar la roca."sFortalecen la parte inferior de sus cuerpos al chocar unos con otros. Son muy amables y no comenzarán peleas."yCuando toma una postura defensiva con sus puños protegiendo su rostro, podría resistir la explosión de una bomba."�Mientras camina, mastica una ramita en lugar de un refrigerio. Intimida a los oponentes al expulsar aire caliente por las orejas."|Cuando se arranca la ramita de su cola, la fricción enciende la ramita. La llama se usa para enviar señales a sus aliados."wMira fijamente la llama en la punta de su rama para lograr un estado concentrado, lo que le permite ver el futuro."�Protege su piel cubriendo su cuerpo con delicadas burbujas. Bajo su aire despreocupado, mantiene un ojo vigilante en su entorno."�Puede lanzar guijarros cubiertos de burbujas con un control preciso, golpeando latas vacías a una distancia de hasta treinta metros."�Aparece y desaparece como un ninja. Juega con sus enemigos usando movimientos rápidos, mientras los corta con estrellas arrojadizas de agua."tTiene orejas como palas. Cavar hoyos fortalece tanto sus orejas que pueden cortar raíces gruesas sin esfuerzo."�Tan poderoso como una excavadora, sus orejas reducen un denso lecho rocoso a escombros. Cuando termina de excavar, holgazanea perezosamente."vEstos amistosos Pokémon se envían señales entre sí con hermosos chirridos y movimientos de plumas en la cola."�Cuanto más caliente esté el saco de llamas en su vientre, más rápido puede volar, pero lleva algo de tiempo encender el fuego."lEn la fiebre de una batalla apasionante, arroja brasas de los espacios entre sus plumas y toma el aire."mEl polvo que cubre su cuerpo regula su temperatura, por lo que puede vivir en cualquier región o clima."�Vive escondido entre las sombras de la espesura. Cuando los depredadores atacan, eriza el pelaje que cubre su cuerpo para amenazarlos."�Vivillon con muchos patrones diferentes se encuentran en todo el mundo. Estos patrones se ven afectados por el clima de su hábitat."Parten solos de su manada y viven solos para volverse más fuertes. Estos Pokémon de sangre caliente son rápidos para luchar."�Con un aliento de fuego de más de 5,500º C, amenazan brutalmente a cualquier retador. Las hembras protegen a los cachorros de la manada."�Cuando encuentra una flor que le gusta, se detiene en esa flor durante toda su vida. Flota en el abrazo del viento con un corazón tranquilo."�Revolotea alrededor de los campos de flores y cuida las flores que comienzan a marchitarse. Saca el poder de las flores para la batalla."�Reclama exquisitos jardines de flores como su territorio, y obtiene poder al disfrutar de la energía emitida por las plantas con flores."wSe cree que es uno de los primeros Pokémon en vivir en armonía con los humanos, tiene una disposición plácida."hHabitan regiones montañosas. El líder de la manada se decide por una batalla de cuernos chocando."�Hace todo lo posible para que sus enemigos lo tomen en serio, pero su resplandor no es intimidante. Masticar una hoja es su marca registrada."�Golpea a los oponentes como un berserker, sin importarle los golpes que reciba. Sus brazos son tan poderosos que rompe postes de teléfono."dHistóricamente, en la Región de Kalos, estos Pokémon eran los guardianes designados del rey."wTiene suficiente energía psíquica para volar todo a 300 pies de sí mismo, pero no tiene control sobre su poder."�Cuando está en peligro, levanta las orejas y libera suficiente poder psíquico para convertir en polvo un camión de 10 toneladas."�Aparentemente, este Pokémon nace cuando un espíritu difunto habita una espada. Se adhiere a las personas y bebe su fuerza vital."�Los complejos patrones de ataque de sus dos espadas son imparables, incluso para un oponente muy hábil en el manejo de la espada."�Aparentemente, puede detectar las cualidades innatas del liderazgo. Quienquiera que reconozca está destinado a convertirse en rey."}En el pasado, en lugar de usar perfume, las damas reales llevaban un Spritzee que emanaba una fragancia que les gustaba."�Su aroma es tan abrumador que, a menos que un Entrenador realmente disfrute el olor, tendrá dificultades para caminar junto a él."~Usa tanto magia blanca como negra. Cosecha las flores que crecen en brujas que regularmente caminan entre la vida y la muerte."tPara enredar a sus oponentes en la batalla, saca hilos blancos tan dulces y pegajosos como algodón de azúcar."�Su sentido del olfato es 100 millones de veces mejor que el de un humano. Incluso el olor más leve le dice todo lo que hay a su alrededor."~Enciende los puntos emisores de luz en su cuerpo, drenando la voluntad de lucha de su oponente para escabullirse y esconderse."�Atrae a su presa con movimientos hipnóticos, luego la envuelve con sus tentáculos antes de acabar con ella con fluidos digestivos."gDos Binacle viven juntos en una roca. Cuando pelean, uno de ellos se moverá a una roca diferente."�Las piernas y las manos de Barbaracle tienen mente propia, y se moverán de forma independiente. Pero por lo general siguen las órdenes del jefe."zCamuflados como algas podridas, rocían veneno líquido sobre la presa que se acerca desprevenida y luego la rematan."fSe cuentan historias de barcos que vagan por los mares donde viven Dragalge, para nunca regresar."_Nacido en aguas impolutas, evitan ser detectados camuflándose con las plantas submarinas."LGalopan en el lecho marino, limpiándolo al juntar algas en sus cascos."vDerriban a sus presas voladoras disparando agua comprimida con sus enormes garras como si dispararan una pistola."Sus enormes garras lanzan balas de cañón de agua lo suficientemente potentes como para perforar los cascos de los petroleros."Hacen su hogar en los desiertos. Pueden generar su energía tomando el sol, por lo que comer alimentos no es un requisito."Brillan sus volantes y generan energía. Un solo Heliolisk puede generar suficiente electricidad para alimentar un rascacielos."}Sus inmensas fauces tienen suficiente fuerza destructiva como para masticar un automóvil. Vivió hace 100 millones de años."iNada podía detener a este Pokémon hace 100 millones de años, por lo que se comportó como un rey."�Este antiguo Pokémon fue restaurado a partir de una parte de su cuerpo que había estado congelada en hielo durante más de 100 millones de años."�Los cristales en forma de diamante en su cuerpo expulsan aire a -150 grados Centígrados, rodeando a sus enemigos y envolviéndolos en hielo."�Aunque su cuerpo es pequeño, sus habilidades de lucha le permiten mantenerse al día con los grandes matones como Machamp y Hariyama."�Utiliza su cola para absorber la electricidad de las centrales eléctricas o de las casas, y luego dispara la electricidad de sus bigotes."�Ha dormido bajo tierra durante cientos de millones de años desde su nacimiento. Ocasionalmente se encuentra durante la excavación de cuevas."gPuede crear instantáneamente muchos diamantes al comprimir el carbono en el aire entre sus manos."tEl Pokémon de tipo Dragón más débil, vive en lugares húmedos y sombríos, por lo que su cuerpo no se seca."�Ahuyenta a los oponentes al excretar un líquido pegajoso que puede disolver cualquier cosa. No puede ver nada por sus ojos involucionados."tEste simpático Pokémon de tipo Dragón abrazará a su amado Entrenador, dejándolo cubierto de baba pegajosa."The iron in Sliggoo's drinking water turned its shell metallic. This Pokémon doesn't come out of its shell on sunny days."�Puede controlar la dureza de su coraza metálica. Detesta la soledad y se pondrá furioso si aquellos que aprecia lo dejan de lado."�Nunca suelta una llave que le gusta, así que la gente le da las llaves de las bóvedas y cajas fuertes como una forma de prevenir el crimen."�Según los viejos cuentos, estos Pokémon son muñones poseídos por los espíritus de los niños que murieron perdidos en el bosque."xPuede controlar los árboles a voluntad. Atrapará a las personas que dañen el bosque, para que nunca puedan irse."�El cuerpo de calabaza está habitado por un espíritu atrapado en este mundo. A medida que se pone el sol, se vuelve inquieto y activo."qEnvuelve a su presa en sus brazos como pelos. Canta alegremente mientras observa el sufrimiento de su presa."�Bloquea los ataques de los oponentes con el hielo que protege su cuerpo. Usa aire frío para reparar cualquier grieta con hielo nuevo."}Su cuerpo cubierto de hielo es tan duro como el acero. Su estructura engorrosa aplasta todo lo que se interpone en su camino."[Este Pokémon arrasa caminos de montaña, atravesando la nieve con su armadura helada."sViven en cuevas completamente negras. Sus enormes orejas pueden emitir ondas ultrasónicas de 200.000 hercios."~Las ondas ultrasónicas que emite desde sus oídos pueden reducir una gran roca a guijarros. Sale de la oscuridad para atacar."zLas leyendas dicen que puede compartir la vida eterna. Durmió durante mil años en forma de árbol antes de revivir."|Cuando su vida llega a su fin, absorbe la energía vital de todos los seres vivos y se convierte en un capullo una vez más."qSe supone que está monitoreando a quienes destruyen el ecosistema desde lo profundo de la cueva donde vive."tEste alborotador envía cualquier cosa y todo a lugares lejanos usando su bucle, que puede deformar el espacio."jExpulsa su vapor interno de los brazos en su espalda. Tiene poder suficiente para volar una montaña."wSe desliza en silencio, acercándose a sus objetivos. Antes de que lo noten, comienza a lanzarles patadas feroces."�Un poco coqueto, pasa su tiempo libre acicalándose las alas. Su preocupación por la suciedad en su plumaje puede dejarlo incapaz de luchar."cAunque básicamente es frío y cauteloso, cuando es cogido por sorpresa, es presa del pánico."kEl aire que Decidueye guarda en los raquises de sus plumas lo insula contra el frío extremo de Hisui."nNo permite que sus emociones se vean fácilmente. Ganarse su confianza lleva tiempo. Prefiere la soledad."jEn su garganta, lleva una campana de fuego. La campana suena cada vez que este Pokémon escupe fuego."�Este Pokémon tiene es violento y egoísta. Si no está de humor para escuchar, ignorará las órdenes de su Entrenador con total indiferencia."�Este Pokémon aspira fluidos corporales por la nariz, inflando globos para aplastar a sus enemigos. Es famoso por ser muy trabajador."�Se preocupa profundamente por sus compañeros. Cuando su Entrenador se siente deprimido, realiza un baile alegre para tratar de ayudar."�Su voz cantarina es su arma principal en la batalla. El Entrenador de este Pokémon debe priorizar el mantenimiento diario de su garganta."�Puede picotear 16 veces por segundo para perforar agujeros en los árboles. Utiliza los agujeros para almacenar alimentos y anidar."wAl doblar su pico, puede producir una variedad de llamadas y convertirse en una molestia ruidosa para sus vecinos."{Dentro de su pico, su gas interno se enciende, lanzando explosivamente semillas con suficiente poder para pulverizar rocas."~Deambula en una búsqueda interminable de comida. Al anochecer, se derrumba por el agotamiento y se queda dormido en el lugar."wCuando encuentra un rastro de su presa, vigila pacientemente el lugar, pero siempre está dormitando al anochecer."eSu fuerte mandíbula le permite raspar árboles y sorber la savia. Normalmente vive bajo tierra."rSu cuerpo es capaz de almacenar electricidad. En los viajes de campamento, la gente agradece tener uno cerca."�Se desplaza rápidamente, en busca de una abertura. Concentra la energía eléctrica dentro de sus grandes mandíbulas para eliminar a sus enemigos."�Golpea tanto que sus pinzas a menudo se desprenden por el uso excesivo, pero vuelven a crecer rápidamente. Su carne es rica y deliciosa."�Lanza puñetazos indiscriminadamente. En momentos de desesperación, puede cortarse sus propias pinzas y dispararlas como cohetes."�Golpea sus alas para crear fuego. A medida que avanza en los pasos de su hermosa danza, baña a los oponentes en llamas intensas."wMiríadas de Cutiefly revolotean sobre las cabezas de las personas que tienen auras parecidas a las de las flores."~Enrolla el polen en bocanadas. Hace muchas variedades diferentes, algunas se usan como alimento y otras se usan en la batalla."�Este Pokémon ha vivido con la gente desde hace mucho tiempo. Puede sentir cuando su Entrenador está deprimido y se mantendrá cerca de su lado."�Cuando se cría adecuadamente desde una edad temprana, se convertirá en un compañero confiable que nunca traicionará a su Entrenador."�Bañado en el sol del ocaso, Wolferoc pasó por un tipo de evolución especial. Un intenso espíritu de lucha sustenta su calma."�Provoca a sus enemigos para que lo ataquen, resiste los golpes, y a cambio, les propina un cabezazo, aplastando sus huesos con su melena rocosa."�Es débil y notablemente sabroso, por lo que todos siempre están dispuestos a conseguirlo. Cualquiera que lo intente recibe una dolorosa lección."�Hunde el pincho de veneno en su cabeza en su presa. Cuando la presa se ha debilitado, Mareanie asesta el golpe final con sus 10 tentáculos."�Los atacados por el veneno de Toxapex sufrirán un dolor intenso durante 3 días y 3 noches. Después de la recuperación, habrá algunas secuelas."�Tiene una disposición obstinada e individualista. Comer tierra, hacer lodo y jugar en el fango forman parte de su rutina diaria."}Sus patadas pesadas y cubiertas de barro son su mejor medio de ataque, y puede reducir camiones grandes a chatarra sin sudar."tSe arrastra por la tierra en busca de comida. Su burbuja de agua le permite respirar y protege su suave cabeza."�A pesar de su apariencia, se preocupa por los demás. Si encuentra Pokémon débiles y vulnerables, los protege en su burbuja de agua."tDurante el día duerme y se empapa de luz. Cuando cae la noche, anda buscando un lugar más seguro para dormir."{Requiere mucho esfuerzo mantener los vivos colores de Lurantis, pero algunos coleccionistas disfrutan de este trabajo."hDispersa esporas que parpadean y brillan. Cualquiera que vea estas luces cae en un sueño profundo."�Los bosques donde viven los Shiinotic son traicioneros por la noche. Las personas confundidas por sus extrañas luces nunca vuelven a casa."Quema sus fluidos corporales para crear un gas venenoso. Cuando sus enemigos se desorientan por inhalar el gas, los ataca."nLleno de feromonas, su gas venenoso se puede diluir para usarlo en la producción de deliciosos perfumes."Un toque de cualquiera, excepto un amigo conocido, lo envía a un frenesí creciente. Es un Pokémon increíblemente peligroso."�Tiene la costumbre de abrazar a sus compañeros. Muchos Entrenadores han dejado este mundo después de que fueron aplastados por su abrazo."{Un delicioso aroma brota de su cuerpo. A menudo son tragados enteros por Toucannon atraídos por esa delicia flotante."�Este Pokémon siempre está rebotando enérgicamente. Otros Pokémon se sienten atraídos por su apariencia vivaz y su agradable aroma."�Sus piernas largas y llamativas no son solo para mostrar, sino para usarlas para patear. Al ganar, patea a su rival, riendo a carcajadas."�Los baños preparados con las flores de su enredadera tienen un efecto relajante, por lo que este Pokémon es un éxito entre muchas personas."�En lo alto de las altas copas de los árboles de la jungla, habita este Pokémon. A veces aparece en la playa para competir con Slowking."tForman grupos de aproximadamente 20 individuos. Su vínculo mutuo es notable: nunca defraudarán a un camarada."�Este Pokémon es un cobarde. A medida que sale corriendo, el movimiento de sus muchas patas deja un camino limpio y reluciente a su paso."xCon un corte resplandeciente de sus gigantescas y afiladas garras, parte el agua de mar, o incluso el aire, en dos."�Toma el control de cualquiera que ponga una mano en su boca. Y así se suma a la acumulación de su cuerpo de montículo de arena."iEnterrados debajo del castillo hay masas de huesos secos de aquellos cuya vitalidad ha sido drenada."�Estos Pokémon bordean las playas. La mucosidad pegajosa que cubre sus cuerpos se puede usar para calmar la piel quemada por el sol."|Debido al peligro de que este Pokémon sintético se vuelva loco, usa una máscara de control para restringir su poder."�Su confianza en su compañero es lo que lo despierta. Este Pokémon es capaz de cambiar de tipo, una flexibilidad que se muestra bien en batalla."�Si su núcleo permanece expuesto, morirá pronto. Es posible que sobreviva si se coloca en una Poké Ball lo suficientemente rápido."�Nace dormido y muere dormido. Todos sus movimientos aparentemente no son más que el resultado de dar vueltas y vueltas en sus sueños."�El caparazón de su espalda es químicamente inestable y explota violentamente si se golpea. El agujero en su estómago es su punto débil."�El pelaje espinoso de su espalda normalmente está en reposo. Cuando este Pokémon se agita, su pelaje se eriza y apuñala a sus atacantes."�Se desconoce su apariencia real. Un erudito que vio lo que había debajo de su trapo se sintió abrumado por el terror y murió a causa del susto."�Aturde a su presa con psicoquinesis y luego la tritura con sus fuertes dientes. Incluso el caparazón de Shellder no es rival para él."�Este Pokémon es amigable con las personas y ama a los niños sobre todo. Baja de las montañas para jugar con los niños que le gustan en la ciudad."}Baldeando su enorme ancla, puede noquear a Wailord de un solo golpe. Lo que parece ser algas verdes es en realidad su cuerpo."�Expresa sus sentimientos golpeando sus escamas. Los sonidos metálicos resuenan a través de las altas montañas donde vive Jangmo-o."jSe lanza sobre su presa con un grito valiente. Sus puñetazos escamosos hacen trizas a sus oponentes."�Cuando detecta enemigos, los amenaza haciendo tintinear las escamas de su cola. Los oponentes débiles se romperán y huirán presas del pánico."�Confunde a sus enemigos al volar demasiado rápido. Tiene un temperamento de gatillo rápido, pero pronto olvida lo que le enfadó."Mientras revolotea, esparce sus escamas extrañamente brillantes. Se dice que tocarlas restaura la buena salud en el acto."}Arranca grandes árboles de raíz y los balancea. Hace que crezca la vegetación y luego absorbe la energía del crecimiento."�La densa niebla que crea trae la caída y destrucción de sus confusos enemigos. Las corrientes oceánicas son la fuente de su energía."�En épocas pasadas, se le llamaba el niño de las estrellas. Se dice que es un Pokémon de otro mundo, pero no se conocen detalles específicos."�Inmóvil como si estuviera muerto, su cuerpo es levemente cálido al tacto. En el pasado lejano, se le llamaba el capullo de las estrellas."wSe dice que este Pokémon es una evolución masculina de Cosmog. Al activar su tercer ojo, parte hacia otro mundo."jSe dice que es una evolución femenina de Cosmog. Cuando se activa su tercer ojo, vuela a otro mundo."�La luz es la fuente de su energía. Si no devora luz, las impurezas se acumulan en ella, y Necrozma se oscurece y deja de moverse."�Uno de varios Ultraentes misteriosos. La gente en la calle informa haber observado que los infestados por él se vuelven violentos."}Este Ultraente apareció de otro mundo. Muestra su cuerpo, pero no está claro si esa exhibición es un alarde o una amenaza."hUno de los Ultraentes. Se niega a tocar nada, tal vez porque siente algo de suciedad en este mundo."�Una de las misteriosas formas de vida conocidas como Ultraentes. Asombrosas descargas eléctricas emanan de todo su cuerpo, según testigos."gUn tipo de Ultraente. Los testigos lo han visto quemar un bosque expulsando gas de sus dos brazos."�Una de las formas de vida conocidas como Ultraentes, se observó cortando una gigantesca torre de acero con un golpe de su espada."}Un Ultraente peligroso, parece estar comiendo constantemente, pero por alguna razón nunca se han encontrado sus excrementos."�Un Ultraente que vive en un mundo diferente, se ríe salvajemente mientras rocía a sus oponentes con veneno de las agujas en su cabeza."~Un tipo de Ultraente, dispara un líquido brillante y venenoso de sus agujas. Este líquido también es inmensamente adhesivo."yApareció de un Ultraumbral. Cada uno parece estar formado por muchas formas de vida apiladas una encima de la otra."�Se desliza hacia la gente. Luego, sin previo aviso, desencadena la explosión de su propia cabeza. Aparentemente es un tipo de Ultraente."lSu cuerpo mecanizado es simplemente un recipiente. Su verdadero yo es su Coránima, un alma artificial."{Capaz de ocultarse en las sombras, nunca aparece ante los humanos, por lo que su existencia misma era materia de mito."�Electrifica sus garras y desgarra a sus oponentes con ellas. Incluso si esquivan su ataque, serán electrocutados por las chispas voladoras."�Funde partículas de hierro y otros metales que se encuentran en el subsuelo, para que pueda absorberlas en su cuerpo de acero fundido."�Reverenciado hace mucho tiempo por su capacidad para crear hierro de la nada, por alguna razón ha vuelto a la vida después de 3000 años."uAtaca con rápidos golpes de su bastón. A medida que golpea con una velocidad asombrosa, se bombea más y más."�Cuando está tocando ritmos rápidos en la batalla, queda tan atrapado en el ritmo que ni siquiera se da cuenta de que ya noqueó a su oponente."�El que tiene las mejores técnicas de percusión se convierte en el jefe. Tiene una disposición amable y valora la armonía entre su grupo."�Tiene almohadillas especiales en la parte posterior de sus patas y una en la nariz. Estas almohadillas irradian un calor tremendo cuando pelea."wPatea bayas de las ramas de los árboles y luego las hace malabarismos con sus pies, practicando su juego de pies."Es hábil tanto en el ataque como en la defensa. Pero si comienza a exhibirse, podría ponerse en una situación difícil."nCuando se moja, su piel cambia de color, y este Pokémon se vuelve invisible como si estuviera camuflado."�Altamente inteligente pero también muy perezoso, mantiene a los enemigos fuera de su territorio tendiendo trampas por todas partes."�Elige los puntos débiles de los enemigos para poder destruirlos con precisión con agua que sale disparada de la punta de sus dedos a Mach 3."�Come bayas sin parar, un hábito que lo ha hecho más resistente de lo que parece. Aparecerá en las granjas, en busca de aún más bayas."{Común en toda la región de Galar, este Pokémon tiene dientes fuertes y puede masticar las cáscaras de bayas más duras."�Saltando ágilmente, este Pokémon de cuerpo pequeño aprovecha incluso la más mínima oportunidad para desorientar a los oponentes más grandes."rLas lecciones de muchas duras batallas le han enseñado cómo juzgar con precisión la fuerza de un oponente."�Con su gran intelecto y habilidades de vuelo, estos Pokémon actúan con mucho éxito como el servicio de taxi aéreo de la región de Galar."wA menudo se encuentra en los jardines, este Pokémon tiene pelos en su cuerpo que utiliza para evaluar su entorno."�A medida que crece dentro de su caparazón, usa sus habilidades psíquicas para monitorear el mundo exterior y prepararse para la evolución."�Emite energía psíquica para observar y estudiar lo que hay a su alrededor, y lo que hay a su alrededor puede incluir cosas a más de 9 Km."�Astuto y cauteloso, este Pokémon sobrevive robando comida a los demás. Borra sus huellas con golpes de cola mientras se lleva su botín."dDe cuerpo ágil y garras afiladas, anda robando comida y huevos. Boltund es su enemigo natural."�Gira en el viento mientras canta una canción alegre. Esta encantadora exhibición ha cautivado a muchos para criar a este Pokémon."|El algodón en la cabeza de este Pokémon se puede tejer en un hilo brillante y hermoso, una especialidad regional de Galar."�Si su vellón crece demasiado, Wooloo no podrá moverse. La tela hecha con la lana de este Pokémon es sorprendentemente fuerte."rSus majestuosos cuernos solo están destinados a impresionar al género opuesto. Nunca ven uso en la batalla."�Comienza las batallas atacando con su cuerno duro como una roca, tan pronto como el oponente retrocede, este Pokémon muerde y nunca lo suelta."�Este Pokémon extiende rápidamente su cuello retráctil para hundir sus afilados colmillos en enemigos distantes y derribarlos."�Se balancea como un peleador de sumo, haciéndolo casi imposible de derribar. Su cuerpo es incluso más resiliente que su caparazón."�Este Pokémon glotón solo ayuda a las personas con su trabajo porque quiere golosinas. Mientras corre, crepita con electricidad."�Envía electricidad a través de sus piernas para aumentar su fuerza. Corriendo a máxima velocidad, rompe fácilmente los 80 Km/h."mPuede correr como un monociclo, incluso en terrenos ásperos y rocosos. El carbón ardiente lo sostiene."�Al girar rápidamente sus piernas, puede viajar a más de 30 Km/h. La temperatura de las llamas que respira supera los 980 grados Centígrados."�Mientras está en combate, su montaña de carbón arderá de color rojo brillante, enviando chispas que quemarán el área circundante."uTan pronto como nace, se entierra en una manzana que depèndiendo del sabor de la fruta determina su evolución."zVuela sobre alas de piel de manzana y escupe un ácido poderoso. También puede cambiar su forma a la de una manzana."�Su cuerpo está cubierto de néctar dulce, y la piel de su espalda es especialmente deliciosa. Los niños solían comerlo como refrigerio."�Exterappli, el que saca la cabeza, e Interappli, el que saca la cola, viven juntos dentro de la manzana y se ayudan el uno al otro."~Se trata de siete seres llamados Viborappli que viven juntos en una manzana de caramelo. El del centro es el líder del grupo."sEscupe arena por sus fosas nasales. Mientras el enemigo está cegado, se entierra en el suelo para esconderse."nSu estilo único de enrollamiento le permite expulsar arena de su saco de arena de manera más eficiente."�Sus escamas en la barriga pueden pulverizar una cantera de arena para usar en batalla. Sus batallas contra Flygon en el ojo de las tormentas son legendarias."�Este Pokémon hambriento se traga entero a Arrokuda. A veces, comete un error y trata de tragarse a un Pokémon que no sea su presa preferida."�Después de que ha comido hasta saciarse, sus movimientos se vuelven extremadamente lentos. Ahí es cuando Cramorant se lo traga."�Hace girar su aleta caudal para impulsarse y arremeter contra la presa, a la que ensarta a una velocidad que supera los 100 nudos."�Manipula la composición química de su veneno para producir electricidad. El voltaje es débil, pero puede causar una parálisis hormigueante."oEste Pokémon irascible y agresivo traga agua estancada para absorber cualquier toxina que pueda contener."�Inconscientemente transmite el audio de sus combates a través de señales de radio. Si lo escuchas en el momento justo escucharás un gran espectáculo."�Envuelve a sus presas con su cuerpo caliente, cocinándolas en sus rollos. Una vez bien hechas, las mordisquea hasta el último bocado."�Si bien su cuerpo en llamas ya es peligroso por sí solo, este Pokémon excesivamente hostil también tiene colmillos grandes y muy afilados."�Incluso el titanio sólido se derretirá en su espiral. Usa el espejismo masivo para confundir a los Volcarona que frencuentemente enfrenta."�Sus tentáculos se arrancan fácilmente, pero no se alarma cuando sucede, sabe que volverán a crecer. Es tan inteligente como un niño de 3 años."wBuscando un oponente para probar sus habilidades, emerge a tierra. Una vez que termina la batalla, regresa al mar."�La taza de té en la que este Pokémon tiene su hogar es una famosa pieza de vajilla antigua. Hay muchas falsificaciones en circulación."rCuando se enoja, lanza té de su cuerpo a la boca del ofensor. El té causa fuertes escalofríos si se traga."nPasa los días relájandose en la playa. Suele ser interrumpido por gente que lo confunde con una bebida."jA pesar de su aroma refrescante, aquellos que beban de su líquido son rápidamente puestos a dormir."qSi este Pokémon siente una emoción fuerte, huirá lo más rápido que pueda. Prefiere las zonas sin gente."�Usando las trenzas en su cabeza, golpea a los enemigos para que se calmen. Un golpe de esas trenzas noquearía a un boxeador profesional."�Si haces demasiado ruido, corres el riesgo de ser destrozado por las garras de su tentáculo. También se conoce como la Bruja del Bosque."Se cuela en las casas de las personas, roba cosas y se da un festín con la energía negativa de los ocupantes frustrados."}Con astucia astuta, trata de atraer a la gente al bosque. Algunos creen que tiene el poder de hacer crecer los cultivos."�Sus pelos funcionan como fibras musculares. Cuando sus pelos se despliegan, se aferran a los oponentes, atrapándolos como si fueran tentáculos."gDicen que cualquier pastelería visitada por Milcery tiene asegurado el éxito y la buena fortuna."cCuando Alcremie está contenta, la crema que segrega de sus manos se vuelve más dulce y rica."�Tan grande que parece desafiar los cielos, presume su posición elevada a otros Pokémon. Le da a su Entrenador conocimiento de lo dulce y amargo."�Los seis trabajan juntos como un Pokémon. El trabajo en equipo también es su estrategia de batalla, y cambian su formación mientras luchan."}Almacena electricidad en cada columna. Incluso si una se rompe, continúa emitiendo electricidad durante al menos tres horas."}Come nieve que se amontona en el suelo. Cuanta más nieve come, más grandes e impresionantes crecen las púas de su espalda."�No tiene piedad de nadie que profane campos y montañas. Volará con sus alas heladas, provocando una ventisca que ahuyentará a los infractores."sUna vez al año, en una fecha específica y a una hora específica, se juntan de la nada y forman un círculo."�Mantiene su cabeza sensible al calor fría con hielo. Pesca para su comida, colgando su único cabello en el mar para atraer a sus presas."�A través de sus cuernos, puede captar las emociones de las criaturas que lo rodean. Las emociones positivas son la fuente de su fuerza."�Lleva consigo semillas tostadas eléctricamente como si fueran tesoros. No importa cuánto coma, siempre vuelve a tener hambre en poco tiempo."�Si un trabajo requiere mucha fuerza, este Pokémon destacará en él. Su cuerpo se empaña con la lluvia y se vuelve de un color verde vibrante."�Estos Pokémon viven en manadas. Sus trompas tienen una fuerza de agarre increíble, lo bastante fuerte como para convertir rocas en polvo."�Luego de evolucionar, toma la apariencia de un gran monumento. Si es venerado, protegerá aldeas cercanas de cualquier desastre."�Los poderosos músculos de su cola generan su electricidad. Comparado con la parte inferior de su cuerpo, la mitad superior es demasiado pequeña."�Vivía en las costas prehistóricas y podía conservar los alimentos con el hielo de su cuerpo. Se extinguió porque se movía muy lentamente."�Sus poderosas piernas son capaces de correr a velocidades superiores a 64 Km/h, pero no puede respirar a menos que esté bajo el agua."�La piel de su cara es impermeable a los ataques, pero las dificultades para respirar hicieron que este Pokémon se extinguiera de todos modos."�El metal especial que compone su cuerpo es muy ligero, por lo que este Pokémon tiene una gran agilidad. No le gusta la lluvia y vive en cuevas."�Nostálgico por su hogar que ahora le queda pequeño, llorará vidrio fundido. Aquellos sin entrenador podrán encontrar compañía de Pokémon pájaro."|Acumula la electricidad estática de su entorno. El rayo que dispara cuando está a cuatro patas posee una potencia colosal."�Si este Pokémon está solo, un niño podría vencerlo. Pero si tiene amigos que lo ayuden a entrenar, evolucionará y se volverá mucho más fuerte."�Sin un Dreepy para colocar en su cabeza y cuidar, está tan inquieto que querrá sustituir cualquier Pokémon que encuentre por el Dreepy perdido."wAparentemente, los Dreepy dentro de los cuernos de Dragapult esperan ansiosamente ser lanzados a velocidades Mach."�Este Pokémon ha dormido durante muchos años. Algunos dicen que es la hermana mayor de Zamazenta, otros dicen que los dos Pokémon son rivales."�Este Pokémon durmió durante eones mientras tenía forma de estatua. Estuvo dormido durante tanto tiempo que la gente olvidó que existió."�Estaba dentro de un meteorito que cayó hace 20.000 años. Parece haber una conexión entre este Pokémon y el fenómeno Dinamax."zSi Kubfu tira de su pelo blanco, su espíritu de lucha aumenta y un gran poder brota desde el interior de su barriga."�Habitando las montañas de una distante región, este Pokémon corre a través de precipicios, entrenando sus piernas y refinando su movimiento."�Una vez que las lianas del cuerpo de Zarude son arrancadas, se convierten en nutrientes. Esto ayuda a que las plantas del bosque crezcan."{Glastrier tiene una fuerza física tremenda, y la máscara helada que cubre su cara es 100 veces más dura que el diamante."~Mientras corre bajo la noche, Spectrier absorbe la fuerza vital de criaturas durmientes. Anhela el silencio y la soledad."�Las leyendas dicen que usando su poder para ver todos los eventos pasados y futuros, este Pokémon salvó las criaturas de un bosque del impacto de un meteorito."@This Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system."GThis Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system. Again!"�Esta es la forma que Castform toma en los días más brillantes. Su piel es sorprendentemente caliente al tacto, así que ten cuidado."�Esta es la forma que Castform toma al ser empapado con lluvia. Cuando su cuerpo es comprimido, agua se escurrirá como una esponja."�Esta es la forma que Castform toma al ser cubierto en nieve. Su cuerpo se vuelve similar al hielo, con una temperatura cercana a los -5 grados Celsius."}Esta es la forma que Castform toma cuando la arena vuela. Su cuerpo está hecho de partículas que giran constantemente."yEsta es la forma que toma Castform cuando la luna aparece. Las partículas de su cuerpo toman propiedades místicas."�Esta es la forma que toma Castform cuando un eclipse cubre el cielo. Se vueve usando sus manos hechas de pure energía psíquica."Este Rotom ha poseído un horno de microondas que usa un motor especial. Tiene cierta habilidad para manipular las llamas."qEsta forma de Rotom disfruta hacer bromas basadas en agua. Ten cuidado si no quieres inundar tu habitación."uRotom asume esta forma cuando toma un refrigerador que tenga un motor especial. Combate expulsando aire gélido."�En esta forma, Rotom aplica su nuevo poder sobre el viento junto con su amor por las bromas. Felizmente mandará a volar cualquier documento importante que encuentre."�Este es Rotom luego de haber tomado control de un cortacésped que tenga un motor especial. Mientras corta el cespéd, esparce este por todas partes."�La luz desencadena el cambio a esta forma, que recuerda al creador de todo lo existente. La colosal fuerza de la que hace gala sugiere que se trata de su verdadera forma."�Esta forma que surca el cielo se asemeja creador de todo lo existente. Se dice que adopta dicha forma para hacerse con su poder."{Pierde las patas al adoptar esta forma. Se sospecha que vive en un mundo en el que no hay distinción entre cielo y tierra."�Incluso Basculin, que devora todo lo que puede con su gran mandíbula, no es más que comida para los organismos más fuertes que él mismo."gHa visto que un mundo de verdad llegará para la gente y Pokémon. Lucha para proteger ese futuro."{Se dice que este Pokémon combate para proteger el mundo ideal que existirá en el futuro para la gente y el Pokémon."{El poder que duerme en su cuerpo ahora cubre su cuerno, transformándolo en una espada que puede atravesar lo que sea."oLos espíritus que deambulan en este mundo se colocan en el cuerpo de Pumpkaboo. Luego van a la otra vida."�Al llevar espíritus al más allá, los Pumpkaboo grandes prefieren los espíritus de los adultos en comparación a los de los niños."uLos Pumpkaboo extragrande se dicen ser el producto de áreas donde un gran número de almas perdidas permanecen."�Gritos macabros emanan de su cuerpo por la noche. Los sonidos se dicen ser el quejido de los espíritus que sufren en la otra vida."rLos Gourgeist toman el aspecto de los adultos, tomando las manos de los niños para llevarlos a la otra vida."gLos Gourgeist extragrande no son caprichosos. Forzosamente arrastrán a cualquiera a la otra vida."�Este es Zygarde cuando el 10% de sus células son ensambladas. Salta al torso de su oponente y clava sus colmillos afilados en él."yEsta es la forma perfecta de Zygarde. Desde el orificio de su pecho, irradia una poderosa energía que elimina todo."lCrea una carga eléctrica frotando sus alas. Baila hacia sus enemigos y les propina golpes eléctricos."}Este Oricorio se relaja meciendose tranquilamente. Esto aumenta su energía psíquica, que luego dispara a sus enemigos."dInvoca a los muertos con su danza. Desde su malicia, usa el poder para maldecir a sus enemigos."�Los Wishiwashi débiles se unen juntos para concentrar su poder. Su fuerza unida los hace el demonio del mar, temidos en todo el mar."�Si su núcleo permanece expuesto, morirá pronto. Es posible que sobreviva si se coloca en una Poké Ball lo suficientemente rápido."�Triste de que su verdadera identidad podría ser expuesta, Mimikyu atacará sin piedad buscando venganza en cualquier oponente que rompa su cuello."�Esta es la forma que toma Necrozma mientras absorbe el poder de Solgaleo, haciéndolo extremadamente feroz e imposible de controlar."vLunala ya no tiene su propia voluntad. Ahora bajo el control de Necrozma, continuamente expulsa toda su energía."rLa luz que emana de todo su cuerpo afecta a las cosas vivas y a la naturaleza, impactándola en varios modos."zLa más mínima provocación es a veces suficiente para que este Pokémon escupa el Arrokuda atascado en su garganta."}El Pikachu a medio tragar está tan sorprendido que aún no combate, pero que aún busca por una oportunidad de contraatacar."�El pelo en su cabeza conecta a la superficie de su cerebro. Cuando este Pokémon tiene algo en su mente, su pelo hiela el aire a su alrededor."�Sirven diligentemente a la gente y Pokémon así pueden reunir sentimientos de gratitud. Las hembras son particularmente buenas con niños."pLas hormonas de hambre afectan su temperamento. Hasta que sea saciado, se pone en todo tipo de malos actos."�Capaz de cortar cualquier cosa con un solo tajo, se conoce como la Espada Regia, inspirando asombro en tanto aliados como enemigos."lAhora equipado con su escudo, puede resistir golpes impresivos, incluyendo los de los Pokémon Dinamax."�Esta forma de Urshifu es un firme creyente en derrotar enemigos mediante grandes ráfagas de golpes sin descanso, que fluyen como un río."�Se dice que este Pokémon una vez evacuó a todo un bosque, y todos los Pokémon que viven allí, a una nueva ubicación en una sola noche."�Las leyendas dicen que usando su poder para ver todos los eventos pasados y futuros, este Pokémon salvó las criaturas de un bosque del impacto de un meteorito."jAl ser lastimado, deja de moverse. Se pone como una roca para meditar, aguzando su mente y espíritu."�Darmanitan toma su forma al estar furioso. No dejará de expulsar llamas hasta que su ira se termine, incluso si su cuerpo empieza a derretirse."�Esta forma ha reunido suficiente energía para que su poder sea mucho mayor al de un Ampharos regular. Se ha calculado que cada orbe tiene 9000 voltios de energía en su interior."�Esta forma de Garchomp es rara debido a las condiciones específicas requeridas. Con la fuerza de sus guadañas puede convertir una casa en astillas."�La agresividad de Gyarados es amplificada en esta forma. Todo lo que puede sentir es ira pura. Varios cruceros han destruidos por meterse en su camino."�El dolor de ver caer a aquellos quienes le importa lo ha convertido en esta forma. Su corazón puro potencia enormemente sus habilidades."~El dolor de ver a aquellos quienes quiere proteger ha causado que esta forma surja. Su corazón puro potencia sus filos rojos."�Sus músculos han sido potenciados con poder psíquico. Sus brazos pueden estirarse tres metros, y puede aplastar titanio con sus manos."�El ADN del Mew original ha crecido exponencialmente en esta forma. Posee suficiente poder psíquico para controlar las mentes de las personas más obstinadas."|Se diferencia de otros Basculin en varios aspectos, incluido el comportamiento. Es mucho más gentil que sus otra variantes."�Este Ursaluna tan particular se protege el cuerpo con una capa de barro tan dura como el hierro. Su ojo izquierdo le permite ver en la oscuridad.">This form also exists to test the PBS Extensions feature.;[_"gWhile it is young, it uses the nutrients that are stored in the seed on its back in order to grow."�To support its weight, Ivysaur's legs and trunk grow thick and strong. If it spends more time lying in the sunlight, it's a sign that the bud will bloom soon."_Its plant blooms when it is absorbing solar energy. It stays on the move to seek sunlight."tFrom the time it is born, a flame burns at the tip of its tail. Its life would end if the flame were to go out."_In the rocky mountains where Charmeleon live, their fiery tails shine at night like stars."fIf Charizard becomes furious, the flame at the tip of its tail flares up in a whitish-blue color."�Its shell is not just for protection. Its rounded shape and the grooves on its surface minimize resistance in water, enabling Squirtle to swim at high speeds."�Its large tail is covered with rich, thick fur that deepens in color with age. The scratches on its shell are evidence of this Pokémon's toughness in battle."dThe jets of water it spouts from the rocket cannons on its shell can punch through thick steel."�Its voracious appetite compels it to devour leaves bigger than itself without hesitation. It releases a terribly strong odor from its antennae."hA steel-hard shell protects its tender body. It quietly endures hardships while awaiting evolution."dWater-repellent powder on its wings enables it to collect honey, even in the heaviest of rains."}Evolutionary power has supercharged its wings and their toxic scales, which turn to pure energy at the slightest provocation."fPredators not warned off by its brightly-colored body are jabbed with the toxic barb on its head."�It remains virtually immobile while it clings to a tree. However, on the inside, it busily prepares for evolution. This is evident from how hot its shell becomes."rIt prefers hit-and-run attacks using its powerful poison stingers, trying to evade blows to its fragile body."�Its final evolution has sent its killer instinct into overdrive. It obeys its trainer unfailingly, but will grow impatient without a good fight."�It has an extremely sharp sense of direction. It can unerringly return home to its nest, however far it may be removed from its familiar surroundings."�This Pokémon flies around, patrolling its large territory. If its living space is violated, it shows no mercy in thoroughly punishing the foe with its sharp claws."dIt spreads its gorgeous wings wide to intimidate enemies. It races through the skies at Mach 2."YCautious in the extreme, its hardy vitality lets it live in any kind of environment."iWith its long fangs, this surprisingly violent Pokémon can gnaw away even thick concrete with ease."{It shows no interest in anything that isn't fresh. If you take it shopping with you, it will help you pick out ingredients."qIt makes its Rattata underlings gather food for it, dining solely on the most nutritious and delicious fare."vFarmers whose fields are troubled by bug Pokémon appreciate Spearow for its vigorous appetite and look after it."�Its long neck and elongated beak are ideal for catching prey in soil or water. It deftly moves this extended and skinny beak to pluck prey."�Ekans curls itself up in a spiral while it rests. Assuming this position allows it to quickly respond to a threat from any direction with a glare."jTransfixing prey with the face-like pattern on its belly, it binds and poisons the frightened victim."`It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled."fThis intelligent Pokémon roasts hard berries with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."�If it stores too much electricity, its behavior turns aggressive. To avoid this, it occasionally discharges excess energy and calms itself down."�Rarely, a Pikachu grows to incredible size instead of evolving into Raichu. It can power settlements so long as it's fed properly."dIt can loose 100,000-volt bursts of electricity, instantly downing foes several times its size."�It loves to bathe in the grit of dry, sandy areas. By sand bathing, this Pokémon rids itself of dirt and moisture clinging to its body."xIts claws and horns often break off. The broken claws and horns can be used to carve plows for tilling farm fields."nLife on mountains covered with deep snow has granted this Pokémon a body of ice that's as hard as steel."�It lives in snowy mountains on southern islands. When a blizzard rolls in, this Pokémon hunkers down in the snow to avoid getting blown away."�Its highly toxic barbs are thought to have developed as protection for this small-bodied Pokémon. When enraged, it releases a horrible toxin from its horn."�When Nidorina are with friends or family, they keep their barbs tucked away to prevent hurting each other. It becomes nervous if separated from the others."�It pacifies offspring by placing them in the gaps between the spines on its back. The spines will never secrete poison while young are present."wIts large ears are flapped like wings when it is listening to distant sounds. It extends toxic barbs when angered."�It's nervous and quick to act aggressively. The potency of its poison increases along with the level of adrenaline present in its body."�When it goes on a rampage, it's impossible to control. But in the presence of a Nidoqueen it's lived with for a long time, Nidoking calms down."bMany appear when the night skies are filled with shooting stars. They disappear with sunrise."�On every night of a full moon they come out to play. When dawn arrives, they return to their quiet mountain retreats and sleep nestled up against each other."�A Clefable uses its wings to skip lightly as if it were flying. Its bouncy step lets it even walk on water. On quiet, moonlit nights, it strolls on lakes."�From its mouth spew flames that seem to resemble the spirits of the deceased. Some people mistakenly think this fire is a ghost."^Legend has it that this mystical Pokémon was formed when nine saints coalesced into one."qIn hot weather, this Pokémon makes ice shards with its six tails and sprays them around to cool itself off."|It lives on mountains perpetually covered in snow and is revered as a deity incarnate. It appears draped in a blizzard."|It constantly demands treats and gifts from its Trainer. An expensive and fashionable hoard is necessary for evolution."�The gifts it received have become a tail of golden light. It weaponizes pure avaricious energy in battle, gaining in power as it is pampered."fIt has a very soft body. If it starts to roll, it will bounce all over and be impossible to stop."{By freely changing the wavelength of its voice, Jigglypuff sings a mysterious melody sure to make any listener sleepy."�The surfaces of its saucerlike eyes are always covered with a thin layer of tears. If any dust gets in this Pokémon's eyes, it is quickly washed away."�Their skin is so thin that they'll be burned if sunlight hits them. When it gets cold out, they gather together to warm one another's bodies."}Its thick fangs are hollow like straws, making them unexpectedly fragile. These fangs are specialized for sucking blood."�Both of its legs have turned into wings. Without a sound, Crobat flies swiftly toward its prey and sinks its fangs into the nape of its target's neck."eIf exposed to moonlight, it starts to move. It roams far and wide at night to scatter its seeds."�A horribly noxious honey drools from its mouth. One whiff of the honey can result in memory loss. Some fans are said to enjoy this overwhelming stink, however."cThe bud bursts into bloom with a bang. It then starts scattering allergenic, poisonous pollen."`When the heavy rainfall season ends, it is drawn out by warm sunlight to dance in the open."pNo matter how much it eats, the mushrooms growing on its back steal away most of the nutrients it consumes."_The large mushroom on its back controls it. It often fights over territory with Shiinotic."[Its big eyes are actually clusters of tiny eyes. At night, its kind is drawn by light."vThe powdery scales on its wings are hard to remove from skin. They also contain poison that leaks out on contact."~Around their crops, farmers plant trees that Diglett like to eat as a way of getting Diglett to plow the fields for them."nDugtrio's heads are sleek and smooth and incredibly hard. It can dig through any soil with its headbutts."�Its head sports an altered form of whiskers made of metal. When in communication with its comrades, its whiskers wobble to and fro."~Its shining gold hair provides it with protection. It's reputed that keeping any of its fallen hairs will bring bad luck."�It loves coins, so if you give it one, you can make friends with Meowth easily. But it's fickle, so you can't count on that friendship lasting."kBehind its lithe, elegant appearance lies a barbaric side. It will tear apart its prey on a mere whim."�Scientists are divided as to whether its incredible length inspired internet memes, or whether seeing memes caused a Meowth to undergo unprecedented evolution."yIt's impulsive, selfish, and fickle. It's very popular with some Trainers who like giving it the attention it needs."qIts round face is a symbol of wealth. Persian that have bigger, plumper faces are considered more beautiful."�These daring Pokémon have coins on their foreheads. Darker coins are harder, and harder coins garner more respect among Meowth."eAfter many battles, it evolved dangerous claws that come together to form daggers when extended."iIf its chronic headache peaks, it may exhibit odd powers. It seems unable to recall such an episode."gIt appears by waterways at dusk. It may use telekinetic powers if its forehead glows mysteriously."�It can spontaneously become enraged. Everyone near it clears out as it rampages and the resulting loneliness makes it angrier still."nIt has been known to become so angry that it dies as a result. Its face looks peaceful in death, however."~When its anger rose beyond a critical point, this Pokémon gained power that is unfettered by the limits of its physical body."`It has a brave and trustworthy nature. It fearlessly stands up to bigger and stronger foes."�Legends tell of it fighting alongside a general and conquering a whole country. Those hearing its bark feel compelled to grovel before it."hIts magnificent bark conveys a sense of majesty. Anyone hearing it can't help but grovel before it."|In rivers with fast-flowing water, this Pokémon will cling to a rock by using its thick lips, which act like a suction cup."uThis Pokémon's sweat is a slimy mucus. When captured, Poliwhirl can slither from its enemies' grasp and escape."�Its percentage of body fat is nearly zero. Its body is entirely muscle, which makes it heavy and forces its swimming prowess to develop."`If Poliwag and Poliwhirl hear its echoing cry, they respond by gathering from far and wide."It can read others' minds and will teleport away when danger approaches. You must clear your mind if you want to catch it."yIt stares at a silver spoon to amplify its psychic powers before it lets loose. Apparently, gold spoons are no good."�Alakazam's brain continually grows, making its head far too heavy to support with its neck. This Pokémon holds its head up using its psychokinetic power instead."�Machop exercises by hefting around a Graveler as if it were a barbell. There are some Machop that travel the world in a quest to master all kinds of martial arts."�Machoke works out every day even as it helps with tough labor. On its days off, this Pokémon heads to the fields and mountains to exercise and train."�It can lift heavy loads with the greatest of ease. It can even heft dump trucks. But its clumsy fingers prevent it from doing any precision work."�Bellsprout's thin and flexible body lets it bend and sway to avoid any attack. From its mouth, this Pokémon spits a corrosive fluid that melts even iron."mIf its prey is bigger than its mouth, it slices up the victim with sharp leaves, then eats every morsel."�It attracts prey with aromatic honey, then melts them in its mouth. Acid that has dissolved many prey becomes sweeter, making it even more alluring."zTentacool is not a particularly strong swimmer. It drifts across the surface of shallow seas as it searches for prey."�It communicates with others of its kind by lighting up the red orbs on its head. When the orbs are blinking, it's a warning sign."�The longer it lives, the more its edges are chipped and worn away. However, this Pokémon's heart will remain hard, craggy, and rough always."�This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom."When Golem grow old, they stop shedding their shells. Those that have lived a long, long time have shells green with moss."�Geodude compete against each other with headbutts. The iron sand on their heads will stick to whichever one has stronger magnetism."�They eat rocks and often get into a scrap over them. The shock of Graveler smashing together causes a flash of light and a booming noise."�It fires rocks charged with electricity. Even if the rock isn't fired that accurately, just grazing an opponent will cause numbness and fainting."eAbout an hour after birth, its fiery mane and tail grow out, giving it an impressive appearance."cVery competitive, this Pokémon will chase anything that moves fast in the hopes of racing it."{This Pokémon will look into your eyes and read the contents of your heart. If it finds evil there, it promptly hides away."�Brave and prideful, this Pokémon dashes airily through the forest, its steps aided by the psychic power stored in the fur on its fetlocks."�Slowpoke uses its tail to catch prey by dipping it in rivers. However, it often forgets what it's doing and spends entire days just loafing at water's edge."�A metamorphosed Shellder has latched onto Slowbro's tail. The tail can't be used for fishing anymore, forcing Slowbro to grudgingly swim and catch prey instead."bWhen its head was bitten, toxins entered Slowpoke's head and unlocked an extraordinary power."|Because Galarian Slowpoke eat the seeds of a plant that grows only in Galar, their tails have developed a spicy flavor."�If this Pokémon squeezes the tongue of the Shellder biting it, the Shellder will launch a toxic liquid from the tip of its shell."cSlowking can solve any problem present to it, but no one can understand a thing Slowking says."{It's frequently the cause of power outages, which is why some power plants send out electrical signals that it can't stand."`When rain clouds form, many Magneton gather in high places to wait for lightning to strike."ZIt evolved from exposure to a special magnetic field. Three units generate magnetism."�The stalk this Pokémon carries in its wings serves as a sword to cut down opponents. In a dire situation, the stalk can also serve as food."~The stalks of leeks are thicker and longer in the Galar region. Farfetch'd that adapted to these stalks took on a unique form."�After deflecting attacks with its hard leaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp leek stalk. The leek stalk is both weapon and food."kBy alternately raising and lowering its two heads, it balances itself to be more stable while running."uIt collects data and plans three times as wisely, but it may think too much and fall into a state of immobility."�Seel hunts in the frigid sea underneath sheets of ice. When it needs to breathe, it breaks through the ice with the sharply protruding section of its head."aIt sunbathes on the beach after meals. The rise in its body temperature helps its digestion."�Its main source of food is the slimy industrial waste of factories. This Pokémon's numbers have been decreasing in recent years."�Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction."mA Grimer, which had been brought in to solve a problem with garbage, developed over time into this form."xThe garbage it eats causes continuous chemical changes in its body, which produce its exceedingly vivid coloration."�This Pokémon's tongue is always hanging out. It uses its tongue with great dexterity to dig up sand from the seabed in its search for food."Cloyster swims by swallowing water, then jetting it out toward the rear. It shoots spikes from its shell using the same system."�When exposed to a strong wind, a Gastly's gaseous body quickly dwindles away. They cluster under the eaves of houses to escape the ravages of wind."jOn moonless nights, Haunter searches for someone to curse, so it's best not to go out walking around."Should you feel yourself attacked by a sudden chill, it is evidence of an approaching Gengar. There is no escaping it. Give up."~Onix has a magnet in its brain. It acts as a compass so that this Pokémon does not lose direction while it is tunneling."jIt chews its way through boulders with its sturdy jaws. Its eyes can see in the darkness underground."�Its crystalline parts resist all attempts to identify them. Titanix's gravitational abilities make some scientists speculate the crystals are neutron matter."wA Pokémon that nourishes itself by eating dreams, it is thought to share common ancestry with Munna and Musharna."uWhile it is an extremely dangerous Pokémon, people who are in need of a good, sound sleep call it their savior."jIf it senses danger approaching, it cloaks itself with bubbles from its mouth so it will look bigger."�Kingler has an enormous, oversized claw, which it waves in the air to communicate with others. However, because the claw is so heavy, it quickly tires."Its claw has become so large that if it finds itself unable to clamp its opponent, it will just smack them with the blunt side."jIt rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode."�They appear in great numbers at electric power plants. Because they feed on electricity, they cause massive and chaotic blackouts in nearby cities."zWhen excited, it discharges the electric current it has stored in its belly, then lets out a great, uproarious laugh."^The tissue on the surface of its body is curiously similar in composition to an Apricorn."�These Pokémon get nervous when they're not in a group of six. The minute even one member of the group goes missing, Exeggcute become cowardly."}Each of its three heads has its own thoughts. When they want to go in different directions, Exeggutor becomes unable to move."�As it grew taller and taller, it outgrew its reliance on psychic powers, while within it awakened the power of the sleeping dragon."�This Pokémon wears the skull of its deceased mother. Sometimes Cubone's dreams make it cry, but each tear Cubone sheds makes it stronger."}This Pokémon overcame its sorrow to evolve a sturdy new body. Marowak faces its opponents bravely, using a bone as a weapon."wIts custom is to mourn its lost companions. Mounds of dirt by the side of the road mark the graves of the Marowak."kTo brush up on its fighting skills, it will challenge anyone. It has a very strong competitive spirit."WIts legs can stretch double. First-time foes are startled by its extensible reach."mIts punches slice the air. They are launched at such high speed, even a slight graze could cause a burn."tIf you are enchanted by its smooth, dance-like kicks, you may get a closer experience with one than you'd like."�It licks filth clean with its tongue. Whatever it licks always stinks afterward, so whether it's really clean is... questionable."Their saliva contains lots of components that can dissolve anything. The numbness caused by their lick does not dissipate."�Getting up close to a Koffing will give you a chance to observe, through its thin skin, the toxic gasses swirling inside. It blows up at the slightest stimulation."fTop-grade perfume is made using its internal poison gasses by diluting them to the highest level."Long ago, during a time when droves of factories fouled the air with pollution, Weezing changed into this form for some reason."�It is so dense, while on a run it forgets why it started running in the first place. It apparently remembers sometimes if it demolishes something."�Rhydon has a horn that serves as a drill. This Pokémon occasionally rams into streams of magma, but the armor-like hide prevents it from feeling the heat."lIt puts rocks in holes in its palms and uses its muscles to shoot them. Geodude are shot at rare times."rIt carefully carries a round, white rock that it thinks is an egg. It's bothered by how curly its hair looks."hIt walks carefully to prevent its egg from breaking. However, it is extremely fast at running away."]This kindhearted Pokémon nurses sick Pokémon to health. It senses feelings of sadness."�Its vines snap off easily and painlessly if they are grabbed, allowing it to make a quick getaway. The lost vines are replaced by new growth the very next day."WIts vines grow so profusely that, in the warm season, you can't even see its eyes."�Though it looks like a plant, its green color comes from its jade scales. Looking into its eyes is said to bring three years of bad luck."�While the snakes covering it are hard as granite, its skin is soft. Predators attacking its unprotected limbs have to contend with its powerful digging claws."�Although it's carrying its baby in a pouch on its belly, Kangaskhan is swift on its feet. It intimidates its opponents with quick jabs."|Mother and daughter fight alongside each other, delivering blows in quick succession. Their battle bond is unbreakable."�They swim with dance-like motions and cause whirlpools to form. Horsea compete to see which of them can generate the biggest whirlpool."�It's the males that raise the offspring. While Seadra are raising young, the spines on their backs secrete thicker and stronger poison."`It stores energy by sleeping at underwater depths at which no other life-forms can survive."�Although known for their splendid tail fins, Goldeen apparently compete among themselves to see whose horn is thickest and sharpest."Trainers who are crazy for Seaking are divided into horn enthusiasts and fin enthusiasts. The two groups do not get along well."kThey obsessively count the pebbles in their rivers, becoming irate if the result is an unlucky number."�Fearsome Pokémon lining a river in a grand procession is a sign of a Makyan Seaking. They offer endless blessings in exchange for servitude."�This Pokémon gets nibbled on by Lumineon and others. Thanks to its red core, it regenerates fast, so it's unconcerned by their snack attacks."�This Pokémon has an organ known as its core. The organ glows in seven colors when Starmie is unleashing its potent psychic powers."^It habitually mimics foes. Once mimicked, the foe cannot take its eyes off this Pokémon."hEmanations from its fingertips solidify the air into invisible walls that repel even harsh attacks."uIt can radiate chilliness from the bottoms of its feet. It'll spend the whole day tap-dancing on a frozen floor."mIts amusing movements make it very popular. It releases its psychic power from the pattern on its belly."�While young, they live together deep in the mountains, training themselves in how to fight with their scythes and move at high speeds."ZIt has a steel-hard body. It intimidates foes by upraising its eye-patterned pincers."�Only exceptionally aggressive or well-trained Pokémon will willingly engage one in combat. Its ripping pincers threaten to turn foes to shrapnel."iA violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone."�If its face gets even slightly dirty, Smoochum will bathe immediately. But if its body gets dirty, Smoochum doesn't really seem to care."cIts cries sound like human speech. However, it is impossible to tell what it is trying to say."�It's not good at storing electricity yet. This Pokémon sneaks into people's homes, looking for electrical outlets to eat electricity from."�While it's often blamed for power outages, the truth is the cause of outages is more often an error on the part of the electric company."�In terms of electrical-energy output, Electivire is one of the best among all Electric Pokémon. It discharges high-voltage currents from its tails."�This Pokémon makes its home near volcanoes. At the end of the day, Magby soaks in magma, resting and recovering from the day's fatigue."_When it breathes deeply, heat mirages form around its body, making it hard to see clearly."�When Magmortar inhales deeply, the fire burning in its belly intensifies, rising in temperature to over 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit."nAlthough it's tough, it can't handle cold well. When night falls, it buries itself in leafage and sleeps."�When the buzz of its wings becomes a roar, it's about to bolt at full speed. It isn't uncommon for its charges to send opponents through buildings."fWith its Herculean powers, it can easily throw around an object that is 100 times its own weight."They can be seen watching the sky, trying to find a place to stand for when they inevitably attempt to deadlift the world."}When Tauros begins whipping itself with its tails, it's a warning that the Pokémon is about to charge with astounding speed."�Miltank's milk has been sought after due to its taste and nutrition. The local treat of Castelia City, Casteliacones, is made from fresh Moomoo Milk."�Its swimming muscles are weak, so it is easily washed away by currents. In places where water pools, you can see many Magikarp deposited there by the flow."gBrutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times."oOnce endangered, they are now overabundant. Their mournful songs have died out as the population rebounds."�The musical staff around its body is made of ice particles. The symbols are indecipherable, but some say they've heard Saurenaid speak its own language."sWith its astonishing capacity for metamorphosis, it can get along with anything - except for its fellow Ditto."iEevee has an unstable genetic makeup that suddenly mutates due to the environment in which it lives."`When Vaporeon's fins begin to vibrate, it is a sign that rain will come within a few hours."zIts lungs contain an organ that creates electricity. The crackling sound of electricity can be heard when it exhales."_A dedicated omnivore, Flareon will eat anything - as long as it's been slow-roasted first."tIts fur is so sensitive, it can feel minute shifts in the air and predict the weather...and its foes' thoughts."qWhen exposed to the moon's aura, the rings on its body glow faintly and it's filled with a mysterious power."aJust like a plant, it uses photosynthesis. As a result, it is always enveloped in clear air."_It lowers its body heat to freeze its fur. The hairs then become like needles it can fire."�Sylveon's ribbon-like feelers emit an aura that erases any sense of hostility, enabling it to stop fights. Its feelers allow it to read their Trainer's feelings."|Its fluffiness, friendliness, and massive size make it beloved by nearly everyone. Attackers don't know where to begin."~This Pokémon was created using the cutting-edge science of 20 years ago, so many parts of it have since become obsolete."ZWith planetary development software installed, it became capable of working in space."zIts programming was modified to enable it to travel through alien dimensions. Seems there might have been an error..."�Rely on LuxTech's literal firewall! Featuring a unique* typing and cutting-edge network threat purgation protocols, this innovative new form has your back."�Because some Omanyte manage to escape after being restored or are released into the wild by people, this species is becoming a problem."|Its heavy shell is thought to be the reason this ancient Pokémon died out. It's apparently a distant ancestor of Octillery."uThis Pokémon likes to team up with the strongest Pokémon it can find. Some researchers fear its dormant power."�Some people claim this Pokémon ruled over an unnatural subterranean realm long ago. It resembles an enemy from a popular video game."rThis species is almost entirely extinct. Kabuto molt every three days, making their shells harder and harder."vKabutops slices its prey apart and sucks out the fluids. The discarded body parts become food for other Pokémon."�Its fossils were found in the depths of Makyan caves. However, it is alien to anything from the same time. It resembles a monster from a popular video game."�After evolution, this Pokémon began to resemble other extinct Pokémon of their time. They multiply by converting native biomass into more Kabuto."�It flew through the open skies over the ancient continent as if they were its own. When it touched ground, its walk was weak and slow."tIn ancient times, this Pokémon was an apex predator. It has the strength to fly with a Tyrantrum in its claws."vIt conceals food under the long fur on its body. It carts around this food stash and swallows it without chewing."Its stomach is said to be incomparably strong. Even Muk's poison is nothing more than a hint of spice on Snorlax's tongue."�Dratini continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels."�Dragonair stores an enormous amount of energy inside its body. It is said to alter weather conditions in its vicinity via crystals on its neck and tail."^It is said to make its home somewhere in the sea. It guides crews of shipwrecks to shore."eA legendary bird Pokémon that is said to appear to doomed people who are lost in icy mountains."zIts feather-like blades are composed of psychic energy and can shear through thick iron sheets as if they were paper."cThis legendary bird Pokémon is said to appear only when a thundercloud parts into two halves."�One kick from its powerful legs will pulverize a dump truck. Supposedly, this Pokémon runs through the mountains at over 180 mph."gOne of the legendary bird Pokémon. It is said that its appearance indicates the coming of spring."�This Pokémon's sinister, flame-like aura will consume the spirit of any creature it hits. Victims become burned-out shadows of themselves."tCreated from the DNA of Mew, this Pokémon is a dangerous combination of overwhelming power and a savage heart."�It's very intelligent and can use an incredible variety of moves. Many believe that all other Pokémon are descendants of this one."bIt uses the leaf on its head to determine the temperature and humidity. It loves to sunbathe."MThe buds that ring its neck give off a spicy aroma that perks people up."eMeganium's breath has the power to revive dead grass and plants. It can make them healthy again."[It has a timid nature. If it is startled, the flames on its back burn more vigorously."kBe careful if it turns its back during battle. It means that it will attack with the fire on its back."bIt has a secret, devastating move. It rubs its blazing fur together to cause huge explosions."�Said to purify lost, forsaken souls with its flames and guide them to the afterlife. Its form had been influenced by the energy of Mt. Coronet."jIts powerful, well-developed jaws are capable of crushing anything. Even its Trainer must be careful."eOnce it bites down, it won't let go until it loses its fangs. New fangs quickly grow into place."kWhen it bites with its massive and powerful jaws, it shakes its head and savagely tears its victim up."�This Pokémon is very cautious. It stands on its tail in order to see enemies from far away. If it does then it alert its pack by thumping its tail on the ground."rIt makes a nest to suit its long and skinny body. It uses tunnels in order to make a quick getaway from foes."tThe eye on its stomach enables its psychic powers and never blinks. Dirt and dust are telekinetically repelled."|It burrows at night, leaving only the eye on its stomach exposed. The eye will stare into space while the rest of it sleeps."\It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, the movement can rarely be seen."_When it needs to think, it rotates its head 180 degrees to sharpen its intellectual power."}Its down insulates it against any cold. In winter it will lay dormant beneath snow banks, only to pop out during spring."iWhen its shadow passes over someone, they feel a horrible chill. Some Trainers find it invigorating."jIt is timid and clusters together with others. The fluid secreted by its feet indicates its location."lThe spot patterns on its back grow larger or smaller depending on the number of stars in the night sky."kIt lies still in the same pose for days in its web, waiting for its unsuspecting prey to wander close."jIt attaches silk to its prey and sets it free. Later, it tracks the silk to the prey and its friends."kIt shoots positive and negative electricity between the tips of its two antennae and zaps its enemies."{It blinds prey with an intense burst of light. With the prey incapacitated, the Pokémon swallows it in a single gulp."}Togepi shares its joy with the people who take care of it. It can act maliciously, causing havoc and bad luck to its enemies."cThey say that it will appear before kindhearted, caring people and shower them with happiness."eIt shares many blessings with people who respect one another's rights and avoid needless strife."oIt usually forages for food on the ground but may, on rare occasions, hop onto branches to peck at shoots."kThey say that it stays still and quiet because it is seeing both the past and future at the same time."bIt stores lots of air in its soft fur, allowing it to stay cool in summer and warm in winter."oIf its coat becomes fully charged with electricity, its tail lights up. It fires hair that zaps on impact."gThe tail's tip shines brightly and can be seen from far away. It acts as a beacon for lost people."\It swings its large, nutrient-filled tail around to fight opponents bigger than itself."^The tip of its tail is filled with oil that is lighter than water, so it acts as a float."^The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it's in the water."kIt prefers an arid atmosphere. It leaks water that looks like tears when adjusting its moisture level."nIt disguises itself as a tree to avoid attack. It hates water, so it will disappear if it starts raining."jIt drifts on winds. It is said that when Hoppip gather in fields and mountains, spring is on the way."bIt spreads its petals to absorb sunlight. It also floats in the air to get closer to the sun."lEven in the fiercest wind, it can control its fluff to make its way to any place in the world it wants."dIts tail is so powerful that it can use it to grab a tree branch and hold itself up in the air."STo eat, it deftly shucks nuts with its two tails. It rarely uses its arms now."nIt lives by drinking only dewdrops from under the leaves of plants. It is said that it eats nothing else."]It gets energy from warm sunlight and is known for its habit of moving in pursuit of it."jIf it flaps its wings really fast, it can generate shock waves that will shatter windows in the area."{This six-legged Pokémon is easily capable of transporting an adult in flight. The wings on its tail help it stay balanced."dWhen the temperature cools in the evening, they emerge from water to seek food along the shore."eThis carefree Pokémon has an easygoing nature. While swimming, it always bumps into boat hulls."eFeared and loathed by many, it is believed to bring misfortune to all those who see it at night."QBecoming active at night, it is known to swarm with numerous Murkrow in tow."cIt likes playing mischievous tricks, such as screaming and wailing to startle people at night."`Its cries sound like incantations to torment the foe. It appears where you least expect it."\Shaped like ancient writing, it is a huge mystery whether language or Unown came first."XIt grows strong by pushing up against others en masse. It loves eating sweet fruit."hTo keep its pitch-black tail hidden, it lives quietly in the darkness. It is never first to attack."kIts tail has a small brain of its own. Beware! If you get close, it may react to your scent by biting."�Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig's."eIt looks just like a pinecone. Its shell protects it from bird Pokémon that peck it by mistake."mIt remains immovably rooted to its tree. It scatters pieces of its hard shell to drive its enemies away."�Scientists believe that it used to fly with its wings during ancient times. Nowadays it burrows under the ground, sharing tunnels with other Pokémon."�This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles."wThe gentle Dududunsparce will put Pokémon that wander into its nest onto its back and carry them to the entrance."fIt flies straight at its target's face, then clamps down on the startled victim to inject poison."uIts flight is soundless. It uses its lengthy tail to carry off its prey... Then its elongated fangs do the rest."]Small Pokémon flee from its scary face. It is, however, considered by women to be cute."eIt can make most any Pokémon run away simply by opening its mouth wide to reveal its big fangs."hThe small spikes covering its body developed from scales. They inject a toxin that causes fainting."nFishers detest this troublesome Pokémon because it sprays poison from its spines, getting it everywhere."{Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname "sea fiend." It slurps up poison to nourish itself."oIt stores berries inside its shell. To avoid attacks, it hides beneath rocks and remains completely still."eIts paws conceal sharp claws. If attacked, it suddenly extends the claws and startles its enemy."kThey live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination."�Its sturdy, curved claws are ideal for traversing precipitous cliffs. From the tips of these claws drips a nerve-destroying venom."�Because of Sneasler's virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on frozen highlands."cBefore food becomes scarce in wintertime, its habit is to hoard food in many hidden locations."mAlthough it has a large body, it is quite skilled at climbing trees. It eats and sleeps in the treetops."�It is believed that the swampy terrain of its ancient home region gave Ursaluna its burly physique and capacity to manipulate peat at will."YIts body is made of magma. If it doesn't keep moving, its body will cool and harden."gIts body is as hot as lava and is always billowing. Flames will occasionally burst from its shell."]If it smells something enticing, it dashes off headlong to find the source of the aroma."cBecause the long hair all over its body obscures its sight, it just keeps charging repeatedly."hIts impressive tusks are made of ice. The population thinned when it turned warm after the ice age."pThey prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water."�It will regrow any branches that break off its head. People keep particularly beautiful Curesola branches as charms to promote safe childbirth."|Sudden climate change wiped out this ancient kind of Corsola. This Pokémon absorbs others' life-force through its branches."lBe cautious of the ectoplasmic body surrounding its soul. You'll become stiff as stone if you touch it."iUsing its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a Mantine's underside to scavenge for leftovers."eIt traps foes with the suction cups on its tentacles, then smashes them with its rock-hard head."vWhen it swims close to the surface of the ocean, people aboard ships are able to observe the pattern on its back."iWhile elegantly swimming in the sea, it ignores Remoraid that cling to its fins seeking food scraps."�Food rots and milk curdles in their presence. Because of this, they're commonly seen fleeing from angered Pokémon such as Miltank or Alcremie."�It pelts houses with hail that sounds like knocking, trying to get those inside to open a door or window. People used to import Skarmory to defend against them."^It carries food all day long. When someone is lost in the mountains, it shares that food."UDespite being clad entirely in iron-hard armor, it flies at speeds over 180 mph."`To corner prey, they check each other's location using barks that only they can understand."bThe flames it breathes when angry contain toxins. If they cause a burn, it will hurt forever."~They are the steeds of the Elite Four of the Apocalypse, and their howls will ring in the end of days... or so the stories go."�Phanpy uses its snout to shower itself with water. However, its snout is so strong that when it bumps into you, it may send you flying."cThe longer and bigger its tusks, the higher its rank in its herd. The tusks take long to grow."kThe curved antlers subtly change the flow of air to create a strange space where reality is distorted."�The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well."bOnce it becomes an adult, it has a tendency to let its comrades plant footprints on its back."uBorn deep underground, it comes aboveground and becomes a pupa once it has finished eating the surrounding soil."iIts shell is as hard as sheet rock, and it is also very strong. Its thrashing can topple a mountain."`If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward."�Raikou embodies the speed of lightning. This Pokémon's roars send shock waves shuddering through the air and ground as if lightning bolts were crashing down."�Entei embodies the passion of magma. This Pokémon is thought to have been born in the eruption of a volcano. It blasts fire that consumes all that it touches."�Suicune embodies the compassion of a pure spring of water. It runs across the land with gracefulness. This Pokémon has the power to purify dirty water."hIt is said to be the guardian of the seas. It is rumored to have been seen on the night of a storm."jA legend says that its body glows in seven colors. A rainbow is said to form behind it when it flies."�This Pokémon traveled through time to come from the future. It bolsters grass and trees with its own strength, and it can heal wounds, too."�Treecko has small hooks on the bottom of its feet that enable it to scale vertical walls. This Pokémon attacks by slamming foes with its thick tail."�The leaves growing out of Grovyle's body are convenient for camouflaging it from enemies in the forest. This Pokémon is a master at climbing trees in jungles."�The leaves growing on Sceptile's body are very sharp. This Pokémon is very agile - it leaps all over the branches of trees and jumps on its foe from above or behind."sThese Pokémon travel in small groups, searching for travelers to rob. As they march, their tails drum a beat."}Though they are skilled with swordplay, they never fight fair. They swish their tails in unison to intimidate groups of prey."�This Pokémon's tail is so heavy it must run on all fours to spear foes. The sound of wind in its feathers is the only warning before impact."�Torchic has a place inside its body where it keeps its flame. Give it a hug - it will be glowing with warmth. This Pokémon is covered all over by a fluffy coat of down."uCombusken battles with the intensely hot flames it spews from its beak and with outstandingly destructive kicks."�Blaziken has incredibly strong legs - it can easily clear a 30-story building in one leap. This Pokémon's blazing punches leave its foes scorched and blackened."sThis Pokémon is drawn to sounds of revelry. It is commonly sighted in the crowd at fairgrounds and festivals."{This Pokémon invents a new dance routine every day. After performances, it tosses treats and trinkets into the crowd."�This Pokémon ensures festivities will remain both safe and lively. It deftly leaps between tents and rooftops, subduing anyone who would ruin the fun."�In water, Mudkip breathes using the gills on its cheeks. If it is faced with a tight situation in battle, this Pokémon will unleash its amazing power."�The surface of Marshtomp's body is enveloped by a thin, sticky film that enables it to live on land. This Pokémon plays in mud on beaches."_It can swim while towing a large ship. It bashes down foes with a swing of its thick arms."�This Pokémon was only found recently, as upheavals unsealed ancient caves rife with old life, where it promptly hid from sight in narrow spaces."yThis Pokémon is much stronger than before, yet lazy. It is quick to make friends, but it might eat them in a pinch."�Living in underwater caves with no light has given this Pokémon great sensitivity to vibrations. It pinpoints prey with extreme precision."tIt has a very tenacious nature. Its acute sense of smell lets it chase a chosen prey without ever losing track."gIt chases down prey in a pack of around ten. They defeat foes with perfectly coordinated teamwork."bA Pokémon with abundant curiosity. It shows an interest in everything, so it always zigzags."fIt charges prey at speeds over 60 mph. However, because it can only run straight, it often fails."lThought to be the oldest form of Zigzagoon, it moves in zigzags and wreaks havoc upon its surroundings."\This very aggressive Pokémon will recklessly challenge opponents stronger than itself."�It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch."jIt lives among the tall grass and in forests. It repels attacks by raising up the spikes on its rear."eIt drinks dew that collects on its silk and waits for evolution. Its hard cocoon repels attacks."gIt has an aggressive nature. It stabs prey with its long, narrow mouth to drain the prey's fluids."cIt never forgets any attack it endured while in the cocoon. After evolution, it seeks payback."iIt violently flutters its wings to scatter toxic dust when attacked. It becomes active after sunset."�Its horns efficiently regulate its body temperature. It seeks out Fire- and Ice-type predators to charge itself with energy for evolution."�Its silk makes it blend in with snowy rocks. If attacked, its only recourse is to make itself unappetizing by chilling its own body."�It is less hostile than the Hoennian form, but vicious towards former predators. Its mouthparts inject a fluid similar to liquid nitrogen."}Its flame is kept burning by an organ similar to a Bunsen burner. Curious Pokémon often try to put it out, to no avail."�Its abdomen is actually a sophisticated torch drive. Their migrations can be tracked by following broken trees left by supersonic flybys."lIt searches about for clean water. If it does not drink water for too long, the leaf on its head wilts."fIt has a mischievous spirit. If it spots an angler, it will tug on the fishing line to interfere."]The rhythm of bright, festive music activates Ludicolo's cells, making it more powerful."gWhen it dangles from a tree branch, it looks just like an acorn. It enjoys scaring other Pokémon."mIt lives deep in forests. With the leaf on its head, it makes a flute whose song makes listeners uneasy."bBy flapping its leafy fan, it can whip up gusts of 100 feet per second that can level houses."�This Pokémon is very gutsy and will fight powerful opponents without backing down. On the other hand, when it is hungry it will weaken and cry loudly."bIt dives at a steep angle as soon as it spots its prey. It catches its prey with sharp claws."WIt makes its nest on steep sea cliffs. Riding updrafts, it soars to great heights."\It is a messenger of the skies, carrying small Pokémon and eggs to safety in its bill."bIt is highly attuned to the emotions of people and Pokémon. It hides if it senses hostility."cIt has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future."_It has the power to predict the future. Its power peaks when it is protecting its Trainer."\A master of courtesy and swordsmanship, it fights using extending swords on its elbows."�Its legs can generate oils, helping it glide through the water. The antenna on its head can secrete a thick, sugary syrup that is used to attract prey."_It flaps its four wings to hover and fly freely in any direction--to and fro and sideways."cIt spouts poison spores from the top of its head. These spores cause pain all over if inhaled."jIt scatters poisonous spores and throws powerful punches while its foe is hampered by inhaled spores."kIf it eats just three leaves in a day, it is satisfied. Other than that, it sleeps for 20 hours a day."dIts stress level rises if it cannot keep moving constantly. Too much stress makes it feel sick."~It is the world's most slothful Pokémon. However, it can exert horrifying power by releasing pent-up energy all at once."lIt can sometimes live underground for more than 10 years. It absorbs nutrients from the roots of trees."aBecause it moves so quickly, it sometimes becomes unseeable. It congregates around tree sap."ZA most peculiar Pokémon that somehow appears in a Poké Ball when a Nincada evolves."`If it senses danger, it scares the foe by crying out with the volume of a jet-plane engine."XThe shock waves from its cries can tip over trucks. It stamps its feet to power up."ZIts roar in battle shakes the ground like a tremor--or like an earthquake has struck."hIt grows stronger by enduring harsh training. It is a gutsy Pokémon that can withstand any attack."hIt loves to match power with big-bodied Pokémon. It can knock a truck flying with its arm thrusts."`Its magnetic nose consistently faces north. Travelers check Nosepass to get their bearings."QIt freely controls three small units called Mini-Noses using magnetic force."HIt shows its cute side by chasing its own tail until it gets dizzy."]It is highly popular among female Trainers for its sublime fur. It does not keep a nest."bIt dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself."�Attackers find their weaknesses and regrets reflected in the jewel Rubarior carries. If it feels unloved, it will make its Trainer cry."`Attached to its head is a huge set of jaws formed by horns. It can chew through iron beams."�Fans argue whether it's the cutest terrifying Pokémon or the creepiest cute Pokémon. It will act cute or scary depending on its trainer's whims."�When Aron evolves, its steel armor peels off. In ancient times, people would collect Aron's shed armor and make good use of it in their daily lives."�During territorial disputes, Lairon fight by slamming into each other. Close inspection of their steel armor reveals scratches and dents."�Long ago, there was a king who wore a helmet meant to resemble the head of an Aggron. He was trying to channel the Pokémon's strength."_It eats just one berry a day. By enduring hunger, its spirit is tempered and made sharper."WThrough yoga training, it gained the psychic power to predict its foe's next move."�This Pokémon can go up to four years without eating a single meal. Through intense training, it is able to fight in a manner indistinguishable from a dance."hIt stores static electricity in its fur for discharging. It gives off sparks if a storm approaches."iIt discharges electricity from its mane. It creates a thundercloud overhead to drop lightning bolts."XIf not calmed during storms, it will cause havoc by trying to race lightning bolts."dIt absorbs electricity from telephone poles. It shorts out its body to create crackling noises."]It cheers on friends. If its friends are losing, its body lets off more and more sparks."oIt lives around clean ponds. At night, its rear lights up. It converses with others by flashing its light."WWith its sweet aroma, it guides Volbeat to draw signs with light in the night sky."kOver the winter, it closes its bud and endures the cold. In spring, the bud opens and releases pollen."jRoselia that drink nutritionally rich springwater are said to reveal rare coloration when they bloom."eWith the movements of a dancer, it strikes with whips that are densely lined with poison thorns."mThere is nothing its stomach can't digest. While it is digesting, vile, overpowering gases are expelled."YIt gulps anything that fits in its mouth. Its special enzymes can dissolve anything."eIt lives in massive rivers that course through jungles. It swarms prey that enter its territory."gIt can swim at speeds of 75 mph by jetting seawater through its body. It is the bandit of the sea."�Its propulsion system is the basis for many ramjet engine designs. It eats four times its body weight in food before a battle and will still be hungry by the end."pIt eats one ton of food every day. It plays by shooting stored seawater out its blowholes with great force."bThe biggest of all Pokémon. It can dive to a depth of almost 10,000 feet on only one breath."pThe magma in its body reaches 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit. Its hump gets smaller when it uses Fire-type moves."nIf angered, the humps on its back erupt in a shower of molten lava. It lives in the craters of volcanoes."�Magma builds up in its body over time. If this Pokémon does not regularly erupt, it might accidentally destroy the area around it."\It burns coal inside its shell for energy. It blows out black soot if it is endangered."kIt bounces around on its tail to keep its heart pumping. It carries a pearl from Clamperl on its head."gIt uses black pearls to amplify its psychic power. It does an odd dance to gain control over foes."_The chances of two Spinda having identical spot patterns is less than one in four billion."gIt makes an inescapable conical pit and lies in wait at the bottom for prey to come tumbling down."}It generates ultrasonic waves by violently flapping its wings. After making its prey faint, it melts the prey with acid."hKnown as "The Desert Spirit," this Pokémon hides in the sandstorms it causes by beating its wings."kIt prefers harsh environments such as deserts. It can survive for 30 days on water stored in its body."^Packs of them follow travelers through the desert until the travelers can no longer move."iSwablu is very friendly towards humans, so a Swablu may land on your head and act like a fluffy hat."�Altarias often glide through the clouds while singing or humming. While normally kind, Altaria will attack foes without mercy if provoked."�This Pokémon's singing can bring even the most stoic Trainers to tears. Those who fall asleep on it are said to experience beautiful dreams."eIts fur would all stand on end if it smelled a Seviper nearby. Its sharp claws tear up its foes."kConstant polishing makes the edge of the blade on its tail extremely sharp. It's Zangoose's archrival."�Even being bisected by a Seviper's tail couldn't quell its rage. It attacks enemies on a physical and spiritual level simultaneously."~Its iron body is impenetrable to nearly all attacks. When coiled, it can fire metal projectiles using magnetic induction."iIt was discovered at the site of a meteor strike 40 years ago. Its stare can lull its foes to sleep."jIt absorbs solar energy during the day. Always expressionless, it can sense what its foe is thinking."cIts whiskers make a superb radar. They are used to locate prey, even in the murkiest of water."kIt makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything--if it is alive, Whiscash will eat it."dIts hardy vitality enables it to adapt to any environment. Its pincers will never release prey."xLoving to battle, this Pokémon pinches all Pokémon that enter its territory with its pincers and throws them out."bIt moves by spinning on its foot. It is a rare Pokémon that was discovered in ancient ruins."SIt is said that it originates from clay dolls made by an ancient civilization."This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. Lileep once lived in warm seas that existed approximately 100,000,000 years ago."�It has short legs and can't walk very fast, but its neck and tentacles can extend to over three times their usual length to nab distant prey."�Anorith can swim swiftly by pulling its eight wings through the water like oars on a boat. This Pokémon is an ancestor of modern bug Pokémon."~After evolution, this Pokémon emerged onto land. Its lower body has become stronger, and blows from its tail are devastating."`It is the shabbiest Pokémon of all. It forms in schools and lives at the bottom of rivers."^It is the world's most beautiful Pokémon. There are many works of art featuring Milotic."�Swimming through the air in places of unmourned tragedy, Feebas are easily located due to the sobbing noises they emit when alone."eMilotic are unburdened by sadness. They are said to help restless souls pass into the afterlife."mIt has the ability to change its form into the sun, the rain, or a snow cloud, depending on the weather."uIt changes its shading to match its surroundings so it can sneak up on prey. Only its belly patterns stay fixed."gIt loves vengeful emotions and hangs in rows under the eaves of houses where vengeful people live."qStrong feelings of hatred turned a puppet into a Pokémon. If it opens its mouth, its cursed energy escapes."�Its pink claws and feet appear to be made of flesh, but are actually raw negative energy. When it is finally fully unzipped, it moves on to its next life."kIf it finds bad children who won't listen to their parents, it will spirit them away--or so it's said."_Its body is hollow. It is said that those who look into its body are sucked into the void."`It comes to those whose lives have come to an end and escorts their souls to the afterlife."sThe bunch of fruit around its neck ripens twice a year and is delicious. It's a highly favored tropical snack."hThere is an orb inside its mouth. When it hops, the orb bounces all over and makes a ringing sound."MEmitting ultrasonic cries, it floats on winds to travel great distances."�Swift as the wind, Absol races through fields and mountains. Its curved, bow-like horn is acutely sensitive to the warning signs of natural disasters."�It's loved for its elegantly intimidating looks. It may herald a coming cataclysm, but nothing gets between a trainer and a fashionable Pokémon."TIn Sinnoh, certain folklore says a house will prosper if a Snorunt lives there."_It can instantly freeze moisture in the atmosphere. It uses this power to freeze its foes."�It only closes its mouth to bite its foes, forcing its trainers to learn to interpret its emotions via its changes in eye shape, ear direction, and body temperature."fLegends in snowy regions say that a woman who was lost on an icy mountain was reborn as Froslass."iIt's more efficient for Spheal to roll than to walk. When this Pokémon is happy, it claps its fins."tThis Pokémon has a habit of spinning round things on its nose, whether those things are Poké Balls or Spheal."�Walrein's tusks keep growing throughout its life. Tusks broken in battle will grow back to their usual impressive size in a year."YIt is protected by a sturdy shell. Once in a lifetime, it makes a magnificent pearl."cIt lives deep in the sea. With a tail shaped like a small fish, it attracts unsuspecting prey."qIts swimming form is exquisitely elegant. With its thin mouth, it feeds on seaweed that grows between rocks."�This Pokémon was discovered during deep-sea exploration. Its appearance hasn't changed in 100,000,000 years, so it's called a living fossil."fDuring the spawning season, countless Luvdisc congregate at coral reefs, turning the waters pink."dIt gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds."�Bagon is a solitary Pokémon that doesn't form groups with others of its kind. It also has a head hard enough to cleave a boulder in one strike."�Shelgon ignores its hunger entirely, never eating any food. Apparently, Shelgon will evolve once all its energy stores are used up."�While basking in the joy of flight generally keeps this Pokémon in high spirits, it turns into an uncontrollable menace if something angers it."}From its rear, Beldum emits a magnetic force that rapidly pulls opponents in. They get skewered on Beldum's sharp claws."�Using magnetic forces to stay aloft, this Pokémon flies at high speeds, weaving through harsh mountain terrain in pursuit of prey."�Metagross is the result of the fusion of two Metang. This Pokémon defeats its opponents through use of its supercomputer-level brain."sThe third of the titans, built to commemorate an era of stonecraft. It is as resilient as an ancient monolith."qThe second of the titans, built to commemorate an era of ice. It is as implacable as an encroaching glacier."~The fourth of the titans, built to commemorate an era of metalworking. It is as unfailing as a master swordsmith's blade."The fifth of the titans, built to commemorate an era of electricity. It is as inscrutable as a cutting-edge supercomputer."vThe first of the titans, built to commemorate an era when dragons ruled. It is as terrifying as an apex predator."pThe creator of the titans, who shaped the primal clay in the golden age. Its creative powers are boundless."�Latias is highly sensitive to the emotions of people. If it senses any hostility, this Pokémon ruffles the feathers all over its body and cries shrilly to intimidate them."�Latios has the ability to make others see an image of what it has seen or imagines in its head. This Pokémon is intelligent and understands human speech."�Kyogre is said to be the personification of the sea itself. Legends tell of its many clashes against Groudon, as each sought to gain the power of nature."�Groudon is said to be the personification of the land itself. Legends tell of its many clashes against Kyogre, as each sought to gain the power of nature."�Rayquaza is said to have lived for hundreds of millions of years. Legends remain of how it put to rest the clash between Kyogre and Groudon."]It is said to have the ability to grant any wish for just one week every thousand years."]DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen."�It relies heavily on water to keep its plant healthy, and thus it spends most of its time near lakes. When thirsty, the plant on its head wilts."VIt knows where pure water wells up. It carries fellow Pokémon there on its back."[Small Pokémon occasionally gather on its unmoving back to begin building their nests."aThe gas made in its belly burns from its rear end. The fire burns weakly when it feels sick."[It uses ceilings and walls to launch aerial attacks. Its fiery tail is but one weapon."gIt tosses its enemies around with agility. It uses all its limbs to fight in its own unique style."gBecause it is very proud, it hates accepting food from people. Its thick down guards it from cold."gIt lives a solitary life. Its wings deliver wicked blows that can snap even the thickest of trees."eThe three horns that extend from its beak attest to its power. The leader has the biggest horns."mThey flock around mountains and fields, chasing after bug Pokémon. Their singing is noisy and annoying."XIt lives in forests and fields. Squabbles over territory occur when flocks collide."eWhen Staravia evolve into Staraptor, they leave the flock to live alone. They have sturdy wings."eIt constantly gnaws on logs and rocks to whittle down its front teeth. It nests alongside water."bIt makes its nest by damming streams with bark and mud. It is known as an industrious worker."OWhen its antennae hit each other, it sounds like the music of a xylophone."_It signals its emotions with its melodies. Scientists are studying these melodic patterns."_All of its fur dazzles if danger is sensed. It flees while the foe is momentarily blinded."mStrong electricity courses through the tips of its sharp claws. A light scratch causes fainting in foes."ZLuxray's ability to see through objects comes in handy when it's scouting for danger."jA lifelong jungle dweller from 100 million years ago, it would snap obstructing trees with headbutts."bIts skull is as hard as iron. It is a brute that tears down jungle trees while catching prey."vIt was generated from a fossil dug out of a layer of clay that was older than anyone knows. It has a sturdy face."]Any frontal attack is repulsed. It is a docile Pokémon that feeds on grass and berries."ZIf its cloak is broken in battle, it quickly remakes the cloak with materials nearby."bWhen Burmy evolved, its cloak became a part of this Pokémon's body. The cloak is never shed."GIt flutters around at night and steals honey from the Combee hive."�It collects honey for its colony. At night, they cluster to form a beehive and sleep. If a colony loses their Vespiquen, a new Combee will take its place."\Its abdomen is a honeycomb for grubs. It raises its grubs on honey collected by Combee."fA pair may be seen rubbing their cheek pouches together in an effort to share stored electricity."oIt inflates the flotation sac around its neck and pokes its head out of the water to see what is going on."fIts flotation sac developed as a result of pursuing aquatic prey. It can double as a rubber raft."`It evolves by sucking the energy out of the small ball where it had been storing nutrients."kIf it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun's rays with its whole body."�The colors of this Pokémon change depending on its environment. When it senses danger, this Pokémon excretes a sticky purple liquid."eIt apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools."lThese Pokémon are called the "Signpost for Wandering Spirits." Children holding them sometimes vanish."dIt's drowsy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go."nWhen it senses danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into its fur."bThe ears appear to be delicate. If they are touched roughly, it kicks with its graceful legs."�It patterns its fur and attacks after human fighters it looks up to. Only the most over-the-top action movies can inspire it to reach its true potential."yAccording to legend, the Buneary of Makya came from the moon. They have incredible control of their prehensile ears."}The blue crystals that adorn Makyan Lopunny's fur resemble saccharite, but analysis shows that they're structurally distinct."�A wanderer, Makyan Haerobic has a deep sense of justice and will use the full force of its lunar powers to rescue weaker Pokémon."bWhen it's happy, Glameow demonstrates beautiful movements of its tail, like a dancing ribbon."bTo make itself appear intimidatingly beefy, it tightly cinches its waist with its twin tails."cIt protects itself by spraying a noxious fluid from its rear. The stench lingers for 24 hours."gIt sprays a stinky fluid from its tail. The fluid smells worse the longer it is allowed to fester."cImplements shaped like it were discovered in ancient tombs. It is unknown if they are related."_Ancient people believed that petitioning Bronzong for rain was the way to make crops grow."XIt can learn and speak human words. If they gather, they all learn the same saying."All Spiritomb's mischief and misdeeds compelled a traveler to use a mysterious spell to bind Spiritomb to an odd keystone."�Gible attacks anything that moves, and it drags whatever it catches into the crevice that is its lair. Despite the big mouth, Gible's stomach is small."�Jewels are buried in the caves these Pokémon nest in, but you'll be torn apart by claws and fangs the moment you enter one of these caves."�Garchomp makes its home in volcanic mountains. It flies through the sky as fast as a jet airplane, hunting down as much prey as it can."]The aura that emanates from its body intensifies to alert others if it is afraid or sad."gBy reading the auras of all things, it can tell how others are feeling from over half a mile away."�It fights in a state of complete clarity without mercy, fear, or stress. When it has achieved all its goals, it will simply cease to be."_It enshrouds itself with sand to protect itself from germs. It does not enjoy getting wet."eIt blasts internally stored sand from ports on its body to create a towering twister for attack."pIt burrows under the sand to lie in wait for prey. Its tail claws can inject its prey with a savage poison."fIt has the power in its clawed arms to make scrap of a car. The tips of its claws release poison."sInflating its poison sacs, it fills the area with an odd sound and hits flinching opponents with a poison jab."UIts knuckle claws secrete a toxin so vile that even a scratch could prove fatal."mIt binds itself to trees in marshes. It attracts prey with its sweet-smelling drool and gulps them down."�It hunts other nocturnal predators, trapping them with its sticky tendrils. Its maniacal laugh is a common sound on autumn nights."hAfter long exposure to sunlight, the patterns on its tail fins shine vividly when darkness arrives."cTo avoid detection by predators, it crawls along the seafloor using the two fins on its chest."XIn the spring, it grows berries with the texture of frozen treats around its belly."wIt lives a quiet life on mountains that are perpetually covered in snow. It hides itself by whipping up blizzards."{Blizzards follow it wherever it goes. It's often used as shelter by unsuspecting mountaineers, though it doesn't mind."bIts body is composed of plasma. It is known to infiltrate electronic devices and wreak havoc."mKnown as "The Being of Knowledge." It is said that it can wipe out the memory of those who see its eyes."]Known as "The Being of Emotion." It taught humans the nobility of sorrow, pain, and joy."gKnown as "The Being of Willpower." It sleeps at the bottom of a lake to keep the world in balance."\A Pokémon spoken of in legend. It is said that time began moving when Dialga was born."dIt is said to live in a gap in the spatial dimension parallel to ours. It appears in mythology."gIt dwells in volcanic caves. It digs in with its cross-shaped feet to crawl on ceilings and walls."{This Pokémon is said to live in a world on the reverse side of ours, where common knowledge is distorted and strange."yThose who sleep holding Cresselia's feather are assured of joyful dreams. It is said to represent the crescent moon."kIt drifts in warm seas. It always returns to where it was born, no matter how far it may have drifted."`It starts its life with a wondrous power that permits it to bond with any kind of Pokémon."aIt can lull people to sleep and make them dream. It is active during nights of the new moon."}The blooming of Gracidea flowers confers the power of flight upon it. Feelings of gratitude are the message it delivers."ZIt is told in mythology that this Pokémon was born before the universe even existed."pThey photosynthesize by bathing their tails in sunlight. When they are not feeling well, their tails droop."eWhen it gets dirty, its leaves can't be used in photosynthesis, so it always keeps itself clean."oIt can stop its opponents' movements with just a glare. It takes in solar energy and boosts it internally."bIt loves to eat roasted berries, but sometimes it gets too excited and burns them to a crisp."nWhen its internal fire flares up, its movements grow sharper and faster. When in trouble, it emits smoke."PIt has mastered fast and powerful fighting moves. It grows a beard of fire."rIt fights using the scalchop on its stomach. In response to an attack, it retaliates immediately by slashing."`As a result of strict training, each Dewott learns different forms for using the scalchops."}One swing of the sword incorporated in its armor can fell an opponent. A simple glare from one of them quiets everybody."hHard of heart and deft of blade, its turbulent blows crash into foes like ceaseless pounding waves."qExtremely cautious, one of them will always be on the lookout, but it won't notice a foe coming from behind."vWhen they see an enemy, their tails stand high, and they spit the seeds of berries stored in their cheek pouches."mThough it is a very brave Pokémon, it's also smart enough to check its foe's strength and avoid battle."bIt has black, cape-like fur that is very hard and decreases the amount of damage it receives."uBeing wrapped in its long fur is so comfortable that a person would be fine even overnight on a wintry mountain."zThey steal from people for fun, but their victims can't help but forgive them. Their deceptively cute act is perfect."jStealthily, it sneaks up on its target, striking from behind before its victim has a chance to react."nIt's good at finding berries and gathers them from all over. It's kind enough to share them with friends."tIll tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter."vThis Pokémon lives in caves in volcanoes. The fire within the tuft on its head can reach 600 degrees Fahrenheit."pWhen it gets excited, embers rise from its head and tail and it gets hot. For some reason, it loves sweets."qThe water stored inside the tuft on its head is full of nutrients. Plants that receive its water grow large."wIt prefers places with clean water. When its tuft runs low, it replenishes it by siphoning up water with its tail."kIt eats the dreams of people and Pokémon. When it eats a pleasant dream, it expels pink-colored mist."vThe dream mist coming from its forehead changes into many different colors depending on the dream that was eaten."�When a Munna egg is placed in the care of a brooding dragon, it hatches into this form. It will repeatedly headbutt Togepi if placed near one."�Excess psychic energy is vented as smoke from the hole where its gem once was. Its heart functions as a second brain that lets it communicate telepathically."kThese Pokémon live in cities. They are accustomed to people. Flocks often gather in parks and plazas."sNo matter where in the world it goes, it knows where its nest is, so it never gets separated from its Trainer."vMales have plumage on their heads. They will never let themselves feel close to anyone other than their Trainers."wIts mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use the frequency and rhythm of these flashes to communicate."mThey have lightning-like movements. When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates."qWhen it overflows with power, the orange crystal on its body glows. It looks for underground water in caves."�The blasts of energy it makes from sunbeams have terrifying power. However, it's not able to fire its blasts at night or on rainy days."�In Makyan myth, they were born from meteors that fell when the moon was split by an angry god. Their unfathomably dense armor deflects most anything."mIt was first unearthed in forbidden lands. Its body doesn't abide by the physical laws of this universe."It is more comfortable in alien dimensions than on Earth. The rocky parts of its body can't be analyzed by modern science."�They can't be understood or predicted, making them dangerous opponents. At the end of their lifespan they return to their home universe, reporting to a higher will."oThe heart-shaped mark left on a body after a Woobat has been attached to it is said to bring good fortune."zAnyone who comes into contact with the ultrasonic waves emitted by a courting male experiences a positive mood shift."WBy spinning its body, it can dig straight through the ground at a speed of 30 mph."zMore than 300 feet below the surface, they build mazelike nests. Their activity can be destructive to subway tunnels."uAudino's sense of hearing is superb. Not even a pebble rolling along over a mile away will escape Audino's ears."�They are brought into hospitals when conventional medicine fails. They can hear the number of heartbeats a person has left, but will never tell."iAlways carrying squared logs, they help out with construction. As they grow, they carry bigger logs."tThis Pokémon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch."jRather than rely on force, they master moves that utilize the centrifugal force of spinning concrete."wBy vibrating its cheeks, it emits sound waves imperceptible to humans. It uses the rhythm of these sounds to talk."dIt lives in the water and on land. It uses its long, sticky tongue to immobilize its opponents."dThey shoot paralyzing liquid from their head bumps. They use vibration to hurt their opponents."mWhen it encounters a foe bigger than itself, it wants to throw it. It changes belts as it gets stronger."xTying their belts gets them pumped and makes their punches more destructive. Disturbing their training angers them."kSince this Pokémon makes its own clothes out of leaves, it is a popular mascot for fashion designers."oIt protects itself from the cold by wrapping up in leaves. It stays on the move, eating leaves in forests."vIt keeps its eggs warm with heat from fermenting leaves. It also uses leaves to make warm wrappings for Sewaddle."eIts bite injects a potent poison, enough to paralyze large bird Pokémon that try to prey on it."nIt is usually motionless, but when attacked, it rotates at high speed and then crashes into its opponent."lWith quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails."yPerhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud."lLike the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind."wSince they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants."{Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities."�Its well-developed legs were the result of a life spent on mountains covered in deep snow. The scent it exudes from its flower crown heartens those in proximity."�It seems to pride itself on living in inhospitable conditions. If others take up residence nearby, it will move to even colder climes."�It utters royal proclamations and tyrannical edicts on a whim, becoming petulant when its disobedient subjects can't understand it."xRed and blue Basculin usually do not get along, but sometimes members of one school mingle with the other's school."nClads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream."tThey live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping."{The special membrane covering its eyes can sense the heat of objects, so it can see its surroundings even in darkness."kThey never allow prey to escape. Their jaws are so powerful, they can crush the body of an automobile."rWhen it sleeps, it pulls its limbs into its body and its internal fire goes down to 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit."~Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees Fahrenheit, making enough power that it can destroy a dump truck with one punch."�The colder they get, the more energetic they are. They freeze their breath to make snowballs, using them as ammo for playful snowball fights."�Though it has a gentle disposition, it's also very strong. It will quickly freeze the snowball on its head before going for a headbutt."_Arid regions are their habitat. They move rhythmically, making a sound similar to maracas."sWhen it finds a stone of a suitable size, it secretes a liquid from its mouth to open up a hole to crawl into."rCompeting for territory, Crustle fight viciously. The one whose boulder is broken is the loser of the battle."hProud of its sturdy skull, it suddenly headbutts everything, but its weight makes it unstable, too."oIt can smash concrete blocks with its kicking attacks. The one with the biggest crest is the group leader."gThe guardians of an ancient city, they always fly the same route while keeping watch for invaders."oEach of them carries a mask that used to be its face when it was human. Sometimes they look at it and cry."jGrave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies."hIt's said that this Pokémon was formed when an ancient clay tablet was drawn to a vengeful spirit."qNever touch its shadowlike body, or you'll be shown the horrific memories behind the picture carved into it."uThis Pokémon inhabited ancient seas. Although it can only crawl, it still comes up onto land in search of prey."�Carracosta completely devours its prey - bones, shells, and all. Because of this, Carracosta's own shell grows thick and sturdy."�This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. As research suggested, Archen is unable to fly. But it's very good at jumping."�It needs a running start to take off. If Archeops wants to fly, it first needs to run nearly 25 mph, building speed over a course of about 2.5 miles."_Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places."WConsuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies."�It's unclear what the objects embedded in its body are or where they came from. More must be added over time, though, as anything it absorbs is quickly dissolved."qTo protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon."pBonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents."�A once-departed soul, returned to life. Derives power from resentment, which rises as energy atop its head and takes on the forms of foes."qIt likes to settle grudges and fulfill final wishes. It does so to ensure peaceful passage to the afterlife."mThese Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms."_Cinccino's body is coated in a special oil that helps it deflect attacks, such as punches."{They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see."rAccording to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights."qThey can predict the future from the placement and movement of the stars. They can see Trainers' life spans."gThey drive away attackers by unleashing psychic power. They can use telepathy to talk with others."]When their two divided brains think the same thoughts, their psychic power is maximized."fWhen Reuniclus shake hands, a network forms between their brains, increasing their psychic power."{They are better at swimming than flying, and they happily eat their favorite food, peat moss, as they dive underwater."]Swanna start to dance at dusk. The one dancing in the middle is the leader of the flock."gThis Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. It sleeps buried in snow."jSnowy mountains are this Pokémon's habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas."{Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards."vThe turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon's fur. People use it to mark the seasons."bThey migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring."tThe energy made in its cheeks' electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding."fFor some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet."qThese Pokémon evolve by wearing the shell covering of a Shelmet. The steel armor protects their whole body."gIt lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball, then releases poison spores."mIt lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion."rIf its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return."mThe fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent's habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished."~They are drawn to mysterious machinery and internet influencers. Because of this, they are common in online horror media."�They led explorers to an ancient sunken city in the abyss. Its people had uploaded their minds into machines that slowly failed over the ages."zThey attach themselves to large-bodied Pokémon and absorb static electricity, which they store in an electric pouch."�Galvantula attacks its foes with the electricity stored in the fur in its abdomen. To protect itself from threats, it uses electrically charged webs."mIt absorbs the iron it finds in the rock while clinging to the ceiling. It shoots spikes when in danger."bThey attach themselves to cave ceilings, firing steel spikes at targets passing beneath them."tThe two minigears that mesh together are predetermined. Each will rebound from other minigears without meshing."qA minigear and big gear comprise its body. If the minigear it launches at a foe doesn't return, it will die."kIts red core functions as an energy tank. It fires the charged energy through its spikes into an area."wOne alone can emit only a trickle of electricity, so a group of them gathers to unleash a powerful electric shock."tThese Pokémon have a big appetite. When they spot their prey, they attack it and paralyze it with electricity."yThey crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean."TRumors of its origin are linked to a UFO crash site in the desert 50 years ago."WIt uses psychic power to control an opponent's brain and tamper with its memories."vLitwick shines a light that absorbs the life energy of people and Pokémon, which becomes the fuel that it burns."IIt arrives near the moment of death and steals spirit from the body."]The spirits burned up in its ominous flame lose their way and wander this world forever."yThey mark their territory by leaving gashes in trees with their tusks. If a tusk breaks, a new one grows in quickly."tA broken tusk will not grow back, so it diligently sharpens its tusks on river rocks after the end of a battle."rTheir sturdy tusks will stay sharp even if used to cut steel beams. These Pokémon are covered in hard armor."xTheir snot is a barometer of health. When healthy, their snot is sticky and the power of their ice moves increases."oIt freezes its breath to create fangs and claws of ice to fight with. Cold northern areas are its habitat."tWhen the weather gets hot, these Pokémon turn into water vapor. Cryscross are almost never seen during summer."uWith its icy chains, Cryogonal freezes those it encounters. It then takes its victims away to somewhere unknown."jIt evolves when bathed in an electric-like energy along with Karrablast. The reason is still unknown."vWhen its body dries out, it weakens. So, to prevent dehydration, it wraps itself in many layers of thin membrane."yIt conceals itself in the mud of the seashore. Then it waits. When prey touch it, it delivers a jolt of electricity."�Its conspicuous lips lure prey in as it lies in wait in the mud. When prey gets close, Stunfisk clamps its jagged steel fins down on them."wIn fights, they dominate with onslaughts of flowing, continuous attacks. With their sharp claws, they cut enemies."sUsing the long fur on its arms like whips, it launches into combo attacks that, once started, no one can stop."tIt warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move."`Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It's been active for thousands of years."xIt flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control."jIgnoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey."jBisharp pursues prey in the company of a large group of Pawniard. Then Bisharp finishes off the prey."\Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit."VTheir fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt."xThey will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger."sThey fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying."fScreaming a bloodcurdling battle cry, this huge and ferocious bird Pokémon went out on the hunt."{Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz."vWatching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones."�It stomps on smaller opponents with its powerful legs, sometimes toppling in the process. If its house is broken, terrible wailing emits until it is repaired."�It steeps the remains of prey within the jar it protects, stirring the concoction with its claws. Folklore says its soul is kept within the diseased mass."yIt draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them."bThey attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor."kLacking sight, it's unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves."sAfter it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along."lIt responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!"|The base of volcanoes is where they make their homes. They shoot fire from their five horns to repel attacking enemies."tWhen volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona's fire provided a replacement for the sun."jIt has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon."xSpoken of in legend, this Pokémon used its phenomenal power to destroy a castle in its effort to protect Pokémon."MLegends say this Pokémon confounded opponents with its swift movements."rWhen it is resolute, its body fills with power and it becomes swifter. Its jumps are then too fast to follow."xTornadus expels massive energy from its tail, causing severe storms. Its power is great enough to blow houses away."~The spikes on its tail discharge immense bolts of lightning. It flies around the Unova region firing off lightning bolts."rLands visited by Landorus grant such bountiful crops that it has been hailed as "The Guardian of the Fields.""cAccording to legend, this Pokémon's love gave rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui."gWhen Reshiram's tail flares, the heat energy moves the atmosphere and changes the world's weather."uConcealing itself in lightning clouds, it flies throughout the Unova region. It creates electricity in its tail."sIt generates a powerful, freezing energy inside itself, but its body became frozen when the energy leaked out."qIts melodies are sung with a special vocalization method that can control the feelings of those who hear it."kThis Pokémon existed 300 million years ago. Team Plasma altered it and attached a cannon to its back."yThis Pokémon brings victory. It is said that Trainers with Victini always win, regardless of the type of encounter."nSuch a thick shell of wood covers its head and back that even a direct hit from a truck wouldn't faze it."oThey strengthen their lower bodies by running into one another. They are very kind and won't start fights."iWhen it takes a defensive posture with its fists guarding its face, it could withstand a bomb blast."xAs it walks, it munches on a twig in place of a snack. It intimidates opponents by puffing hot air out of its ears."|When the twig is plucked from its tail, friction sets the twig alight. The flame is used to send signals to its allies."Using psychic power, it generates a fiery vortex of 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit, incinerating foes swept into this whirl of flame."�It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings."dIts swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute's time."�It appears and vanishes with a ninja's grace. It toys with its enemies using swift movements, while slicing them with throwing stars of sharpest water."wIt has ears like shovels. Digging holes strengthens its ears so much that they can sever thick roots effortlessly."}As powerful as an excavator, its ears can reduce dense bedrock to rubble. When it's finished digging, it lounges lazily."cDespite the beauty of its lilting voice, it's merciless to intruders that enter its territory."pThe hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going."nWhen attacking prey, it can reach speeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its prey off with a colossal kick."hThe powder that covers its body regulates its temperature, so it can live in any region or climate."lThe beaks of bird Pokémon can't begin to scratch its stalwart body. To defend itself, it spews powder."|The patterns on this Pokémon's wings depend on the climate and topography of its habitat. It scatters colorful scales."�They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger. These hot-blooded Pokémon are quick to fight."�With fiery breath of more than 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, they viciously threaten any challenger. The females protect the pride's cubs."�When it finds a flower it likes, it dwells on that flower its whole life long. It floats in the wind's embrace with an untroubled heart."iWhen the flowers of a well-tended flower bed bloom, it appears and celebrates with an elegant dance."|In times long past, governors of castles would invite Florges to create flower gardens to embellish the castle domains."vIf it has sunshine and water, it doesn't need to eat, because it can generate energy from the leaves on its back."gThey inhabit mountainous regions. The leader of the herd is decided by a battle of clashing horns."oIt does its level best to glare and pull a scary face, but it can't help grinning if anyone pats its head."�It charges ahead and bashes its opponents like a berserker, uncaring about any hits it might take. Its arms are mighty enough to snap a telephone pole."aHistorically, in the Kalos region, these Pokémon were the designated guardians of the king."vIt has enough psychic energy to blast everything within 300 feet of itself, but it has no control over its power."�The eyeball patterns on the interior of its ears emit psychic energy. It keeps the patterns tightly covered because that power is too immense."�If anyone dares to grab its hilt, it wraps a blue cloth around that person's arm and drains that person's life energy completely."{The complex attack patterns of its two swords are unstoppable, even for an opponent greatly accomplished at swordplay."�Apparently, it can detect the innate qualities of leadership. According to legend, whoever it recognizes is destined to become king."tIn the past, rather than using perfume, royal ladies carried a Spritzee that would waft a fragrance they liked."�Its scent is so overpowering that, unless a Trainer happens to really enjoy the smell, they will have a hard time walking alongside it."{It uses both white and black magic. It harvests the flowers that grow on witches who regularly walk between life and death."TBecause it eats nothing but sweets, its fur is as sticky sweet as cotton candy."�Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human's, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area."�It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent's will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide."�It lures its prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids."�They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline."�Barbaracle's legs and hands have minds of their own, and they will move independently. But they usually follow the head's orders."aIt looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution."XTales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return."eBorn in pristine waters, they escape detection by blending in seamlessly with underwater plants."UThey gallop on the ocean floor, cleaning it by collecting algae on their hooves."~Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock."dBy expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots."iThe frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight."It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds."�This is an ancient Pokémon, revived in modern times. It has a violent disposition, and it'll tear apart anything it gets between its hefty jaws."oThis Pokémon is from about 100,000,000 years ago. It has the presence of a king, vicious but magnificent."�This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. In the past, it lived with others of its kind in cold lands where there were fewer predators."rAurorus was restored from a fossil. It's said that when this Pokémon howls, auroras appear in the night sky."�With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against."�It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers."�It's said that somewhere in the world, there's a mineral vein housing a large pack of slumbering Carbink. It's also said that this pack has a queen."bIt can instantly create many diamonds by compressing the carbon in the air between its hands."^It's covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly."}Its entire body is covered with gooey mucus that can dissolve anything. Be sure to put gloves on if you're going to touch it."uIt attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that's the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers."The iron in Sliggoo's drinking water turned its shell metallic. This Pokémon doesn't come out of its shell on sunny days."�Able to freely control the hardness of its metallic shell. It loathes solitude and is extremely clingy-it will fume and run riot if those dearest to it ever leave its side."wIt never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime."~According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest."|Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It's kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body."^It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on."jIt enwraps its prey in its hairlike arms. It sings joyfully as it observes the suffering of its prey."{Using air of -50 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains."wThe way several Bergmite and Dreepy like to huddle on its back makes it look like an aircraft carrier made of ice."nThis Pokémon barrels along steep mountain paths, cleaving through the deep snow with its hard icy armor."uEven a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves."|The ultrasonic waves it emits from its ears can reduce a large boulder to pebbles. It swoops out of the dark to attack."aWhen the horns on its head shine in seven colors, it is said to be sharing everlasting life."wWhen its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more."iSome say it can change to an even more powerful form when battling those who threaten the ecosystem."dIt gathers things it likes and passes them through its loop to teleport them to a secret place."iIt expels its internal steam from the arms on its back. It has enough power to blow away a mountain."}It sends its feathers, which are as sharp as blades, flying in attack. Its legs are strong, so its kicks are also formidable."rThis narcissistic Pokémon is a clean freak. If you don't groom it diligently, it will stop listening to you."�It nocks its arrow quills and shoots them at opponents. When it simply can't afford to miss, it tugs the vine on its head to improve its focus."tThe air stored inside the rachises of Decidueye's feathers insulated the Pokémon against Hisui's extreme cold."�If you try too hard to get close to it, it won't open up to you. Even if you do grow close, giving it too much affection is still a no-no."�It can act spoiled if it grows close to its Trainer. A powerful Pokémon, its sharp claws can leave its Trainer's whole body covered in scratches."�Although it's rough mannered and egotistical, it finds beating down unworthy opponents boring. It gets motivated for stronger opponents."^The balloons it inflates with its nose grow larger and larger as it practices day by day."It gets excited when it sees a dance it doesn't know. This hard worker practices diligently until it can learn that dance."fTo Primarina, every battle is a stage. It takes down its prey with beautiful singing and dancing."yIt pecks at trees with its hard beak. You can get some idea of its mood or condition from the rhythm of its pecking."WIt can bend the tip of its beak to produce over a hundred different cries at will."~They smack beaks with others of their kind to communicate. The strength and number of hits tell each other how they feel."}It wanders around in a never-ending search for food. At dusk, it collapses from exhaustion and falls asleep on the spot."lOnce it finds signs of prey, it will patiently stake out the location, waiting until the sun goes down."kIf you find its nest, you shouldn't stick your hand inside. You'll get bitten by an irritated Grubbin."�It buries itself in fallen leaves and barely moves, munching away on humus. If you accidentally step on one, you'll get a shock!"�It has an organ that generates electricity in its abdomen. It concentrates energy in its jaws and fires off jolts of electricity."yIts hard pincers are well suited to both offense and defense. Fights between two Crabrawler are like boxing matches."jIt stores coldness in its pincers and pummels its foes. It can even smash thick walls of ice to bits!"�It wins the hearts of its enemies with its passionate dancing and then uses the opening it creates to burn them up with blazing flames."�Cutiefly is able to detect the aura of living things, which it uses to find flowers. Cutiefly tend to gather around beings feeling strong emotions."�Ribombee hates rain as it turns its hair dirty and its pollen damp. When storms are on the horizon, Ribombee hides in tree hollows waiting for it to pass."�As they develop, their disposition grows more violent and aggressive. Many Trainers find them too much to handle and abandon them."xThe sharp rocks in its mane can cut like knives. Lycanroc wears its prey down by degrees before finishing them off."�Bathed in the setting sun of evening, Wolferoc has undergone a special kind of evolution. An intense fighting spirit underlies its calmness."�It goads enemies into attacking, withstands the hits, and in return, delivers a headbutt, crushing their bones with its rocky mane."{They're weak, so they move in schools. However, they can also often be seen all alone, having strayed from the school."|They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off."To attack, this Pokémon sends toxic spikes flying at its enemies. Ones that come close get mown down by the claws on its feet."�It loves playing in the mud. If it isn't showered with mud on a daily basis, it gets stressed out and stops listening to its Trainer."It remains calm and unmoving no matter the situation. It mixes dirt with the saliva in its mouth to make a special kind of mud."�When two Dewpider meet, they display their water bubbles to each other. Then the one with the smaller bubble gets out of the other's way."|It usually passes its time in the water. When its belly is full, it stores its subdued prey in the water bubble on its head."When the sun rises, Fomantis spreads its four leaves and bathes in the sunlight. The tip of its head has a pleasant aroma."dFor self-protection, it pretends to be a bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear keen-edged petals."�It scatters its shining spores around itself. Even though they're dangerous, nighttime tours of forests where Morelull live are popular."�It puts its prey to sleep and siphons off their vitality through the tip of its arms. If one of its kind is weakened, it helps by sending it vitality."`The males will do whatever the females tell them. They give the females most of their food."kSalazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it."�It boasts power enough to split large trees in half. The organ on its rear releases an odor that it uses to communicate with others of its kind."}It waves its hands wildly in intimidation and warning. Life is over for anyone who doesn't run away as fast as possible."wBecause of its sweet, delicious aroma, bird Pokémon are always after it, but it's not intelligent enough to care."�It's protected by its hard sepals, so it plays with bird Pokémon without worry. They peck it relentlessly, but it doesn't care."jA master of grand and beautiful kicks, it can knock out even kickboxing champions with a single blow."�It stretches sticky vines out from its head and picks flowers to adorn itself with. When it doesn't have any flowers, it feels uneasy."|It normally spends its time meditating in the treetops. It throws Poké Balls and gives other Pokémon orders as it pleases."�They use their saliva to stick leaves to their shoulders. You can tell what troop they belong to from the position of the leaves."wIt will pick up anything it finds on the ground. Sometimes it finds coins, so Murkrow and Meowth will go after it."gThe shell covering its body is as hard as diamond. This Pokémon will do anything it takes to win."tIt likes the shovel on its head, so Sandygast will get serious and fight any children who come to take it back."�Each of its grains of sand has its own will. Palossand eats small Pokémon and siphons away their vital essence while they're still alive."�The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore."~A Pokémon weapon developed for a specific mission, it went berserk during an experiment, so it was cryogenically frozen."rThis is its form once it has awakened and evolved. Freed from its heavy mask, its speed is greatly increased."|It lives in the ozone layer, where it becomes food for stronger Pokémon. When it tries to run away, it falls to the ground."lIt stays asleep from the moment it's born. When it falls into a deep sleep, it stops moving altogether."�It lives in volcanoes and eats sulfur and other minerals. Materials from the food it eats form the basis of its explosive shell."`When it's surprised or agitated, the 14 fur spikes on its back will stand up involuntarily."�Although it's a quiet, lonely Pokémon, if you try to look at what's under its rag, it will become agitated and resist violently."�It burrows beneath the sand, radiating psychic power from the protuberance on its head. It waits for prey as it surveys the area."rIf a child it has made friends with is bullied, Drampa will find the bully's house and burn it to the ground."wIt wraps its prey in green seaweed and sucks away their vitality. It only likes to go after big prey like Wailord."�It smacks the scales on its head against rocks or against the ground to frighten its opponents. It can also contact its friends with these noises."lIt makes noise by clanging its scales together. When the rhythm has reached its peak, Hakamo-o attacks."~When it howls after finishing off its prey, the metallic sounds of its celebrating comrades can be heard from all around."�Although it's called a guardian deity, if a person or Pokémon puts it in a bad mood, it will become a malevolent deity and attack."�It heals the wounds of people and Pokémon by sprinkling them with its sparkling scales. This guardian deity is worshiped on Akala."dAlthough it's called a guardian deity, it's violent enough to crush anyone it sees as an enemy."�This guardian deity of Poni Island manipulates water. Because it lives deep within a thick fog, it came to be both feared and revered."oEven though its helpless, gaseous body can be blown away by the slightest breeze, it doesn't seem to care."yThe king who ruled Alola in times of antiquity called it the "cocoon of the stars" and built an altar to worship it."�Sometimes the result of its opening an Ultra Wormhole is that energy and life-forms from other worlds are called here to this world."yRecords of it exist in writings from long, long ago, where it was known by the name "the beast that calls the moon.""~It looks somehow pained as it rages around in search of light, which serves as its energy. It's apparently from another world."fA life-form from another world, it was dubbed a UB and is thought to produce a strong neurotoxin."|Although it's alien to this world and a danger here, it's apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives."mA life-form that lives in another world, its body is thin and supple, but it also possesses great power."�One of the mysterious life-forms known as Ultra Beasts. Astonishing electric shocks emanate from its entire body, according to witnesses."fOne of the dangerous UBs, high energy readings can be detected coming from both of its huge arms."SThis Ultra Beast's body, which is as thin as paper, is like a sharpened sword."zA dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found."\This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world."oIt stores hundreds of liters of poisonous liquid inside its body. It is one of the organisms known as UBs."|It appeared from an Ultra Wormhole. Each one appears to be made up of many life-forms stacked one on top of each other."�It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the explosion of its own head. It's apparently one kind of Ultra Beast."�It synchronizes its consciousness with others to understand their feelings. This faculty makes it useful for taking care of people."�It slips into the shadows of others and mimics their powers and movements. As it improves, it becomes stronger than those it's imitating."�It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they'll be electrocuted by the flying sparks."{It melts particles of iron and other metals found in the subsoil, so it can absorb them into its body of molten steel."Revered long ago for its capacity to create iron from nothing, for some reason it has come back to life after 3,000 years."nIt attacks with rapid beats of its stick. As it strikes with amazing speed, it gets more and more pumped."�When it's drumming out rapid beats in battle, it gets so caught up in the rhythm that it won't even notice that it's already knocked out its opponent."zBy drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle."�It has special pads on the backs of its feet, and one on its nose. Once it's raring to fight, these pads radiate tremendous heat."sIt kicks berries right off the branches of trees and then juggles them with its feet, practicing its footwork."�It's skilled at both offense and defense, and it gets pumped up when cheered on. But if it starts showboating, it could put itself in a tough spot."mWhen it gets wet, its skin changes color, and this Pokémon becomes invisible as if it were camouflaged."mHighly intelligent but also very lazy, it keeps enemies out of its territory by laying traps everywhere."�Its nictitating membranes let it pick out foes' weak points so it can precisely blast them with water that shoots from its fingertips at Mach 3."�It eats berries nonstop, a habit that has made it more resilient than it looks. It'll show up on farms, searching for yet more berries."zCommon throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon has strong teeth and can chew through the toughest of berry shells."�Jumping nimbly about, this small-bodied Pokémon takes advantage of even the slightest opportunity to disorient larger opponents."eThe lessons of many harsh battles have taught it how to accurately judge an opponent's strength."With their great intellect and flying skills, these Pokémon very successfully act as the Galar region's airborne taxi service."iOften found in gardens, this Pokémon has hairs on its body that it uses to assess its surroundings."xAs it grows inside its shell, it uses its psychic abilities to monitor the outside world and prepare for evolution."{It emits psychic energy to observe and study what's around it, and what's around it can include things over six miles away."�Cunning and cautious, this Pokémon survives by stealing food from others. It erases its tracks with swipes of its tail as it makes off with its plunder."lWith a lithe body and sharp claws, it goes around stealing food and eggs. Boltund is its natural enemy."~It whirls around in the wind while singing a joyous song. This delightful display has charmed many into raising this Pokémon."rThe cotton on the head of this Pokémon can be spun into a glossy, gorgeous yarn, a Galar regional specialty."}If its fleece grows too long, Wooloo won't be able to move. Cloth made with the wool of this Pokémon is surprisingly strong."dIts majestic horns are meant only to impress the opposite gender. They never see use in battle."�It starts off battles by attacking with its rock-hard horn, but as soon as the opponent flinches, this Pokémon bites down and never lets go."xThis Pokémon rapidly extends its retractable neck to sink its sharp fangs into distant enemies and take them down."�It balances itself like a sumo wrestler, making it nearly impossible to topple. Its squishy flesh is even more resilent than its shell."This gluttonous Pokémon only assists people with their work because it wants treats. As it runs, it crackles with electricity."rIt sends electricity through its legs to boost their strength. Running at top speed, it easily breaks 50 mph."`It can race around like a unicycle, even on rough, rocky terrain. Burning coal sustains it."�By rapidly rolling its legs, it can travel at over 18 mph. The temperature of the flames it breathes exceeds 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit."}While it's engaged in battle, its mountain of coal will burn bright red, sending off sparks that scorch the surrounding area."gAs soon as it's born, it burrows into an apple. The apple serves as both a food source and a home."sIt flies on wings of apple skin and spits a powerful acid. It can also change its shape into that of an apple."}A nectarous scent wafts from its body, luring in the bug Pokémon it preys on. The skin on its back is especially yummy."�The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out."cSeven syrpents live inside an apple made of syrup. The syrpent in the center is the commander."eIt spews sand from its nostrils. While the enemy is blinded, it burrows into the ground to hide."^Its unique style of coiling allows it to blast sand out of its sand sac more efficiently."�Its rough belly scales can pulverize entire quarries for sand to use in battle. Its fights with Flygon in the center of desert storms are the stuff of legend."�This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda whole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake and tries to swallow a Pokémon other than its preferred prey."nAfter it's eaten its fill, its movements become extremely sluggish. That's when Cramorant swallows it up."�It spins its tail fins to propel itself, surging forward at speeds of over 100 knots before ramming prey and spearing into them."�It manipulates the chemical makeup of its poison to produce electricity. The voltage is weak, but it can cause a tingling paralysis."lThis short-tempered and aggressive Pokémon chugs stagnant water to absorb any toxins it might contain."�It subconsciously broadcasts the audio of its battles over radio waves. Tuning in at the right time will let you hear the performance of a lifetime."�It wraps prey up with its heated body, cooking them in its coils. Once they're well-done, it will voraciously nibble them down to the last morsel."~While its burning body is already dangerous on its own, this excessively hostile Pokémon also has large and very sharp fangs."�Even solid titanium will melt in its coils. It uses the massive mirage it creates to confuse Volcarona in their frequent contests."�Its tentacles tear off easily, but it isn't alarmed when that happens, it knows they'll grow back. It's about as smart as a three-year-old."{Searching for an opponent to test its skills against, it emerges onto land. Once the battle is over, it returns to the sea."{The teacup in which this Pokémon makes its home is a famous piece of antique tableware. Many forgeries are in circulation."�Leaving leftover black tea unattended is asking for this Pokémon to come along and pour itself into it, turning the tea into a new Polteageist."pIt spends days relaxing on the beach. Its rest is often interrupted by someone who confuses it for a drink."lDespite its refreshing scent, those who drink of its colorful liquid are swiftly put into a deep sleep."sIf this Pokémon senses a strong emotion, it will run away as fast as it can. It prefers areas without people."�Using the braids on its head, it pummels foes to get them to quiet down. One blow from those braids would knock out a professional boxer."�If you're too loud around it, you risk being torn apart by the claws on its tentacle. This Pokémon is also known as the Forest Witch."tIt sneaks into people's homes, stealing things and feasting on the negative energy of the frustrated occupants."tWith sly cunning, it tries to lure people into the woods. Some believe it to have the power to make crops grow."}Its hairs work like muscle fibers. When its hairs unfurl, they latch on to opponents, ensnaring them as tentacles would."\They say that any patisserie visited by Milcery is guaranteed success and good fortune."_When Alcremie is content, the cream it secretes from its hands becomes sweeter and richer."�So tall it seems to defy the heavens, it lords its elevated position over other Pokémon. It grants its Trainer knowledge of sweet and sour."�The six of them work together as one Pokémon. Teamwork is also their battle strategy, and they constantly change their formation as they fight."�It stores electricity in each spine. Even if one gets broken off, it still continues to emit electricity for at least three hours."|It eats snow that piles up on the ground. The more snow it eats, the bigger and more impressive the spikes on its back grow."�It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away."pOnce a year, on a specific date and at a specific time, they gather out of nowhere and form up in a circle."�This Pokémon keeps its heat-sensitive head cool with ice. It fishes for its food, dangling its single hair into the sea to lure in prey."{Through its horns, it can pick up on the emotions of creatures around it. Positive emotions are the source of its strength."�It carries electrically roasted seeds with it as if they're precious treasures. No matter how much it eats, it always gets hungry again in short order."�If a job requires serious strength, this Pokémon will excel at it. Its copper body tarnishes in the rain, turning a vibrant green color."~These Pokémon live in herds. Their trunks have incredible grip strength, strong enough to crush giant rocks into powder."�After evolution, it has taken on the appearance of a great monument. If revered, it will protect nearby villages from all manner of disaster."|The powerful muscles in its tail generate its electricity. Compared to its lower body, its upper half is entirely too small."�This Pokémon lived on prehistoric seashores and was able to preserve food with the ice on its body. It went extinct because it moved so slowly."Its mighty legs are capable of running at speeds exceeding 40 mph, but this Pokémon can't breathe unless it's underwater."sThe skin on its face is impervious to attack, but breathing difficulties made this Pokémon go extinct anyway."�The special metal that composes its body is very light, so this Pokémon has considerable agility. It lives in caves because it dislikes the rain."�Nostalgic for the cavern home it has outgrown, it will weep molten glass. Those without trainers may find company serving as rookeries for bird Pokémon."|It gathers static electricity from its surroundings. The beams it launches when down on all fours are tremendously powerful."�If this weak Pokémon is by itself, a mere child could defeat it. But if Dreepy has friends to help it train, it can evolve and become much stronger."�Without a Dreepy to place on its head and care for, it gets so uneasy it'll try to substitute any Pokémon it finds for the missing Dreepy."nApparently the Dreepy inside Dragapult's horns eagerly look forward to being launched out at Mach speeds."{This Pokémon has slumbered for many years. Some say it's Zamazenta's elder sister, others say the two Pokémon are rivals."{This Pokémon slept for aeons while in the form of a statue. It was asleep for so long, people forgot that it ever existed."�It was inside a meteorite that fell 20,000 years ago. There seems to be a connection between this Pokémon and the Dynamax phenomenon."~If Kubfu pulls the long white hair on its head, its fighting spirit heightens and power wells up from the depths of its belly."�Inhabiting the mountains of a distant region, this Pokémon races across sheer cliffs, training its legs and refining its moves."{Once the vines on Zarude's body tear off, they become nutrients in the soil. This helps the plants of the forest grow."xGlastrier has tremendous physical strength, and the mask of ice covering its face is 100 times harder than diamond."|As it dashes through the night, Spectrier absorbs the life-force of sleeping creatures. It craves silence and solitude."�Calyrex is a merciful Pokémon, capable of providing healing and blessings. It has the power to cause hearts to mend and plants to spring forth."@This Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system."GThis Pokemon exists just to test the PBS Extensions system. Again!"{This is the form Castform takes on the brightest of days. Its skin is unexpectedly hot to the touch, so approach with care."|This is the form Castform takes when soaked with rain. When its body is compressed, water will seep out as if from a sponge."�This is the form Castform takes when covered in snow. Its body becomes an ice-like material, with a temperature near -5 degrees Celsius."uThis is the form Castform takes when sand sweeps up. Its body is made of particles that are constantly spinning."yThis is the form Castform takes when the moon rises. The particles in its body take on mystical fae-like properties."|This is the form Castform takes when an eclipse covers the sky. It moves around using its hands made of pure psychic energy."|This Rotom has possessed a convection microwave oven that uses a special motor. It also has a flair for manipulating flames."yThis form of Rotom enjoys coming up with water-based pranks. Be careful with it if you don't want your room flooded."zRotom assumes this form when it takes over a refrigerator powered by a special motor. It battles by spewing cold air."�In this form, Rotom applies its new power over wind to its love of pranks. It will happily blow away any important documents it can find."�This is Rotom after it's seized control of a lawn mower that has a special motor. As it mows down grass, it scatters the clippings everywhere."�Radiant light caused Dialga to take on a form with the appearance of the creator. Dialga now wields such colossal strength that this must be its true form."�It soars across the sky in a form that greatly resembles the creator of all things. Perhaps this is Palkia's strategy for gaining Arceus's powers."�Giratina loses its legs upon changing into this form. This Pokémon must hail from a world where the heavens and the earth are as one."Even Basculin, which devours everything it can with its huge jaws, is nothing more than food to organisms stronger than itself."rIt has foreseen that a world of truth will arrive for people and Pokémon. It strives to protect that future."It's said that this Pokémon battles in order to protect the ideal world that will exist in the future for people and Pokémon."xThe power that lay hidden in its body now covers its horn, turning it into a sword that can slice through anything."mSpirits that wander this world are placed into Pumpkaboo's body. They're then moved on to the afterlife."mWhen taking spirits to the afterlife, large Pumpkaboo prefer the spirits of adults to those of children."gMassive Pumpkaboo are said to be the product of areas where a great number of lost souls lingered."�Eerie cries emanate from its body in the dead of night. The sounds are said to be the wails of spirits who are suffering in the afterlife."lLarge Gourgeist put on the guise of adults, taking the hands of children to lead them to the afterlife."^Supersized Gourgeist aren't picky. They will forcefully drag anyone off to the afterlife."�This is Zygarde when about 10% of its pieces have been assembled. It leaps at its opponent's chest and sinks its sharp fangs into them."|This is Zygarde's perfected form. From the orifice on its chest, it radiates high-powered energy that eliminates everything."�It creates an electric charge by rubbing its feathers together. It dances over to its enemies and delivers shocking electrical punches."tThis Oricorio relaxes by swaying gently. This increases its psychic energy, which it then fires at its enemies."tIt summons the dead with its dreamy dancing. From their malice, it draws power with which to curse its enemies."�Weak Wishiwashi school together to concentrate their power. Their united force makes them the demon of the sea, feared near and far."�If its core stays exposed, it will soon die off. It's possible that it may survive if it's put into a Poké Ball quickly enough."{Sad that its true identity may be exposed, Mimikyu will mercilessly seek revenge on any opponent that breaks its neck."|This is Necrozma's form while it's absorbing the power of Solgaleo, making it extremely ferocious and impossible to control."yLunala no longer has a will of its own. Now under the control of Necrozma, it continuously expels all of its energy."sThe light pouring out from all over its body affects living things and nature, impacting them in various ways."pThe slightest shock is sometimes enough to get this Pokémon to spit out the Arrokuda lodged in its throat."{The half-swallowed Pikachu is so startled that it isn't struggling yet, but it's still looking for a chance to strike back."�The hair on its head connects to the surface of its brain. When this Pokémon has something on its mind, its hair chills the air around it."�They diligently serve people and Pokémon so they can gather feelings of gratitude. The females are particularly good at babysitting."rHunger hormones affect its temperament. Until its hunger is appeased, it gets up to all manner of evil deeds."�Able to cut down anything with a single strike, it became known as the Fairy King's Sword, and it inspired awe in friend and foe alike."zNow that it's equipped with its shield, it can shrug off impressive blows, including the attacks of Dynamax Pokémon."�This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in defeating foes by raining many blows down on them. Its strikes are nonstop, flowing like a river."~It's said that this Pokémon once moved a large forest—and all the Pokémon living there—to a new location overnight."�Legend says that by using its power to see all events from past to future, this Pokémon saved the creatures of a forest from a meteorite strike."jWhen wounded, it stops moving. It goes as still as stone to meditate, sharpening its mind and spirit."�Darmanitan takes this form when enraged. It won't stop spewing flames until its rage has settled, even if its body starts to melt."�This form has gotten enough energy to go further beyond a normal Ampharos' power. It has been calculated that each orb has over 9000 volts of energy each in it."�Garchomp taking this form are rare due to its specific conditions required. This is good as it can turn a house into splinters if left unchecked."�The already aggressive Gyarados is only amplified by this form. All it can feel in this form is pure rage. Cruise ships have been bisected for getting in its path."�The pain of seeing those it cares for fall has brought out this form. Its pure heart powers its abilities to be much more powerful."|The pain of seeing those it wishes to protect fall has causes this form to emerge. Its red blades are powered by pure heart."|Psychic power has augmented its muscles. Its arms are able to stretch up to ten feet, and it can crush titanium in its grip."�The DNA from the original Mew has grown exponentially in this form. It has gained enough psychic power to control the minds of even the strongest willed people."zIt differs from other Basculin in several respects, including demeanor. It is much gentler than other color variants."vThis special Ursaluna can see in the dark with its left eye and protects itself with mud that is as hard as iron.">This form also exists to test the PBS Extensions feature.Iu;␀�[[�"A"Normal"Plant Cloak"Overcast"West Sea"
