 attack. The user's HP is restored by 75% of the damage dealt."aThe user makes a scary sound by shaking, forcing the target to switch out. Always goes last."UThe user wraps the target in its vines, trapping and binding it for three turns."_The user whips their legs into the target like a plant. This has a 10% chance of leeching."|Guaranteed to critical hit if the target has no stat step changes. The target is surged forward, raising all its stats."nThe user assists an ally's next move, boosting its power by 50% and letting it move right after the user."QA flare of electricity creates a bright light, damaging all nearby battlers."TFor the rest of the round, the target's healing is reversed. Always goes first."�The user and the target pit their energy against one another. The damage is based on the target's Sp. Atk rather than their Sp. Def."�The user surges with electricity. If it deals less than 50% of the target's max health, the user takes the difference as recoil."jThe user wraps their body in electricity and crashes into the target. The user also takes 20% recoil."ERevives a fainted party member to 1 HP. Only one use per battle."cThe user breaks down all insulation to send a barrage of electricity to rampage for two turns."rThe user forces electricity between opposite points on the target's body. Super effective versus Steel-types."_The user harnesses a blade of lightning and slices at the target. Can random critical hit."dThe target is punched with a tremendous electric force. This move can't be used twice in a row."PThe user lets out an electric roar, raising the user's Speed by four steps."mThe user slashes all opposing Pokémon with tendrils of electricity, lowering their Attack by two steps."xThe user attacks with courage. Sets a Spikes hazard layer if Full. If Hangry, deals double damage and is Dark-type."rThe user dances to heal an ally by half of their max HP. They're cured of any non-volatile status conditions."jCloaking itself in light energy, the use