 ItemsIu;␀7[[�"TAn item that prevents wild Pokémon from appearing for 100 steps after its use."ZRare contraband. Any average solo trainer will flee from the stench of its explosion."WRare contraband. Use it to become invisible to average solo trainers for 15 steps."ZA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It is colored orange."bA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It has a thunderbolt pattern."_A peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It is a clear, light blue."[A peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It has a leaf pattern."eA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It is as black as the night sky."]A peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It is as red as the sun."bA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It is as dark as dark can be."[A peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It sparkles like eyes."eA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It shines with a dazzling light."`A peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. It has a snowflake pattern."kA many-colored stone that makes a lot of Pokémon evolve. Can be used in place of any evolution stone."MA glimmering tiara made of diamonds. It makes a certain Pokémon evolve.":A shining helmet. It makes a certain Pokémon evolve."6A cool scarf. It makes a certain Pokémon evolve."XA beautiful floral wreath from Alola that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve."ZA wreath made from woven Galarica Twigs. It makes certain species of Pokémon evolve."cA peculiar apple that can make a certain species of Pokémon evolve. It's exceptionally sweet."bA peculiar apple that can make a certain species of Pokémon evolve. It's exceptionally tart."dA peculiar apple that can make a certain species of Pokémon evolve. It's exceptionally syrupy."QA fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It resembles Omanyte."PA fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It resembles Kabuto."`A piece of amber that contains the genes of an Aerodactyl. It is clear with a reddish tint."PA fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It resembles Lileep."QA fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It resembles Anorith."XA fossil from a prehistoric Pokémon that lived on the land. It resembles Cranidos."XA fossil from a prehistoric Pokémon that lived on the land. It resembles Shieldon."cA fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea in ancient times. It resembles Tirtouga."`A fossil of an ancient Pokémon that flew in the sky in ancient times. It resembles Archen."[A fossil from a prehistoric Pokémon that once lived on the land. It resembles Tyrunt."[A fossil from a prehistoric Pokémon that once lived on the land. It resembles Amaura."_A fossil from a strange Pokémon that once lived on the land. It resembles Makyan Omanyte."^A fossil from a strange Pokémon that once lived on the land. It resembles Makyan Kabuto."JA sweet honey with a sweeter aroma. It can be sold to shops for $750."=A beautiful feather. It can be sold to shops for $1,500."CA beautiful metal feather. It can be sold to shops for $7,500."AA small and rare mushroom. It can be sold to shops for $250."CA large and rare mushroom. It can be sold to shops for $2,500."ZA rare mushroom which gives off a nice fragrance. It can be sold to shops for $7,500."gA somewhat-small pearl that sparkles in a pretty silver color. It can be sold to shops for $1,000."dA quite-large pearl that sparkles in a pretty silver color. It can be sold to shops for $4,000."bVery large pearls that sparkle in a pretty silver color. It can be sold to shops for $10,000."[Lovely, red-colored sand with a loose, silky feel. It can be sold to shops for $1,500."^A shard of a pretty gem that sparkles in a red color. It can be sold to shops for $6,000."cA shard which fell to the ground when a comet approached. It can be sold to shops for $12,500."_A nugget of pure gold that gives off a lustrous gleam. It can be sold to shops for $5,000."dA big nugget of pure gold that gives off a lustrous gleam. It can be sold to shops for $20,000."HA very tasty tail of something. It can be sold to shops for $4,000."dA bone that is extremely valuable for Pokémon archaeology. It can be sold to shops for $2,500."dA copper coin used in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. It can be sold to shops for $1,000."dA silver coin used in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. It can be sold to shops for $5,000."cA gold coin used in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. It can be sold to shops for $10,000."^A vase made in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. It can be sold to shops for $30,000."bA bracelet made in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. It can be sold to shops for $80,000."[A stone figure made in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. Can be sold for $150,000."TA crown made in a civilization about 3,000 years ago. Can be sold for $300,000."bHeld item that makes the holder immune to Ground-type moves. Bursts once hit with any attack."hWhen held by a Pokémon who can still evolve, reduces move damage taken by 33%. Prevents evolution."KA held item. In battles, it sets the holder's base Attack stat to 120."LA held item. In battles, it sets the holder's base Sp. Atk stat to 120."FA very light stone. It halves the weight of a Pokémon when held."PA held item. It raises Sp. Def by 50% but prevents the use of status moves."PA held item. It raises Defense by 50% but prevents the use of status moves."[A held item. Its Attack and Sp. Atk raise by four steps if hit by a move it's weak to."iWhen held, it boosts Speed by two steps when intimidated, fascinated, or frustrated once per battle."\Damages attackers for 1/8th of their HP when they hit the holder with physical attacks."[Damages attackers for 1/8th of their HP when they hit the holder with special attacks."[If the holder is hit by an attack, it will switch with another Pokémon in your party."kA card with a mysterious power. When the holder is hit by an attack, the attacker is forced to switch."\A held item. This discarded carapace lets the holder switch out of battle without fail."`A held item. It is an egg filled with happiness that earns 50% extra Exp. Points in battle."pA held item. If the wielder enters a battle, money and coins generated in that battle are increased by 50%."ZA held item. The comforting chime of this bell makes it gain happiness twice as fast."cA held item. It prevents wild Pokémon encounters if the holder is the first one in the party."LHeld item which ups Attack by 40%, but allows the use of only one move."MHeld item which ups Sp. Atk by 40%, but allows the use of only one move."MHeld item which boosts Speed by 40% but allows the use of only one move."SHeld item which boosts move damage by 25%, but lowers the user's Speed by 15%."HA held item. When the holder summons sunshine, it lasts 50% longer."IA held item. When the holder summons rainstorm, it lasts 50% longer."KA held item. When the holder summons a sandstorm, it lasts 50% longer."DA held item. When the holder summons hail, it lasts 50% longer."GA held item. When the holder summons eclipse, it lasts 50% longer."HA held item. When the holder summons moonglow, it lasts 50% longer."]An item to be held by a Pokémon. Protective screens will be effective for 3 more turns."^An item to be held by a Pokémon. It doubles the duration of Rooms created by the holder."JA held item that doubles the duration of binding moves and abilities."YA held item. It makes "two to five" multi-hit attacks consistently hit 4 or 5 times."ZA held item. The user gets both of its legal abilities, but its stats are cut by 10%."JA held item. Signature attacks made by the holder are boosted by 40%."\A held item. The holder recovers 30% more HP from draining moves, Aqua Ring, and leech."_Item that restores the HP of Poison-types by 1/16th. Inflicts 1/8th damage on other types."PA held item. The holder's HP is restored by 1/16th at the end of each turn."QA held item. The holder restores 1/5th HP of the damage it deals with moves."pA held item. At half health, the holder breaks the balloon and gains an Aqua Ring, healing 10% HP per turn."QA held item. It snaps the holder out of a variety of mental warping effects."9A held item. It restores any lowered stat in battle."GA held item. Lowered stats on the holder are also applied to foes."IA held item. Doubles the Speed of the holder's move once per battle."cA held item. Boosts the power of a special move by 15% and makes it physical, once per battle."cA held item. Boosts the power of a physical move by 15% and makes it special, once per battle."NA held item. It allows the immediate use of a move that charges up first."SA held item. It allows user to skip the recharging turn of an exhausting move."[A held item. When a foe raises their stats, the herb is consumed to copy the increase."[A held item. When a foe raises their stats, the herb is consumed to reset their stats."OA held item. Ensures a random additional effect activates once per battle."OA held item. Ensures a less than full accuracy move lands once per battle."]A held item. It boosts the power of moves by 30%, but at the cost of 10% HP on each hit."KA well-worn belt that boosts the holder's supereffective moves by 20%."nA held item. Boosts a move used consecutively by 20% more each time. This resets if another move is used."RA held item. It is a headband that boosts the power of physical moves by 15%."^A held item. It is a thick pair of glasses that boosts the power of special moves by 15%."9A held item. They are boots that boost Speed by 10%.";A held item. Doubles the holder's critical-hit chance."SA held item. It is a magnifying lens that boosts the Accuracy of moves by 35%."LHeld item which forces the holder to move last in its priority bracket."bA held item. If it has full HP, the holder will endure one potential KO attack, leaving 1 HP."VA held item. A bizarre orb that inflicts burn on the holder at the end of a turn."[A held item. A bizarre orb that inflicts frostbite on the holder at the end of a turn."XA held item. A bizarre orb that inflicts poison on the holder at the end of a turn."lA held item that damages the holder on every turn. It may latch on to Pokémon that attacks the holder."YA held item. When the holder's stats are lowered, it will be switched out of battle."GThese boots prevent the effects of hazards set on the battlefield."`Raises Sp. Atk by two steps when the Pokémon uses a sound move the first time each battle."_Raises Attack by two steps when the Pokémon uses a slice move the first time each battle."]Raises Speed by two steps when the Pokémon uses a wind move the first time each battle."`Raises Speed by two steps when the Pokémon uses a kicking move the first time each battle."hConsumed to heal for one third of max HP when the Pokémon uses a punching move. This can overheal."eConsumed to heal for one third of max HP when the Pokémon uses a pulse move. This can overheal."UBlinds all foes when the Pokémon uses a biting move the first time each battle."TBlinds all foes when the Pokémon uses a light move the first time each battle."OA held item. The holder is protected from the negative effects of weather."dA held item. It changes the holder's type in battle. You can change which type between battles."nA set of memory discs, one for each type. If held by a Silvally, you can change its type between battles."mA tablet that boosts same-type moves by 20%. If held by Arceus, you can change its type between battles."LAn item to be held by a Pokémon. It counts as a member of every tribe."]A held item. The holder doesn't trigger items, abilities, or effects of targets it hits."qA held item. Moves used against the holder deal 10% less move damage and can't trigger random added effects."9A held item. The holder is protected from flinching."WA held item. The holder is protected from stat drops (except 